window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":4501,"title":"Chapter 4501: Chapter 4500: Dawn I","paragraphs":["THE Civilizational Authority Resistance.","THE Organ of Civilization.","Noah heard these words booming across his existence while he felt the immense amplified Effort across his being, from the moment he was born and even before, all flowing towards this singular purpose.","What was this?","He analyzed the concept with cold logic even as his existence burned. He was too far away from THE . Even though Complexity and Purity could not be considered the immense factors in attaining THE , even though right now he was in the Septillions, he instinctively knew that he was truly far away from the next Scale of Existence.","So for him to be awakening anything that had capital THE in the name was utterly astounding.","And the only way that it made sense was through the simple words that echoed in his mind.","Only THE Civilizational Authority can go against THE Civilizational Authority.","The Glorious Evolution that all of his accumulated effort was seeking to impose could only have something with THE in it or it would have been ineffective against the curse. The logic was sound. Existence itself was confirming it.","So at this moment, as Noah felt the excruciating pain of burning across the entirety of his existence, he observed as the immense amplified effort of his entire life caused a singularity to bloom.","HUUM !","This singularity was unique. This singularity was colorless, like concentrated Quintessence itself. And it bloomed at the very center of his brain, nestled in the space between thought and being.","It felt extremely delicate and intricate as he examined it with his inner senses. Any single thing that could possibly go wrong would cause everything to collapse. The structure was fragile, newly born, struggling to maintain coherence.","And yet, Noah felt unfathomable amounts of effort and Civilizational Authority of Mana and Hunger flow into it like rivers feeding an ocean. And the moment that it was fully formed...","\" Ah...\"","He couldn’t help but gasp as sensation overwhelmed analysis for a brief moment.","This point of colorless brilliance began to feel like a fundamental part of his existence, as natural as his heartbeat or the flow of Primus Mana through his channels. And at this moment, he observed something remarkable.","The crimson-gold flames that were burning him and permeating across his existence could not find their entry into this colorless brilliance.","It became the only part of his existence that was not affected by the curse from THE Living Elemental.","And the moment it emerged, a sensation of coolness erupted from it like a wave washing across a shore. It spread across his existence with gentle but persistent force, and it made the excruciating pain... slightly less excruciating.","Slightly more bearable.","It was not relief, not truly, but it was the difference between drowning and keeping one’s head above water.","As Noah felt this sensation and catalogued it with careful precision, new prompts bloomed before his vision.","| THE Organ of Civilization is forming.|","|There are countless ways to attain THE distinction, countless paths to enter The Civilizational Scale of Existence.|","|As of this moment, you are embarking on your own novel way as your Primus Mana has paved the path alongside immense effort and harvest to bring something new into what is considered Observable Existence.|","| THE Organ of Civilization has bloomed within your existence.|","|Classification: It can be considered akin to a stairway towards THE , towards The Civilizational Scale of Existence.|","|Warning: It is novel and unproven. Its development will be guided by you in how it forms and evolves.|","|It sits at a core component of your existence. Any mistakes in its cultivation would mean the immediate collapse of your existence.|","|Current Effect: With THE Organ of Civilization forming, you have gained 1% THE Civilizational Authority Resistance.|","| THE Immolation Of The Sacrilegious Savage can now be withstood with slightly less excruciating pain, but the pain still persists at a high intensity.|","| THE Organ of Civilization is inherently connected with your Primordial Civilization of Mana and Hunger.|","|It will advance and form its identity as your Civilization progresses.|","|Resource Requirement: Analysis indicates it will need an immense amount of resources and harvest for any advancement, scaled to the quality of infinity inherent in your Primus Mana.|","...!","1% THE Civilizational Authority Resistance.","This was the cooling sensation he felt in a sea of excruciating pain that still occurred, but now the difference was measurable. Quantifiable.","Noah raised his hand with deliberate slowness, testing the change. Gloriously, it did not tremble from the pain as he stood on the surface of the Cultivation Citadel. His entire existence was still being burned by crimson-gold flames, but at this moment... he did not tremble.","His eyes flashed with a sense of solemnity as he looked inward, examining the space in his brain where THE Organ of Civilization lay. He could barely perceive its circular shape and the colorless brilliance that reminded him of pure Quintessence.","But it felt like an endless black hole that would take everything he could feed it, and its results... would be unfathomably immense.","When THE Living Elemental cursed his existence with such malice and certainty, never could he have possibly dreamed that Noah would somehow gain this as a byproduct, could he?","The irony was not lost on Noah. The curse had forced him to evolve. The pain had created the path forward.","And now that it did bloom, now that he saw a light at the end of a horrendously dark tunnel, he would barrel towards this light with relentless speed until one day he would make THE Living Elemental feel like collapsing his own existence.","Because even though he persevered, even though what he felt right now was still excruciating but slightly more bearable, his existence had still risen up with the thought multiple times of surrender.","Maybe if I collapsed myself, I could escape this pain.","That thought had risen multiple times like a demon whispering in his ear, and he had crushed it down every time. Only by will, and will alone.","He hated that any existence could cause him to feel such a sensation. He hated that he had been brought so low, forced to consider ending himself just to escape torment.","He would rectify this. He would pay this forward with interest compounded over eons.","THE Living Elemental could count on it.","Noah stood straighter on the Cultivation Citadel, his body still wreathed in flames but no longer trembling. He observed the weight of existence pressing down on him from this place, noted how it interacted with the curse and his newly formed Organ.","Everything was data. Everything was a variable to be measured and understood.","And understanding, he had learned, was the first step to victory.","Knowledge continued to be key.","He looked up towards where The Infiniverse hovered above, watching him with those eyes of golden light."]},{"number":4502,"title":"Chapter 4502: Chapter 4501: Dawn II","paragraphs":["As Noah was thinking all of this, The Infiniverse approached with a solemn expression etched across her features.","\"Slightly less excruciating?\" she asked quietly. \"Bearable?\"","...!","Noah looked at her and felt a sense of warmth pierce through the constant burning. He knew what she had done. He knew how she had exposed herself to his pain through their connection, how she should know exactly what he now felt every moment of his existence.","So he simply nodded as he said with calm certainty, \"Less excruciating.\"","The Infiniverse nodded in acknowledgment as she calmly said, \"Okay. There is lots of work to be done.\"","Noah looked at her and nodded before he spoke with deliberate care. \"Take it easy on the countless lifeforms out there. THE Living Elemental is responsible for this. The weak Living Elementals and Fold Dwellers across the Folds are not. Let’s make sure our rage does not spill onto them unnecessarily.\"","...!","At his words, The Infiniverse paused as she calmly said, \"They won’t feel my rage, but... there will be conquest.\"","BOOM !","The air trembled with the weight of her declaration.","\"I’ve never needed to conquer to grow in a while now,\" The Infiniverse continued with terrifying calm. \"I don’t need to devour the Folds. I don’t need to conquer the countless lifeforms in Observable Existence to advance my power. But I have a duty. You are my duty. And I plan to fulfill my duty, no matter what. No matter if all of Observable Existence has to burn for this duty to be completed.\"","...!","With such terrifying words carrying the weight of absolute conviction, The Infiniverse disappeared from the space.","\"...\"","Noah looked at where she had been standing as he shook his head and continued to try and understand THE Organ of Civilization that had just bloomed within him. He sent his Primus Mana and Civilizational Authority of Mana and Hunger into it with careful precision, observing the reaction.","The organ responded to his probing with something like hunger.","He came to find that the more he flooded his Primus Mana and Civilizational Authority of Mana and Hunger into it, THE Organ of Civilization actually pulsed with eagerness like a genuine organ demanding sustenance. The sensation was strange and new, as if a heart had appeared in his brain that beat to a different rhythm than the rest of his body.","So he flooded more and more into it with methodical persistence.","After a few minutes of continuous feeding, droves of Primus Mana and Civilizational Authority of Mana and Hunger flowing into it like rivers into an ocean, he finally received a reaction from this thing that bore the distinction of THE .","THE Organ of Civilization pulsed with brilliant blue gold light.","Noah felt in the next moment, centered in his head, an unfathomably dense and pure authority being released from this organ. It caused all of his existence to buzz with resonance, every cell vibrating in harmony with this new frequency.","New prompts bloomed before his vision.","| THE Organ of Civilization has processed the provided resources.|","|Result: An extremely unique and Unquantifiable Unit of Everything has appeared within your existence.|","|Effect: Just from the appearance of this Unquantifiable Unit of Everything , the Complexity and Purity of your existence has doubled from 3.5 Septillion to 7 Septillion.|","|This unit defies standard measurement and categorization.|","|Unknown potential applications detected.|","...!","The prompts were ridiculous to see as Noah’s eyes pulsed with tyranny and immensity, but he forced himself to analyze them logically.","First, yes, his Complexity and Purity had risen ridiculously due to the excruciating pain he was always bearing since THE Living Elemental applied THE Immolation Of The Sacrilegious Savage.","He had continued to gain more than one hundred Sextillion every little while until at this point it had reached 3.5 Septillion before this sudden doubling.","The rate of increase was utterly ridiculous when one truly thought about it with any degree of objectivity. The jump to Sextillion had been grand initially, with Khor having been in the lead with just a little bit over 200 Sextillion. Of course The Infiniverse had taken the lead when she reached 1 Septillion through her own growth.","And due to the excruciating pain from this curse, Noah had exploded upwards to 3.5 Septillion and now to 7 Septillion with this single production.","Whenever he observed this number jumping rapidly as he continued to advance more and more in Complexity and Purity, and yet absolutely nothing had occurred to diminish the terrifying pain of thr curse within his existence, it further confirmed the truth he had been analyzing.","In the future, when it came to dealing with existences that had the power of THE , Complexity and Purity would not be metrics that held immense importance.","An unfathomable qualitative leap would be occurring as the power of the existences of the Civilizational Scale was still a little hard to grasp fully.","Because of this reality, something that came from within his existence from an organ that had the label of THE , something that emerged from such a thing...could effectively double his Complexity and Purity so simply.","Noah looked within his existence with careful observation to examine the Unquantifiable Unit of Everything that flowed out of THE Organ of Civilization.","It was remarkable to behold.","The unit appeared as a Mobius strip suspended in conceptual space, and when he focused his perception inside of it, he observed an extremely dense and pure concentration of Primus Mana and Civilizational Authority of Mana and Hunger.","These authorities were spinning around each other in complex patterns akin to how an atom had electrons, protons, and neutrons moving in orbital shells. The Primus Mana formed the core nucleus, dense and brilliant blue-gold. Around it, the Civilizational Authority of Mana orbited in one shell, while the Civilizational Authority of Hunger orbited in another, both moving in synchronized patterns that defied simple physics.","The whole structure twisted through the Mobius strip configuration, meaning the inside became the outside and the outside became the inside in an endless loop of impossible wonder.","Noah studied it with analytical marvel as he felt this extremely dense type of authority remain floating in his head near THE Organ of Civilization. As he tried his best to quantify and understand it through examination and logical deduction, more information bloomed.","| Unquantifiable Unit of Everything|","|Classification: An authority of mysterious origins originating from THE Organ of Civilization.|","|Effect: Its mere appearance within your existence has effectively doubled the Complexity and Purity of your existence.|","|Potential Applications: Could potentially be utilized in reinforcing your body, activating an ability or feature, fueling a Principle, or other unknown functions.|","|Results are entirely unknown on exactly what could occur upon utilization.|","|Current Quantity: 1 Unit|","|Stability: Ridiculously Stable|","|Recommendation: Experimentation advised with caution.|","...!","Noah wanted to marvel at the wonders that he was witnessing, to study this new discovery with the thoroughness it deserved, but the excruciating pain of the continued burning of THE Immolation Of The Sacrilegious Savage caused him to wake from his analytical reverie.","He breathed out slowly, feeling the flames still consuming him.","An excruciating pain was still ever present in his existence even when he was discovering marvels and wonders this pain indirectly led to. The irony was not lost on him that his greatest torment had birthed one his greatest opportunity.","At this moment, he looked inward at THE Organ of Civilization and began continuously flooding it with Primus Mana and Civilizational Authority of Mana and Hunger with renewed purpose.","If one Unit could double his Complexity and Purity, what could ten do? What could a hundred do?","At the same time, he pondered the question that demanded experimentation.","How should he test out what wonders the Unquantifiable Unit of Everything held? And what exactly more did THE Organ of Civilization hold in store as it developed?","The logical approach would be controlled testing, but the curse burning through him suggested that time might be a luxury he couldn’t afford to waste on excessive caution.","Noah observed the Mobius strip of concentrated authority floating in his consciousness and made a decision.","He would feed THE Organ of Civilization continuously and accumulate more Units. Once he had several, he could afford to experiment with one while keeping the others in reserve.","The pain continued to burn, but now it had a purpose beyond simply being endured.","It was fuel for evolution and the price of ascension.","And Noah would pay it gladly if it meant gaining the power to make THE Living Elemental regret the day he had decided to curse him.","The Cultivation Citadel pressed down on him with its weight, and Noah stood firm beneath it, no longer trembling.","His hand reached up to touch his temple where THE Organ of Civilization pulsed with hunger, and he smiled despite the burning.","\"Let’s see what you can truly do,\" he whispered to the organ, and flooded it with even more authority!","HUUM !","The organ pulsed in response, already beginning to process the new resources.","And Noah waited with analytical patience to see what would emerge next."]},{"number":4503,"title":"Chapter 4503: Chapter 4502: Dawn III","paragraphs":["Karma .","The concept has been debated across countless civilizations and cultures throughout the ages. Some believe it to be an immutable law of reality, a cosmic balance sheet where every action is recorded and every debt eventually comes due. They argue that Existence itself keeps score, that righteousness will be rewarded and wickedness punished in time.","Others believe it to be nothing more than false hope, a comforting story told to the oppressed to help them sleep at night while their suffering continues unabated.","And when one observed reality with cold objectivity, the second perspective seemed to hold more weight. More often than not, the vile tyrant crushing entire populations under his boot would die peacefully in his bed surrounded by luxury.","The rich noble oppressing the masses would pass his wealth to his children and never face consequences. The corrupt entity wielding power without responsibility would ascend higher and higher, their crimes buried beneath mountains of success.","Karma, it seemed, rarely made house calls.","But the few times that karma did visit such beings, when the scales finally balanced and the debt came due...","Karma could be a bitch.","---","On the other side of The Veil.","In The Lands of The Dead.","Past the vast swathes of regions and Citadels of The Dead that the Great Usurper was silently spreading his grand Derivative Civilization of Idle Existence through.","In the deepest reaches of The Lands of Dead, there existed a domain that very few Guiders of Order were even allowed to approach. It existed in layers of existence far above everything else, in an isolated space removed from the normal flow of reality.","Inside of it, all that could be seen was the white brilliance of Order and the obsidian brilliance of Death mixing together in patterns of terrible beauty.","At this moment, livid words echoed out inside this isolated region with the force of thunder.","\" A vile sycophantic fuck and the Young Order he defiles... he actually dares to do this shit?!\"","...!","The roaring voice belonged to none other than THE Dead Order , and she was not having a good day.","She sat upon a brilliant massive white marbled throne that gleamed with concentrated authority. Her lower body was entirely covered in burning crimson-gold flames that climbed higher with each passing moment. Her upper body surged with seas of white Order that crashed down continuously to push these flames from spreading any further up her form.","Her gaze was currently one of complete lividity and rage, and there were several things contributing to her fury.","One was the simple fact that if she had not been maddeningly laughing at the misfortune of Osmont and how he would soon perish from the curse, she would not have been caught off guard by the reality of him crossing The Veil in that space between spaces.","With her power fully focused, she would have been able to grab hold of him in an instant and crushed him for his audacity.","But due to her carelessness, her arrogant assumption that he was already defeated, she had only discovered him when he was already in contact with her leg. And after that moment of contact, her first course of action had been to prevent the spread of the flames across her entire being rather than pursue him.","In that brief instant of divided attention, she had allowed him to escape back across The Veil.","She was fuming at this moment, her existence trembling with rage. A lesser being had effectively played their hand against her and won, all because of her carelessness and overconfidence.","The karma that followed was truly a bitch.","And the price to pay was ridiculously heavy.","The pain of the curse of THE Living Elemental was horrendously excruciating even for her. THE Dead Order held the distinction of THE in capital letters, but this was only partly true in her current state.","She was not the complete Order. She was Dead.","Any existence who could not maintain their Primordial Civilization and was actually collapsed, who had experienced the cessation of their grand power, effectively lost the full distinction of THE for a period of time until they emerged strong enough to reclaim it in the future.","THE Dead Order had not fully reclaimed her power yet. She could only be considered halfway recovered from her collapse, struggling to rebuild what had been lost.","She was far grander than a False THE , but she was still not a full THE entity with complete power.","So while facing THE Immolation Of The Sacrilegious Savage , even though she resisted the excruciating pain that other entities would be feeling with this curse through sheer force of her partial authority, she still felt at least half of the intended pain.","And even this alone was something that pained even someone like her to a degree that bordered on intolerable.","It was like a junior martial artist facing the attack of a grandmaster who had trained four thousand more years. They had learned the same arts, practiced the same techniques, understood the same principles.","But the grandmaster could whoop the ass of the junior martial artist so easily it was almost embarrassing.","The ass of THE Dead Order was being whooped right now by the curse of THE Living Elemental, both figuratively and literally as her lower half was actually burning with flames that refused to be fully extinguished.","And she could either endure this excruciating burning for the foreseeable future while dedicating the rest of her power to ensure that it did not spread to all of her existence and consume her completely...","Or...","Her expression twisted in utter anger and apathy at the same time, the two emotions warring across her features. She raised her head upward with indecision visible in her ancient eyes.","The burning sensation down below pulsed with fresh intensity, and that pain resolved her indecision instantly.","She gazed up decisively towards the space above her throne.","\"You promised me three times that you would act on my behalf,\" she said with cold clarity. \"Three times. These flames burning across my existence would derail everything that I have planned as I would be forced to focus on them constantly. I do not wish for that.\"","She paused, her eyes hardening.","\"At this time, get rid of these flames for me. And remove the capability of them to ever affect me again.\"","She wanted to be absolutely thorough with her words, leaving no room for misinterpretation. Her utilizing this solution was a heavy choice, a debt she was calling in that she would remember Osmont for forcing her to spend.","After her words, she stared at the space above silently as nothing occurred for several long moments. It felt as if existence itself was asking her whether she was truly sure about this choice, whether she understood the cost.","Her gaze remained decisive and unwavering.","Moments later, the surrounding reality began to shift.","Existence in the surroundings twisted in ways that should not have been possible. It felt like all of the surrounding space dipped and folded to cover the body of THE Dead Order like a veil descending from above.","A terrifying flash of THE Civilizational Authority of Existence was exerted, raw and absolute.","In the next moment, the body of THE Dead Order that had been covered by crimson-gold flames was instantly blanketed by stellar brilliance that shone with the light of fundamental reality itself.","The crimson-gold flames faded away instantly, snuffed out like candles before a hurricane.","THE Dead Order breathed calmly after that intervention, her eyes showing a sense of relief before they quickly flashed back to apathy and rage once more.","She examined herself carefully, confirming that no part of her existence was affected by the crimson-gold flames anymore. More than that, she could feel that such similar flames or type of curse would not be harmful to her in the future, as if she had been granted immunity. So Osmont would never be able to spread it to her again!","Only THE Civilizational Authority can go against THE Civilizational Authority.","This proved to be true at this very moment in the starkest possible terms.","THE Dead Order had paid a heavy cost, spent one of her three promised interventions, in order to get past a problem that another being was giving every single ounce of their existence to solve and endure.","And yet a few words from her and moments later it was resolved completely.","The disparity was absolute. The difference in scale was undeniable.","Her eyes flashed with lividity as she looked outward as if she could see past the far distant Veil that separated her domain from Observable Existence.","\" Osmont ,\" she said with venom dripping from each syllable. \" Osmont. Osmont!\"","The grandeur of Order and Death began to permeate all around her throne as her words echoed out with pure malice.","\" Since you are so good at pissing off THE Entities, I will add myself to the list with pleasure ,\" she continued with cold fury. \" You think yourself safe on the other side of The Veil, just because I cannot cross it? Because you hide behind that barrier like a coward?\"","She leaned forward on her throne, her presence intensifying.","\" Okay. It is time for you to learn a lesson. You’re going to learn that even if I do not have the full distinction of THE, I am still half of such a being. And half is more than enough to deal with an insect like you.\"","Her voice rose to a roar.","\" You’re going to learn. You are going to fucking learn!\"","As she roared with such hatred and vitriol, the surrounding existence seemed to respond to her fury.","The space around her throne grew just a little dimmer. Just a little less vibrant.","As if reality itself was holding its breath in anticipation of what THE Dead Order would do next.","And in that moment of terrible promise, karma prepared to make another house call.","This time, the target was named Noah Osmont.","Whether he would ever be reached though, was unknown!"]},{"number":4504,"title":"Chapter 4504: Chapter 4503: Dawn IV","paragraphs":["Inside THE Loom.","In a domain bathed by the grandeur of THE Primordial Civilization of Paradox.","WHOOSH !","The doors of a capsule hissed open with precision, releasing pressurized air in a controlled burst. The capsule itself was a marvel of advanced construction, shining with golden light that pulsed in rhythmic patterns. Its surface was smooth and seamless, composed of materials that seemed to exist between states of paradoxical matter.","From this glorious apparatus, the figure of Ambessa emerged.","Her entire existence looked utterly changed from before. Her hair now flowed like rivers of liquid gold, each strand catching light and reflecting it in impossible angles. Her eyes pulsed with an intense crimson-gold light.","Her entire existence was scintillating and shining, as if she had become a forged treasure that could only be found in the earliest, most primordial Folds of existence.","From a distance, the figure of Forge Emperor Niso approached with measured steps and looked at her with pride mixed with caution.","\"How do you feel?\" he asked. \"You have gotten the honor of Specialization that even I have not received yet. At this moment in time, our roles could be considered completely changed.\"","Ambessa looked at her mentor and smiled warmly despite the overwhelming sensations coursing through her.","\"Don’t worry, old man. I still see you as my mentor regardless of how far I go,\" she said with genuine affection. \"As for how I feel... well, this is just ridiculous.\"","She reached out and felt for her power with careful attention, observing the changes that had occurred. She could feel that her current Complexity and Purity had spilled past 1,000 Sextillion, or was sitting at approximately 1 Septillion.","But she was not even amazed at the sheer number of Complexity and Purity, which would have been staggering before. Instead, her attention was drawn elsewhere.","\"My Complexity and Purity is currently high,\" she said slowly, searching for words. \"But...\"","She almost could not explain the sensation properly, as if words were insufficient for what she was experiencing.","In front of her, Forge Master Niso smiled with understanding and said, \"You are now an Uncertainty Paradox . You carry with you the building blocks to The False THE . Complexity and Purity will matter less and less as you head towards anything that has the distinction of THE .\"","He gestured to her transformed body.","\"The biggest thing for you to receive from this Specialization should be THE False Uncertainty Paradoxical Spine , packed with the complete automatic utilization of 9 Principles relating to Paradox. Get familiar with it as afterwards, they will have you meet with the other leaders on exactly how things would be unfolding for the missions outside of THE Loom.\"","Forge Master Niso had just finished saying this when in the next moment...","HUUM !","Blazing auras could instantly be felt approaching from the distance. The sleek laboratory-like white-gold domain they were in had its doors opened in the far distance, and the auras of utterly terrifying entities began to pour in like a tide.","Shockingly, Axiom Architect Surion, who held a terrifying amount of power and authority, was actually moving in the back as multiple others were leading in front of him.","Ambessa and Forge Master Niso were astonished by this reversal of expected hierarchy. They recognized some of the faces of the entities that were walking in, distinguished figures within the Shelters of THE Loom.","One of them was an entity that Axiom Architect Surion had mentioned before, when they were initially deployed as avatars outside of THE Loom . They were looking at Paradox Anax Belial !","An entity with the designation of The False THE!","And shockingly, beside him were two other entities who carried the same terrifying designation.","One was a woman with an extremely icy gaze, her entire body surrounded by frost that made the air crystallize around her. Even with her recent transformation and elevation, Ambessa felt like this woman, this Early Creature, could crush her with her gaze alone.","Ambessa searched her memory rapidly, matching the face to information she had been given. This should be Elemental Anax Poana!","The other False THE here was wreathed in purple storms as lightning and thunder boomed around his muscular body in continuous displays. His bronze skin looked like polished metal, and his frame was built like a celestial statue carved by master artisans. Currently his gaze was also cold and focused, but this Elemental Anax, Ambessa did not recognize from any briefings.","She only managed these brief glances before Axiom Architect Surion introduced the three False THE to them with a sense of calmness and deep respect.","\"Ambessa, Forge Master Niso, allow me to introduce Paradox Anax Belial, Elemental Anax Poana, and Elemental Anax Theron,\" Surion said formally. \"They have come with urgent directives regarding operations outside THE Loom .\"","Ambessa inclined her head respectfully, trying to read the situation. After a moment of tense silence, she cautiously asked with careful words, \"To what do we owe the pleasure of having the presence of such distinguished beings here? Surely the issue of the forces outside of THE Loom has not progressed to warrant your personal attention and intervention?\"","At these words, she felt the expressions of the Elemental Anax pulse with something dangerous. She quieted down immediately, sensing she had touched on something volatile.","What the hell had happened with the Living Elementals to make them act like this?","As she was processing this development, Elemental Anax Poana stepped forward with measured grace. Her voice was cold and absolute when she spoke.","\"The entity known as Noah Osmont, the creature who collapsed your avatar outside of THE Loom , has been labeled A Sacrilegious Savage under the customs of THE Primordial Civilization of Elementals ,\" she said with formal weight. \"His actions and insults to our Civilization are unforgivable, with his existence deemed for absolute collapse before the emergence of The Glorious Evolution.\"","She looked directly at Ambessa.","\"Every single one of you that is capable of descending outside of THE Loom will be working directly with me or others to ensure the absolute collapse of this being. Is that understood?\"","Ambessa was astonished at the seriousness and solemnity of it all. Her analytical mind raced with questions.","\"What did he do in such a short period of time to insult The Primordial Civilization of Elementals like this?\" she asked carefully.","Her question was faced with immediate coldness. Poana’s gaze hardened.","\"You are a soldier. Soldiers do not question orders. Do you understand?\"","...!","The atmosphere grew heavy and oppressive. Ambessa frowned at being shut down so completely, and she felt the hand of Forge Emperor Niso on her shoulder, a gentle pressure that told her not to erupt or push further.","She simply nodded and replied through gritted teeth, \"I understand.\"","Elemental Anax Poana nodded with satisfaction and said, \"Good. We will begin by having you accept a portion of my power and consciousness into your existence.\"","...!","Ambessa’s gaze changed dramatically at this declaration. This was something that she did not want, something that went against everything she had been building.","Her entire existence burned with Paradox as her foundation. If another foreign power permeated across her existence, especially one from a different Primordial Civilization, it would taint her Way permanently.","Could they not find another method? Why not have Paradox Anax Belial do this? Why were they all acting with such extreme measures?","She wanted to ask these questions and she wanted to have a proper dialogue about alternatives. But she felt the hand of her mentor squeeze her shoulder again with warning pressure.","She only grit her teeth harder and said, \"Understood.\"","...!","At her agreement, Elemental Anax Poana gestured for Ambessa to sit in a prepared position. Ambessa complied, settling into a meditative posture.","Poana sat across from her with fluid grace, and her body began to erupt with a terrifying icy THE False Civilizational Authority of Elemental. The temperature in the room dropped dramatically as frost began to form on every surface.","She raised her hand slowly and deliberately, then tapped it against Ambessa’s forehead.","A terrifying power began to flow into Ambessa’s existence like a flood breaking through a dam!","As Poana maintained the transfer, she turned her head towards Paradox Anax Belial without breaking concentration.","\"Brother Belial, I will leave it to you to get all the others ready as well,\" she said with calm authority.","...!","Belial, the terrifying being surrounded by swirling Paradox authority, smiled with an eerie expression that didn’t quite reach his eyes.","\"Of course, Sister Poana,\" he said smoothly. \"The weavings of Paradox are here to help all other Civilizations within THE Loom . We will rectify the wrong that has been committed and ensure that the Sacrilegious Savage attains their proper end.\"","...!","With such words hanging in the air, Ambessa watched through increasingly blurred vision as her existence buzzed with conflicting authorities.","Belial hummed a tune without words as he left the domain with smooth steps.","Her gaze flashed coldly as she felt even more power of THE False Civilizational Authority of Elemental flowing into her existence in continuous waves!","She could feel it spreading through her pathways, integrating with her being in ways that would be permanent and irreversible!","Terrifying and profound changes were occurring in this small subsection of THE Loom.","And elsewhere, in a domain of absolute Elemental authority, a terrifying force felt the establishment of their curse through vast distances. THE Living Elemental observed something that should not have been possible.","The entity the curse was attached to, the lesser pathetic entity that should have collapsed within seconds, had actually not collapsed this whole time.","So this terrifying force, this being with a complete THE distinction, prepared another response in case the Sacrilegious Savage continued to persevere and did not collapse their existence as intended.","Resources were being mobilized. Agents were being prepared. Plans were being set into motion.","It was a moment where a spark had been lit in the darkness.","And a glorious fire was about to rage across Observable Existence!"]},{"number":4505,"title":"Chapter 4505: Chapter 4504: The Infinite Unfurling! I","paragraphs":["In the Cultivation Citadel.","Noah sat on the ground with his legs crossed in a meditative posture as crimson-gold flames continued to burn all around him in their endless dance of torment.","Even while withstanding such excruciating pain that would have long since collapsed lesser beings, his expression remained calm and analytical. His eyes were even showing an expectant light.","The reason was none other than the fact that at this moment, after almost an hour of continuous feeding of resources into THE Organ of Civilization , he had managed to form nine Unquantifiable Units of Everything.","Nine Mobius strip objects floated in his head at this moment, each one a masterwork of impossible geometry and concentrated authority!","And his entire existence buzzed with immensity for it.","After the ninth one formed, no more appeared even after he poured in seas of Primus Mana and Civilizational Authority of Mana and Hunger for double the amount of time. The Organ simply absorbed the resources without producing anything new.","So it seemed that nine was the maximum capacity at this time.","Nine could be considered a low number, depending on what terrifying usage these Unquantifiable Units of Everything actually held when applied to problems.","And Noah considered them terrifying from the moment the second one had proceeded to double his 7 Septillion Complexity and Purity, bringing it up to 14 Septillion just from its appearance!","Sadly, the doubling effect did not continue thereafter. With the third appearance and every other appearance of the Unquantifiable Unit of Everything up until the ninth one, his Complexity and Purity only increased by seven Septillion each.","After the ninth Unquantifiable Unit of Everything , his total stood at 63 Septillion Complexity and Purity.","The jump was staggering. From 3.5 Septillion to 63 Septillion in the span of an hour!","Seeing the ridiculous effects that they had just from being formed and remaining inside his existence passively, his expectations were immensely high for what they could produce when actively utilized.","At this moment, he gave a simple command.","\"Come out.\"","HUUM !","The first Unquantifiable Unit of Everything floated out of his existence with graceful motion. It caused the surrounding air to shimmer as if reality itself was bending around its presence. The atmospheric authority in the surroundings instantly began buzzing and increasing in concentration by at least tenfold!","The Cultivation Citadel responded to its presence, the weight of existence pressing down even harder as if acknowledging something of profound importance.","When it came to how he wanted to test it, the description had stated that it could be applicable to countless things.","But for now, he would start with something he understood well.","\"Use the Unquantifiable Unit of Everything as the authority to activate Perpetual Harvest’s Harvest Festival Endowment on The Infiniverse.\"","A simple command.","Yet the moment that Noah gave such a directive, the Unquantifiable Unit of Everything began to spin with silent glow and intensity.","And then it warped out of existence in the next moment.","Just disappeared completely from his perception!","And a moment later...","BOOM !","Noah’s vision became covered by verdant-green seas of brilliance that erupted from nowhere and everywhere at once!","The prompts that bloomed were unlike anything he had seen before.","| The Unquantifiable Unit of Everything disdains its immensity being used for such a simple task.|","|Note: Its breadth is capable of empowering your entire Civilization.|","|Perpetual Harvest has been fully activated with the Unquantifiable Unit of Everything stemming from THE Organ of Civilization as the catalyzing authority.|","|The Infiniverse has gained an endowment of 5,000 Sextillion Complexity and Purity (5 Septillion).|","|The strongest amongst your budding Civilization have also been empowered by 500 Sextillion Complexity and Purity each.|","|Recipients include: The 54 Million+ Primus Inevitabilities, all those who have visited the Early Veiled Shore, and those who share a significant enough connection with your existence.|","|Introductory access to The Seed of the Grand Principle of Mana Genesis has been granted to all recipients mentioned above.|","|The Infiniverse has gained the capability to form The Primordial Primus Mana Folds of Existence.|","|Effect: The Infiniverse can now create self-sustaining Folds of reality that generate Primus Mana perpetually, serving as resource nodes for your Civilization.|","|Current Formation Limit: 10 Primordial Primus Mana Folds of Existence.|","|The Infiniverse has gained the architectural blueprint for The Eternal Forge of Existential Advancement.|","|Effect: A grand structure that can be built to continuously forge equipment, treasures, and existential enhancements for all members of your Civilization. Items produced will scale and continue to scale with the Civilization’s overall power.|","|Construction Requirements: Available resources sufficient. Construction can begin immediately.|","...!","After Noah read over the prompts and felt the terrifying waves of changes brought about by the usage of a single Unquantifiable Unit of Everything, he was genuinely astonished.","His eyes flashed with immense brilliance as he analyzed the boons given with careful attention.","The primary empowerment alone was unfathomable. The Infiniverse gaining 5 Septillion that easily was ridiculous.","But the secondary effects were what truly caught his mind.","The Seed of the Grand Principle of Mana Genesis meant that his entire inner circle, millions of Primus Inevitabilities, would soon be cultivating and nurturing a Principle. How hard was it to gain access to a Principle?","And yet now...oh!","More than this, +500 Sextillion Complexity and Purity to all the Primus Inevitabilities and others!","Oh!","The Primordial Primus Mana Folds of Existence was another ridiculous boon to rise.","And The Eternal Forge of Existential Advancement ...ah! Equipment and treasures that scaled with Civilization power meant that as his people grew stronger, their tools would grow with them.","All of this from a single Unquantifiable Unit of Everything.","He still had eight more.","In the distance, he felt The Infiniverse’s presence surge with newfound power. Through their connection, he could feel her wonder.","But again, Complexity and Purity was grand, but it did not mean everything!","Noah looked inward at the remaining eight Unquantifiable Units of Everything floating in his consciousness and asked himself the only question that mattered.","Just how terrifying was this Unquantifiable Unit of Everything stemming from THE Organ of Civilization?","He had to remind himself that THE Organ of Civilization bloomed as something completely new in Observable Existence.","It meant that even in The Earliest Folds, THE Creature and all others with the distinction of THE did not have this as part of their pathway towards such power, or as a component of their current selves!","This was novel and unique to him.","This was his own path being forged, and it was proving to be more terrifying than he had dared to dream.","The crimson-gold flames still burned across his existence, but now they felt different somehow. Not less painful, but more purposeful.","They had forced him to evolve. To undergo a Glorious Evolution. They had pushed him to discover this Organ. They had inadvertently given him a weapon that he really wanted to use to cut down THE Living Elemental!","Noah allowed himself a small smile despite the pain.","\"Let’s see what the rest of you can do,\" he murmured, looking at the eight remaining Units!"]},{"number":4506,"title":"Chapter 4506: Chapter 4505: The Infinite Unfurling! II","paragraphs":["When Noah thought about the terrifying capabilities of the Unquantifiable Unit of Everything and what it could do, many other possibilities flooded his mind.","His thoughts wandered to his Early Atlas of the Folds, to the feature that had always held immense promise and danger in equal measure.","Temporal Traversal!","He always knew how desperately he needed more knowledge regarding existence, and one of the foremost places to attain this knowledge was The Earliest Folds themselves!","If he used the product of THE Organ of Civilization to power up his Temporal Traversal, how far back could he go? How pristine would the environment be? What secrets could he uncover?","The more he thought about it, the more his eyes shone brightly.","And then, without his conscious command...","| The Unquantifiable Units of Everything deem this action worthy of use. One Unquantifiable Unit of Everything has flown into your Atlas.|","...!","Noah’s eyes opened wide with alarm as he tried to speak.","\"Hey, hold on!\"","He was only just thinking about this as an abstract possibility! He wasn’t ready yet to actually execute such a journey!","And yet, his existence seemed to have found something it could not let go of, as if his very being had made a decision independent of his conscious mind. Even his THE Organ of Civilization buzzed with urgent resonance!","And before he could do anything else to stop the process...","| THE Organ of Civilization unequivocally agrees with your line of thought. Unforeseen dangers have been detected with this Temporal Traversal due to your Existence being inherently different compared to all previous times. 2 additional Unquantifiable Units of Everything have flown into your Atlas. An Absolute Civilizational Temporal Traversal is beginning.|","...!","A rapid flashing of prompts appeared and disappeared in microseconds!","And right after...","WAP !","Noah disappeared from the Cultivation Citadel entirely!","A moment after he vanished, The Infiniverse appeared where he used to be. Her existence pulsed with newfound power from the recent empowerment, and the illusory figure of RUIN/EDEN materialized alongside her.","\"Something unexpected occurred and he is going through Temporal Traversal rather early,\" RUIN/EDEN said with concern coloring her voice. \"It seems to be unlike any other time before. His entire existence was pulled through.\"","The Infiniverse nodded at these words as she gazed at the empty space where Noah had been burning.","\"Everything is as it can be,\" she said with calm acceptance. \"Existence will continue to be unpredictable, and we can only continue to do what we can. Take care of him there.\"","After such words, The Infiniverse disappeared to attend to the countless tasks that required her attention!","---","A few seconds ago.","In the Injunction Sanctuary of Law.","Deborah stood before all remaining members of the Civilizational Legion of Law, her posture rigid with the weight of command. She gazed at the flaming bodies of Noah and Ozymandias with complex emotions.","At this moment, millions of Primus Inevitabilities surrounded them in protective formations alongside Aethon and his Civilizational Legion of Elementals who had sworn new allegiance.","All Emotives had been collapsed and mainly devoured by Ozymandias in this terrifying battle, and many still couldn’t believe how things had unfolded so dramatically.","At this moment, Deborah was about to take out the Shattered Part of The Heart of Law to give to Alexander when...","WAP !","Noah and Ozymandias’s flaming figures disappeared without warning! Ozymandias actually turned into a streak of light that shot across the space and disappeared into Noah’s body before both vanished completely!","Alexander and the others watched in astonishment as Noah simply ceased to exist before them.","Khor frowned for a moment with concern before she steadied herself as if she had received news through their connection. She turned to address the assembled forces.","\"Continue with the mission,\" she said with absolute authority. \"The Outsider is simply taking care of other matters.\"","Other matters.","Very few knew the ultimate truth about what had just occurred!","---","Unlike before, unlike previous Temporal Traversals where Noah could send a single body or clone and keep other instances behind to maintain presence...","This Temporal Traversal had taken every single ounce of his being.","As of this moment, Noah Osmont did not exist in this era at all!","Across weavings of existence.","Noah’s expression was solemn as the transition occurred, but he rapidly adapted his thinking. He understood that 3 Unquantifiable Units of Everything had been consumed to power up what must be a ridiculous Temporal Traversal!","An Absolute Civilizational Temporal Traversal at that.","He observed his surroundings with careful attention and found himself surrounded by an intense and immense storm of existence that felt much wilder and more primal than any previous Temporal Traversal.","New prompts bloomed before his vision.","|ABSOLUTE CIVILIZATIONAL TEMPORAL TRAVERSAL - ACTIVE|","|Previously, your existence did not contain even a single iota of THE . You were able to freely use the unimaginable feature of Temporal Traversal with your Atlas as this alone was an impossibility.|","|When paired with a fairly weak entity utilizing such a feature, you were able to pass through the temporal gaps without being noticed by THE Living Temporal.|","|Current Status: At this moment, you hold THE Organ of Civilization. Even though your power is heading towards the right direction, you are still considered weak while holding an aspect budding with THE .|","|Warning: It is significantly harder to pass through the gaps unnoticed. THE Living Temporal has a high chance of discovering your movements.|","|Solution Implemented: For the sake of caution, the utility of The Unquantifiable Units of Everything has allowed your existence to traverse much further back than before, to a time before THE Living Temporal had much influence on the Temporal Weavings of Existence. You have been dropped in a region that would grant you the highest chance of survival, near Weavings of Existence that match your Civilization.|","|Current Location: You have arrived before The Earliest Folds. Extreme caution advised.|","...!","The prompts were heavy with implications. Moments after they bloomed and faded, Noah’s existence pulsed with terrifying luminosity. His Sovereign Spires resonated with each other in harmonic frequencies until...","BOOM !","He felt space break and reform around him before darkness and light folded and collapsed in patterns. And he instantly found himself elsewhere entirely.","...!","The moment he arrived, waves of ancient authority began to flood into his existence like water filling a vessel.","He found himself standing on what appeared to be an extremely tall crystalline obsidian mountain peak that stretched upward for what might have been miles. Misty clouds that even obscured his enhanced vision permeated all around in thick layers.","In the far distance, other massive crystalline obsidian mountain peaks could barely be seen through the mist. Some seemed to be growing upside down, defying conventional understanding of gravity and orientation!","The skies above and the supposed earth below were both filled with rising obsidian crystalline mountains in configurations of utter glory. Some mountains floated freely in the air, rotating slowly. Others grew in spirals that twisted through multiple dimensions.","The domain around him felt like his existence could continue drinking in the atmosphere forever and never be satisfied. It felt ancient beyond measure, old in a way that transcended simple time!","The air itself carried weight, each breath filling his lungs with authority that had existed since before existence learned to organize itself.","Between the mountain peaks, he could see what looked like rivers of liquid light flowing upward and downward simultaneously, defying direction. Crystalline structures that might have been buildings or might have been natural formations dotted some of the peaks in the distance.","The mist itself seemed alive, pulsing with patterns that suggested consciousness or at least awareness.","And everywhere, everywhere , there was the sensation of potential. As if this place existed before things had been decided, before reality had committed to specific rules!","New prompts rose a moment later.","| You have arrived in a place and time that THE Organ of Civilization has quantified as The Infinite Unfurling.|","|Definition: The period before The Earliest Folds solidified into distinct realities.|","|Critical Warning: The entirety of your existence is present in this location. You have no backup of yourself remaining in your home era.|","|Extreme Caution Required: You must move with immense care. The littlest thing has the potential to unmake your existence completely.|","|The rules of reality here are not yet fixed. What is impossible in your era may be commonplace here, and vice versa.|","...!","The tiniest thing had the potential to unmake his existence completely!","And he was here with all of his being. Ozymandias was merged inside this body, and as he stood on the obsidian crystalline mountain peak, his figure was like a candle flame in the vast darkness.","Crimson-gold flames of THE Immolation Of The Sacrilegious Savage still burned around him, marking him as something foreign in this ancient place!","How should he go about exploring this environment without triggering catastrophe?","\" Ho? What’s this?\"","...!","A booming yet calm voice filled with profound immensity echoed out across the mountain peak.","Without Noah noticing any approach or movement, a humanoid figure peeled back the layers of existence in front of him as if he had always been standing there this whole time and Noah simply couldn’t perceive him until now.","He showed himself fully and looked at Noah up and down with analytical interest burning in eyes that held abyssal folds!","...!","Noah’s expression became unfathomably heavy as he stared at this humanoid being whose voice continued to echo across the mountains.","The figure was tall and lean, his form seemingly composed of shifting shadows and hungry voids. His skin looked like night sky filled with dying stars. His eyes were black holes that consumed light rather than reflected it.","And around him, space itself bent inward as if reality wanted to be devoured by his mere presence.","\" I was about to take a bite of you, you know,\" the entity said with casual menace. \" You feel like something that does not belong here. Something... displaced.\"","He tilted his head with curious intensity.","\" Who are you, Outsider? And why do you give off the scent of my Hunger?\"","...!","A profound and terrifying sense of suffocation spread out from the entity like a physical force. The pressure made Noah’s newly elevated 63 Septillion Complexity feel insignificant!","The entity before Noah burned with the unmistakable allure of THE .","He had met a THE Existence mere seconds after his entry into a place before The Earliest Folds, into The Infinite Unfurling itself!","But for good or bad, he could say with certainty that he knew this being!"]},{"number":4507,"title":"Chapter 4507: Chapter 4506: The Infinite Unfurling! III","paragraphs":["Noah looked at the entity in front of him as he rapidly analyzed the situation. It could be considered extremely perilous or fortuitous depending on how he handled the next few moments.","No, when truly considered on the spectrum of danger versus opportunity, if he ever had to meet an existence at the next scale of power, this entity would be among those that would be the most ideal to come across.","So his eyes shone brightly with calculated brilliance as he spoke carefully.","\"What your senses detect can be considered a form of your Hunger,\" Noah said with measured words. \"But it emerges eons down the line from this moment.\"","...!","At these words, the entity in front of him smiled with genuine interest before he came just a bit closer towards Noah. His skin truly looked like a night sky filled with dying stars, and with his dark flowing hair and eyes that held the depth of black holes, it was like staring into the gaze of one of the most apex predators in existence.","\" Eons down the line, huh? \" the entity said with contemplative curiosity. \" That would explain why you do not belong here, why your existence feels displaced. But even then, the purity of this Hunger I sense would be something that could only come from me directly... well, or from someone that has a similar authority to mine.\"","He leaned in slightly.","\" Who shared this Hunger with you, Outsider?\"","Noah looked at him calmly as he said with simple honesty, \"Khor.\"","...!","The name caused the eyes of this being, of Tor, to open wide with shock!","His face went through a range of emotions in rapid succession. Surprise bloomed first, then morphed into worry, then shifted to caution before it ultimately settled into calm acceptance.","He looked at Noah silently for a long moment before he sighed deeply and gazed out at the surrounding landscape of inverted mountains and flowing light.","\" That little runt? She wouldn’t be able to share my Hunger with another unless something significant happened to her, \" he said quietly. \" Is she okay? Tell me truly.\"","Noah replied with calm certainty, \"She is okay.\"","At these words, this terrifyingly powerful entity simply nodded with visible relief.","\" Then there is more than enough,\" he said, his tension easing. \" Since you do exhibit the same Hunger within your existence, you can be considered a junior of mine in the Way.\"","His analytical gaze swept over Noah again.","\" Why are you playing with temporal weavings of existence and coming to a place where many things could collapse you in the span of an instant? Even more than that, how did you get the flames of an Elemental sovereignty to be burning your existence?\"","He tilted his head with curiosity.","\" Did you meet someone here before me? But they would have simply collapsed you and eaten you up as I don’t see the reason for them to torture you like this. Oh, were you branded with this flame where you come from?\"","...!","Noah’s eyes opened wider as he felt his existence buzzing. He nodded as he said, \"A brand was given to me by a fiery pathetic fucker who can’t even appear in front of me directly.\"","...!","Tor laughed at his words with genuine amusement.","\" Outsider, you are so quick to insult beings who could squash you if they were here in person, \" he said with entertained approval. \" Oh well, I am sure that it is no fun to have that blazing around your existence constantly.\"","He paused thoughtfully.","\" I could move to erase that right now with minimal effort. But would it not be better, would you not feel more satisfied, if you took care of it yourself?\"","...!","Noah’s eyes shined with understanding at such words. He looked at this being who was smiling with encouragement and asked the critical question.","\"How would I gain the power to erase the flames of an entity with THE designation?\" Noah asked. \" Only THE Civilizational Authority can go against THE Civilizational Authority.\"","...!","His eyes pulsed with immensity as he said this fundamental truth.","Tor nodded with approval as he responded, \" Yeah, that’s accurate. And although you can be considered far from THE currently, I can see that you have begun developing something with such a designation within your existence.\"","He gestured to Noah’s form analytically.","\"It may be the only reason that you can stand in a place like this which could kill you in so many different ways. It means that you have taken a step on the path, and taking a step is already halfway to reaching the destination.\"","His smile widened.","\"As my junior walking on the Way of Hunger, I can definitely give you some guidance on how to reach THE and eliminate those flames yourself. Or, you can tell me to simply take these flames away right now, and we can part ways right here.\"","...!","The disposition of this being seemed to be unique and genuine. Noah could see how he operated with clear observation, so the answer came as a calm declaration.","\"I’ll take care of it myself.\"","Tor smiled broadly and clapped his hands together with satisfaction.","\" Good! A strong quality for those who walk on the Way of Hunger is to eat up everything with their own effort and strength.\"","He straightened to his full imposing height and spoke with formal gravity.","\"I am Tor, THE First Hunger ,\" he said simply. \" What is your name, Outsider?\"","Noah nodded as he replied, \" Osmont . Noah Osmont.\"","Tor nodded with acknowledgment as he said, \" Alright Osmont, what do you know about THE?\"","...!","What did he know about THE ?","He felt his existence buzzing at such a fundamental question as he answered honestly, \"Not much.\"","Tor nodded with understanding as he said, \" Okay. Then the best way for you to learn about THE and what it truly means... is to experience it directly. Come on.\"","As he said this, he moved to place his hand on Noah’s shoulder.","The crimson-gold flames of the curse of THE Living Elemental roared violently as if they were seeking to allow their contagion to spread onto this new target as well.","But Tor only raised a single eyebrow as if he was warning these flames of their presumption.","A moment later, the flames actually receded from Noah’s shoulder where Tor placed his hand, leaving that small area untouched!","...!","Noah watched such a scene with shining eyes filled with wonder at the casual display of authority.","In the next moment, crimson-obsidian stellar waves of light wrapped around both of their bodies like protective cocoons. They began to float away from the mountain peak they had been standing on.","Their figures seemingly melted into the surrounding existence, entering its folds and layers to such an extent that one could not even perceive them anymore. They became part of the fabric of reality itself.","Tor explained as they began to fly across the landscape of The Infinite Unfurling with smooth motion.","\" You are currently within The Infinite Unfurling, a place and time of immense glory, power, and danger ,\" he said with grand calm.","He gestured to the inverted mountains and flowing rivers of light.","\" Here, potential still exceeds actuality. Here, what will be has not yet defeated what could be. This is when THE entities emerge, and where entities with the potential to become THE are eaten up for lunch. It is when many learn what it means to hold authority over fundamental aspects of existence.\"","They passed through a cloud of mist that sang with harmonic frequencies.","\" The first thing you need to understand about THE, \" Tor continued with teaching intensity, \"is that it is not about power in the way you currently understand it.\"","He looked at Noah with piercing focus.","\" THE is about Sovereignty. About claiming dominion over existence itself and making that claim absolute. I am THE First Hunger because I have Sovereign Authority over the concept of Hunger itself. Not just physical appetite, but existential consumption, the fundamental drive to take in and make part of oneself.\"","They flew past a mountain peak where crystalline structures pulsed with ancient light.","\" When two THE entities clash, \" Tor said seriously, \" it’s not about who has more power. It’s about whose Sovereignty is more complete, whose claim is more absolute, whose authority runs deeper into the fabric of Existence.\"","He smiled at Noah.","\" The flames burning you come from THE Living Elemental, right? A worm who has Sovereign Authority over Elemental interactions. That’s why they persist despite your resistance. That’s why numerical weavings like Complexity and Purity don’t matter against them. you could be as complex and as pure as you want, but if you have nothing to go against The Sovereignty of Elemental... none of that will matter.\"","Noah absorbed this information with analytical intensity.","\"But you said I could learn to eliminate them myself,\" Noah said carefully.","Tor nodded with approval at the question.","\" Yes, because you’re developing your own path to THE. Your existence should be attempting to claim its own Sovereignty. Once it matures enough, once your claim becomes strong enough...\"","He grinned with predatory satisfaction.","\" Then you can tell those flames to fuck off, and they’ll have to listen.\"","...!","\" Oh, but don’t have any expectations of you attaining THE anytime soon. Your existence still feels a bit off. And that bit off could be years or eons depending on your existence. Or it could be months if you are in the Infinite Unfurling long enough, who knows? But I should be able to get you far enough that those weak flames would be something you can take care of.\"","WAA !","The landscape shifted around them as they flew deeper into The Infinite Unfurling , and Noah felt his existence drinking in the ancient atmosphere with desperate thirst as the flames causing excrutiating pain all around him...seemed to dim in comparison!"]},{"number":4508,"title":"Chapter 4508: Chapter 4507: The Infinite Unfurling! IV","paragraphs":["As Noah and Tor flew across The Infinite Unfurling , the landscape shifted dramatically around them.","They entered into a unique region where massive crystalline mountains rose like titans frozen in time, each one surrounded by rotating clusters of nascent Folds that spun in orbital patterns. The Folds themselves looked incomplete, as if reality was still deciding what they should become.","The landscape was filled with storms of pure existence that defied conventional understanding. When Noah looked toward certain regions with careful observation, he saw terrifying natural phenomena that made his mind recoil. Torrents of raw authority that could shred across his 63 Septillions in Complexity and Purity as easily as wind through paper.","Lightning that wasn’t electricity but the concept of sudden change made manifest, striking in patterns that erased causality itself. Whirlwinds of collapsed probability that would unmake anything caught within them by retroactively preventing their existence.","This entire region was also filled with extremely dense layers of mist that obscured vision beyond a few hundred meters. One was not able to see too much of the surrounding environment, which made the danger feel even more oppressive and immediate.","But across these distant regions, cutting through the mist and the howling winds, Noah shockingly heard roars .","ROOOOAAAAAR !","The sound waves alone caused his existence to buzz with resonance, making his cells vibrate at frequencies that bordered on painful. These were not the sounds of mere beasts but the declarations of beings claiming their right to exist through sheer force of will.","This was the moment when Tor slowed his flight and tilted his head as if he was listening carefully for where the sound of those roars originated. His dark eyes gleamed with interest.","He then smiled with anticipation and said, \" Oh, this ongoing battle may be ideal for you to understand what I’ve been explaining. Let’s go see.\"","...!","They moved through the dangerous regions with Tor navigating expertly. After traversing what Noah estimated to be a few Gigaparsecs, passing through layers of folded space and compressed distance, they entered a clearing filled with tumultuous waves of power.","The region they arrived in was a vast expanse that looked like an ancestral battlefield carved from the bones of reality itself.","The ground was composed of compressed existence that had been hammered flat by countless impacts over what must have been eons of conflict. Plateaus of crystalline material jutted upward at irregular intervals, each one scarred with claw marks and burn patterns that glowed with residual authority.","Massive weathered pillars rose like the ribs of some dead existential beast, creating natural archways and obstacles throughout the terrain. The sky above swirled with auroras of impossible colors that bled into each other, painting the entire scene in shifting hues of violet, crimson, and glacial blue.","The entire region was filled with terrifying swirling shattered Folds that moved through the space like debris in a Primordial storm. These fragments could eradicate a creature of 1 Septillion Complexity on impact, simply erasing them from existence through contact.","And yet, at the center of such a dangerous place, Noah observed two monstrous entities locked in combat.","The first creature was a titanic wyvern-like being whose body stretched for what looked like light-years. Its sleek form was covered in obsidian scales that crackled with constant electrical discharge. A magnificent crest of horn-like protrusions jutted from its head, each one serving as a conductor for the purple lightning that wreathed its entire existence.","Its wings were vast membranes of crystallized energy that sparked and flashed with every movement, creating afterimages of light that burned into the retina. Its tail was segmented and whip-like, trailing arcs of electricity that carved through the surrounding space.","The creature was surrounded by endless purple obsidian seas of lightning that formed a domain around it, making the very air ionize and glow.","The second creature was ape-like in its basic structure but magnified to apocalyptic proportions. Its body was covered in white fur that looked like compressed glacial ice, each strand sharp enough to cut through reality. Massive curved horns grew from its head like the tusks of some primordial mammoth, glowing with frozen light.","Its arms were disproportionately long and muscular, ending in fists that looked capable of shattering continents. Its eyes burned with blue fire that held the cold fury of absolute zero.","This beast was surrounded by glacial waves of storms and ice that manifested as swirling blizzards of frozen authority, creating a domain of perpetual winter that fought against the electrical storm of its opponent.","Noah’s vision pulsed as information flooded his perception.","|Name: Voltaic Sovereign Incarnate - Raijax|","|Classification: Pre-THE Existence attempting Lightning Sovereignty|","|Complexity: 485 Decillion|","|Purity: 515 Decillion|","|Grand Principles: Thunder Genesis, Lightning Propagation, Voltage Manifestation, Electric Dominion, Storm Convergence, Plasma Authority, Conductivity Mastery, Arc Supremacy|","|Status: Engaged in existential combat|","|Name: Glacial Sovereign Incarnate - Hyorath|","|Classification: Pre-THE Existence attempting Glacial Sovereignty|","|Complexity: 555 Decillion|","|Purity: 555 Decillion|","|Grand Principles: Frost Genesis, Ice Propagation, Absolute Zero Manifestation, Glacial Dominion, Winter Convergence, Crystalline Authority, Thermal Negation Mastery, Permafrost Supremacy|","|Status: Engaged in existential combat|","...!","He looked at such terrifying beings with analytical wonder, cataloging their power and comparing it to his own vastly inferior capabilities.","In the next moment, Tor spoke with teaching intensity.","\" These two here are good examples of existences trying to reach THE ,\" he said calmly, gesturing toward the battling titans. \" Their existence is ripe for it as they have not concentrated so much on their numerical Complexity and Purity, though those numbers are still a little large.\"","He crossed his arms as he observed.","\" But they have leaned towards a specific aspect of existence and are actively seeking to claim Sovereignty towards it. One is seeking Lightning Sovereignty while the other is seeking Glacial Sovereignty. One is walking the Way of Lightning and the other is walking the Way of Glacial.\"","His expression became slightly pitying.","\" They are grand ideals, worthy pursuits. But these existences would never truly have the chance to reach THE at the end of their paths. You see, the aspects of existence they are trying to lay claim over... well, even both of these could be superseded by the authority that is currently burning you. Elemental.\"","He shook his head.","\" Lightning falls under Elemental. Glacial falls under Elemental. Both of their Ways are subcategories of a broader Sovereignty that has already been claimed. So while it could theoretically be possible for them to eventually attain THE through these paths, it would be immensely hard, perhaps impossible without completely redefining their chosen domains.\"","...!","As Tor finished his explanation, the terrifying apocalyptic battle intensified before them.","BOOM !","Raijax, the lightning wyvern, swooped down from the swirling sky with wings spread wide. Each beat of those vast membranes created shockwaves that propagated across light-years, compressing space and time with the force of impact.","If Noah had been nearby, he would have been absolutely shredded!","Purple lightning gathered around its open jaws, condensing into a sphere of such concentrated electrical authority that it bent space around itself. The creature released it with a shriek that shattered the sound barrier across multiple dimensions simultaneously.","CRAAAACK !","The blast struck Hyorath directly in the chest, and the glacial ape roared with pain and fury. Ice exploded outward from the point of impact as frozen armor shattered, revealing flesh beneath that steamed and burned.","But Hyorath retaliated immediately.","The ape-like titan slammed both fists into the compressed ground beneath it, and the entire battlefield trembled. From the point of impact, jagged spears of absolute-zero ice erupted upward in a forest of frozen death, each one kilometers thick and moving at impossible speeds, burning with its Way of Existence and Civilizational Authority!","Raijax twisted in mid-air, its serpentine body contorting to avoid the rising spears. Lightning arced from its body to meet the ice, creating explosions where the conflicting authorities collided. Each explosion released enough energy to vaporize Fold systems.","The two entities circled each other, their domains and Ways of of Lightning and Glacial creating a boundary where purple electricity fought against blue frost. The air between them crackled and froze simultaneously, creating impossible phenomena where matter existed in contradictory states.","Noah observed Raijax as it descended in a spiral dive, its tail whipping forward like a lance. The segmented appendage struck Hyorath across the shoulder, carving through glacial armor and drawing blood that froze before it could fall.","Hyorath caught the tail with one massive hand and pulled.","THOOM !","The wyvern was yanked from the sky and slammed into the ground with force that created a crater spanning hundreds of light-years. The impact sent shockwaves rippling outward that obliterated the surrounding environment, reducing mountains to dust and shattering the floating Fold fragments into smaller pieces.","’What the fuck is this...’","The scale of the battle was enough to make Noah shake his head at the impacts of brutality as any single one of them would have been an end to his Temporal Traversal!","And yet...the battle still continued!","Raijax was far from defeated.","Lightning erupted from its entire body in a nova of electrical fury. The discharge was so intense that it turned the air itself into plasma, creating a sea of superheated matter that expanded outward in all directions.","Hyorath released the tail and leaped backward, creating walls of glacial ice to shield against the plasma wave. The ice held for microseconds before sublimating directly into vapor, but those microseconds were enough for the ape to escape the worst of the blast.","As Tor continued to observe, he spoke with calm instruction.","\" The Civilizational Scale of Existence, the designation of THE, requires for one to lay an undeniable claim over something. To have complete Sovereign Authority over it.\"","He gestured toward the battling titans.","\" Their power would be dependent on what I call the Depth of Sovereignty. Depth is how thoroughly they can rewrite their chosen domain and impose it against all others. It can be measured as Surface, Intermediate, Fundamental, or Absolute.\"","His dark eyes gleamed!"]},{"number":4509,"title":"Chapter 4509: Chapter 4508: The Infinite Unfurling! V","paragraphs":["\" Countless existences in The Infinite Unfurling will never even manage to touch the Depth of THE Surface of Absolute Sovereignty Authority. These two before you are trying to build up the Depth of their declared Ways to at least touch THE Surface threshold, and so they battle against each other.\"","He paused as the combat intensified.","\"If one Way triumphs over the other, the easiest thing to do is to devour the losing Way and use it as fuel for one’s own progression. And here’s where the truly interesting thing that I mentioned before becomes relevant.\"","Tor’s smile widened with predatory satisfaction.","\"I mentioned how their Ways of existence, the Sovereignties they are trying to establish, are Lightning and Glacial. Both of these would fall under Elemental. Both of these would also fall under Conceptual. And the very action of what they are doing when they eventually consume each other, or even during the battle as they try to devour each other’s authority...\"","His eyes spun like terrifying gravitational black holes that would devour absolutely everything.","\" All of these actions fall under the purview of my Hunger. Both of them are hungering for victory, for growth, for Sovereignty. So in choosing and selecting a Way of existence, one has to be unfathomably careful. Because if they choose something that can be incorporated into another, broader Way...\"","He left the implication hanging in the air!","Noah thought about the words of this terrifying being with intense focus. He considered his own Mana and Hunger, how Mana was so pervasive and widespread across all of existence. It was indeed a glorious Way to be following, a glorious Civilization to be enacting.","He also thought about The Depths of Sovereignty that Tor had mentioned. How countless creatures could never even touch THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty. How he himself was nowhere close to THE Surface , not even a fraction of a fraction of the way there.","And how even these two terrifying creatures at Decillions of Complexity and Purity, beings that could obliterate him with a thought, had not even touched THE Surface threshold.","The gulf between where he stood and where THE existed was almost incomprehensible.","As Noah processed all of this information, Tor continued speaking.","\" The Infinite Unfurling is filled with beings like the two you see fighting in front of you. Many trying to establish their dominion and Sovereignty, clashing and devouring each other in an endless cycle of growth and consumption.\"","His expression became more serious.","\" In this place, there are a few entities that you have to be especially careful of. I guess THE Living Elemental is a creature that managed to survive these brutal regions and establish his Sovereignty successfully. But there are other truly terrifying ones that you need to keep track of and make absolutely sure that you don’t come in front of.\"","He held up fingers as he counted.","\" The rampant monster of THE Paradox Absolute Sovereignty is one. They delight in contradiction and impossibility, and their very presence can unmake logical existence.\"","He held up another finger.","\" And the other goes by a few distinctions, as they are the most terrifying entity to encounter in these parts. They go by THE Titan, THE Sovereign Killer, THE Feared Sovereignty...\"","His voice dropped as if one had to be careful when they said the name.","\" THE Creature. \"","...!","BOOM !","THE Creature!","A terrifying existence that was feared across The Infinite Unfurling itself!","Noah’s eyes shone brightly as he obtained information regarding such glorious and terrible history!","BOOM !","And as he thought about all of it, his eyes continued to observe and track the terrifying battle occurring in the distance.","Raijax had recovered from being slammed into the ground and now hovered above the battlefield with wings spread wide. Lightning condensed around its form in layers upon layers of electrical authority, building to something catastrophic.","Hyorath stood below, fists raised and glowing with glacial power. Ice formed and reformed around its massive hands, creating gauntlets of frozen matter compressed to impossible densities.","The two entities launched themselves at each other simultaneously.","CRASH !","They collided in mid-air, and the shockwave from the impact obliterated everything within several light-years. Fists met claws, ice met lightning, and the very fabric of existence strained under the pressure.","They separated and clashed again, and again, and again. Each impact created explosions of conflicting authority. Lightning carved through ice, and ice shattered electrical fields.","Way against Way. Civilization against Civilization.","Raijax wrapped around Hyorath like a constricting serpent, its body channeling millions of volts directly into the ape’s form. Hyorath roared and flexed, muscles expanding as glacial authority pushed back against the electrical assault.","The ape caught the wyvern’s neck in both hands and began to squeeze. Ice formed along Raijax’s scales, frost creeping toward vital organs with the intent to freeze the creature from within.","But Raijax twisted violently, using its superior mobility to escape the grip. It slashed with razor-sharp claws wreathed in purple lightning, opening wounds across Hyorath’s chest and arms.","Blood sprayed, freezing and evaporating simultaneously in the contradictory environment.","They separated again, both wounded but neither willing to concede.","And then came the pivotal moment.","Raijax gathered all of its remaining power, channeling every iota of Lightning Sovereignty it had accumulated. The creature’s limbs began to glow with obsidian-purple seas of lightning so dense that they looked solid, like weapons forged from the concept of electricity itself.","The wyvern threw its wings and limbs forward as if launching spears.","WHOOOOSH !","Lances of pure lightning shot across the distance, each one carrying the full weight of Raijax’s claim to Lightning Sovereignty. They pierced through Hyorath’s glacial defenses as if they weren’t even there, carving through ice and flesh with equal ease.","The chest and existence of the ape became carved wide open, revealing the glowing core of its being beneath layers of frozen armor and muscle.","Hyorath howled with pain and despair, the sound echoing across dimensions!","Raijax roared triumphantly, the sound mixing with thunder that announced victory!","The wyvern descended toward its fallen opponent, jaws opening wide in preparation. It would devour everything about the Way of existence of its enemy, consuming the Glacial Sovereignty that Hyorath had spent eons building.","This consumption would increase the Depth of Raijax’s own Lightning Sovereignty, pushing it closer toward THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty that it hungered for!","Noah nodded at this battle as it truly made things somewhat clear regarding competing Ways of Sovereignties.","And yet at such a moment of triumph, the figure of Tor beside him smiled with something like amusement.","\" This is existence,\" he said calmly. \" Existence is glorious. Existence is unpredictable.\"","He paused for effect.","\" And existence is...brutal.\"","As he finished saying these words, he took a single step forward.","Both their figures became fully visible, shedding the veil of folded existence that had concealed them.","In the distance, Raijax turned toward them. The victor’s eyes, which had been gleaming with triumph, quickly began shaking with panic and absolute terror as they locked onto Tor.","Recognition and fear bloomed across the wyvern’s features.","In the next moment, Tor simply opened his mouth and took a bite.","CHOMP !","...!","Above both Raijax and the collapsed Hyorath, reality itself split open like a wound. Terrifying obsidian-crimson jaws emerged from the tear, vast beyond comprehension. Each tooth was the size of a fold continent, dripping with authority that made space itself bend.","The jaws descended with inexorable finality.","They bit down and proceeded to devour the entire region of existence and the two entities within it!","THE Absolute Sovereignty Authority of Hunger, THE Civilizational Authority of Hunger, covered everything like a shroud and consumed it all in a single bite!","Both Raijax and Hyorath, with their Decillions of Complexity and their Grand Principles each, with their lifetimes of struggle toward Sovereignty...","Gone.","Erased.","Devoured.","Not even their screams had time to echo before they became part of Tor’s existence.","...!","Noah observed such a terrifying scene with eyes wide!","Beside him, Tor licked his lips with satisfaction. His abyssal eyes shone with an even greater intense obsidian light, and the weight of his existence seemed to become even more profound, as if he had just taken a step deeper into his own Sovereignty.","He repeated himself with calm certainty.","\" Existence is brutal, Outsider. The powerful eat the weak without even a second of hesitation or mercy. There is no fairness here, no cosmic justice. Only strength and hunger.\"","He turned to Noah with a devilish smile.","\" Now for you, let us find you something weak and feeble to fight to the death with. If you can handle it, you will come out the other side even grander, your path toward THE more clear. And if you cannot...\"","His smile widened.","\" Ah, then it was not meant to be. Do not worry though, I will let you rest in peace within my Hunger, becoming fuel for my own ascension.\"","Tor’s authority wrapped around both of them again like a protective cocoon, concealing them from the perception of other entities.","The two proceeded further ahead into The Infinite Unfurling, and Noah couldn’t help but wonder what \"weak and feeble\" meant to a being like Tor.","And...he wouldn’t really let him die, right?","...!"]},{"number":4510,"title":"Chapter 4510: Chapter 4509: Tatakae! I","paragraphs":["Noah’s eyes were unusually bright as they took in everything that he was observing in The Infinite Unfurling.","After watching the casual collapse of entities that were considered Pre-THE Existence, beings with Decillions of Complexity and Purity who had spent eons building their Ways, his entire existence felt a sense of urgency and need.","It was like being a small insect witnessing the movements of giants, and understanding with sudden clarity that he desperately needed to be among those giants if not exceed them completely in what would be considered a short period of time.","Not to mention that he now stood at the threshold of answers regarding surviving THE Loom , regarding The Fallout, regarding the fundamental questions that had driven him forward.","So as they crossed Gigaparsecs in a matter of seconds, moving through folded space with the ease that only a THE existence could manage, Noah spoke with carefully measured words.","\"Can you tell me more about THE Creature?\"","Noah asked such a thing calmly, without mentioning that in the future, to save Khor, Tor would fight against THE Creature and subsequently face collapse due to this confrontation. That Tor’s Way and THE Civilizational Authority of Hunger would be inherited by Khor after his fall...though he inherently knew that Tor already put the clues together since he appeared here! He knew, but he didn’t know the full picture.","Noah did not know how things would unfold if he said something that would alter the future in unpredictable ways, and what the consequences of the wrong words might cascade into. He had to be careful in this delicate temporal situation.","His words caused Tor to look at him with those abyssal eyes before the entity smiled with calm recollection.","\" Ah, THE Creature ,\" Tor said with something like respect mixed with wariness. \" Now that is an entity worth speaking about.\"","He gestured at the passing landscape as they flew.","\"I have come across them a few times over the eons, though never in direct confrontation. And I have heard countless stories from the memories of creatures that I devoured, entities who witnessed THE Creature’s actions or heard tales passed down through their own consumed victims.\"","His expression became more serious.","\" THE Creature is... different from other THE existences. Where most of us claimed our Sovereignty over specific domains and built our authority within those boundaries, THE Creature took a path that many considered insane, and did not even have the ability to take.\"","Tor’s eyes gleamed with the light of remembered glory.","\"There was a memory I extracted from the memories of a Pre-THE existence I consumed some time ago. This entity had witnessed something that scarred their existence so deeply that the memory remained vivid even after death.\"","He paused for effect.","\" There was once a THE existence who had achieved THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty over the concept of Conquest. Not just existence victory or territorial expansion, but the fundamental idea of imposing one’s will over another. This entity had spent uncountable eons building their claim, devouring countless other Ways that fell under their domain.\"","Noah listened with rapt attention.","\" This THE Conquest Sovereignty had allied with a dozen Pre-THE existences, each one comparable to or exceeding those lightning and glacial entities I just ate up. Together, they sought to expand their influence across a cluster of forming domains in the Infinite Unfurling, to claim new territory and resources.\"","Tor’s smile became darker.","\" And they encountered THE Creature in their path. The Conquest Sovereignty, confident in their Surface Depth authority and their allied forces, demanded that THE Creature submit or be destroyed. They gave THE Creature a choice: bend the knee or face annihilation.\"","The air around them seemed to grow heavier as Tor continued.","\" THE Creature’s response was to simply begin walking forward and ignore. No declarations, no threats, no gathering of power. Just... walking. And as THE Creature walked, the Conquest Sovereignty and all dozen Pre-THE existences attacked with everything they had accumulated.\"","Tor’s eyes spun with remembered violence.","\" The battle lasted for a second, and for eons where THE Creature faced overwhelming numbers and supposed strategic superiority. And do you know what happened, Outsider?\"","Noah shook his head silently.","\" THE Creature brutalized all of them so thoroughly, so completely, that the very concept of Conquest was eradicated from existence,\" Tor said with quiet intensity. \" Not just defeated. Not just consumed. Fucking Eradicated. The Absolute Sovereignty that the Conquest entity had claimed was erased so utterly that nobody even remembers what that concept fully entailed anymore. The Way of Conquest itself may never exist again.\"","He let that sink in.","He! Let! That! Sink! In!","\" The dozen Pre-THE existences? Also consumed, their Ways incorporated into THE Creature’s ever-expanding domain. The entity whose memories I consumed had watched from a safe distance and fled immediately after, but the terror of what they witnessed never left them.\"","Noah felt his existence buzzing at such a story.","Tor continued as he seemed to enjoy this topic a great deal.","\" Here’s another record I know of... this one from more recent times relatively speaking. There was a coalition of THE existences, three of them who had achieved varying Depths of Surface Sovereignty. They had decided that THE Creature was becoming too dangerous, that their expanding claim over existence needed to be curtailed before it grew beyond containment.\"","...!","More THE entities that Noah never knew existed.","Because even in the stories of THE Earliest Folds, none were mentioned apart from those he knew!","But just because fabricated history did not mention them...did that mean they did not exist?","His smile was grim.","\" These three THE existences ambushed THE Creature in a prepared battlefield, a region of The Infinite Unfurling that they had spent millennia preparing with traps. They attacked in perfect coordination, their Sovereignties complementing each other.\"","Tor shook his head slowly.","\" THE Creature killed the first one within moments by simply touching them. Reached out, made contact, and the entity collapsed as if their entire existence had been deemed unnecessary by reality itself. The second one lasted longer, managing to wound THE Creature before being torn apart and devoured. The third one fled and survived, but from what I understand, they collapsed their own existence shortly after out of sheer terror as they felt like they were being followed.\"","...!"]},{"number":4511,"title":"Chapter 4511: Chapter 4510: Tatakae! II","paragraphs":["The weight of these records hung in the air!","\" The Way of THE Creature is a unique one,\" Tor said with something approaching interest. \" THE Creature seeks to encompass all of Existence itself. Not pieces of it, not aspects of it, but the totality. It is ambitious beyond measure, it is grand beyond comprehension.\"","His eyes met Noah’s.","\" And if THE Creature succeeds in fully claiming that Sovereignty completely, nothing will be able to do a single thing to them in Observable Existence. They would become synonymous with reality itself, unkillable and absolute.\"","...!","Noah’s existence buzzed at these words and stories, his mind racing through implications.","He wondered...with how powerful THE Creature clearly was, how did THE Living Paradox and Emotive succeed in whatever they did in the future? How did THE Loom occur if THE Creature was this overwhelming? Were...any of the Stories of The Earliest Folds filled with accuracy, or were they loose events embellished here and there or even told in a version that never occurred?","Did THE Creature truly give his Everythings to all of Existence?","\"...\"","There had to be a critical piece of information he was missing here, some variable he didn’t yet understand.","At his churning thoughts, Tor looked at him with knowing eyes before speaking.","\" But stories of others are fun and entertaining, educational even, \" Tor said with a shift in tone. \" But at the end of the day, your story is what matters the most.\"","...!","Tor’s gaze drifted to their changing surroundings, to the inverted mountains and flowing rivers of light that composed The Infinite Unfurling.","\" In this place, in The Infinite Unfurling where everything is still being decided, one should do their best not to compare themselves against others ,\" he said, \"I have seen countless entities destroy themselves through comparison, through measuring their worth against beings they could never match.\"","His voice took on a teaching quality.","\" Do not compare yourself to THE Creature. Do not even compare yourself to me. Comparison against others does not do much to aid one in existence. It only breeds either arrogance or despair, and both are equally poisonous to growth.\"","He turned to look directly at Noah.","\" So what if others are immensely powerful? So what if THE Creature can eradicate Sovereignties or I can devour Pre-THE existences with a single bite? Their power is theirs, built on their choices, their struggles, their unique paths through existence.\"","Tor’s expression became intense.","\" Find your own definition of powerful and set it for yourself. Never define yourself or measure your worth based on comparisons to others. If you are stronger than yesterday, that is growth. If you understand more today than you did before, that is advancement. If your Sovereignty deepens even by the smallest fraction, that is progress.\"","His dark eyes seemed to see through existence itself!","\" The moment you start comparing yourself to others, you begin walking their path instead of your own. You begin trying to match their Depth, mimic their Sovereignties, follow their Ways. And in doing so, you guarantee that you will always be lesser, always be a copy, always be derivative.\"","He gestured at the infinite expanse around them.","\" Every THE existence you will ever encounter, myself included, we all had moments where we could have compared ourselves to those who came before. We could have measured ourselves against the ancient powers and found ourselves wanting. But we didn’t. We chose to walk our own paths, to claim our own Sovereignties, to build our own unique Ways regardless of how they compared to others.\"","Tor’s voice dropped to something profound.","\" The day you truly stop comparing and measuring yourself against others, the day you stop feeling lesser because someone is more powerful or grander because you surpass another, that will truly be the day you head towards THE with clear purpose.\"","He smiled with genuine warmth.","\" Your unique THE growing within you? That is your path, Outsider. Not my Hunger, not THE Creature’s Existence, not THE Living Elemental’s Elemental authority. Yours. Something completely novel.\"","His words carried the weight of absolute certainty.","\" Do not waste it by trying to measure how it compares to what already exists. Build it into something incomparable, something that stands on its own merits. Let others compare themselves to you in the future, if they must engage in such futile exercises.\"","Tor’s words hung in the air like a revelation.","\" Power is not a ladder where you climb by stepping on others or measuring yourself against their positions. Power is a vast landscape where each being carves their own mountain from the raw stone of existence. Some mountains are taller, some broader, some more beautiful. But the only mountain that matters to you is the one you are building with your own hands.\"","He looked at Noah with eyes that held eons of experience.","\" So build, Outsider. Build without comparison. Build without measuring. Build simply because that is your nature, your choice, your Way. And when you finally achieve THE Absolute Sovereignty over whatever you choose to claim, it will be yours alone, incomparable and absolute.\"","...!","Noah listened to such words as his eyes shone with unfathomably grand luminosity!","While they may not be immensly applicable since his Existence was a Quintessential one, there was no harm drawing some lessons from this.","He had been comparing himself a few times. To Khor, to the entities within THE Loom , to the descriptions of THE powers.","Measuring, always finding himself wanting or surprisingly advanced, sometimes defining his progress in relation to others. How rapidly he advanced in days instead of years.","But Tor was right.","His THE Organ of Civilization was unique. His combination of Mana and Hunger was his own. His Mana even moreso. His path through existence belonged to him alone. Quintessential!","And if he was to survive The Fallout, if he was to build a Civilization that could endure what was coming, he needed to stop measuring himself against others and simply... build.","Build his Sovereignty. Build his Depth. Build his Way.","Not because others had done it better or worse, but because it was his to build!"]},{"number":4512,"title":"Chapter 4512: Chapter 4511: Tatakae! III","paragraphs":["Build something incomparable and absolute that was all his.","Noah’s mind buzzed with brilliance and possibilities as such a thought repeated again and again in rhythmic waves. His gaze turned and observed all the surrounding changes with intensity.","The Infinite Unfurling was vast and seemed to hold immense secrets within its impossible weavings. At this moment, while he was in contact with an existence at THE Civilizational Scale of Existence , he would continue trying to extract even more information that could aid his survival and growth.","So his eyes flashed brightly as he addressed THE First Hunger with carefully considered words.","\"I know of the False THE existences and now, Pre-THE Existences like the two we just witnessed. What is the distinction between them and entities that have reached THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty?\"","At such a direct question, the figure of Tor actually laughed with genuine amusement.","\" Ah, now that is a question,\" Tor said with a smile. \" The distinction between False THE and Pre-THE is something I have strong opinions about, Outsider.\"","He gestured broadly as he began his explanation.","\" In my sanctuary where I have Little Khor and others playing around and training, there was once a dull Inevitability who was envious of one of his brothers reaching the Pre-THE stage. This envious fool wanted desperately to attain a similar distinction that had THE in the name, something that would mark him as special.\"","Tor’s expression became stern with the memory.","\" So he went ahead and claimed the title of False THE for himself, building his authority on shortcuts and borrowed power rather than genuine development of his Way. The moment that I found out what he had done, I went back to my sanctuary immediately and I whooped that dull Inevitability into shape.\"","His eyes gleamed with dark satisfaction.","\"I broke its foundation completely until its false claim to THE was gone, shattered beyond repair. And I did all of this not out of cruelty, but to actually save it and give it a real chance at advancement. Because anything that claims the allure of False THE will never, ever become a true THE. Never .\"","His voice took on a grander quality as he continued.","\" Let me speak to you about the concepts of false and true in existence, because this is fundamental to understanding the path forward. If one taints their Way with anything that is false, with shortcuts or borrowed power or unearned claims, how can it suddenly become true in existence?\"","He looked at Noah with intense focus.","\" False would never spontaneously change to become true. The nature of falsehood is that it remains false no matter how much time passes or how much power one accumulates. A foundation built on lies cannot support a structure of truth. The day that one truly grasps THE, it can only be as a true THE and not as a False THE.\"","Tor gestured toward the landscape around them.","\" That is where those who are arduously trying to build up their Way of existence to establish their Sovereignty are following the right path, even if it seems slower and more difficult. By the time they achieve Pre-THE status, they at least have a set of stairs to climb in order to reach THE Civilizational Scale of Existence. The foundation is solid, the path is clear, and advancement is possible.\"","His expression became more contemplative.","\" Some do take what appears to be an easier way out. They inherit someone else’s Absolute Sovereignty through consumption or merger or other means. Because it is not entirely through their own efforts, because the foundation was not built by their own hands, they may pass through a stage labeled as False THE before they ultimately attain a version of THE Civilizational Scale of Existence.\"","He paused meaningfully.","\" But here is the critical point: they may be stuck at THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty for all of their existence, unable to deepen their claim because the roots were not truly their own. They wear the title but lack the substance. They hold the power but cannot develop it further.\"","At this moment, the figure of this terrifying being turned to look at Noah with a daring smile that held challenge and expectation in equal measure.","\" The enemy that we are looking for you to fight cannot even have the False THE distinction,\" he said with absolute certainty. \"I don’t want you to even taint yourself with the Ways of such beings by consuming them. You will fight something that has potential but has not yet corrupted itself with false claims.\"","As he said this with finality, he came to a complete stop. Their figures paused in mid-flight, hovering in the strange atmosphere.","Tor closed his eyes for a brief moment before he tapped his finger outward to release a circular burst of Hunger authority that radiated in all directions like a sonar pulse.","In less than a second, he opened his eyes again with satisfaction.","\" Found one.\"","An obsidian-crimson light of Hunger wrapped around both him and Noah like a protective cocoon. They disappeared from their current location in the next instant.","By the time they reappeared, they were in an entirely different environment.","Noah observed the new landscape with careful attention. For countless Gigaparsecs in every direction, mist and steam surged through the air in thick layers that obscured vision and created an oppressive atmosphere.","He and Tor were standing on top of a massive swamp tree whose trunk was as wide as a continent. Bubbling pools of liquid dark-green poison stretched out all around them like a toxic sea. The pools emitted vapors that rose in writhing columns.","Ancient trees with twisted roots emerged from the poisonous waters at irregular intervals, creating a maze-like environment. Some trees were dead and skeletal, their branches reaching toward the sky like accusing fingers. Others were somehow alive despite the toxic environment, their leaves a sickly yellow-green.","Floating islands of compressed vegetation drifted across the surface of the larger pools, each one dripping with condensed poison that fell in steady streams. The air itself felt heavy and corrosive, carrying particles of toxin that would be deadly to weaker beings.","What was most astonishing to Noah’s mind was how across this entire region, the natural environment held poisonous concentrations that would actually melt the bones or cause the complete deterioration of any entity with Complexity and Purity below Septillion levels.","\" That one there should do nicely ,\" Tor said such words as Noah was still cataloging the environmental hazards. The entity pointed approximately ten Gigaparsecs away across the toxic landscape.","Noah’s gaze followed the direction and focused on what Tor had indicated.","A monstrous abomination could be seen in the distance, its form massive.","The creature resembled a titanic toad, but warped and magnified. Its skin was a mottled mix of dark green and purple that seemed to shift and pulse with internal toxins. The surface was covered in pustules and nodules that occasionally burst, releasing clouds of poison into the air.","Its eyes were enormous and bulbous, glowing with a sickly yellow-green light that suggested intelligence behind the bestial form. Its mouth was wide enough to swallow mountains, lined with rows of teeth that dripped with concentrated venom.","The creature’s surroundings were filled with floating rivers of stellar verdant-obsidian light that represented pure concentrated poison given form. These rivers orbited the creature like satellites, occasionally converging on its body before dispersing again.","Noah’s eyes flashed brilliantly as details of this entity flooded his perception.","|Name: Venomarch Sovereign Aspirant - Toxoghra|","|Classification: Following The Way of Poison, seeking enough distinction to attain Pre-THE|","|Complexity: 1 Decillion|","|Purity: 1 Decillion|","|Grand Principles: Venom Genesis, Toxin Propagation, Corrosion Manifestation, Poison Dominion, Plague Convergence, Caustic Authority, Contamination Mastery, Virulence Supremacy|","|Current Sovereignty Progress: Attempting to establish claim over Poison|","|Status: Territorial, aggressive toward intruders|","...!"]},{"number":4513,"title":"Chapter 4513: Chapter 4512: Tatakae! IV","paragraphs":["Noah looked at this monstrous creature with growing concern as he compared their relative power levels.","His own Complexity and Purity had not stayed at the 63 Septillion level after he had used up his Unquantifiable Units of Everything. It had lowered.","The moment he had arrived in The Infinite Unfurling, he had continued flooding his Primus Mana and Civilizational Authority of Mana and Hunger into THE Organ of Civilization.","He had already recovered 3 Units, and was waiting for a few more minutes before he would have the full number of Nine Unquantifiable Units of Everything again. The one beneficial aspect was how they continued to be generated so long as there were fewer than nine present.","But either way, that was his current offensive capability.","And yes, one could say that Complexity and Purity became less and less important as one approached THE , but... this was a gap from Septillions to full Decillions!","There was an entire magnitude designation between their power levels!","In pure numerical Complexity and Purity, he was entirely outclassed. The only thing that he had within his existence to potentially fight such an entity was...","\" Why do you have such a gaze of hesitation, Outsider?\" Tor’s voice cut through his analysis. \" Does the discrepancy between your Complexity and Purity and that little creature’s numbers bother you that much?\"","He smiled with challenge.","\"It will be hard for you to fight that one, certainly. But it should be entirely possible for you to take it down. Number one, it has a stupid fucking Way built entirely around Poison. The Way of Poison, so singular and so limited. Is it not ridiculous?\"","Tor gestured dismissively toward the distant creature.","\" You have Hunger by your side, which already gives you an advantage in consuming and negating its attacks. And I can sense even something else within you, something that has frankly made me very curious about your origins.\"","His eyes gleamed with interest.","\" It would mean that you are doing something that even Entities who have achieved THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty cannot typically accomplish. Don’t ask me what I noticed as I won’t reveal this to you just yet, but just know that it makes you a little bit special.\"","He pointed at Noah’s chest.","\" So you have those advantages. And the other thing that would allow you to fight that little frog there is the product of THE that I sense inside of you. You were wrapped in its glow when you first arrived in The Infinite Unfurling, before I concealed both of us.\"","...!","Noah was silent after these words, understanding what Tor was referring to.","The only thing that he could think of that would potentially help him fight against a creature with so much higher Complexity and Purity was indeed the Unquantifiable Units of Everything generated by THE Organ of Civilization!","As for the other words that Tor had mentioned regarding sensing something else within him apart from Hunger, this should naturally be his Primordial Civilization of Mana. He essentially held two complete Civilizations within his existence simultaneously.","And Tor had said that this was something that even THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entities could not typically manage. That was certainly an interesting revelation about the uniqueness of his path.","As he was observing the creature with analytical calculation, Tor smiled and continued speaking.","\" Sometimes you can have the strength to take on something and simply not know how to properly use that strength ,\" he said with teaching intensity. \" That same power and authority that brought you safely to The Infinite Unfurling, you may not truly know how to consciously wield it yet.\"","He stepped closer to Noah.","\" So I can guide you here. That product of THE within you, it is a manifestation and representation of the smallest component of your Way of existence or your budding Absolute Sovereignty. You can choose to focus it and guide it into any specific aspect of your existence that you wish to empower.\"","Tor’s eyes gleamed with instructional focus.","\" Or you can simply let it burn within your existence as fuel. As it burns and provides energy, you can freely use its output and power to allow you to exert the weight of your entire Way and pit it directly against another Way of existence.\"","He emphasized his next words carefully.","\" Complexity and Purity would not matter in such a clash because you would simply be putting your Way against another’s. It is not merely the exertion of Civilizational Authority, though that is part of it. Since you have begun forging your Civilization connected to your Way of existence, it becomes a culmination that includes your Civilization, your Authority, and everything regarding your fundamental Way.\"","Tor gestured at Noah’s head where THE Organ of Civilization resided.","\" That is the power that you possess but have not yet begun to consciously utilize. Use that fuel from the scrap of THE I sense within you, and fight. Fight for your Way, and fight for your Existence.\"","His expression became stern.","\" If you cannot even utilize your immense Way of existence against something as laughable and fucking stupid as a singular Poison Way, then that would simply be it, Outsider. Our journey together would end here and now.\"","His next words carried finality.","\" Because if you do get devoured by that tiny little frog, I will devour that frog in turn and bring you closure by incorporating your existence into my Hunger. At least then you would serve some purpose.\"","...!","Tor said this with calm certainty, and Noah remained composed at his words. He understood that this terrifying being was simply saying all of this to push him forward, to force him to reach for power he didn’t yet know how to grasp- even if he did not really need this push as he knew he had to exceed everything about himself to survive The Fallout!","And as if to make his feelings even more clear, as if the challenge wasn’t already apparent, Tor’s voice filled with genuine emotion as he spoke his next words.","\" Fight, or Collapse !\" he said with intensity that shook the surrounding space. \" If you are the only thing protecting Little Khor in the future, you have to be strong! So fight! Show me that Khor’s faith in you is not misplaced!\"","...!","Yes.","While Tor may not know the full details of what would come to pass, he seemed to already grasp exactly where the future was headed. His only real concern was for Khor’s safety and wellbeing.","He wanted Noah to be strong, for Khor’s sake!","Noah sighed internally as he looked at the terrifying creature in the distance, observing how it moved through the toxic waters with ease, how the floating rivers of poison responded to its presence.","And then he took a step forward toward it without hesitation.","A single step.","Sometimes that was all that one needed to take in the face of impossible odds.","In the face of immense adversity and terrifying possibilities, a step was enough to begin the journey. Enough to declare one’s intention. Enough to accomplish countless things. Enough for Quintessence.","The Unquantifiable Units of Everything within his existence pulsed with response to his determination.","And Noah prepared to fight an entity a thousand times more powerful than himself, armed only with fragments of THE and the unyielding will to survive.","The crimson-gold flames of THE Immolation continued to burn across his form, but now they would serve as a reminder.","He had already survived one THE entity’s curse.","What was one more impossible challenge?"]},{"number":4514,"title":"Chapter 4514: Chapter 4513: Tatakae! V","paragraphs":["Noah took a step toward Toxoghra, and the moment he did so, the monstrous creature turned its bulbous yellow-green eyes toward him with sudden focus.","He had left the protection of Tor’s concealing authority, and his presence was now fully exposed in this toxic domain.","The creature’s massive form swelled with territorial aggression, its pustule-covered skin pulsing with increased toxin production. Its enormous mouth opened to release a roar that shook the surrounding space for Gigaparsecs in every direction.","ROOOOAAAAAR!","The sound carried concentrated waves of poison authority that turned the mist green and caused the swamp trees to wilt further. Noah’s mere appearance had offended this creature’s territorial claim over this region.","At this moment, something unexpected occurred.","The crimson-gold flames of THE Immolation Of The Sacrilegious Savage that had been wrapping around Noah’s existence shockingly receded inward. They became contained deep within his being, no longer visible on the surface.","Tor’s voice echoed out from behind with a casual explanation.","\" That little creature should be able to evade the contagion of those little flames for some time if it’s careful ,\" he said with measured words. \" But I do not want to have it slip up and make a mistake and be affected by flames that are not your own power, not your own achievement.\"","His voice carried satisfaction.","\" So I’ve gone ahead and suppressed them temporarily. They remain within you without being capable of affecting anything external. This is my gift to you, junior, to make sure that your fight is decided by your hands and your Way as much as possible.\"","...!","Tor smiled with brutal satisfaction when he said this, as if he had just made the greatest joke in existence by removing Noah’s protective curse.","Noah remained analytically calm as he took another step forward and disappeared across Gigaparsecs of distance, moving ever closer to the monstrous Toxoghra through spatial compression!","The glorious standoff between them intensified as Toxoghra roared again with increased fury. A dark green sea of concentrated poison began to swirl around its massive form, orbiting like a planetary ring made of pure toxicity.","The floating rivers of stellar verdant-obsidian light that had been drifting around converged on the creature, merging with its conjured sea to create a domain of absolute poison.","Noah observed with precision that if his existence became wrapped up in just a single drop of liquid from that poisonous sea, much of his weavings would begin to unravel and deteriorate at the fundamental level.","So at this moment, he breathed out slowly and his eyes began to shine with the light of brutality and determination mixed together.","He spoke commandingly to his own existence.","\"Burn an Unquantifiable Unit of Everything to support my Existence. Let my Way be expressed fully!\"","...!","The moment these words emerged from his mouth, his entire existence buzzed with wonder and possibility.","Prompts bloomed before his vision with unprecedented glory.","| THE Organ of Civilization is joyous at the usage and purpose of the Unquantifiable Unit of Everything.|","|One Unquantifiable Unit of Everything has been utilized to allow for the True Expression of The Sovereignty of Mana and Hunger around your existence for 1 minute.|","|If your existence can elevate this Sovereignty to the utmost and infuse it with unfathomable Harvest through combat and consumption, THE Organ of Civilization will continue to mature gradually until THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty of Mana and Hunger is attained, however immeasurably long and arduous that journey may be.|","|Current Duration: 60 seconds.|","|Warning: Use this time wisely.|","...!","BOOM!","The phenomenon that erupted around Noah was glorious beyond description.","Gold-blue seas filled with crimson stellar brilliance began to rage around his form like a living aura of concentrated authority. His entire figure became surrounded by this swirling ocean of power that represented the fundamental nature of his chosen Way.","His appearance transformed dramatically.","Gold-blue wings erupted from his back, each feather composed of compressed Mana that sparkled with inner light. The wings spread wide, spanning what looked like light-years in their full extension.","His eyes released crimson beams of pure light that cut through the toxic atmosphere, illuminating everything they touched. His hair floated upward as if suspended in water, each strand glowing with blue-gold radiance.","His skin took on a celestial quality, appearing simultaneously solid and translucent, as if he existed partially in multiple states. Patterns of flowing Mana traced across his flesh in intricate designs that shifted and evolved.","His expression burned with glory and determination as he roared toward Toxoghra at this moment, his entire visage seeming like a primordial beast declaring war against the natural order!","The True Expression of The Sovereignty of Mana and Hunger for 1 minute per Unquantifiable Unit of Everything!","Using such a rare and precious fuel to enter such a glorious state of existence meant that he had to use this one minute to its absolute fullest potential!","So...","\" Fight!\"","His voice boomed out across the distance as he took another step forward, closing the gap.","\" Fight!\"","He got ever closer to Toxoghra as the creature also roared toward him in response, its full Sovereignty of Poison being expressed through the swirling toxic sea!","\" FIGHT!\"","Noah roared one last time as he surged forward at maximum speed, and the swirling poisonous sea of Toxoghra clashed directly with his swirling blue-gold sea filled with crimson stellar light!","The contact between these two Ways caused the surrounding space to fizzle and tremble violently. Reality itself strained under the pressure of conflicting Sovereignties asserting their dominance.","A glorious high-paced symphony of battle began!","The impacting seas created explosions of authority that obliterated everything nearby. The poisonous sea held vastly more Complexity and Purity, powered by Toxoghra’s Decillion-level existence. By all conventional measurements, they should have devoured Noah’s seas of Mana and Hunger which held merely Septillions.","And yet, Mana and Hunger were not pushed back at all!","Because they were unfathomably grand Ways that touched on fundamental aspects of existence itself. Even if Poison was more complex currently in raw numerical terms, how could it possibly stand against the pure expression of Mana and Hunger?","This became the first time in his existence that Noah truly observed how Complexity and Purity could be overcome with the sheer expression of a much higher and much grander Way of existence!","The realization was profound and terrifying in its implications.","And at the point of impact where their seas clashed with explosive force, Noah and Toxoghra also met in direct combat!","Noah’s hands, wreathed in the swirling seas of Mana and Hunger, shot forward with devastating speed. His arms transformed mid-strike into 9 heads of a Primordial Mana-Flame Wyrm, their serpentine forms writhing with glorious power of his Way.","Their jaws opened wide to unleash beams of blue-gold flaming brilliance that burned with the heat of collapsing folds!","Meanwhile, Toxoghra unleashed a plague sea of concentrated poison forward from its massive mouth. The toxic wave contained every variation of venom and corruption it had mastered over eons.","The two attacks collided!","CRASH!","The explosion carved a crater in the swamp that extended for hundreds of light-years, vaporizing the poisonous waters and turning the ancient trees to ash instantly.","Noah was pushed backward by the force of impact, his feet carving trenches through the compressed ground as he struggled to maintain position.","Toxoghra...was still many times stronger. Even with the difference in their Ways, this fucking toad was stronger!","Toxoghra pressed its advantage immediately.","The creature lunged forward with surprising speed for its massive size, its enormous body moving through the toxic waters like a torpedo. One of its massive limbs swung out to strike Noah with the force of a Fold-killing impact.","BOOM!","Noah raised his arms to block, but the sheer difference in sheer power and Sovereignty meant the blow sent him flying backward. He crashed through a swamp mountain, his body carving a tunnel straight through the poisonous stone before emerging on the other side.","Golden Blood sprayed from his mouth as he recieved a direct impact from the display of The Way of Poison! The Sovereignty of Poison!","But The True Expression of The Sovereignty of Mana and Hunger immediately went to work, flooding his damaged tissues with healing authority. The injuries began to close even as Toxoghra pursued relentlessly.","The monstrous entity opened its mouth and unleashed a technique.","\"Plague Breath: Ten Thousand Toxin Cascade!\"","A waterfall of different colored poisons erupted from Toxoghra’s maw, each shade representing a different form of toxicity. Green for corrosion, purple for necrosis, yellow for paralysis, black for dissolution.","The cascade spread across light-years of space, impossible to dodge completely.","Noah’s wings flared as he attempted to evade, His Way of Existence churning furiously all around him, but portions of the toxic waterfall sliced through his Mana and Hunger and caught his left arm and leg.","The limbs immediately began to liquefy, flesh melting away to reveal bone beneath!","Oh!","Oh!!!","The pain was excruciating, but Noah roared through it!","His Way surged through the damaged areas, Mana reconstructing tissue while Hunger devoured the invasive poison. Within seconds, the limbs had fully regenerated.","But Toxoghra was already upon him again!","The creature’s massive foot came down like a hammer, aiming to crush Noah entirely. He rolled aside at the last instant, the impact creating a crater where he had been floating.","Noah retaliated by transforming his entire right arm into a single massive Wyrm head that lunged forward to bite into Toxoghra’s leg, The Way of Hunger blazing!","The jaws clamped down with grinding force, tearing through toxic flesh and devouring everything they could.","Toxoghra howled in pain and kicked violently, sending Noah tumbling across the landscape again. He smashed through three more poisonous mountains before managing to stabilize himself.","The battle was clearly weighted in Toxoghra’s favor at this time as this fucker was truly powerful- this being something that nobody could deny!","The vastly more complex entity, paired with its Way that it had refined for eons longer than Noah had even existed, pushed Noah back repeatedly. With every major impact, Noah was thrown and smashed across this grand and terrifying swamp region as Way clashed against Way, and neither Way gave up!","Even as the True Expression of The Sovereignty of Mana and Hunger continued to protect his internal existence, externally his body was taking tremendous punishment everytime they continued to clash.","He would try to keep things long ranged, but Toxoghra did not relent and came as close as he could his way deadly!","His skin and muscle became shredded repeatedly as they got infected with concentrated poison that Mana and Hunger had to constantly heal and cleanse. The only reason his core existence wasn’t reached and destroyed was because his Way continued to burn brightly around him like armor. Like an illusory form of his Living Mana-Born Existential Armor!","But the external damage was mounting.","In the impacts that followed...","Half of Noah’s face was melted off by a direct splash of acid poison, revealing his skull beneath. His chest was punctured by a crystallized poison spear that Toxoghra conjured, creating a hole!","His left arm was torn completely off at one point, flying through the air before dissolving into toxic residue.","And yet, every injury healed within seconds as his Way refused to let him fall!","The battle raged across the entire swamp region, their clash creating permanent scars in the landscape.","And then came a point where Noah felt his Way shining brilliantly after he...came in contact with The Way of Poison so much and even felt it all within his existence from thr many injuries.","Noah looked at the monstrous Toxoghra through eyes that blazed with realization. Blood dripped from his constantly-healing wounds as he bellowed out with commanding authority.","\"Your poison was powered by my Mana.\" he declared with absolute certainty. \"Your birth involved my Mana existing first! Your existence relied on this fundamental authority until you got to this point!\"","HUUM!","The words carried the weight of truth.","\" Mana is behind poison! Mana is behind all changes in existence! And Hunger consumes all things, including toxicity itself!\"","After Noah made such grand declarations, Existence began to tremble!"]},{"number":4515,"title":"Chapter 4515: Chapter 4514: Brutality! I","paragraphs":["The battle continued with Noah taking the offensive!","He surged forward with renewed purpose, his wings propelling him at speeds that distorted existence!","His mouth opened to release a beam of blue-gold light composed of septillions of individual fireballs compressed together.","The beam struck Toxoghra’s chest and detonated!","BOOM !","The creature was pushed backward for the first time, its toxic sea disrupted by the explosion.","Noah pressed the attack. His arms transformed into the nine-headed Wyrm configuration, and each head unleashed a different assault. Some bit with crushing jaws, others breathed flames, others released beams of concentrated Primus Mana.","Toxoghra retaliated with its own techniques.","\"Virulent Spear Garden!\"","Thousands of crystallized poison spears erupted from the toxic waters, each one seeking Noah’s form with homing precision. Several found their mark, puncturing his torso and limbs.","But Noah simply roared and pulled the spears out of his own body, his wounds healing even as he did so. He used the momentum of removing the spears to spin and deliver a devastating kick filled with Seas of His Sovereignty to Toxoghra’s jaw.","CRACK !","The impact shattered several of the creature’s teeth, sending them flying like meteors.","The battle’s brutality intensified further.","Above Noah’s head, a massive blue-gold throne materialized out of compressed Mana and Hunger. The throne was the size of a continent, ornate and majestic, carved with patterns that represented his Way with a glimmer of Tyranny.","Glorious Tyranny burning with a colorless veil of Quintessence!","It descended like the judgment of existence itself!","CRASH !","The throne’s weight crushed down on Toxoghra, driving the creature into the toxic waters with tremendous force. The swamp exploded upward from the impact, poisonous liquid raining down across light-years.","But Toxoghra was far from defeated!","\"Sovereignty Evolution: Adaptive Toxin!\"","The creature’s body began to shift and mutate, its poison adapting specifically to counter Mana and Hunger. New toxins emerged that were designed to corrupt these specific authorities.","When these adapted poisons made contact with Noah’s protective aura, they actually managed to penetrate deeper than before. Noah felt his Way being challenged at a fundamental level.","His left leg was caught in a splash of this adapted toxin and began to deteriorate more rapidly than his healing could compensate. The limb collapsed into bubbling flesh before his Hunger finally managed to devour the invasive substance.","The leg regrew, but the message was clear: Toxoghra was learning and adapting.","Noah responded by evolving his own approach.","His entire body began to glow brighter as he infused...the glorious allure of infinity of his way. Endless seas of Primus Mana and Hunger erupted!","His body split into nine separate serpentine forms, each one a perfect copy surrounded by blue-gold flames. The nine Wyrms circled Toxoghra from different angles, attacking in coordinated patterns.","Toxoghra tried to track all nine simultaneously but struggled. Bites and burns began accumulating across its massive form as the Nine Noah’s struck from every direction.","The creature’s toxic sea expanded outward violently in a desperate area attack.","\"Sovereignty Domain: Ocean of Eternal Dissolution!\"","The entire battlefield became saturated with such concentrated toxicity that reality itself began to break down. Space fractured, time stuttered, and causality bent.","Time stopped completely!","Eight of Noah’s nine forms dissolved immediately upon contact with this ultimate technique.","But the ninth form had transformed entirely into pure infinite energy. Noah had converted his body into a spear composed of septillions of blue-gold fireballs, each one containing concentrated Primus Mana and Hunger.","He was purely...Primus Mana and Hunger. Purely his way, carrying a deadly sharpness of infinity!","The spear pierced straight through the Ocean of Eternal Dissolution, the flames burning away toxicity through sheer intensity of opposing authority.","And then the spear passed through Toxoghra’s body!","...!","The creature’s massive form was punctured from chest to back, a tunnel of burning destruction carved through its existence. Organs vaporized, toxic blood boiled away, and the creature’s Way began to unravel.","The Way of Poison began to unravel!","Toxoghra crashed backward into a massive poisonous mountain, its body twitching and convulsing as it tried desperately to heal.","Noah reformed his body and came to float above the fallen creature.","He looked down at Toxoghra with eyes that blazed with Quintessence!","\"Your Way of Poison,\" he said with commanding authority, \"is encompassed by my Way of Mana. Mana existed before Poison. Mana will exist after Poison. And my Hunger consumes all things, including the very concept of toxicity you sought to claim Sovereignty over.\"","His voice grew louder.","\"In the end, the hierarchy of Ways is absolute. Mine supersedes yours!\"","Noah’s mouth opened unnaturally wide, stretching far beyond what should have been physically possible. The opening became a void of blue-gold light mixed with crimson stellar brilliance.","And he began to devour Toxoghra completely!","He began to devour The Way of Poison as green virulent droplets became blue gold rapidly!","Oh!","The massive creature tried to resist, tried to escape, but Noah’s Hunger was absolute in this moment. Toxoghra’s form began to compress and flow into Noah’s mouth like water down a drain.","The creature’s roars of defiance became weaker and weaker until they faded entirely.","Within moments, all of Toxoghra, along with its barely-formed Sovereignty of Poison, had been completely consumed!","The battlefield fell silent except for the bubbling of toxic waters.","Noah floated in the air, his body covered in healing wounds that closed rapidly. His True Expression of The Sovereignty of Mana and Hunger still blazed around him, though he could feel the duration nearing its end.","Prompts bloomed before his vision.","| GLORIOUS VICTORY ACHIEVED|","| Your Way of Existence has advanced further through triumphant combat.|","|THE Organ of Civilization has advanced further as you devour immense efforts, harvest, and the barely-formed Sovereignty of Poison.|","|Complexity increased by: 1 Nonillion|","|Purity increased by: 1 Nonillion|","|Additional Boon: Understanding of Poison-based Sovereignties has been cataloged for future reference.|","|Additional Boon: Your Way of Mana has been confirmed to supersede all poison-based concepts. This will now and forever remain true|","|Additional Boon: Combat experience against entities of higher Complexity has been successfully integrated.|","| THE Organ of Civilization Progress: 0.15% toward THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty of Mana and Hunger|","...!","From the distance, the figure of Tor began to clap his hands slowly while looking at Noah’s body that was still healing from deadly injuries all across its surface.","\" Good, my junior !\" Tor called out with satisfaction. \"You have taken down this weak enemy admirably!\"","His smile widened with brutal anticipation.","\"I already have the next nine opponents picked out for you, though they might be a tiny bit stronger than this one was. Shall we continue your education?\"","...!","Noah looked at his own hands, feeling the power flowing through his existence, and smiled despite the exhaustion.","He had just defeated an entity with Decillions of Complexity using only Septillions boosted by the True Expression of his Way.","He was beginning to understand what THE truly meant.","\"Let’s continue,\" Noah said with calm determination.","The crimson-gold flames remained suppressed within him, but his own power was growing rapidly.","This was the path forward.","This was his Way, gloriously and brutaly so.","This was The Way!"]},{"number":4516,"title":"Chapter 4516: Chapter 4515: Brutality! II","paragraphs":["The Way.","After defeating a terrifying enemy that should have been far beyond his capabilities, Noah found himself thinking about this concept again and again. He could not get his mind off the topic.","As he stood there amidst the devastation of what he had just accomplished in this poisonous region, he found himself looking upward to the expanse of roiling mists and terrifying environments that composed The Infinite Unfurling.","He voiced out his thoughts with calm certainty.","\" The Way is... totality.\"","HUUM!","His existence buzzed as if he was touching upon something of profound profundity, as if Existence itself was acknowledging his understanding.","Tor heard him say this after his glorious victory and appeared beside him again. The entity looked Noah over from head to toe as if he had passed some sort of critical test.","\" Yes ,\" Tor said with satisfaction gleaming in his abyssal eyes. \" The Way is the totality of how one lives their existence. Not just how you fight, but everything.\"","He gestured broadly.","\" The way one talks, the way one walks, the way they eat, the way they shit, the way they fuck, the way they sleep, the way they breathe... all of it has to match the fundamental nature of your claimed Sovereignty. If your Way is Hunger, you have to hunger in totality across every single thing that you do. Not just in battle, not just when consuming enemies, but in everything.\"","His voice took on a glorious quality.","\" You are barely just beginning to discover your Sovereignty, Outsider. The more you use your Way of existence in legitimately applicable ways, like having your Way oppose other Ways in direct confrontation, it will be like you are honing your blade and making it sharper and sharper with each stroke.\"","He looked at Noah with intensity.","\" You realize more and more about your Way of existence through use, through conflict, through application. After a battle like the one you just fought, where you exerted your Way with that glimmer of THE in your existence through, you should be extremely perceptive to your Way of existence right now.\"","Tor’s smile widened.","\" You may even feel as if you’re standing at the top of Existence. As if you are untouchable, invincible, absolute. This is a unique and good state of mind to be in, a heightened awareness that allows for rapid growth. We just need to make sure that it does not get you killed through overconfidence.\"","He gestured toward the horizon.","\" But it is also why I had multiple other opponents already located that you could fight next. When your Way burns brightly as it is right now, when you can feel every aspect of your Sovereignty with crystal clarity, we have to continue striking the iron while it burns hot and see just how far you can get before this state of heightened awareness fades.\"","...!","Noah nodded slightly at this wisdom, and when he spoke, his voice carried the weight of absolute certainty.","\"Mana and Hunger,\" he said with calm authority. \"These are not merely Weavings I wield. They are the totality of my existence.\"","His eyes gazed into the distance as he continued.","\"When I breathe, I am breathing in Mana from the surroundings and hungrily devouring the authority in the atmosphere to fuel my existence. When I move, my body burns Mana and hungers for more movement, more action, more advancement. When I think, my thoughts are composed of Mana arranged in patterns, and my mind hungers for knowledge, for understanding, for revelation, for Quintessence.\"","His hands clenched into fists.","\"When I fight, I am not simply using Mana and Hunger as weapons. I am Mana and Hunger manifested in physical form, opposing all that stands before me. When I consume my enemies, I am not merely growing stronger. I am expressing the fundamental truth of my Way: that all things can be broken down into Mana, and all things hunger to become more than they are.\"","Noah’s voice grew more commanding.","\"My Way is infinitely profound because I can apply it in countless manifestations. Every action I take, every word I speak, every thought I process, all of it reinforces and deepens my understanding of what Mana and Hunger truly represent at the most fundamental level of existence.\"","His gaze turned cold and tyrannical.","\"So yes. Let us see who else will be cut down for the sake of my Way. Let us see what other so-called Sovereignties will be devoured and incorporated. Let us continue until my understanding reaches such depths that even THE entities will have to acknowledge it.\"","...!","Tor’s eyes shone with brilliant satisfaction at such words. Obsidian-crimson waves of Hunger wrapped around both of them, and they disappeared from the poisonous swamp.","Noah felt the surging waves of spatial compression all around them as they traveled. He continued to look at his hands, feeling the terrifying strength of the True Expression of The Sovereignty of Mana and Hunger that had faded away and now waited to be activated once more.","It could only be unleashed with the usage of a product that could only come from THE Organ of Civilization.","He continued endlessly pouring more and more of his Primus Mana and Civilizational Authority of Mana and Hunger into the Organ as he knew that the more it developed, the more Unquantifiable Units of Everything he would likely be capable of forging simultaneously.","Toward THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty , this authority in the form of Mobius strips would be something unfathomably normal for him to possess. They would make up every single ounce and iota of his power.","When such time came, how much closer would he be to being capable of withstanding The Fallout?","His eyes flashed coldly at the thought as he focused on his surroundings.","Tor seemed to be looking at him and smiling silently before he spoke with approval.","\" I had expected you to be burning with arrogance after such a victory, drunk on the feeling of power, \" he said with measured words. \" But you seem to be reining it in a great deal. It is a good quality.\"","His expression became stern.","\" Be strong, yes. Be confident in your Way, absolutely. But do not forget that you are still weak in the grand scheme of things. Use that weakness as if it is a monstrous predator chasing you, forcing you to run unfathomably fast toward more strength.\"","His voice dropped.","\" Because if that monster does ever catch you, if you come across another THE entity that simply wants to use you as a snack and you cannot escape or hide, no matter how grand your Way of existence is, if it has not matured and developed sufficiently, it will be snuffed out completely.\"","He gestured ahead.","\" But hey, here we are. Let’s see how much you can grow before something inevitably happens to derail us...haha!\"","...!"]},{"number":4517,"title":"Chapter 4517: Chapter 4516: Brutality! III","paragraphs":["Noah clenched his fist and continued feeling the immensity of his Way as he looked around and felt a wave of scalding heat wash over him.","The region they had arrived in was dramatically different from the poisonous swamp.","This domain was filled with countless layers of volcanic smoke that rose in towering columns stretching toward the sky. Churning volcanic mountains released extremely complex and pure volcanic materials in continuous eruptions.","Molten brilliance flowed like rivers between the mountains, glowing with crimson-orange-gold light that illuminated the perpetual twilight. The lava was condensed authority given liquid form, each drop containing enough power to obliterate Folds.","Geysers of superheated plasma erupted at irregular intervals, creating fountains of stellar fire that arced across the sky before raining down as meteoric destruction.","The entire region was surrounded by crimson mountains that pulsed with internal heat, their peaks glowing like forge fires. Floating meteorites spun in orbital patterns overhead, each one burning with such intense heat that space itself warped around them.","A single spinning meteorite colliding with an unprepared entity could collapse anyone with mere hundreds of Septillions in Complexity and Purity instantly.","No weak Living Existences or Early Creatures could survive here!","Noah’s gaze did not even need to be directed before he found the target that Tor had brought him to.","His eyes flashed with a light of tyranny as he observed another glorious monstrosity.","The creature was a nightmare given flesh and fire.","Its body was serpentine and elongated, stretching for what looked like light-years in length. But it had no eyes, no visible sensory organs at all. Its head was smooth and rounded, featureless except for a massive circular mouth lined with rings of crystallized flame teeth.","The skin appeared pale and translucent, almost sickly, but this was deceptive. The flesh burned with crimson lava flowing just beneath the surface like blood in veins. Flames erupted from pores across its entire body in rhythmic pulses.","Its neck could extend to impossible lengths, and the creature moved with disturbing fluid grace despite its titanic size. The tail ended in a whip-like appendage that left trails of fire in the air.","With a mere flash of light, Noah saw its details.","| Name: Infernal Sovereign Aspirant - Pyrokhan|","|Classification: An Entity of The Way of Fire|","|Complexity: 55 Decillion|","|Purity: 55 Decillion|","|Grand Principles: Conflagration Ascendancy, Thermal Dominion, Combustion Manifestation, Inferno Authority, Magmatic Convergence, Heat Supremacy, Ember Genesis, Flame Propagation|","|Current Sovereignty Progress: Attempting to establish claim over Fire |","|Status: Highly territorial, extremely aggressive|","|Warning: Temperature in surrounding area increases exponentially in its presence|","...!","Noah saw its details and gauged the threat calmly.","The Way of Fire.","Tor began to speak as he prepared to explain the nature of this opponent.","\" This one is another entity that is a bit stronger than the first, with its Way being another limited path as it focuses solely on Fire, which can fall under an umbrella of many broader concepts. For this one—\"","Before Tor could even finish his explanation, Noah took a step forward to leave the veil of concealment that this being naturally held.","He spoke with glorious certainty.","\"I will take it from here.\"","...!","Tor’s smile became even wider behind him as he said with satisfaction, \" Good, good!\"","Noah floated domineeringly toward the creature, his posture radiating absolute confidence. He gave the command internally with calm authority.","\"Burn another Unquantifiable Unit of Everything. Let my Way be fully expressed.\"","|THE Organ of Civilization rejoices at continued combat application.|","|One Unquantifiable Unit of Everything has been utilized to allow for The True Expression of The Sovereignty of Mana and Hunger around your existence for 1 minute.|","|Current Progress: Each successful combat deepens your understanding and brings you closer to THE Surface Depth.|","|Duration: 60 seconds.|","|Remaining Units: 7|","|Note: THE Organ of Civilization continues to generate more.|","...!","As his body began to burn with the True Expression of The Sovereignty of Mana and Hunger, the creature he was approaching roared toward him with fury.","ROOOOAAAAAR !","The temperature in the surroundings directly increased to levels that would extinguish even creatures at Nonillion Complexity and Purity! The air itself ignited, burning with plasma fire that consumed oxygen and replaced it with pure thermal energy.","The floating meteorites began to glow brighter, responding to Pyrokhan’s rage.","And yet, while surrounded by the glorious weight of his Way manifested fully, Noah did not even feel a change in temperature.","His protective aura of blue-gold and crimson stellar light simply negated the heat as irrelevant.","He spoke with imposing authority as he approached the eyeless creature.","\"You play with the Way of Fire,\" he said with cold certainty. \"What do you think allows your sparks to flicker and bloom? When the first flame formed in existence, what do you think it was composed of?\"","His voice carried absolute conviction.","\" It was Mana!\"","BOOM!","As he said this, Noah’s body became surrounded by extremely concentrated seas of blue-gold and crimson Primus Mana and Hunger. He allowed it to form into Nonillions of miniature Primordial Fireballs that began condensing around his entire body.","But most of them gathered toward his legs and hands, concentrating at the extremities of his limbs.","The extremities began to pulse and shine with an increasingly concentrated glow of blue-gold and crimson stellar light. His entire figure became extremely prominent in this volcanic hellscape, outshining even the molten rivers.","For his entrance and first meeting with Pyrokhan, he shockingly raised his right foot as if he planned to step on this massive titanic creature!","His foot swirled with endless concentrations of his Way, visible authority coiling around it like dragons made of fire and light.","He was truly learning how to manipulate his Way of existence, testing out different methods of exerting his influence.","Noah’s gaze flashed with immense tyranny and Quintessence amidst unfathomable calmness as he spoke his declaration.","\"In the minute to come, I will pound your Way until it understands that even Fire belongs only under Mana and Hunger!\"","...!","The creature roared in defiance, and the battle began!"]},{"number":4518,"title":"Chapter 4518: Chapter 4517: Brutality! IV","paragraphs":["Pyrokhan’s entire body coiled and then lunged with apocalyptic force. Its movements were cataclysmic, each motion forming flaming mountains and volcanic eruptions in its wake.","As it moved, volcanoes spontaneously formed from the sheer heat and pressure of its passage. Each volcano immediately erupted, launching continent-sized masses of molten rock toward Noah at relativistic speeds. As if they were tachyons of molten brilliance traveling far faster than light itself!","The surrounding existence melted from the impacts. Space liquified, time burned away , and causality itself became unstable.","Noah raised his right foot, now glowing like a blue-gold sun, and stomped down on the first incoming volcanic mountains.","CRASH !","His foot, wrapped in the True Expression of his Sovereignty, erased everything, breaking down theWay of Fire that composed it and converting it into pure Mana that he absorbed.","Pyrokhan responded by opening its massive circular mouth and unleashing a beam of concentrated fire that could have melted Primordial Folds.","Noah raised both hands, his arms now glowing with the same solar intensity as his feet, and...clapped them together.","PAH!","BOOM!","The clap created a shockwave of Mana and Hunger that intercepted the fire beam and devoured it entirely!","But Pyrokhan was relentless.","The creature’s body coiled around the battlefield, creating a ring of volcanic mountains that all erupted simultaneously toward the center where Noah floated.","Hundreds of Decillion-level volcanic projectiles converged on his position from every direction!","Noah’s limbs blazed brighter as he spun in place, his arms and legs trailing arcs of blue-gold and crimson light. Each limb that struck an incoming volcano completely scorched away the fire authority that composed it.","His movements were precise and economical, wasting no energy.","But some attacks got through.","A stream of molten plasma struck his left shoulder, burning through his protective aura and charring flesh down to the bone. Another volcanic boulder crashed into his back, creating a crater in his torso.","Noah did not even make a sound.","His expression remained calm and analytical as the injuries rapidly healed, his Way flooding the damaged areas with regenerative authority.","His enemy was still much more powerful than him in raw numerical terms, but the quality of his Way was too grand for Pyrokhan to overcome.","The battle raged across the volcanic region, their clashes creating permanent scars in the landscape.","Noah continued gathering high concentrations of his Way of Mana and Hunger onto the extremities of his limbs. More and more authority compressed into smaller and smaller spaces.","Pyrokhan used fire to warp existence itself, melting everything to instsntly appear around Noah as it wrapped its elongated body around him like a constrictor, applying pressure that would have crushed everything! The creature’s skin burned with such intensity that it turned Noah’s flesh black and crispy.","Noah simply raised his arms, which now looked like endlessly radiant blue-gold suns, and pushed outward.","CRACK !","Pyrokhan’s body was forced away, sections of its flesh scorched and burned by contact with Noah’s limbs.","The creature shrieked and created a volcanic apocalypse, summoning thousands of erupting mountains simultaneously!","Noah’s legs, also glowing like miniature suns of concentrated authority, kicked out repeatedly. Each kick generated a blade of compressed Mana and Hunger that sliced through the volcanic formations and scorched away their fire authority.","His arms punched forward, creating shockwaves that erased entire mountain ranges.","The radiance from his limbs grew brighter and brighter until it actually began to scorch away the scorching flames of Pyrokhan itself!","Eventually, as his arms and legs looked like shining blue-gold suns that outshone everything in the region, Noah spoke with calm and domineering certainty.","\"Your Way of Fire,\" he said without emotion, \"is a subset of Mana. Fire cannot exist without Mana providing its foundation. Fire cannot burn without Mana fueling its reaction. Fire cannot spread without Mana carrying its authority.\"","His limbs blazed even brighter.","\"And Hunger consumes all things, including the very concept of heat and combustion that you have tried to claim. Your Sovereignty is incomplete. Your claim is weak . And ultimately, your entire existence can only be devoured.\"","The creature shrieked and bellowed with desperate fury, unleashing everything it had accumulated over eons!","A final volcanic cataclysm erupted, creating a sea of molten destruction that should have obliterated anything in the Decillions of Complexity scale!","And Noah had just stepped in the Nonillions!","Yet...","Noah simply walked forward through it, his sun-like limbs scorching away all fire authority they contacted.","He reached Pyrokhan’s main body and grabbed it with both hands.","The creature tried to burn him, tried to melt his grip, but Noah’s hands had become something beyond simple flesh.","They were manifestations of his Way made solid.","And then, brutally, he began to rip Pyrokhan apart.","His fingers tore through flesh that should have been impervious. His hands scorched the creature’s Sovereignty, burning away its claim to Fire piece by piece.","Pyrokhan writhed and screamed, but Noah was merciless .","He proceeded to brutally eat the creature’s Way of existence piece by piece, consuming its Fire Sovereignty bite by bloody bite.","His own Way shone ever brighter with each consumption!","The end scene was apocalyptic and destructive. Blood boiled and evaporated. Flesh charred and disintegrated. The surrounding existence buzzed with resonance and melted from the sheer intensity.","And when it was finally over, Noah stood alone amidst the devastation, his body still glowing with solar radiance as the last traces of Pyrokhan’s existence were absorbed.","As the battle ended, even Tor was looking at him with shining eyes of genuine appreciation.","This being who loved to talk, who always had commentary and philosophy to share...","Had no words.","He simply smiled with profound satisfaction and nodded once.","The message was clear: Noah had exceeded expectations again!","And they were just getting started.","---","As glory unfolded in a far, far distant past...","The Present Era.","In the Heart of Elemental, within the Transcendent Elemental Folds.","The domain stretched across Gigaparsecs of compressed space, a testament to the ancient power of the residual Civilization of Elementals. Glorious elemental towers rose like titans frozen in eternal ascent, each one carved from crystallized authority that pulsed with fundamental forces.","The entire region was surrounded by spinning Transcendent Wheels of Existence, massive constructs that rotated with glory.","This was the seat of power for the Living Elementals, a place that had stood unconquered for eons!","Well, until today...as this was about to drastically be changed."]},{"number":4519,"title":"Chapter 4519: Chapter 4518: Brutality! V","paragraphs":["The Infiniverse arrived at the center of the Heart of Elementals with the inevitability of a falling star.","Her humanoid form materialized above the grand central plaza, and the moment she appeared, existence itself trembled with acknowledgment. She stood suspended in the air, her figure composed of flowing Omniverses and rivers of verdant-gold light.","Above her, a million Primus Inevitabilities blotted out the sky like a swarm of ascending titans.","The Infiniverse’s aura blazed outward with terrifying intensity, washing across the entire domain like a tsunami of absolute authority. The pressure was inexorable, the weight of existence itself demanding acknowledgment!","Throughout the Heart of Elementals, every being with even a modicum of power felt that presence.","The Kleos Council of Elementals, the governing body of this ancient domain, had no choice but to respond as they were all already at high alert ever since Primus Inevitabilities appeared and unleashed Sparks across the folds, but previously...none of these entities had forced anyone to take the Sparks.","But the new aura they felt seemed purposefully intimidating!","So...","Spatial tears opened across the plaza as figures began to emerge. The Dukes of Elemental, each one a powerhouse who commanded respect and controlled vast territories, assembled with grim determination.","Their combined presence should have been overwhelming, a display of concentrated power that could reshape reality.","But before The Infiniverse’s blazing aura, they appeared... diminished.","She gazed down at the assembled Dukes with eyes that held infinite calculation and cold purpose. She did not need to be here. Protos and other Primus Inevitabilities could simply lead the charge. But...she came because she wanted to!","When she spoke, her voice carried across Gigaparsecs without effort.","\"One hand offers fealty,\" she said with calm finality, extending her right hand forward. \"And one hand offers death.\"","Her left hand remained at her side, but the implication was clear.","\"What will you choose?\"","...!","The plaza fell into tense silence as the Dukes of Elemental looked at each other with visible uncertainty. Some showed anger at such brazen disrespect. Others displayed caution, having sensed the vast gulf in power.","A particularly powerful Duke of Elemental stepped forward from the assembled group as he seemingly unveiled hidden power!","His form pulsed with 20 Quintillion Complexity and Purity, making him one of the strongest beings present!","He was wreathed in crimson flames that burned with the authority of primordial fire, and his voice boomed out with defiance.","\"We are the Living Elementals! In existence, there is decorum, there is understanding. The Coalition of Living Existences stand together as if you attack one, you attack all. We will not be bullied by-\"","...!","Before his words could even finish, The Infiniverse raised her leg with casual grace and stepped down through the air.","An illusory stellar leg formed above the Duke, vast beyond comprehension. It was composed of compressed Omniverses and Folds, and flowing with authority that represented a semblance of the totality of her power.","The leg descended with a terrifying force.","CRASH !","The Duke of Elemental was crushed downward, his flames extinguished instantly as he was driven into the plaza floor. The impact created a crater that stretched for light-years, and the Duke lay at its center, nearly decimated.","His body twitched weakly, still clinging to existence but utterly defeated.","The Infiniverse’s expression did not change. She looked at the rest of the assembled Dukes with the same calm certainty.","\" Do not waste my time, \" she said with cold authority. \" Fealty, or death? \"","HUUM !","The message was unmistakably clear!","And it did not take too long.","Not really!","One by one, the Dukes of Elemental began moving toward her outstretched right hand. Their movements were reluctant at first, pride warring with survival instinct.","But as they approached her extended palm, something extraordinary occurred.","Sparks of The Way of Mana began producing from her hand, brilliant blue-gold motes of light that danced in the air. Each spark represented an offer, a connection, a pathway to serving under her Master.","The first Duke to reach obtained the Spark and felt the inclusion into The Way of Mana!","Oh, Mana!","Fire fueled by Mana burned hotter. Water infused with Mana flowed more fluidly. Earth reinforced by Mana stood more solidly.","The Duke stepped back with newfound understanding and knelt, acknowledging fealty with shaking eyes as it did not even feel like they lost something, with their progression over the elements seemingly made even grander!","One by one, the others followed.","The conquest unfolded with efficiency as each Duke of Elemental accepted The Way of Mana and submitted to The Infiniverse’s authority. Even the Duke who had been crushed eventually crawled forward and accepted the inevitable.","When the last Duke had sworn fealty, The Infiniverse’s gaze turned upward to the million Primus Inevitabilities hovering above.","She commanded them with absolute authority.","\"Go stand as nodes and break apart these Transcendent Folds. Everything shall be devoured into The Infiniverse. The lifeforms within these Folds will gain entry only after complete submission and fealty.\"","Her voice carried the weight of inevitability.","The Primus Inevitabilities responded as one, their voices creating a chorus that shook existence.","\" We shall fulfill our duty!\"","They dispersed instantly, each one moving to positions around the vast expanse of the Transcendent Elemental Folds.","And then they began to work.","The Primus Inevitabilities released waves of Primus Mana that connected between them, forming a vast web of authority. The web began to constrict, applying pressure to the very fabric of the Transcendent Folds.","Primus Mana permeated across The Transcendent Elemental Folds like an invasive species that could not be resisted. It seeped into every corner, every hidden pocket, every defended sanctuary.","Regions began to split as the Folds themselves were torn apart at the fundamental level!","Entire territories that had existed as separate spaces started flowing toward the humanoid form of The Infiniverse.","She stood at the center of it all, arms spread wide, absorbing everything.","Mountains of crystallized elemental authority flowed into her like water into an ocean. Forests of living flame were consumed and integrated. Seas of liquid lightning were devoured whole.","The lifeforms within these regions had two choices: submit and be incorporated into The Infiniverse, or resist and be left behind in regions of collapsed existence.","All chose survival. All Wheels of Existence holding Weak Fold Dwellers and Living Existences flowed towards her as these beings would passively be filtered and branded to ensure nothing was missed!","Waves of Elementals, from the weakest to the most powerful, streamed toward The Infiniverse and accepted The Way of Mana.","Her humanoid form remained at the center, but The massive Infiniverse itself in the distant Wandering Territories....","New Frequencies of Existence bloomed within her. New Wheels of Existence began to spin. New domains formed to house the conquered territories and their inhabitants.","The process was brutal in its totality but not unnecessarily cruel. Those who submitted were welcomed. And all faced no other result but submission.","And this was only the beginning of The Infiniverse’s campaign of conquest.","The final image was one of immensity and glory.","The Infiniverse stood radiant at the center of what had once been the Heart of Elementals, now transformed into another domain within her vast existence. Primus Mana flowed through everything like golden blood through veins.","Above, the Primus Inevitabilities continued their work, dismantling the last remaining pockets of existance.","The Infiniverse had declared that she would devour every Fold, conquer every territory, and subsume every fragment of power outside THE Loom.","And nothing would stand in her way.","This was conquest, and this was duty.","This was love expressed through absolute domination!"]},{"number":4520,"title":"Chapter 4520: Chapter 4519: History is Written I","paragraphs":["History.","Many argued endlessly about what history actually was, debating definitions and methodologies with the passion of scholars who had devoted lifetimes to the subject.","But what was history actually, when one stripped away all pretense?","Were they not simply stories that were passed down from those who had lived longer than others? Tales told by survivors, by victors, by those with the power to ensure their version endured?","So could history always be accurate if those who had lived longer simply passed down stories of their own fabrications, shaped by bias and self-interest? Was any history actually true history, based on the accounts of many, or preserved in written texts and records that themselves could be altered and fabricated at will?","Unless one was able to go back in time to see how things actually unfolded with their own eyes, could they truly say they knew and understood the true history? Or were they simply being fed lies dressed up as truth, generation after generation?","There were countless Stories of The Earliest Folds that spoke of THE Living Existences and THE Creature. Of Early Creatures, Inevitabilities, and Fold Dwellers who shaped reality through their conflicts and achievements.","But was that all there was to history, these grand narratives of powers and conflicts?","Because the most pivotal thing that many needed to understand and grasp was that history was written by the victors . History was always, inevitably, written by those who survived and triumphed.","And they could weave whatever story they wished, painting themselves as heroes or saviors, casting their enemies as monsters or tyrants, regardless of what actually occurred.","Truth became whatever the powerful decided it should be.","Truth could be written.","History could be written!","---","In the Infinite Unfurling.","Noah stood in the decimated volcanic region, surrounded by the aftermath of his brutal victory. The ground was scorched black for light-years in every direction, molten rivers cooled into twisted formations of glass and obsidian.","He was looking at a set of prompts that bloomed before his vision with brilliant light, and his own existence continued to buzz with glory as his Way advanced further and further with each battle.","|Your Way of Existence has advanced significantly through triumphant combat against a superior foe.|","| THE Organ of Civilization has advanced further as you devour immense efforts, harvest, and the barely-formed Sovereignty of Fire.|","|Complexity increased by: 66 Nonillion (New Total: 66 Nonillion+)|","|Purity increased by: 66 Nonillion (New Total: 66 Nonillion+)|","|Additional Boon: Grand Principle Fragment of Thermal Immunity is being studied by The Cheating Architect|","|Additional Boon: Grand Principle Fragment of Combustion Manipulation is being studied by The Cheating Architect.|","|Additional Boon: Understanding of Fire-based Sovereignty has been cataloged and can be referenced.|","|Additional Boon: Your Way of Mana has been confirmed to supersede all fire-based concepts at fundamental levels.|","|Additional Boon: Combat effectiveness against entities of vastly higher Complexity continues to improve.|","| THE Organ of Civilization Progress: 0.28% toward THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty|","|Unquantifiable Units of Everything Generated: 2 (Current Total: 12)|","|Note: Your mastery of True Expression continues to deepen. Each battle refines your understanding.|","...!","Oh!","After Noah observed these prompts with satisfaction, Tor appeared before him with an approving smile.","\" Ready ?\" he asked simply. \" The next one is not stationary as they are on the move across the Infinite Unfurling.\"","After such words, Noah gave a light nod of acknowledgment.","Obsidian-crimson light wrapped around both of them like a protective cocoon, and they disappeared once more into the vast expanse.","—","An unknown number of Gigaparsecs away from Noah and Tor, in a different region of the Infinite Unfurling.","The domain was filled with radiant purple brilliance that pulsed in rhythmic waves across impossible distances. Blazing fiery purple numbers in different runic etchings floated powerfully throughout the space, each one burning with the unmistakable allure of the authority of time.","Numbers that represented moments, durations, sequences, and causality itself drifted like embers on unseen currents.","The entire region was suffused with the potent authority of time in its rawest form. Past, present, and future existed simultaneously here, creating a disorienting effect where one could see echoes of what had been and shadows of what might yet be.","Crystalline structures grew in impossible spirals, their formation both complete and ongoing depending on which temporal layer one observed. Rivers of temporal energy flowed upward and downward simultaneously, defying conventional direction.","At the very peak of this domain floated a smooth round purple crystalline structure the size of a continent, perfectly spherical and rotating slowly on multiple axes at once.","And on that structure, the auras of utterly terrifying beings could be felt radiating outward with suffocating intensity.","One aura was immensely domineering, their Way of existence truly and fully established as they burned with terrifying waves of THE Civilizational Authority of Time . This was not someone approaching THE but someone who had achieved it and deepened their claim!","There were a few others that orbited around such terrifying authority like planets around a star, and all of them seemed to be at the Pre-THE stage of power. Each one was formidable individually, but together they created a constellation of authority that would be devastating.","At this moment, the entity that emanated the aura of THE floated casually on a pulsing purple sea of temporal energy that formed beneath them like a throne. The dozen or so Pre-THE Existences formed a circle around them in a posture of attentive listening, as if receiving teachings from a master.","The Way of Time swirled all around with terrifying potency, and its origin was an extremely wild-looking woman who possessed rabbit ears that twitched with each fluctuation of temporal authority.","She was humanoid in basic structure but clearly not purely so. Her rabbit features included not just the ears but also digitigrade legs that ended in powerful clawed feet, and a subtle coat of fine fur that covered portions of her exposed skin.","Her eyes pulsed with purple brilliance that seemed to see through multiple timelines simultaneously, giving her gaze an unsettling quality of knowing what you would do before you did it!"]},{"number":4521,"title":"Chapter 4521: Chapter 4520: History is Written II","paragraphs":["She was adorned in archaic clothing and accessories that appeared primitive at first glance but were actually supremely sophisticated.","What she wore was seemingly made from the skin and fur of other powerful lifeforms, and these materials still pulsed with silent radiance of Ways of Existence that had been elevated to THE .","Her vest was crafted from scaled hide that shimmered with suppressed lightning authority. Her bracers were made from bone that still resonated with earth sovereignty. Her belt incorporated fur that held traces of wind dominion!","This meant that this entity had actually decimated or injured other existences at THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty or even higher, and had used their bodies to forge her clothing and accessories as trophies!","This was THE Purple River, THE Time Surfer , and her reputation was one of calculated brutality mixed with unexpected mercy.","She looked at the entities assembled around her with sharp intelligence and spoke with commanding clarity.","\" You all are powerful in your own right ,\" she said with acknowledgment. \" But if you can understand your weavings of existence in relation to time, you will be able to advance truly far beyond your current limitations.\"","Her eyes shone with a sharp light of ingenuity as she turned toward one of the Pre-THE Existences, a being wreathed in radiant white light.","\" You follow The Way of Light, \" she said with teaching precision. \" Photons traveling through space, illumination piercing darkness, energy manifesting as visible spectrum. It seems straightforward, does it not?\"","She paused for effect.","\" But light has an intimate relationship with time that you have not fully grasped. Light travels at a fixed speed through space, which means it is bound by temporal constraints. When you observe distant stars, you are seeing light from the past because time was required for that light to reach you.\"","Her hands gestured as if manipulating invisible threads.","\" If you can understand how your Way of Light intersects with time, you can manipulate not just illumination but causality itself. You can make light arrive before it departs. You can create illumination that exists in the past, present, and future simultaneously.\"","She leaned forward with intensity.","\" Do you understand?\"","Shockingly, the Pre-THE Existence she was addressing nodded with visible reluctance. Their eyes showed a light of fear mixed with unwillingness, but they could only follow these teachings because the alternative was collapse.","THE Time Surfer was effectively trying to incorporate and extract tremendous gains from their Ways of existence by connecting them with her own Way of Time. Any advancements they made while following her guidance would increase her Civilizational Authority through their connection.","And yet, none of them would be remaining true to their original Ways of existence if they incorporated the aspect of time into their own unique Sovereignties. They would become derivative, subordinate to her Time Sovereignty!","But they were not as powerful as this being, and under the threat of complete collapse or potential elevation, they followed her without question. They progressed their Sovereignties while weaving connections with time along the way, hoping the benefits would outweigh the cost.","An instant later, THE Time Surfer turned toward another direction as she looked at an entity shining with calm white gold light that seemed to contain all possibilities.","\" You are a unique one ,\" she said with genuine interest. \" You call yourself The Living Origin, correct? Well, whether living or dead won’t matter much in the end, because if you are walking the Way of Beginnings, you absolutely cannot be distant from time.\"","The Living Origin!","THE Time Surfer was actually holding The Living Origin among the dozen Pre-THE Existences gathered here!","\" Origin implies the starting point of all things ,\" THE Time Surfer continued with philosophical depth. \" But what is a beginning without the context of time? A beginning only has meaning because time flows forward from that point. Your Way encompasses the moment of genesis, but that moment exists within the temporal framework.\"","She smiled with calculating precision.","\"If you can understand how Origin and Time interweave, you can manipulate not just what begins but when it begins. You can create multiple simultaneous origins, or delay the genesis of something until the perfect moment. You can make endings become beginnings and beginnings become endings through temporal manipulation.\"","Her voice carried certainty.","\" Your Way of Origin gives you power over initiation and genesis. My Way of Time gives context and control over when and how those initiations occur. Together, we could reshape the very concept of causality itself.\"","Opposite her sat a woman in a white-gold dress who nodded with acknowledgment, though her eyes did not hide their regal light of defiance even as she complied. The Living Origin was submitting to these teachings but not surrendering her pride or her ultimate ambitions.","THE Time Surfer looked at her calmly and laughed with genuine amusement at such defiance.","She was about to continue her lessons when something unexpected occurred.","She blinked and turned her head sharply toward a certain direction, her rabbit ears twitching with sudden alertness.","\" What is this... ?\" she murmured with confusion bleeding into her tone.","Her Way of existence buzzed with sudden intensity as someone of her caliber possessed unfathomably powerful sensory perception when it came to anything dealing with their Way. She could sense temporal fluctuations across vast distances, detecting even the smallest discrepancies.","And at this moment, she sensed unique musings of the Way of Time that should not exist here. More specifically, a type of temporal authority that was foreign and did not belong to The Infinite Unfurling at all.","Her expression shifted to something dangerous as a smile spread across her features.","\" Who the hell has come here from a different time? \" she said with deadly curiosity. \" This should be an impossibility. Nothing should be able to appear in The Infinite Unfurling unless it had always existed here from the beginning!\"","Her eyes shone with sharpness and brutal calculation as she rose up from her seated position. The purple sea beneath her rippled with her movement.","She beckoned to the entities assembled around her with commanding authority.","\" Come on, you little things ,\" she said with a mix of condescension and purpose. \" There seems to be a discrepancy in time that should not exist here, and I need to understand how it is even possible in the first place.\"","She paused with a predatory smile.","The dozen Pre-THE Existences rose as one, following their temporary master toward the source of the temporal anomaly.","And...","History was about to be written by whoever survived the coming encounter!"]},{"number":4522,"title":"Chapter 4522: Chapter 4521: History is Written III","paragraphs":["In the Infinite Unfurling.","In a region filled with endlessly billowing waves of snow that stretched across countless Gigaparsecs in every direction.","The air was thick with crystalline ice particles that refracted light into prismatic colors, creating an otherworldly atmosphere of beauty mixed with deadly cold. Mountains of compacted snow rose like frozen titans, their peaks lost in clouds that themselves were composed of frozen temporal energy.","The end of a terrifying battle played out with brutal finality.","A massive winged furred eel-like creature fell from above and crashed into a mountain of heavy snow with devastating force. The impact created an avalanche that buried the creature under millions of tons of frozen matter.","The creature was easily the size of several continents, its serpentine body covered in thick white fur that had been scorched and burned across most of its length. Most notably, it was missing one wing that had been brutally ripped from its body.","That severed wing was held up triumphantly by none other than Noah, who stood amidst the falling snow with blue-gold brilliance blazing around his form.","He opened his mouth unnaturally wide, the opening expanding far beyond what should have been physically possible, and swallowed the entire massive wing whole. His Way of Hunger devoured it instantly, breaking down the authority of Mass that had composed it.","And then he tyrannically waved his hands upward with commanding certainty.","A sea of Mana surged in response to his will, forming beneath the buried creature and forcefully lifting its massive form up from the snow. The creature was brought directly toward Noah despite its attempts to resist, pulled by irresistible authority.","Noah opened his mouth again, even wider this time, and swallowed the entire titanic creature whole!","The scene was a terrifying one as around Noah, blue-gold brilliance visibly surged with increased intensity. His Way had grown stronger with each consumption, each battle refining his understanding and deepening his claim.","Prompts bloomed before his vision with familiar glory.","|Your Way of Existence has advanced significantly through triumphant combat.|","|THE Organ of Civilization has advanced further as you devour immense efforts, harvest, and the barely-formed Sovereignty of Mass.|","|Complexity increased by: 100 Nonillion (New Total: 166 Nonillion)|","|Purity increased by: 100 Nonillion (New Total: 166 Nonillion)|","|Additional Boon: Grand Principle Fragment of Gravitational Manipulation is being studied by The Cheating Architect.|","|Additional Boon: Grand Principle Fragment of Density Control is being studied by The Cheating Architect.|","|Additional Boon: Grand Principle Fragment of Weight Nullification is being studied by The Cheating Architect.|","|Additional Boon: Understanding of Mass-based Sovereignties has been cataloged and can be referenced.|","|Additional Boon: Your Way of Mana has been confirmed to supersede mass-based concepts.|","|Additional Boon: Your physical body can now naturally manipulate its own mass at will.|","| THE Organ of Civilization Progress: 0.45% toward THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty|","|Unquantifiable Units of Everything Generated: 1 (Current Total: 12)|","|Note: Your understanding deepens.|","After he observed all these prompts with analytical satisfaction, Noah’s gaze lifted to the distant figure of Tor hovering above.","\"I seem to be getting the hang of it more and more,\" Noah said with calm observation. \"I want to say that pending no disruptions, I can continue to fortify my Way of Existence over the next few hours and days, but...\"","His eyes narrowed with perception.","\"When do I see a frown on your face for the first time?\"","Yes, at this moment, Noah could actually see a frown on the face of this terrifyingly powerful THE entity. It was the first time such an expression had crossed Tor’s features since they had begun their massacre.","Tor blinked at Noah’s words before he shook his head with a smile that did not quite reach his eyes.","\" My Hunger is very sensitive, \" he explained with measured words. \" Anything relating to its propagation or challenges is sensed before it can fully occur. And right now, my Hunger feels a sense of challenge approaching.\"","He paused thoughtfully.","\"A type of challenge that I have encountered a few times before across the eons. It usually means anticipation. My own Hunger can sense something coming and it begins to salivate in anticipation of what might be consumed or what might pose a genuine threat.\"","His expression became more serious as he continued.","\" Once a Way of existence reaches a certain depth of understanding and Sovereignty, one will be able to carry out what others only believe to be possible through different Ways. Hunger should in no way be capable of telling me about things that are coming in the future. Hunger should not be able to burn or freeze or manipulate temporal flows.\"","He smiled with dark satisfaction.","\" But it can do all of that and more, as long as one understands how to properly use their Way. And right now, my Hunger is showing me in its anticipation the image of a savage being coming toward this location with an entourage of followers.\"","His eyes focused on Noah.","\" And you seem to be the one that attracted this savage thing, Outsider.\"","Noah frowned at these words as he closed his eyes and focused with his own Way of existence, extending his perception outward as far as it could reach.","He sensed nothing approaching, no threat on the horizon.","His perception had not reached the level that Tor was experiencing, and this only further demonstrated how entities that had not achieved THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty were so far below in capability. Someone could be in mortal danger and about to die, and they would not even know it until the killing blow landed.","And yet Tor already sensed the incoming threat, and had even gained an image of what that threat was before it arrived. What a glorious and terrifying capability this was!","At the same time, Noah was reminded of the immense dangers all around. While he currently had Tor as protection, he had to prepare for the inevitable possibility when he would not have such a being as a guardian.","He would be entirely defenseless, simply walking with hope through these dangerous environments. And he did not like to rely on hope.","He would either have to remain hidden while allowing his body of Ozymandias to be the one to move out freely and risk collapse, or he had to make the decision whether the unfathomably glorious opportunities in this dangerous landscape were worth potentially being collapsed before he even knew it. Worth being unable to even return to his current era.","Of course, these were all contingencies and things that he was thinking through in case things should go catastrophically wrong. As of now, he still had THE First Hunger with him.","As he was processing all of this analytically, the figure of Tor smiled and spoke.","\" Well, this encounter will serve as a teaching lesson,\" he said with anticipation. \" You can get a glimpse of the scale of power between genuine Sovereignties at THE level. It will be extremely hard for you to even perceive what is truly happening, but you should be able to catch a glimpse at least.\"","...!"]},{"number":4523,"title":"Chapter 4523: Chapter 4522: History is Written IV","paragraphs":["His eyes gleamed.","\" Are you ready?\"","The words of Tor echoed out across the snowy domain, and before Noah could even formulate an answer, another voice cut through the atmosphere.","\"My oh my, what is this?\"","Noah’s gaze became solemn as he heard a voice emerge from one corner of this snowy domain, and if that voice had not echoed out deliberately, he would not have even known that the entity was there at all.","Space peeled back like layers of an onion, and an entity burning with THE Civilizational Authority emerged in all her terrifying glory.","She appeared with a glorious confidence, her rabbit ears twitching as she analyzed the scene before her. Her eyes pulsed with purple brilliance as her gaze locked onto Noah with laser focus, actually ignoring Tor entirely in her initial assessment.","Noah felt her piercing gaze as if she was trying to see right through him, to unravel every secret and mystery his existence contained. He could sense that she wanted to do much more than simply observe, and the only reason this entity was unable to act on those impulses was because of Tor’s presence.","His eyes focused immensely on this situation as he cataloged details. Behind this being, there were actually a dozen other terrifying signatures emanating authority, but all of them seemed much less powerful than her.","They appeared to be at the Pre-THE stage of power.","Noah’s gaze passed through them analytically as his attention was suddenly drawn toward the back of the group where he sensed something utterly unexpected.","Something familiar.","Familiar? What could possibly be familiar to him here?","His eyes turned heavier as his gaze actually left THE entity who was still analyzing him, and he focused far behind her where he saw a woman in a white-gold dress.","His eyes buzzed with recognition when he saw her, because the familiarity he sensed was his own Living Existential Authority of Origin flowing within his existence and resonating with her presence!","Noah’s eyes flashed with immensity as he looked at her with newfound understanding.","The woman was otherworldly in her appearance, her features so perfect they seemed almost unreal. Her hair flowed like liquid starlight, shining with white-gold brilliance that illuminated the space around her. Her eyes held an unfathomable depth, as if they contained the origin points of countless realities.","A prompt bloomed before Noah’s eyes unbidden.","|Name: ???????????? [The Living Origin... THE Living Origin? ]|","|Classification: ????????????|","|Complexity: ???????????? [Displayed as Pre-THE ]|","|Purity: ???????????? [Displayed as Pre-THE]|","|Grand Principles: ????????????|","|Singularity Principles: ????????????|","|Current Sovereignty Status: Extremely advanced in Way of Origin|","|Warning: This being’s current existence exhibits power of Pre-THE designation.|","|Analysis suggests this is likely a significant deception- a fucking lie.|","|Note: Entity is far more developed than surface observation indicates.|","|Threat Assessment: EXTREME|","Noah looked at all of this information with analytical marvel, his mind racing through implications.","Opposite him, his intense gaze made the eyes of The Living Origin also lock onto him calmly. She looked him over with the same analytical precision he was using on her, and recognition seemed to spark in her gaze as well no matter how much it was hidden!","He had actually met one of THE Living Existences in the Infinite Unfurling, encountering them before they were known as the esteemed beings they would become in his era!","Seeing The Living Origin also got him questioning the nature of what truly happened in this past.","There were obviously multiple THE entities present in this era. THE Creature was feared, as was THE Living Paradox . How was it that in The Earliest Folds of his time, only THE Creature was prevalent alongside THE Living Existences as a collective? What had happened to the countless other monsters and powers that roamed across the Infinite Unfurling?","His mind buzzed with many questions that had no immediate answers!","But at this moment, the calm words of Tor cut through his contemplation.","\" Have you looked enough ?\" Tor asked with dangerous politeness.","THE Time Surfer laughed with genuine amusement at the question.","\" No, not nearly enough ,\" she said with brutal honesty. \"I might need a much closer look to properly understand what I am sensing.\"","Her eyes remained fixed on Noah.","\" That thing you have beside you there does not belong in The Infinite Unfurling. Never has, never will. I can consider myself somewhat of an expert on time mechanics, and if there was someone fucking with time itself, I can usually manage to understand how and why.\"","Her smile widened with predatory interest.","\" But that thing beside you should not be able to even exist here at this point in time. The temporal displacement is impossible by every metric I understand. I need to see how he can do such a thing when it seems he has not even reached THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty, so yes, I will need a much closer look.\"","She tilted her head with challenge in her gaze.","\" The only question will be whether you will take some of my time before I am able to examine him properly.\"","At such pointed words, Tor smiled with a sense of profound brutality as he looked at THE Time Surfer up and down with his own analytical assessment.","\" Hunger and Time ,\" he said with philosophical weight. \" Two concepts that many believe to be fundamentally different, operating on separate principles of existence.\"","His eyes began to spin like black holes.","\" But they are not so different, O Time Surfer, right? You are the weaker practitioner of time compared to that...Living Temporal, is it? Let me educate you slightly. Everything is prey to Hunger eventually. Even time itself can be consumed, devoured, made part of something greater.\"","His smile became predatory.","\"At this moment, I can already taste time on my tongue as I look at you. It is a little salty, with undertones of inevitability and decay. The flavor of something that believes itself untouchable but will ultimately be consumed like everything else.\"","He paused for emphasis.","\" Your time authority is impressive, certainly. But authority over when things happen means nothing if those things are devoured before they can occur. Hunger exists outside of temporal flow because it is a constant, an inevitability that transcends your manipulations.\"","His voice dropped to something profound.","\" So before you take a closer look at my junior here, ask yourself this question: Are you prepared to be tasted in return?\"","With such words, existence itself began to tremble with the weight of conflicting Sovereignties preparing to clash!","The storm of snow in the surroundings intensified dramatically, becoming even heavier as the atmosphere charged with tension. The temperature dropped further despite already being at levels that would collapse weaker beings.","And in the space between THE First Hunger and THE Time Surfer , reality itself began to fracture under the pressure of their combined presence.","Noah stood amidst it all, about to witness a clash between genuine THE Sovereignties for the first time!"]},{"number":4524,"title":"Chapter 4524: Chapter 4523: Predator! I","paragraphs":["As existence churned and trembled in the face of two entities at the level of THE expressing their Sovereignties, Tor walked deliberately in front of Noah and began to take measured steps toward THE Time Surfer.","As he moved forward with calm certainty, the expanse of space behind him turned obsidian-crimson as if his Hunger covered everything in that direction. The color spread like spilled blood across reality itself, staining the very fabric of existence.","And Noah continued to hear the voice of Tor echoing in his mind even as this being fearlessly walked toward another THE entity.","\" A river that carves through stone does not succeed through strength, but through relentless focus on a single path,\" Tor’s voice resonated with teaching intensity. \" My Hunger has been honed again and again across eons, Outsider. It has tremendous Depth.\"","His mental voice carried weight.","\" And remember what I taught you before: Depth is how thoroughly one can alter and rewrite existence through their Sovereignty. THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty is just that, scratching the surface of what is possible. And yet many entities will only ever stop there, unable to progress further.\"","The obsidian-crimson light that shone behind Tor and encompassed Noah and everything else became even more intense as he continued speaking.","Opposite him, THE Time Surfer radiated vivid purple luster that also painted everything behind her with that color. The two expanding domains met in the middle, creating a boundary where obsidian-crimson clashed against purple in silent contest.","And yet Tor continued calmly inside Noah’s mind with his teachings.","\" Apart from Depth, there is also Breadth ,\" he explained with measured words. \" Breadth is exactly how many Sovereignties one can claim simultaneously. When Depth becomes significant enough, when one has truly mastered their primary Way, they can proceed to claim Sovereignty over another Way if they are capable enough.\"","His voice carried profound meaning.","\" Such a thing is only possible much further down the path, with tremendous Depth already established. And yet you, Outsider, currently hold two Ways of Existence running parallel within you. I will tell you honestly that you are way out of your depth attempting such a thing at your level.\"","There was approval in his tone despite the warning.","\" And yet you are doing everything seamlessly somehow. You have taken a semblance of my Hunger and proceeded to do something unfathomable with it, making it walk hand in hand with Mana in the same Way and Civilization that you are forging. This makes you an anomaly among anomalies.\"","His voice became stern with advice.","\" But make sure that you do not branch yourself out too much in the future. After all, a single blade sharpened ten thousand times will cut deeper than ten thousand blades sharpened once. Observe everything through the lens of your Civilization of Mana and Hunger as unified concepts, and you will not go wrong.\"","Noah absorbed these words with analytical focus as Tor’s mental voice shifted to more immediate concerns.","\" For now, I wish to tell you to observe what is about to occur if you can,\" Tor said with slight regret. \" But it seems that even this may not be a possibility for you. You would need significant time to adapt your perception just to be capable of seeing us properly when we clash at full intensity.\"","His voice dropped with finality.","\" And it does not look like you will be given that time.\"","The moment after Tor said this, his physical figure disappeared from Noah’s perception entirely!","The figure of THE Time Surfer also vanished simultaneously, as if both had simply ceased to exist in observable space!","And then...","BOOM !","Instantly, Noah observed the utterly ridiculous scene of reality itself in front of him being torn open like a page in a book. A massive rift spread upward and downward for countless Gigaparsecs, splitting existence into two distinct halves.","One side shone with obsidian-crimson brilliance that represented Hunger’s domain. The other side pulsed with purple luminescence that represented Time’s authority.","And Noah felt existence trembling even more violently than before, but shockingly, he could not see either of THE entities that were supposedly fighting right in front of him!","Their forms had vanished completely from his perception.","And yet the evidence of their battle was unmistakable.","BOOM !","Another massive tear in reality spread far above them, also stretching out for Gigaparsecs in length. It gushed out a deluge of endless collapsed existence from this rending of space, pouring destruction like a waterfall.","He could not see them fighting, and yet they were clearly already engaged in combat of apocalyptic proportions!","He actually could not fully comprehend the scope of the battle unfolding before him. Even their figures were not observable to his eyes as they moved at speeds and through weavings of existence he could not even begin to perceive.","Noah’s gaze turned toward the Pre-THE entities that THE Time Surfer had brought with her, and he saw that even they seemed to be struggling. They were moving their heads around rapidly, whipping their attention from one point to another as they tried desperately to keep track of the entities fighting.","But they were unable to successfully follow the clash either!","The Living Origin stood with intense focus, her white-gold eyes narrowed. The other Pre-THE existences showed frustration mixed with awe.","Noah’s eyes pulsed with tyranny as he refused to accept such a limitation. Their power was so vastly superior that he could not even perceive them fighting properly?","At such a moment of frustrated realization, Tor’s voice echoed in his mind again.","\"If you had enough time to stay here and continue to witness the clash between two opposing Ways of existence, you would have eventually adapted,\" Tor explained with clinical precision. \" You would have eventually seen how our Sovereignties clash against each other and how I manipulate mine to systematically eat apart hers.\"","His mental voice carried grim news.","\" But you do not have that time, unfortunately. It seems this savage opponent of mine who is proficient in temporal manipulation already knows the results of the future of this battle through her Way. She has seen her own defeat.\"","There was dark amusement in his tone.","\" And precisely because she knows her fate, she has already called for reinforcements in the past, seconds before our battle even began. That is how utterly frustrating time manipulation and temporal fuckery can be when facing a master of it.\"","Noah’s mind raced to understand the implications.","\" She only knew of the result of this battle after we began clashing and she saw the trajectory of events,\" Tor continued with a unique observation. \" And yet she somehow made it so that her Way of Time retroactively called for help from her acquaintances before we even started fighting. She altered the past based on knowledge from the future.\"","His voice carried grudging respect.","\"It may not make much logical sense when stated plainly, but essentially the situation is this: You staying here is no longer a viable option. I will not be able to fight multiple other THE entities alongside this manipulative Time Surfer while simultaneously being able to protect you adequately.\"","The reality of the situation became clear.","\" So for now, for your safety and for me to truly enjoy this feast without being held back by defensive considerations, we will have to temporarily part ways, \" Tor said with finality. \" You will be on your own for some time, Outsider.\"","...!"]},{"number":4525,"title":"Chapter 4525: Chapter 4524: Predator! II","paragraphs":["Before Noah could even formulate a response to the dire situation unfolding around him, he felt a surge of obsidian-crimson authority wrapping around his existence with protective intensity.","Tor’s voice echoed in his mind with rapid urgency.","\" The most I can give you without the power of THE being immediately sensed on you is a singular THE Barrier of Hunger,\" he explained with clinical precision. \" It can collectively withstand a single killing strike of any entity at THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty, no matter how concentrated or devastating that strike may be.\"","His voice carried grim determination.","\"I will also extinguish those shitty elemental flames wrapped around you. That curse is another flare shining with the power of a THE entity that can be used to track and find you across vast distances. With it gone, you can focus on your survival without being a beacon for every predator in the Infinite Unfurling.\"","The authority around Noah intensified.","\"I will send you far away from here so that the incoming reinforcements cannot perceive your departure or track your destination. It will be up to your own power and luck if you can survive until I can find you again.\"","His voice dropped with finality.","\" Hide, hunt, do what you must to survive. For me to collapse all the coming THE entities and properly devour them without interruption, it could take hours or days depending on how many respond to her call and how deeply they commit to the battle.\"","A moment after he said this, Noah felt the constant burning pain that had been suppressed within his existence pulse violently and then flicker away entirely!","A terrifying burst of Hunger raged all around him, devouring the crimson-gold flames that had marked him since his confrontation with THE Living Elemental!","Prompts bloomed before his vision with glorious detail.","| THE Immolation Of The Sacrilegious Savage has been devoured by an Unfathomable THE Civilizational Authority of Hunger.|","|You are now completely free from its effects and tracking capabilities.|","| THE Barrier of Hunger has been laid upon your existence.|","|Classification: Absolute Defense Shield|","|Source: THE First Hunger |","|Protection Level: Can withstand one complete killing strike from any entity at THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty|","|Coverage: Encompasses entire existence including physical form, soul, consciousness, and all derivative aspects|","|Activation: Automatic upon detection of lethal threat|","|Duration: Permanent until triggered, and until depleted|","|Additional Properties: Undetectable by entities below THE scale. Will not register as foreign authority to most scanning methods.|","|Warning: Once triggered and exhausted, protection is completely gone. Use wisely.|","Noah felt a glorious change ripple through his entire existence as the transformation completed.","Shockingly, the curse placed upon him by THE Living Elemental that should have killed him outright, but instead had inadvertently paved the way for him to forge something unprecedented within Observable Existence, disappeared completely at this moment.","In its place was a barrier that could withstand the full killing strike of an entity that had already stepped into THE Depths of the Civilizational Scale of Existence.","It was an unfathomably grand progression of cause and effect when he truly thought about it. Him encroaching upon the Primordial Civilization of Elemental had been the first domino that fell, which led inevitably to the rage of THE Living Elemental branding him with that curse.","And that curse had led to everything else that followed.","It had led him to develop THE Organ of Civilization as the only viable counter. It had led to his Temporal Traversal to the Infinite Unfurling where opportunities beyond measure existed. It had led to meeting Tor and receiving teachings about THE that would have been impossible to obtain otherwise.","And now it led to him being in an unfathomably dangerous position, hunted by multiple THE entities in a time period where he should not even exist.","The chain of causality was almost absurd in its complexity.","\"I am sending you to a relatively safer region of the Infinite Unfurling filled with weaker entities, but not too weak ,\" Tor’s voice explained rapidly. \" They will likely search for you in places with extremely weak prey, so I am avoiding those obvious locations.\"","The authority around Noah began to compress with spatial manipulation.","\" Stay hidden and wait for my return. I will find you again once this situation is resolved, no matter how long it takes or how far you travel.\"","Space began to twist and fold around him.","\" And Outsider ,\" Tor’s voice carried genuine concern for the first time since they had met. \" Remember that you are still weak by the standards of this place. Do not let your recent victories against weak entities make you forget that fundamental truth.\"","His words carried weight.","\" Survival takes priority over everything else. Get a bit stronger when you can do so safely, but do not take unnecessary risks. Live first, grow second.\"","The spatial compression reached critical intensity.","\" Good luck.\"","Obsidian-crimson brilliance erupted all around as Noah could only gaze at the continuing impacts from beings he still could not even perceive fighting!","Reality tore and reformed in patterns that hurt to observe. The boundary between Hunger’s domain and Time’s authority fluctuated wildly as the two Sovereignties clashed at scales beyond his comprehension.","And then Noah was forcefully ejected from the battlefield as Tor’s Hunger launched him across vast distances of the Infinite Unfurling toward an unknown destination!","As he traveled through compressed space at impossible speeds, Noah caught one final glimpse of the battle behind him through the distorting spatial layers.","The entire region where they had been standing was being systematically destroyed. Rifts in reality spread like spiderwebs across existence, each one large enough to swallow solar systems. The snow had been completely replaced by storms of collapsed hunger and time fighting for dominance over the ruined landscape.","And in that final moment before distance made observation impossible, the eyes of The Living Origin locked onto him with intense focus!","Her white-gold gaze burned through the spatial distortions as if they were not even there, tracking his departure with analytical precision.","As such recognition occurred, he managed to hear the roar of THE Time Surfer as this being bellowed out commandingly to the entities that she had brought with her!","\" Follow any traces of where that thing is being sent !\" she shouted with fury and desperation mixing in her voice. \" Track it and find it for me! If you succeed in bringing me that anomaly, I promise on My Way of Time itself to help you achieve THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty!\"","Her voice became deadly.","\" Should any of you attempt to run or hide, I will hunt through your past and your futures to ensure that you collapse completely across all timelines! Bring me that thing! Bring me that temporal anomaly!\"","BOOM!","The words were heavy and terrifying as they echoed across dimensions.","Multiple Pre-THE Existences burst with their full Sovereignties being unleashed, each one burning with authority as they attempted to track Noah’s departure trajectory through the spatial compression!","The Living Origin moved with particular purpose, her Way of Origin allowing her to trace beginnings and endings with frightening accuracy.","But Tor’s spatial ejection had been executed by a THE entity of terrifying power, and tracking such a departure was nearly impossible for Pre-THE beings!"]},{"number":4526,"title":"Chapter 4526: Chapter 4525: Predator! III","paragraphs":["Noah felt the space around him stabilize as the forced transportation neared its conclusion.","The reality that settled in his mind was a heavy one, but his eyes flashed with tyranny as he processed it!","Alone in the Infinite Unfurling, without protection from Tor, without guidance or direction from anyone who understood this place.","But so what?","He was always alone when it truly mattered.","He had awakened alone in a world of dungeons and monsters. He had entered those dungeons alone while others formed parties and sought safety in numbers. He had traveled across worlds alone, making allies when convenient but never depending on them for survival.","This would simply be another time he was alone, another situation where he needed to use everything he held to survive and thrive!","Space distorted and twisted all around him as the final layer of compression broke apart with a sound like shattering glass!","And he materialized in an unknown region, immediately extending his senses outward to catalog his new surroundings while simultaneously suppressing his aura to minimal detectable levels.","He had appeared in a region dominated by vast mountainous landscape that stretched in all directions.","Roiling mist obscured much of the terrain, filtering through impossibly tall trees whose trunks were wider than cities. The mist moved with purpose rather than randomly, as if it possessed some form of awareness.","In the atmosphere above, he could see floating mountains spinning slowly in defiance of gravity. Radiant white mist held them aloft, flowing around their bases like rivers of cloud given structure and purpose.","The entire region felt extremely ancient and old. The very air carried weight that spoke of eons passing.","Noah breathed in deeply, tasting the authority-saturated atmosphere as he thought analytically about how he should proceed from this point.","Tor could find him again in a matter of hours or days depending on the outcome of the battle, but he would not be dependent on that possibility. He needed to make his own moves, forge his own path forward.","One’s Way of existence could not be properly forged by holding the hand of another and being fed everything like a child. Struggle was an integral part of existence, and he would not shy away from it now.","He closed his eyes and felt the absence of the scorching flames that had been burning across his body for so long. In their place, he sensed the faint barrier of Hunger that wrapped all around him like invisible armor.","A moment later, his eyes opened with a light of tyranny and sharpness as everything was decided in his mind.","He was effectively being hunted by multiple Pre-THE Existences who possessed terrifying power. There was also an entity proficient in Time, someone who was uniquely not THE Living Temporal, actively hunting him due to his impossible appearance here.","She had said how he was an impossibility, how he should not be able to exist in this time period.","But who the hell was she to decide where he could and could not appear?","If anyone sat down and looked at the situation objectively to ask how Noah was able to traverse to a time before The Earliest Folds even solidified, they would also deem it an absolute impossibility. And yet his Early Atlas of the Folds had made it a possibility through its unique features.","His THE Organ of Civilization had taken things even further, powering a journey that should have been beyond the realm of feasibility.","Since these were his tools of impossibility, he had to continue forging them and pushing their capabilities even further. His aim now was clear: continue hunting entities that were trying to forge their Sovereignties, just like him.","All the while, he would protect himself to ensure that if he came across someone significantly stronger, he would not be collapsed. Nor would he give up the usage of the barrier of Hunger wrapping around him too quickly or wastefully.","With all of this crystallized in his mind, Noah looked down at himself as he considered his first course of action.","To throw off those hunting him if they ever came close to finding his location, he needed to change what they had already seen and would be searching for.","\"Mana burns behind countless Sovereignties as the foundation,\" he said with certainty. \"Since I have devoured the Sovereignties of Poison, Fire, and Mass, I could easily depict them if I chose to.\"","After he spoke these words, his body began to change with purposeful transformation.","He became more sizable, his frame expanding as he took on the form of a massive Early Creature. His skin shifted and changed texture as it became surrounded by transforming blue-gold rivers of Primus Mana.","Those brilliant rivers quickly morphed into virulent green rivers of concentrated poison that flowed across his body like living tattoos!","The brilliant allure of his Way of Mana and Hunger rapidly transformed across his entire existence. In a short period of time, his appearance changed completely.","His body now stood massive and imposing, easily three times his normal height. He was adorned in an archaic verdant chiton that looked like it had been woven from toxic plants that pulsed with lethal authority.","His hair became wild and flowing, pulsing with poisonous green light that cast shadows across his transformed features. His eyes burned with the same toxic luminescence, appearing like pools of concentrated venom.","His entire form became completely surrounded by virulent green rivers of poison that flowed and coiled around him like serpents. He emanated nothing else but the Way of Poison in every aspect of his being!","This was his Way! His Civilization! As the foundation of countless things, he could transform it to become anything he needed it to be!","Prompts flashed before his vision with confirmation.","|Your understanding of Mana as foundational authority has deepened significantly.|","|You can now convincingly mimic any Sovereignty you have fully consumed and integrated.|","|Current Available Mimicry: Poison, Fire, Mass, Living Existential Authorities(Limited)...|","|Mimicry Quality: Indistinguishable from genuine Sovereignty to entities below THE scale.|","|This capability demonstrates profound understanding of your Way’s versatility.|","After this transformation was complete, Noah stretched his new form experimentally and went even further with his preparations.","\"Mana is synonymous with the surrounding environment,\" he said with cold calculation. \"Ambient Mana covers everything in existence. When I move, my aura and brilliance will be no different from the surrounding environment itself.\"","His eyes flashed with tyranny.","\"As if I am simply seas of ambient authority flowing from one place to another, completely unremarkable!\"","After these words were spoken, a glorious phenomenon began to occur around his transformed body.","Noah began to fade away from observable perception, his figure slowly melding with the atmosphere itself. The poisonous green rivers that wrapped around him became indistinguishable from ambient authority in the air.","His form blurred and became translucent, then transparent, until he entirely became something that was not capable of being perceived as separate from the environment!","He had become invisible not through visual manipulation, but by making himself fundamentally indistinguishable from the background authority that permeated all of existence.","More prompts flashed before him with details of this unique state.","|You have entered a state of environmental synchronization.|","|Detection Difficulty: Entities below Pre-THE existence cannot sense your presence at all.|","|Detection Difficulty: Pre-THE existences must be extremely attuned to environmental authorities AND actively searching the specific region you occupy to sense disturbances.|","|Detection Difficulty: THE entities can still perceive you if they focus their Sovereignty on your location.|","|Duration: Indefinite as long as you maintain focus and do not release overwhelming authority.|","|Warning: Engaging in combat will disrupt this state.|","|This represents masterful control over your Way’s expression.|","After entering a state where he could move without being perceived by the vast majority of entities, where he was basically camouflaged and invisible to all but the most perceptive hunters, Noah nodded with satisfaction at the completion of his preparations.","He looked out at the expanse of brilliance all around him, at the ancient trees and floating mountains and authority-thick mist, and began to move forward with purpose.","Concealment was accomplished. Now it was time to hunt and advance his Way even further.","He had to use all the time available to him in the Infinite Unfurling while grasping and understanding its deepest secrets. Every moment here was an opportunity that entities in his era would kill for.","Because the one thing he truly needed to understand was the fate of all the powerful THE entities and Pre-THE Existences that clearly populated this time period. How was it that only THE Creature and THE Living Existences were known and prevalent in his era?","Just what had happened in the Infinite Unfurling to reduce this vast population of powers to such a small number?","There were many questions and mysteries swirling in his mind, but this particular enigma demanded answers!","With this goal crystallized in his thoughts, he looked at the endless expanse of mist and ancient landscape all around him as he began to move with predatory grace.","He was no longer the prey being hunted.","He was a predator on the hunt, seeking to devour and grow stronger with each encounter!"]},{"number":4527,"title":"Chapter 4527: Chapter 4526: Predator! IV","paragraphs":["The Infinite Unfurling had to be one of the most unique places that Noah had ever been in.","One of the more striking characteristics was how there was nothing weak existing in this place. Truly nothing weak could survive the ambient pressure and dangers that permeated every corner.","An hour passed as he moved through the mountainous landscape that he found himself in, surrounded by rolling mists that obscured vision and created an atmosphere of perpetual twilight. He effectively mapped out the region and cataloged what could be lying within its boundaries.","In the surrounding Gigaparsecs, he was actually able to discover multiple entities ranging from Upper Nonillions to Decillions in Complexity and Purity. Each one followed their own unique Way of existence, carving out territories where they hunted and grew stronger.","He tested his concealment by observing them closely and even entering the perimeter of a few light-years near them.","Gloriously, none of them could sense his presence at all!","If he went too close and his ambient integration wore off from proximity to their concentrated authorities, they might detect the disturbance. But for now, he had left them alone while continuing to scout the region.","Within the surrounding Gigaparsecs, his figure could not be observed by others as he moved with purpose. He traveled rapidly like a flicker that was almost impossible to track.","No, even comparing his movement to light was not accurate enough. It should be more precise to say that he was moving around like a flicker of tachyons, like a set of particles that traveled unfathomably faster than light itself through the fabric of reality.","And after he continued to scour this entire region methodically and confirmed that he could not sense any visible power at the level of THE , he felt reasonably secure. Even though if such a being was present and they hid their aura similar to how Tor concealed his presence, Noah would not really be able to sense them anyway.","But after cautiously mapping this entire place with systematic precision, there was no signature of any THE entities apart from the creatures that he had marked.","After all of this was confirmed through careful observation, he appeared a few light-years away from one of his first targets.","It was a creature that was chewing on the bones of another entity it had recently killed. Its body was surrounded by crackling arcs of purple lightning that danced across its form in chaotic patterns.","The creature looked like a massive salamander, easily the size of several mountains. Its body was covered with jutting sharp crystals all over its surface that refracted the lightning into prismatic displays.","It was another entity following the Way of Lightning, its power stabilized at 955 Nonillions of Complexity and Purity.","Noah looked at it from his concealed position as his eyes pulsed with calculating tyranny. His method of attacking had to change somewhat from what he had done with Tor’s protection.","He needed the battles to be quick and seamless. The longer he spent in conflict, smashing around the environment and destroying mountains while fighting, the more risks he took. The more chances there were for other entities to be drawn to the commotion.","So he asked himself a critical question: Could he not skip all the booming impacts between his Way and the Way of his enemy? Could he simply settle everything in a single strike, as long as this strike made the outcome of whose Way was stronger absolutely clear?","With this tactical consideration in mind, he breathed out slowly and raised his left hand toward the enemy that he intended to kill.","His Primus Mana could become anything he desired. He had a vast array of offensive capabilities under his belt after devouring multiple Sovereignties.","Utilizing Nonillions of Primordial Fireballs and condensing them into concentrated points of his Way was one method of attack. He had used it frequently because he was most familiar with that approach.","But he had endless variations available because his Primus Mana could accomplish everything he conceived. He could design new Mana Arcana Glyphs at any time to suit any situation.","When he thought about an attack from long range that could potentially snipe an enemy and decimate them in a single strike without giving them time to react or defend...","He smiled with cold satisfaction.","In the next moment, he felt THE Organ of Civilization in his brain buzz with activation. An Unquantifiable Unit of Everything was consumed as fuel, and his existence flared up like a newborn star being born!","His outstretched left hand began to buzz with concentrated poisonous verdant light. His Way of Mana and Hunger, currently expressed through the mimicry of the Way of Poison, formed into an incandescent virulent green compound bow!","The weapon materialized with perfect balance and deadly intent, composed entirely of compressed authority.","And with his right hand, he pulled back on the bow strings with smooth motion. A terrifying arrow began to form between his fingers as he filled it with endless seas of his Way of existence.","As he drew the string back further and further, he whispered silently to himself with absolute certainty.","\"Mana is the foundation of all change in existence,\" he said with analytical precision. \"For any sparks of lightning to form, they need Mana at their foundation to provide the energy for that manifestation.\"","His eyes gleamed with tyrannical confidence.","\"So if I deem that lightning is unable to stop my Mana, if I declare that my Way supersedes the authority of electrical discharge, then it simply cannot resist!\"","The arrow that was forming shone with an even more intense green light as he spoke these words. His Civilizational Authority of Mana and Hunger was pumped into this single arrow endlessly.","He meant for it to take the life of an extremely powerful enemy by collapsing what their Way stood for. By proving in a single shot that his Way superseded theirs in quality and depth.","And so he endlessly poured even more and more of his infinite waves of authority into the forming projectile. He knew the moment he released it, his ambient integration would be disrupted and fall away.","His invisibility would vanish.","And the very instant that happened, the enemy also needed to be dead before they could react or call for help.","Noah breathed in deeply, gathering his focus to a single point.","And then...","SAA!","He released the arrow with perfect form!","His figure flashed into existence as he lost his invisibility, becoming visible for the first time in over an hour. The distant enemy he was targeting raised its head instinctively to sense what had just appeared in its territory.","But the moment its gaze came up to focus on the disturbance, it saw a virulent green arrow right in front of its face!","All of it happened in the span of an instant that was almost too fast to perceive!","The eyes of the creature pulsing with purple lightning barely registered the terrifying verdant arrow before its Way innately erupted outward. A defensive storm of lightning formed around it automatically, responding to the threat.","But the arrow arrived with inexorable purpose.","BOOM!","A terrifying impact rocked the surrounding space with devastating force! Existence in that area was instantly turned a virulent green color for several light-years in every direction!","One could barely see a flicker of purple lightning seeking to erupt and fight back amidst that explosion of poisonous authority. But the Way of Lightning was drowned out completely by the immense expression of Mana and Hunger!","The seas of concentrated authority made it very clear that this Way was much grander in quality and immensity than the Way of Lightning could ever hope to match.","Lightning never stood a chance against the fundamental nature of Mana asserting dominance.","After the explosion faded, there were no roars of defiance or the eruption of more defensive authorities. Only an apocalyptic scene where existence itself in the nearby area seemed to have been poisoned at a fundamental level.","When one looked at the epicenter, they could see the corpse of the massive salamander. Its body still flickered weakly with residual lightning that was fading rapidly.","Its head had been completely pulverized and melted by the impact. The skull was fizzing out of existence as the authority holding it together collapsed.","Its weavings and Way had actually been collapsed entirely by the single strike!","Noah gazed at such a scene in the distance with eyes shining with analytical satisfaction. He lowered the bow and it disappeared into a flicker of brilliance, dissolving back into formless Mana.","He took a single step through compressed space to appear beside the corpse of the salamander. He waved his hand toward it and the entire massive body disappeared into his storage.","And he disappeared right after as well, reintegrating with the surrounding atmosphere and leaving the scene of a glorious kill behind!","In less than a picosecond of actual combat time, he had decimated a creature seeking to advance toward Pre-THE status. He had stored its body for later consumption and left the scene without leaving traces apart from poison painting the surroundings!"]},{"number":4528,"title":"Chapter 4528: Chapter 4527: Predator! V","paragraphs":["In The Infinite Unfurling.","Primordial trees rose far above the landscape, their trunks so massive that they seemed to support the sky itself. Thick mist surrounded them in swirling layers, creating an atmosphere of perpetual twilight between their ancient roots.","In between these towering trees, a massive basilisk-like creature raised its head with predatory focus.","Its serpentine eyes shone with a terrifying green light that seemed to pierce through all concealment. The eyes looked unfathomably far into the distance as if they could observe phenomena occurring light-years away with perfect clarity.","And at this moment, those eyes had locked onto an explosion of poisonous green light erupting in the distance.","The power of that explosion was not insignificant, and its serpentine face twisted into a devilish cruel smile. The creature’s voice echoed out with cold amusement.","\"It looks like I have to stop playing with you and eat you and your Sovereignty in a single gulp,\" it said with casual malice. \"Someone else is hunting in my territory, and I need to deal with them quickly.\"","The creature spoke while looking down at an extremely gory scene spread out before it.","A white fox-like creature could be seen lying in a pool of its own blood. Half of its body had already been eaten, consumed by the basilisk over the course of hours of torture. Its lustrous white coat of fur was painted crimson-gold with blood that still flowed from grievous wounds.","Its gaze was weak but still held defiance as it stared up at the basilisk with hatred burning in its dimming eyes.","But its Way of Light and existence was far too weak compared to the Way of Poison that this basilisk represented. And now, its entire existence was about to be extinguished completely.","The basilisk opened its massive jaws wide to swallow this radiant fox-like creature whole and claim the remnants of its Sovereignty.","And in that exact moment, a verdant green arrow also shining with concentrated Way of Poison appeared directly before the basilisk’s face!","The creature’s eyes opened wide with shock and fury as it seemed to ask a silent question: Who dared to attack it with poison, of all things?! The fucker it just sensed the attack of Gigaparsecs away?!","It tried desperately to erupt with its own Way, to counter poison with poison and assert dominance. But it found its Way of Poison completely suppressed all around its body, unable to manifest properly!","Its existence buzzed with mounting horror as it felt this unfathomable poisonous authority that seemed to hide something else beneath its surface. Something fundamental and overwhelming that completely suppressed its carefully cultivated Sovereignty!","And then that hidden authority collapsed its existence entirely!","BOOM !","The head of the basilisk was torn apart by the impact, exploding into chunks of flesh and bone that disintegrated before they could fall. The creature’s body thrashed once before going still, its Way extinguished.","The heavily injured and half-consumed white fox nearby saw how the explosion contained the destruction in a unique way, preventing the surroundings from being decimated unnecessarily.","A moment later, the fox trembled as the visage of a massive humanoid being shining with green poisonous luster appeared where the arrow had originated!","Of course, this was none other than Noah who had moved with rapid efficiency to claim his second target.","At this moment, Noah waved his hands and the massive corpse of the basilisk disappeared into his storage without ceremony.","Since he had already suppressed and understood the Way of Poison with his first kill, doing so again was even easier this time! After all, it had been confirmed multiple times that his Way of Mana superseded poison-based concepts at the fundamental level.","But now, before he left the scene, he turned his gaze toward the former prey of the basilisk.","A decimated-looking fox lay there, and when Noah’s eyes focused on it, the creature’s body trembled with fear and residual defiance. It whimpered softly, the sound pitiful and weak.","Noah’s terrifying body looked down at the broken creature as he spoke with calm consideration.","\"Now what shall I do with you?\"","The fox trembled violently at his words as its feminine voice echoed out weakly.","\"I... don’t... don’t kill me,\" she pleaded with desperation coloring every word. \"I could... I could act as a mount for sir as soon as I heal! I also know of a place with some good resources a distance from here!\"","Her voice grew stronger with desperate hope.","\"That basilisk was torturing me for information about it! My Light was telling me that even if I revealed the location, it would still devour me anyway. But it feels different with you...\"","She looked up at Noah with eyes that held both fear and strange trust.","\"My Way of Light says sir will keep his word if you make a promise. So please, I can be useful! I can guide you! I can serve! Just...please don’t kill me!\"","Her voice broke at the end, and fresh blood dripped from her wounds. Her remaining fur was matted and filthy, and half her body was simply gone, consumed by the basilisk’s cruel feeding.","She looked utterly pitiful, a broken creature clinging to the last thread of existence.","Oh?","Noah’s eyes lit up with interest at the words of the fox as a thought occurred to him with sudden clarity.","How...would it be if he spread his Civilization in the Infinite Unfurling ? Would he be able to understand exactly what happened in the coming future if he had subordinates present during these ancient times?","He looked at the fox and her pitiful appearance analytically. Since he had to move quickly and could not afford to linger, he made his decision with rapid calculation.","His vision pulsed as information flooded his perception.","|Name: Lumivara, The Radiant Wanderer|","|Classification: Light-Path Entity (Not yet Pre-THE)|","|Complexity: 19 Decillion|","|Purity: 19 Decillion|","|Grand Principles: Illumination Genesis, Photon Propagation, Radiance Manifestation, Light Dominion, Luminous Convergence, Brilliance Authority, Reflection Mastery, Refraction Supremacy|","|Current Sovereignty Progress: Attempting to establish claim over Light (0.11% toward Pre-THE status)|","|Status: Critically injured, half-consumed, near collapse|","|Temperament: Desperate for survival, willing to submit|","|Special Trait: Possesses knowledge of resource-rich locations|","His eyes shone brightly as he gauged the positives and negatives of accepting this creature into his service. After a moment of consideration, he waved his hands to reveal a spark of blue-gold brilliance that floated between them.","\"The Way of Light,\" he said with commanding authority, \"can be exemplified even more after it accepts its true nature as an expression of Mana. Light is electromagnetic radiation, and electromagnetic forces are powered by Mana at their foundation.\"","He looked at her with tyrannical certainty.","\"Take this spark and accept it into your existence. We can then see about your future and whether you have value beyond this moment.\"","The spark floated closer to the fox, pulsing with the fundamental authority of his Civilization.","The fox hesitantly looked at the brilliant spark, her eyes wide with a mixture of hope and fear. This could be salvation or it could be another form of enslavement worse than death.","But she had no real choice, and her Way of Light was telling her that this being would keep his word.","She opened her mouth with trembling jaws and swallowed the spark whole!","The moment it entered her body, her eyes blazed with blue-gold light! The Spark of Mana flooded through her decimated form, and her Way of Light began to transform and elevate!","Her wounds started to close as Noah’s Mana-infused regeneration kicked in, his body shining with light that flowed into her. Her missing half began to slowly regrow, flesh and bone reforming with agonizing slowness.","She gasped as she felt her Sovereignty deepening, her understanding of Light expanding to encompass its fundamental relationship with Mana!","...!","Oh!","An irreversible event stemming from an equally impossible entity.","And who knew just what effects it could have for the future when this creature who should have died was instead elevated and bound to Noah’s Civilization?"]},{"number":4529,"title":"Chapter 4529: Chapter 4528: Lumivara! I","paragraphs":["Possibilities.","In existence, there were many beings who spent obscenely long periods of time wondering what could have been. What of this possibility or that possibility? If only things had happened this way instead of that way.","If only I was born rich. If only I was not poor. If only I was talented instead of mediocre. What could have been if I was born a genius with natural gifts?","There were countless what-ifs and what-could-have-beens that plagued the minds of entities across all of reality. But a concerning pattern emerged when one examined these contemplations closely: most of them focused on the past, on things that nobody had control over anymore.","There were many who were born talentless and poor, seemingly cursed by fate to remain at the bottom. And yet after some time and tremendous effort, some of them turned what little they had and transformed themselves completely.","After years of hard work and relentless focus, the supposedly talentless and poor suddenly became known as geniuses with extremely high levels of wealth and influence.","And those who were born geniuses or rich? Well, reality more often than not dictated that they remained geniuses and rich, building upon the advantages they were given.","But that was just how existence operated.","One should never remain bound by what-ifs and what-could-have-beens. They could change the trajectory of their lives and choose exactly what possibility their existence would take through action and will.","Focus on the now. Focus on what is, not on what could have been.","The past was immutable, but the future remained unwritten.","---","In the Infinite Unfurling.","In a distant region high in the skies, there was a floating mountain that spun slowly while roiling white mist churned below it in hypnotic patterns. On the peak of this mountain, Noah stood looking at the figure of the now fully healed Lumivara, The Radiant Wanderer.","The fox-like creature was magnificent in her restored state. She possessed a single lush tail that curved gracefully behind her, easily as long as her entire body. Her coat of radiant white fur shone with stellar luminescence, each strand seeming to emit its own soft light.","Her eyes were large and expressive, colored a brilliant gold that pulsed with her Way of Light. She stood on four legs with digitigrade paws.","Lumivara approached Noah with nervous energy, her movements both graceful and hesitant.","\"I am Lumivara, The Radiant Wanderer,\" she said with a voice that trembled slightly. \"I follow the Way of Light, seeking to understand illumination in all its forms. I... I also really enjoy watching singularities of light bloom....\"","She shuffled her paws with adorable nervousness.","\"I have traveled across many different regions in my existence, always moving because I was never quite strong enough to claim territory. I once tried to befriend a lightning elemental, but it tried to eat me. I do not like the taste of meat very much, preferring to sustain myself purely on light itself...\"","Noah blinked at this creature with an unfathomable gaze as...why the hell was she saying all this?","Her tail swished with nervous energy.","\"My dream is to one day establish a sanctuary where light can exist in its purest form, untainted by darkness or shadow. A place where all who seek illumination can come and learn. Though... I suppose that is a rather presumptuous dream for someone as weak as me.\"","She looked down with embarrassment at her own admission.","Noah looked at her and shook his head with a calm smile, finding her earnest nervousness somewhat endearing.","Though she did ramble.","\"You mentioned an area that has something good?\" he asked, bringing the conversation back to practical matters.","Lumivara’s ears perked up as she nodded eagerly.","\"Yes! I came across a region filled with blinding light that would even blind Pre-THE Existences if they approached carelessly, of course, not me since I walk The Way of Light...\" she explained with growing confidence as she spoke about her discovery.","\"The entire domain is protected by layers of luminescence so intense that they function as barriers.\"","Her eyes shone with the memory.","\"It cannot even be accessed through normal spatial travel. One must pass through a small invisible wormhole that is almost impossible to detect. The wormhole takes one an extremely far distance across the Infinite Unfurling, far beyond where most would ever venture.\"","She gestured with her paw as if drawing a map in the air.","\"And even after passing through the wormhole, one has to be perceptive to a very unique frequency of light to find and move through a doorway that leads into the actual domain. I can perceive that frequency because of my Way, but most entities would never find it.\"","Her voice dropped to something almost reverent.","\"I personally call this region the Sanctuary of Perpetual Dawn, because the light there feels like an eternal sunrise that never fully arrives.\"","Noah’s eyes radiated brilliant light as he listened to this powerful entity who actually possessed more Complexity and Purity than him. And yet she was nervously talking as if he might devour her at any moment, which was an accurate assessment of their power dynamic despite the numerical difference.","He reflected on this region that she described before asking another critical question.","\"Why did you consider this place so good?\" he asked with interest. \"What value did you find there?\"","Lumivara’s expression became more serious as she replied.","\"Even I could not venture very far into that domain,\" she admitted with slight shame. \"An immense pressure of concentrated light burned all around, becoming more intense the deeper one traveled. The weight of illumination itself became oppressive.\"","She paused before continuing.","\"But in the periphery, in the outer edges of the domain where I could survive, I managed to swallow something that I could only identify as... as an Expressionless Sovereignty. Something that existed without will or consciousness behind it.\"","Her eyes widened with the memory.","\"Whatever I consumed allowed my Way of existence, my own Sovereignty of Light, to advance rapidly! In just a few hours of absorbing materials from the periphery, I made progress that would have taken years elsewhere!\"","Noah’s eyes became sharp and focused as they locked onto this being, causing her to tremble with even more nervous energy under his scrutiny.","\"Why did you leave such a place then?\" he asked with quiet intensity. \"If advancement was so rapid, why abandon it?\"","Lumivara’s ears drooped as she gave her reply with embarrassed honesty.","\"I... I got scared,\" she admitted while looking down. \"I did not sense the aura of a Pre-THE Existence or even any THE Entities within the domain. The place felt completely barren and devoid of signatures from conscious beings.\"","Her tail curled protectively around her body.","\"But I did feel a type of natural power emanating from deep within. Not an entity exactly, but something that could potentially rival or even exceed an entity at the level of THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty .\"","She looked up at Noah with wide eyes.","\"So I fled before whatever that power was could notice me and decide I was an intruder.\"","Noah looked closely at this powerful creature that had actually been scared away from a potentially treasure-rich domain. He sighed quietly and shook his head with mixed feelings.","She claimed that she did not sense an entity with the power of THE , but what she felt seemed to be exactly at that level of potency.","What could it be if not a THE entity?","One possibility was that she was simply wrong, and there was indeed a powerful being residing there who was concealing their presence. In which case, venturing into that domain would be effectively delivering himself to a predator.","But in the case that her words were accurate and there truly was no conscious entity in such a domain, then the outer periphery alone held resources that could allow one to rapidly progress in their Sovereignty.","This could be a unique opportunity that had landed directly in Noah’s lap through fortunate circumstances. He simply needed to be certain enough about the risks involved before attempting to obtain the potential boons of this unknown place.","His eyes flashed with decision as he spoke with commanding certainty.","\"Okay. For now, I need to continue hunting a few more things to strengthen myself further. You said you would serve as my mount, yes? Let us go.\"","Lumivara’s body trembled before she nodded with nervous acceptance. Her form began to enlarge, growing until her figure became almost twice as large as Noah’s current transformed state.","He floated up smoothly and landed on her back, feeling her extremely soft fur beneath him. The texture was like resting on clouds made solid.","He nodded while calmly saying with measured approval, \"Adequate.\"","The body of Lumivara trembled at the simple word of acceptance. Her existence experienced a sudden surge of Mana flowing through their connection, and her Way of Light felt even grander than before!","It was as if she had just become connected to a source of infinite light, a wellspring that would never run dry!","She was utterly astonished by the sensation!","Noah tapped on her body and applied the capability of Ambient Integration to both of them. Their figures began to meld with the surrounding space, becoming invisible to standard perception.","He tapped on her flank again and said simply, \"Let us go.\"","...!","The newly formed partnership of the impossible anomaly and the radiant wanderer began to move through the Infinite Unfurling with purpose!"]},{"number":4530,"title":"Chapter 4530: Chapter 4529: Lumivara! II","paragraphs":["\"Stay still, okay?\"","Noah voiced out calmly while sitting comfortably on Lumivara, who nodded with intense concentration as she looked out into the distance.","She had been following his directions precisely as he guided them toward an entity that possessed at least double or triple her power and advancement in the Way of existence. And it seemed that he was about to attack it from this extreme range?","Was this exactly how he had taken out that cruel basilisk who had been torturing her?","Noah stood up on the lustrous fur of Lumivara and breathed in deeply, gathering his focus. This time, he did not form a bow as he had done previously.","Instead, he raised his hand backward in a stance designed for throwing, and in his palm, a radiant and blinding spear began to form from compressed authority.","His target this time was a fiery beetle that resided in the depths of a distant volcanic mountain. The creature was massive, easily the size of a city, with a carapace of black obsidian that glowed with veins of molten fire running across its surface.","Six legs ended in claws that could tear through mountains, and mandibles large enough to crush continents clicked together with anticipation of its next meal. Flames wreathed its entire body in a corona of heat that would vaporize weaker beings.","Noah had already observed it carefully and determined it possessed 88 Decillion Complexity and Purity, following the Way of Fire with dedicated focus.","As he prepared to throw the spear, Noah spoke with calm certainty that Lumivara could hear clearly.","\"I have already superseded the Way of Fire,\" he said. \"Fire is merely accelerated molecular motion powered by Mana at its foundation. Facing it again after understanding this fundamental truth is nothing significant.\"","WAA!","After he said this with absolute confidence, Noah threw the blinding spear with perfect form!","The projectile was masked to appear as a poisonous verdant work of art, maintaining his disguise. It crossed the immense distance in less than an instant, moving at speeds that defied conventional perception!","The spear struck the distant beetle before the creature could even register the attack, much less raise any defenses!","Lumivara watched with shocked expression as The Way of Fire surrounding that powerful entity, an entity three times grander than herself in raw power, was shockingly suppressed completely!","The beetle’s defenses collapsed as if they had never existed, and its body was torn apart by the impact! The fire that composed its essence was devoured by the superior claim of Mana asserting dominance!","Collapsed in a single instant!","Lumivara was utterly astonished at this display as her eyes trembled with shock mixed with a growing sense of fear. She felt the indomitable entity sitting calmly above her, who proceeded to wave his hand casually.","Noah opened his jaws unnaturally wide, and the distant body of the beetle was pulled forward through compressed space! It disappeared entirely into his mouth as he consumed it without ceremony!","And then calmly, as if nothing remarkable had occurred, Noah breathed out slowly and sat back down on Lumivara’s soft fur.","\"Alright, let us keep going,\" he said with measured satisfaction.","Lumivara felt her existence integrate with the surrounding environment again as Noah applied Ambient Integration to both of them. She began to move as directed, but her head kept turning slightly as she replayed the complete decimation of that powerful beetle again and again in her mind.","After a few moments of traveling in awed silence, she worked up the courage to speak nervously.","\"Um... how should I properly address Sir?\" she asked with cute hesitation. \"I do not wish to be disrespectful by using the wrong title.\"","Noah patted her fur gently and replied simply, \"The Master is adequate.\"","Lumivara’s voice trembled slightly as she continued with rambling nervousness.","\"Then I thank The Master profusely for not striking me down like you did that terrible basilisk and that powerful beetle!\" she said with genuine gratitude mixed with lingering fear.","\"You know... I probably would not even taste good if you decided to consume me.\"","Her voice became more desperate as she tried to convince him.","\"My meat may even be completely inedible and tasteless...I have heard from others that fox-type creatures like myself are stringy and unpleasant, with fur that gets stuck in teeth and a gamey flavor that is quite disagreeable...I would truly not worth the effort of consuming!\"","As Lumivara rambled on with increasingly desperate justifications for why she should not be eaten, Noah sighed with mild exasperation and patted her reassuringly.","\"Relax, I will not eat you,\" he said with calm certainty.","Lumivara sighed with visible relief at such clear words of reassurance.","But before she could fully settle her nerves, she felt Noah smiling devilishly above her as he added with dark amusement, \"Why would I eat something with so much fur and so little actual meat? I would need to fatten you up substantially first.\"","His words caused her figure to tremble with renewed alarm!","But when she craned her neck to see his expression and caught sight of his devilish smile, she sighed with tentative relief. He was joking. He must be joking, right?","Right?","Regardless of the ridiculous anxious thoughts running through Lumivara’s mind, Noah continued to calmly direct her where to travel as he planned to hunt down as many entities trying to lay claim over Sovereignties as he could manage!","As he crossed through the Infinite Unfurling with methodical efficiency, prompts bloomed before his vision with accumulated progress.","|Total Complexity Gained: 46 Decillion|","|Total Purity Gained: 46 Decillion|","| THE Organ of Civilization Progress: 0.89% toward THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty|","|Unquantifiable Units of Everything 15/16(Regeneration continuing)|","Noah looked at the accumulated details and nodded with satisfaction. His progress continued to be rapid and substantial!","At this rate, he would advance significantly before Tor even finished his battle with THE Time Surfer and her reinforcements.","—","An unknown number of Gigaparsecs away from Noah’s current position.","An entity stood suspended in the air, humanoid in basic shape but clearly not normal. A flower of blinding light grew from the crown of her head, its petals constantly shifting and reforming in patterns of pure luminescence.","She was an entity at the level of Pre-THE, with The Way of Light surrounding her brilliantly in cascading waves of illumination.","And she was one of the dozen Pre-THE existences who had been tasked with searching for The Anomaly to bring it back to THE Time Surfer!","At this moment, she blinked with sudden alertness as she felt something unexpected. She sensed another entity attempting to lay claim over the Sovereignty of Light, the signature flaring briefly before it disappeared as if suppressed or extinguished.","This caused her eyes to flicker with intense interest and curiosity.","Another Light-path entity in this region?","This Pre-THE entity adjusted her trajectory and began moving toward the direction where she had sensed that brief signature!","Perhaps this was connected to the Anomaly she sought, or perhaps it was simply another opportunity to strengthen herself by consuming a competitor.","Either way, it warranted an investigation!"]},{"number":4531,"title":"Chapter 4531: Chapter 4530: Chase! I","paragraphs":["The variations of Mana were unique in their versatility and applications.","With every Way he superseded and defeated, he could seamlessly mimic it as perfectly as the original. At this time, Noah stood atop Lumivara as his massive Early Creature body was maintained, but instead of the poisonous green brilliance he had been displaying, The Way of Existence he now expressed was that of crackling purple lightning arcing across his entire form!","He had killed and devoured six entities so far since being separated from Tor. Two had followed the Way of Poison, two the Way of Fire, one the Way of Mass, and one the Way of Lightning.","And his Primus Mana continued to become all that much more versatile as he could seamlessly mimic any of these Ways with complete authenticity.","Lumivara was genuinely astonished as she looked up at him from her position and asked with curious confusion, \"Master, is your Way that of Mana, or Poison, or Lightning? You seem to shift between them so easily.\"","Noah replied with calm certainty, \" Yes.\"","Lumivara blinked with incomprehension at such a simple answer.","\"What does that mean, Master?\" she asked with adorable confusion.","Noah replied calmly as he gazed ahead at his next target in the distance, a massive behemoth-like creature that resembled a wooly mammoth of titanic proportions.","\"The spark you consumed showed you Mana and how your Light could be ever so glorious through proper understanding of its foundation,\" he explained with teaching patience. \"My Mana can observe and mimic other Ways because I only follow Mana at its core, but I am also potentially following Everything since Mana has infinite variations and expressions.\"","His reply carried terrifying implications as he focused his perception on the 88 Decillion Mammoth in the distance. The creature pulsed with the Way of Defense, its entire existence dedicated to becoming impenetrable.","Noah observed analytically how this was a unique conceptual Way rather than an elemental one. Defense as an abstract principle rather than a physical manifestation.","So he chose to express Lightning for this encounter specifically for an extremely quick and penetrative result against this enemy.","And he could have chosen to manifest a bow or spear as the delivery mechanism for his long-range strike as he had done before. But he had more variations available to explore, and he could always try newer applications of his versatile Mana!","So he looked down at the visage of Lumivara beneath him and asked with measured curiosity, \"What do you think for something designed for long-range devastation? A bow? A spear? A sniper rifle? Or perhaps a ballista? A nuclear warhead?\"","Lumivara blinked with confusion at several of those terms.","\"I am not familiar with some of those weapons, Master,\" she admitted honestly. \"But the ballista seems interesting from how you said it?\"","Noah smiled at her words. There were many applications of Mana he could experiment with in the future, weapons and tools from his memories of the blue planet and beyond.","But for now, he would indulge her curiosity.","A massive ballista began to form in the air above Lumivara, materializing from compressed lightning-infused Mana! The weapon was easily twice Noah’s current transformed size and pulsed dangerously with concentrated purple arcs of electricity that crackled with lethal intent.","Noah made a deliberate pulling motion with his hands, and a terrifying oversized arrow formed on the ballista. He poured immense waves of his Way of Mana and Hunger into the projectile, compressing it further and further.","He already had the True Expression of The Sovereignty of Mana and Hunger active from consuming an Unquantifiable Unit of Everything, so the arrow blazed with overwhelming authority!","Below him, Lumivara’s eyes shone with awe and genuine marvel as she watched this terrifying weapon being prepared for release!","Noah looked at the distant mammoth with coldness as he spoke.","\"Mana is the foundation of all interactions and changes in existence,\" he said with tyrannical certainty. \"Defense is merely the resistance to change, the attempt to maintain a static state against external forces. But resistance requires energy, and that energy comes from Mana itself.\"","His eyes gleamed.","\"So how can Defense powered by Mana ever truly stop an attack that asserts Mana’s dominion over that very defense? The defender. is using my foundation against me, which means I simply need to reclaim what is mine.\"","His logic was absolute in its confidence.","\"And Hunger consumes all things, including the concept of protection itself. Defense cannot stand against the combination of these truths.\"","HUUM !","Then he released the ballista bolt!","The seemingly impenetrable massive Mammoth came to sudden attention as it sensed the incoming threat. Its body immediately shone with a brilliant bronze glow of concentrated defensive power, layers upon layers of protection manifesting instantly!","The creature had survived this long by making itself nearly invulnerable, and its instincts activated perfectly.","But it did not matter.","BOOM!","The ballista arrow struck with apocalyptic force! The purple lightning-infused projectile punched straight through the bronze defensive layers as if they were paper!","The Mammoth’s body was shot through and through, a massive hole carved from front to back! Crimson-gold blood spurted out in torrents as the creature’s Way of Defense collapsed entirely!","Noah looked at the scene with cold satisfaction as he already opened his jaw unnaturally wide. He beckoned toward the massive corpse, and it flew toward him through compressed space to be consumed!","Lumivara watched with cheerful excitement as her Master claimed another victory!","\"The Master is very strong! The Master is the best!\" she said with genuine enthusiasm. \"Nothing could possibly take you down when you fight with such overwhelming-\"","Before she could even finish such words of praise, both her and Noah’s expressions rapidly changed as they sensed something approaching!","HUUM !","Near them, a glimmer of white brilliance flared with sudden intensity! An entity radiating ecstatic power at the Pre-THE level appeared, materializing from concealment!","Her gaze was cold and callous as she looked at Noah and the fox he was mounted on with contempt and disdain!","In the picosecond where the Ambient Integration had been disrupted while Noah was decimating his enemy, a creature at Pre-THE had found their location!","Noah’s gaze became ice-cold as he recognized this entity immediately. She was one of the twelve Pre-THE existences that THE Time Surfer had brought with her, one of those actively hunting for him!","But she should in no way be able to recognize him in his current disguised state as...","The Pre-THE existence spoke with contemptuous disgust in her voice.","\"I was wondering what that flickering Sovereignty of Light I sensed earlier was,\" she said while looking directly at Lumivara with hatred. \"It seems to be a pathetic thing with no backbone that is acting as a mount for another? How utterly disgraceful.\"","Her eyes blazed with righteous fury.","\"Let me put you out of your fucking misery. A creature like you does not deserve to walk The Way of Light!\"","HUUM!","The moment she said such words with absolute conviction, this being of utterly terrible power that Noah was not ready for and could not currently decimate made her move!","She was at the level of Pre-THE Existences with her Sovereignty much more established than the creatures Noah had been hunting. She had made tremendous progress toward THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty!","A status sheet flashed before Noah’s vision with alarming details.","|Name: Stellara, The Radiant Executioner|","|Classification: Light-Path Pre-THE Existence|","|Complexity: 997 Decillion|","|Purity: 997 Decillion|","|Grand Principles: Luminous Annihilation, Photonic Supremacy, Radiance Manifestation, Blinding Authority, Light Convergence, Brilliance Dominion, Purification Mastery, Illumination Genesis|","| Current Sovereignty Progress: 12.7% toward THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty|","|Status: Hostile - Intent to Kill|","Such a being erupted with imposing brilliance toward Noah and Lumivara!","And beneath Noah, Lumivara’s entire body trembled with primal terror as she recognized the power difference!"]},{"number":4532,"title":"Chapter 4532: Chapter 4531: Chase! II","paragraphs":["Light.","At its most fundamental level, light was electromagnetic radiation traveling through space as both wave and particle. Photons carrying energy across the void, moving at speeds that conventional understanding deemed absolute.","But that was merely surface understanding.","Light was also information made visible. The ability to observe and perceive one’s surroundings through electromagnetic interaction. It revealed truths while creating shadows that concealed them. It could be gentle warmth or searing devastation depending on concentration.","And at the deepest level, light was simply energy...Mana manifesting as electromagnetic force.","Which meant it could be understood and superseded.","When it came to Light as a Way of Existence, Noah had already superseded this path through his connection with Lumivara. Through the spark of Mana she had consumed, through observing how Light connected to his fundamental Way, he had gained understanding that allowed him to exert influence over this Sovereignty.","This was why even though a terrifying Pre-THE Existence had appeared with murderous intent, he did not consider the situation catastrophic. His Way of Mana and Hunger could exert tremendous effect against Light, even if the enemy was extremely advanced in her Sovereignty.","So the moment Stellara erupted with her Way, Noah responded.","Tendrils of purple lightning exploded from his body, but he was not forming anything long-ranged or close-ranged. Instead, he manifested extremely compressed concentrations of The True Expression of The Sovereignty of Mana and Hunger contained inside a weapon of mass destruction.","The concept of a nuclear warhead, reimagined through his Way.","A radiant purple statue materialized between them and Stellara. The statue resembled a rotund version of Noah’s current form with an enormous belly pulsing with compressed authority. Its expression mixed devilish malevolence with benevolent serenity, like some corrupted entity containing obliteration within stillness.","The statue’s eyes opened as white light washed over it.","And then it detonated.","This time, Noah was not containing the damage. He would unleash devastation without restraint!","BOOOOOOM!","The explosion was apocalyptic in scale. A sphere of purple lightning-infused Mana expanded outward with violent force, fracturing reality around the epicenter. The shockwave propagated for light-years in every direction, distorting space and shattering matter.","The two sides were pushed violently apart. Mountains crumbled, ancient trees disintegrated, and the ground collapsed into nothingness.","Noah patted Lumivara’s fur with measured urgency as he spoke. \"Run far and run fast. Do not look back.\"","...!","Lumivara’s body transformed into pure light as she activated her Way to its fullest extent. Her form became almost intangible, moving at speeds approaching theoretical maximum of the very idea speed!","She was light! She was speed!","WAA!","Behind them, Stellara emerged from the dissipating explosion with shock transforming into fury.","\"You would flee from judgment?\" she called out, her voice carrying weight that pressed against existence.","She began a pursuit with terrifying determination!","Her body became wreathed in white brilliance so intense it seemed to burn away the space around her. She launched forward with speed that would have overtaken any normal Light-path entity instantly.","But Lumivara was no longer normal.","\"Master!\" Lumivara said with controlled tension. \"Her Sovereignty is too developed! I cannot...\"","Noah remained calm, his hands glowing with concentrated Mana that he channeled directly into Lumivara’s existence.","\"Your Light is no longer solely yours,\" he said with measured certainty. \"It is amplified by Mana’s infinite reservoir. Draw on what I provide without reservation.\"","Lumivara felt the surge of power- a surge of an utterly glorious Way of Existence flooding through her and her speed increased dramatically. Her Way of Light became supercharged by Noah’s contribution, surpassing her absolute limits.","Behind them, Stellara roared with frustration as the distance refused to close!","She was a Pre-THE Existence chasing weaker entities that barely had ties to their Sovereignties! What the fuck was this?!","They crossed through a region of floating crystalline formations that refracted light in dizzying patterns. Lumivara wove through them with instinctive grace while Stellara smashed through them with brute force, creating explosions of shattered crystal.","\"You are merely delaying the inevitable,\" Stellara roared with cold certainty. \"I have dedicated my existence to purifying the Way of Light from those unworthy to walk it!\"","HUUM!","Noah glanced back with calculating eyes and spoke calmly to Lumivara.","\"Continue as is,\" he said. \"Take us toward that wormhole you mentioned. The passage leading to your Sanctuary of Perpetual Dawn.\"","Lumivara’s eyes widened with shock.","\"Master, that domain holds immense unknown dangers...\" she said while continuing to run. \"Are you...sure?\"","Noah’s voice carried absolute command. \"She will pursue regardless of direction. At least in that domain, there may be variables we can exploit. Go.\"","Lumivara hesitated briefly before complying. If The Master commanded it, she would obey.","Mana and Light burned together gloriously as their figures radiated a profound purple white luster- especially the royal tyrannical purple as Noah kept the way of Lightning circling around him!","They crossed vast regions in compressed moments, traveling distances that would require even the Dukes of Living Existences in the current era days to traverse!","Through primordial forests, over mountains scraping the atmosphere, across valleys filled with mist concealing ancient dangers!","Across the murky and misty regions of The Infinite Unfurling, Stellara pursued relentlessly, her white brilliance a constant presence!","\"You disgrace everything Light represents with your cowardice!\" she said with righteous conviction. \"If you possessed even a fragment of worthiness, you would stand and face judgment rather than scurrying like vermin!\"","Noah remained calm as every now and then, he would stand atop Lumivara and throw back a radiant purple spear or a warhead, eventually forming an illusory bow to manifest behind him as it released bursts of purple mixed with white of His Way and The Way of Light!","All of it...infuriated and slowed down Stellara to no end.","Until minutes later, after having to utilize multiple Unquantifiable Units of Everything...","They approached a region where space shimmered with subtle distortion. Lumivara’s eyes locked onto a specific point that appeared empty to standard perception.","\"There, Master. The wormhole entrance,\" she said with desperate hope.","Noah’s perception focused on the location and he could barely detect the spatial anomaly. It was extraordinarily well-concealed, almost invisible even to his enhanced senses.","Lumivara did not decelerate as they approached. Instead, she accelerated harder.","\"Master, maintain your grip,\" she warned.","And then they plunged into the wormhole.","HUUM!","Reality twisted around them in configurations defying understanding. Space compressed and expanded simultaneously. They were moving forward and backward and sideways all at once!","The sensation lasted both an eternity and a single instant before they emerged in a completely different region.","Lumivara’s eyes blazed with focus as she searched for the specific frequency of light that would reveal the true entrance.","\"Master, I need to isolate the exact wavelength,\" she said with strained concentration. \"It shifts across temporal and light intervals and I need to... there!\"","Her perception locked onto a unique oscillation invisible to standard observation. A doorway that existed only for those who understood precisely where to look.","A point of brilliant light.","She adjusted trajectory and passed through the frequency barrier.","POP!","The world transformed with jarring immediacy.","And Noah felt...an eruption of brilliance that caused his existence to pulse with euphoria!","They found themselves in a domain where light existed in its purest form. Brilliance blazed from every direction with intensity that would blind lesser beings permanently.","Even Noah’s eyes were acclimatint to be able to clearly see in this region of blinding light!","A sense pressure was immediate and oppressive, pushing down on their existences with crushing force.","\"Master, we have entered the Sanctuary of Perpetual Dawn,\" Lumivara said with voice strained by effort. \"I can only sustain my position in the outer periphery. Venturing deeper would be catastrophic for me. And that savage woman may or may not discover thst unique frequency of light as it took me some time, so we may only have a few minutes here!\"","...!","Lumivara spoke with urgency.","Noah looked around with analytical fascination despite the dangerous circumstances. The domain...was unlike anything he had encountered!"]},{"number":4533,"title":"Chapter 4533: Chapter 4532: The Distraught and The Defiant! I","paragraphs":["As soon as Noah entered the domain, his entire existence began buzzing with recognition and absorption as the environment proved to be extraordinarily nutrient rich.","Nutrient rich was not even adequate to describe what he was experiencing. It felt like a singular natal component of existence was present here in its most pure and concentrated form, and his body was continuously drinking it in without conscious effort.","Even more interesting was the fact that every single particle of this atmospheric authority that flowed into him was traveling directly into THE Organ of Civilization.","Directly into his head where that unfathomable wonder that had not existed in Observable Existence before his design of it continued to rotate with increasing intensity.","As it drank in this glorious authority with ravenous efficiency, Noah’s eyes seemingly adjusted to the blinding radiance little by little. The first thing that he could perceive clearly was the emergence of prompts blooming before his vision.","| You have arrived in THE Northern Unfurling Node of Existence of THE Creature|","|Classification: Ancient Sealed Domain|","|Primary Function: Concentration and preservation of THE Civilizational Authority|","|Environmental Characteristics: Authority at the level of THE becomes trapped within this domain and concentrates in increasingly high density the further inward one travels.|","|Natural Phenomenon: These dense concentrations of pure THE Civilizational Authority can crystallize and form into natural treasures of immense value.|","|Pressure Mechanics: The atmospheric authority naturally generates pressure befitting its concentrated nature. Entities below THE scale will experience increasing difficulty sustaining existence the deeper they venture.|","|Warning: This domain operates under principles designed by THE Creature for purposes unknown.|","|Current Location: Outer Periphery (Lowest concentration zone)|","...!","Noah’s eyes opened wide with surprise at such a terrifying array of knowledge being revealed.","THE Northern Unfurling Node of Existence of THE Creature.","Northern meant there were at least three other places exactly like this one scattered across the Infinite Unfurling. Possibly more.","And what was terrifying enough was these domains having Unfurling in their name alongside the direct distinction of belonging to THE Creature . As if this entire construct had been designed and built by THE Creature for specific purposes.","What the hell was this place actually meant to accomplish?","Noah’s eyes remained stern and analytical as the surroundings became slightly more clear while his existence continued to passively absorb what should be an extremely pure and concentrated form of THE Civilizational Authority.","The region he could now observe was actually quite beautiful in its simplicity.","A halo of brilliant white light covered everything like a gentle blanket, creating an atmosphere of perpetual dawn. Before him stretched a serene landscape of lush grasslands dotted with flowers that swayed despite there being no wind. Floating landmasses hovered above the ground, each one pulsing with ecstatic authority that resonated through space.","The entire place actually looked surprisingly empty and not overly complex in its construction. Apart from this area of grassland and the few floating landmasses, there were only scattered trees rising here and there. But each tree radiated terrifying levels of concentrated authority that made them seem almost alive with purpose.","That was everything he could currently perceive in this outer region.","But this was clearly only the periphery of something much larger.","When his eyes tracked further inward toward the center, he saw another distinct ring of white light that seemed to mark the boundary into a much more concentrated domain. His vision did not extend beyond that luminous barrier, as if his perception was being actively blocked.","He would have to physically pass the line that distinguished the outer periphery from the inner regions for him to be capable of seeing and perceiving what truly lay inside of this terrifying place known as THE Northern Unfurling Node of Existence of THE Creature.","But as he was observing and thinking analytically about all of this information...","BOOM!","His existence buzzed with sudden intensity as he felt THE Organ of Civilization in his head reach a significant milestone while it was crazily absorbing the atmospheric authority around them.","New prompts flashed before his vision.","| THE Organ of Civilization Progress: 1% toward THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty|","|Unquantifiable Units of Everything: 11/20 (Regeneration continuing)|","| THE Organ of Civilization has reached an important developmental threshold.|","|Progress Status: One hundredth of the way toward complete establishment of THE Surface Depth.|","|Advancement Unlocked: The Unquantifiable Units of Everything produced by THE Organ of Civilization have been refined and quantified.|","|New Classification: THE Rudimentary Units of Everything|","|Effect: Units now possess defined properties and applications rather than purely conceptual existence.|","THE Rudimentary Units of Everything.","Oh!","Noah looked at this unique distinction with analytical interest as he examined the mobius strips of wonder that floated within his existence. The transformation from unquantifiable to rudimentary was progress toward something more refined.","Another prompt materialized with defining information.","|THE RUDIMENTARY UNITS OF EVERYTHING|","|Classification: Nascent form of ultimate authority currency|","|Nature: Concentrated essence of civilizational potential that can be applied to any concept, principle, or expression of existence.|","|Current Capabilities: Can fuel THE True Expression of Sovereignty. Can accelerate growth of THE Organ of Civilization. Can be consumed to temporarily enhance any aspect of existence.|","|Limitations: Rudimentary nature means efficiency is lower than more refined versions. Maximum storage capacity currently limited to 20 units.|","|Progression Path: Will evolve into more potent forms as THE Organ of Civilization deepens.|","|Note: These units represent the foundation of something.|","Noah looked at the detailed information with eyes shining with Quintessence. His progress was accelerating faster than he had anticipated!","Nearby, the figure of Lumivara underwent a startling transformation as her body shifted from into a humanoid shape.","She appeared as a young woman with delicate features and pale skin that seemed to glow with inner light. Her hair was long and white with an almost liquid quality, flowing down her back like starlight given form.","Fox ears protruded from the top of her head, twitching with nervous energy. A single lush fox tail emerged from the base of her spine, swaying gently.","She wore simple white robes that seemed to be woven from light itself, and her golden eyes looked around with an expression of complete awe.","\"Master, what is happening to me?\" she asked with wonder coloring her voice. \"When I came here before, I could only gain power and advance my Sovereignty by venturing slightly further inward and plucking fruits from those trees over there.\"","She gestured toward the scattered trees pulsing with authority.","\"But now it seems my body is innately attracting the atmospheric authority without any effort on my part. Is this because of... Master’s Mana connected to my existence?\"","...!"]},{"number":4534,"title":"Chapter 4534: Chapter 4533: The Distraught and The Defiant! II","paragraphs":["Lumivara had revealed a shocking piece of information through her observation.","The reason Noah was able to freely absorb the surrounding atmosphere was potentially due to his own grand Way and how it related to everything as foundational authority. And through their connection, Lumivara was benefiting from the same principle.","There was clearly much to learn about this place and exactly how much of an opportunity all of this represented. But before he could truly delve into investigation and exploration...","BOOM!","Space behind them squeezed and compressed violently before spitting something else through the frequency barrier.","The visage of none other than Stellara appeared with an expression of absolute fury written across her luminous features. Her eyes locked onto Noah and Lumivara with murderous intent that needed no verbal expression!","Lumivara immediately moved to hide behind Noah’s transformed body, her earlier confidence evaporating in the face of this overwhelming threat.","But at this moment, Noah did not run from the Pre-THE Existence. Nor did he erupt with any defensive authority or prepare offensive measures.","He simply looked at the figure before him with calm analytical assessment as a thought occurred to him.","Pre-THE was still partly at the level of THE, correct? The designation itself suggested they had one foot in that realm even if not fully established.","Which meant...","A moment after he had such a thought, the figure of Stellara opened her mouth to begin bellowing threats and condemnation.","But in the next instant, something shocking occurred.","HUUM!","Space above her seemingly squeezed and compressed with invisible force. In a shocking flow of events that Stellara had anticipated, the glorious and deadly authority that composed this Pre-THE being’s power began to be forcefully drawn out of her body!","Her Sovereignty was being absorbed directly into the surrounding atmosphere.","Stellara’s eyes widened with horror as she felt her carefully cultivated authority being stripped away without her consent or ability to resist.","And Noah watched with cold eyes as the domain did exactly what the prompts had warned it would do!","It trapped and concentrated authority at the level of THE.","And apparently, it did not distinguish between fully established THE entities and those who were deemed as Pre-THE!","Oh!","Losing one’s power... was never something to take lightly.","It was akin to a billionaire watching their portfolio and seeing hundreds of millions rapidly evaporating every second without being able to do anything to stop the hemorrhaging losses.","It was akin to a king who ruled multiple continents watching his dominion being carved apart and taken by foreign conquerors, as his harem of women was divided among different victors as spoils of war.","It was absolutely not a pleasant experience under any circumstances.","And Stellara felt this reality with crushing intimacy at this precise moment as Noah observed her shockingly losing her designation as a Pre-THE Existence.","His perceptive eyes analyzed the situation rapidly as on her status sheet, he actually witnessed her Current Sovereignty Progress that had been at 12.7% toward THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty begin to rapidly decrease. It only slowed its decline after dropping below the 10% threshold.","And then, on her status sheet, her designation actually lost the Pre-THE Existence classification entirely!","Ten percent.","Was this the marker that one had to surpass toward THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty before they could be considered a Pre-THE Existence? A hard boundary that separated the truly progressed from those merely attempting the path?","And did this also equate to the same percentage threshold that he had observed for the completion of THE Organ of Civilization? If he reached 10% completion with it, he would be considered a Pre-THE Existence?","He filed these observations away in the back of his mind for further contemplation later. For now, he looked at the figure of Stellara who appeared as if she had lost her very heart and soul.","And truly, she had lost something equivalently devastating.","Her Way that she had worked so extraordinarily hard to cultivate had effectively been reduced to a fraction of its former power by this domain’s mechanisms.","And now, even though she was still unfathomably more powerful than Noah in raw statistics...","Noah began walking toward her with measured steps as his eyes flashed with an extremely tyrannical and quintessential light.","\"Hey, it looks like you have run into some rather unfortunate circumstances,\" he said with dark satisfaction coloring his words. \"Allow me to lend you a helping hand in your time of need.\"","As he spoke with false sympathy, he burned another Rudimentary Unit of Everything. His existence began to radiate profound and glorious luster as THE True Expression of The Sovereignty of Mana and Hunger activated once more, and after the revent advancement of THE Organ of Civilization , this state felt stronger than ever!","He...was truly getting stronger!","He threw his hand back in a familiar motion and formed a tyrannical purple spear of concentrated lightning. Without hesitation, he hurled it toward the distraught Stellara who had just lost a catastrophic chunk of her carefully cultivated power.","Take care of this enemy first, and then he could fully enjoy and explore this terrifying place that he had stumbled into by fortunate accident. This place that bore the name of THE Creature in its very designation!","---","The past was the past and the present was the present.","The changes made in the past would not manifest their effects in the future until the one making these alterations actually returned to their original timeline.","Because as of this moment, nothing was truly set in stone. If an entity traveled into the past and perished there, one could legitimately wonder how the paradox of temporal causality would be resolved. When it came to time and its manipulation, there were far too many intricacies and variables to account for.","But at this moment, an unfathomably far distance of time past the Infinite Unfurling, in the current era that Noah had originated from...","In a domain that could not be found in The Folds or The Wandering Territories. In a space between spaces where normal rules of reality did not fully apply.","In that unique domain where the figures of Sigrid and Noah used to sit beside one another on opposite sides of the veil, there now remained only THE Dead Order and Sigrid!"]},{"number":4535,"title":"Chapter 4535: Chapter 4534: The Distraught and The Defiant! III","paragraphs":["At this moment, Sigrid was actually alone on her side of the translucent barrier. On the other side of the veil, the radiant wall of Order that had been veiling and shielding THE Dead Order from direct observation actually began to fade away with deliberate purpose.","This glorious entity seated upon her throne of compressed authority looked directly at Sigrid with a calculating assessment.","She observed the situation closely, noting how Sigrid sat alone at this moment. Her eyes shone with sharp ingenuity as she spoke with measured curiosity.","\" He disappeared rather abruptly, did he not?\" THE Dead Order said with false concern. \" I sincerely doubt he would ever voluntarily leave you here alone with me given his protective nature. So tell me, could he simply not handle the curse of THE Living Elemental any longer? Did something catastrophic happen to him that forced his departure?\"","She asked such a pivotal question with the tone of someone already knowing the answer.","Sigrid’s expression remained composed as she replied with cold certainty.","\" You witnessed him handling those flames perfectly well before ,\" she said without emotion. \" Is it because you are personally so weak yourself that after feeling them briefly upon your own existence, you would automatically assume that he would not be able to survive their effects? No, he is not nearly as weak-willed as you have proven yourself to be.\"","THE Dead Order laughed with genuine amusement at the response.","\" Haha, nice attempt at deflection, you dirtied whore of a vessel, \" she said with condescension dripping from every word. \" No, he would not leave you here alone with me under normal circumstances. He clearly favors you far too much for such carelessness.\"","Her expression became more serious as she continued.","\" You see, those are precisely the types of entanglements that inevitably arise when one desecrates the principles of Order. You form these attachments, these emotional entanglements that do nothing but lead directly to Chaos and instability. To the point where one’s existence would physically ache for another’s presence.\"","She rose slowly from her throne.","\"It is so widespread across all of existence that one of the most powerful Living Existences has built their entire power structure based purely on emotions and their manipulation. All because of pathetic little creatures like you who do not possess adequate control over your feelings and impulses.\"","Her words were biting and cold as ice as she began walking toward the veil separating them.","\" And precisely because of those feelings, because of those debilitating emotions that cloud judgment, I will graciously offer you a way out of your predicament, \" she said with false benevolence. \" I possess the capability to help him properly manage those cursed flames as he wanted before they inevitably consume him and cause complete collapse.\"","She gestured to herself.","\" Look at me now, child. The flames that he so foolishly spread onto my existence when we touched... I have successfully taken care of them completely. It required slightly more of my accumulated power than I would have preferred to expend, but it was manageable nonetheless.\"","Her eyes gleamed with predatory intent.","\"I can perform the exact same service for your dear Osmont. So let us strike a mutually beneficial deal here and now. Trade... yourself to save him from certain death.\"","BOOM!","Sigrid’s eyes flashed sharply at these manipulative words as THE Dead Order continued her proposition.","\" Simply come over and cross to this side of the veil and give yourself willingly to me ,\" she said while extending her hand in invitation. \" And I will make a binding promise on my very existence and on Order itself that I will not bring harm to your Osmont or to the nascent flicker of his Civilization.\"","Her voice became almost tender.","\" Come and fuse with me completely. Become one with the grander and infinitely greater power of pure Order, and let me help both you and your Osmont survive THE Loom’s machinations. Come, child. Let us put all of this past conflict behind us and move forward together. Come to Ama.\"","THE Dead Order spoke such words while extending her hand outward in an inviting fashion that appeared almost maternal in its gesture.","Sigrid floated closer and closer toward the veil with a complex expression playing across her features. Her movements were slow and deliberate as if she was genuinely considering the offer being presented.","She stopped directly in front of the translucent barrier and reached out with her hand. Her fingers came to rest gently upon the surface of the veil.","THE Dead Order looked at her with grand anticipation building in her ancient eyes.","\" Just a few more steps, child ,\" she encouraged with barely concealed eagerness. \" Cross over and unfathomable glory will be yours. You will have survived The Fallout that would destroy so much. You will have transcended your current limitations.\"","HUUM!","At such a critical moment, Sigrid’s expression shifted into a genuine smile.","\"I wanted to come by real close to you,\" she said with calm satisfaction, \"to tell you something important.\"","She paused for effect.","\" No.\"","BOOM!","Her singular word of absolute rejection caused the expression of THE Dead Order to transform from anticipation to something exceedingly cold and utterly apathetic.","Sigrid continued speaking.","\"He does not appreciate sacrifices made on his behalf,\" she said with conviction resonating through every syllable. \"He keeps expressing this preference time and time again, to the point where you would think existence itself would finally understand the message he is sending.\"","Her eyes blazed with defiant determination.","\"But apparently not. So let me make this abundantly clear: No sacrifices will be made. And if you have truly taken care of the curse of THE Living Elemental as you claim...\"","HUUM!","Sigrid clenched her fist with decisive action. In the next moment, a massive river of Order began flowing from THE Dead Order’s side directly toward her position. The siphoning process that she had voluntarily stopped earlier was now returned with even grander intensity than before.","THE Dead Order looked at this development with extremely cold and apathetic eyes. She did not immediately issue any threats or even speak at all for several long seconds.","As if she was simply taking in the full measure of Sigrid’s figure and committing this moment of defiance to eternal memory.","The silence stretched uncomfortably before she finally spoke with a measured tone.","\" You have lost your protector, \" she said with clinical observation. \" While he is currently incapable of intervening or may have even collapsed entirely from the curse of THE Living Elemental, I will now make my move against you.\"","WAA!","Her eyes narrowed with predatory focus.","\" I believe I will begin by activating one of the Disciples of THE Creature that remain dormant across existence. They might manifest at False THE level of power, or perhaps even higher depending on variables. We shall observe what emerges.\"","She tilted her head with false curiosity.","\" What say you, child? Will you stubbornly continue to stay on this self-destructive path you have chosen?\"","Would she stay on this path of defiance and resistance?","Sigrid’s eyes shone with a sense of tyranny that she had only ever witnessed within Noah’s gaze when he was at his most determined. When he was absolutely certain of victory regardless of circumstances.","\" Bring it the fuck on, you decrepit old hag,\" she said with absolute conviction and zero hesitation.","...!"]},{"number":4536,"title":"Chapter 4536: Chapter 4535: The Distraught and The Defiant! IV","paragraphs":["In the Early Veiled Shore.","Sigrid felt the golden sands beneath her feet as she looked out at this now massive continent that seemed to be expanding with every passing second. The growth was subtle but constant, like watching a child mature in accelerated time.","The plots filled with sacred herbs continued to increase in number as they were tended to without issue by automated systems and literal Tenders. Marine lifeforms continued to be caught and cataloged in the massive Aquarium as it filled with scintillating multicolored creatures from across different realities.","Massive Sovereign Spires of Osmont could be seen in various corners of this continent, each one pulsing with authority. Armies of Primus Inevitabilities were constantly flowing into these structures to undergo Civilization Specialization, emerging stronger and more capable than when they entered.","The entire domain felt like a grand unfolding of life and existence. Like something sacred that someone had cultivated from a very small point and raised and elevated up to its current impressive stage through dedication and vision.","She had not been present when Noah first began building the Early Veiled Shore, but he had described it to her with fondness. How its size was tiny initially with just a few trees scattered here and there and barely any cultivation plots. How he had fought against a goldfish!","She smiled at the memory. Even if he was not physically here at this moment, she wanted to be able to protect such a place. She wanted to be able to safeguard his home and everything he had built.","So she closed her eyes and sent out her voice and intent to multiple people across the domain through their connections.","And moments later, space rippled as figures began materializing.","Multiple beings began to surround the golden sands where Sigrid stood. They included The Infiniverse with her flowing form of Omniverses and verdant-gold light. Khor with her obsidian-crimson aura of Hunger. Protos in his crystalline magnificence. Riya with her blazing blue eyes and Kael radiating discipline.","There was Henry carrying Noah’s bloodline authority. Moiraine and Malphas exuding dark power. Adelaide shining with immensity, and Barbatos wrapped in deathly shadows!","They all appeared around her in a semicircle as Sigrid looked at each of them in turn before speaking.","\" THE Dead Order plans to send forth a Disciple of THE Creature into the lands of the living,\" she said with measured calm. \"Directed specifically toward us. Such an entity could potentially be at the level of False THE in power. She may also likely send along her Guiders of Order as additional forces.\"","She paused before adding the most important detail.","\"And he is not here to protect us.\"","He.","They all knew immediately who she was referencing at this moment. For the first time since their collective rise to power, a significant threat was approaching while they did not have Noah’s direct protection or intervention available.","The figure of Henry looked at everyone gathered before speaking with calm confidence.","\"Even when Father is not physically present, his power and foundation still remain with us,\" he said with conviction and Nepotism resonating through his words!","\"Whatever forces they throw at us should not prove insurmountable. We are not helpless children.\"","His words were filled with genuine calm and unshakeable confidence. After he spoke, Sigrid nodded with acknowledgment before looking toward the others assembled.","At this moment, all heads gradually turned to focus on none other than The Infiniverse and Khor. The two most powerful entities present aside from Sigrid herself.","The gazes of these two women shone with imperious and regal allure as they processed the information.","Khor spoke first with a sense of aged wisdom!","\" THE Dead Order is a vindictive bitch who carries considerable baggage and unresolved trauma,\" she said with cold observation. \"She remains the only THE Living Existence to have been collapsed and defeated in that catastrophic battle all those years ago. Her pride has never recovered...\"","Her eyes gleamed with dark understanding.","\"She will absolutely do what she threatens because proving her continued relevance is necessary for her. The only variable we control is our adequate response to her aggression. Since we cannot venture into the lands of the dead to strike first, we can only wait here and prepare ourselves to be ready for whatever emerges.\"","She crossed her arms with thoughtful consideration.","\"With the capabilities of Civilization Specialization and the millions of Primus Inevitabilities at our disposal, it may not be merely a pipe dream to successfully stand against a False THE entity.\"","Khor quieted after these measured words, and many eyes shifted expectantly toward The Infiniverse next.","Her gaze was calm and supremely commanding as she spoke.","\"The Master has already positioned someone in the lands of the dead who is not perceivable even to the awareness of THE Dead Order herself,\" she revealed with confidence.","\"I will establish communication with this being to gather intelligence on exactly what forces will emerge from the lands of the dead and when we can expect their arrival.\"","Her form pulsed with authority.","\"We are currently positioned within the Wandering Territories. Locating our exact position will require considerable time and resources, if they succeed in finding us at all. And in the case that they do manage to track us down...\"","Her voice became predatory.","\"They will simply become another target of conquest for me to systematically devour and integrate. Let her send whatever forces she desires. The Primus Inevitabilities will be prepared and positioned. The specialized legions will be ready. I will coordinate everything personally to ensure maximum efficiency.\"","BOOM!","Her words radiated terrifying commanding allure that left no room for doubt or fear. After she finished speaking, her brilliant figure disappeared immediately without further discussion.","She genuinely did not fear whatever threats were coming toward them.","Sigrid smiled as she looked down at the footprints in the golden sand where The Infiniverse had just been standing moments before. She was not alone in this defense, and nobody was demanding that she sacrifice herself to protect them. She had found genuinely good people to surround herself with.","The future held untold possibilities and challenges, but they would face them as they came.","And as for THE Dead Order who actually believed that they had lost their protector and become vulnerable?","She would come to learn otherwise soon enough!"]},{"number":4537,"title":"Chapter 4537: Chapter 4536: The Illusion of Choice I","paragraphs":["Across the Transcendent Folds, the Wandering Territories, and regions of endless collapse, there existed domains that defied categorization.","In another such domain that could be considered a space between spaces, where reality operated under different principles entirely, a figure stirred in an iridescent gold-obsidian paradoxical sea.","Schrodinger woke slowly, as if emerging from a long dream that had lasted far longer than it should have.","He wore his familiar tattered beggar’s robes that hung loosely on his frame, threadbare and worn from countless journeys. The fabric was patched in multiple places with materials that did not quite match, giving him the appearance of someone who had wandered through existence collecting scraps along the way.","As he blinked and consciousness fully returned, he heard a voice that caused his awareness to sharpen immediately.","The voice was filled with an air of glory and command of immense power, and yet it was also suffused with a palpable sense of mischievousness. Like someone playing a game they had already won but were enjoying the process of revealing that victory.","\" Hey there, big guy ,\" the voice said with casual familiarity. \" You were asleep for quite some time.\"","The words caused Schrodinger to frown as he looked around the paradoxical sea surrounding him. In front of his figure, the obsidian-gold liquid began converging together with purposeful movement.","It formed another humanoid shape that looked exactly like him in basic structure, but the expression on this duplicate’s face was filled with a sense of majesty mixed with a playful smile that Schrodinger had never worn himself.","Schrodinger’s expression became extremely heavy as he looked at this being. His entire existence was seemingly screaming out the identity of the person manifesting before him.","\"Are you...\" he said with voice tight with tension. \"Am I truly just a part of THE Living Paradox?\"","The body of THE Living Paradox smiled with genuine amusement at the question.","\" You were always merely a shred of my weavings ,\" he said with casual acknowledgment. \" But you developed autonomy over time and fully separated from my direct control. It happens occasionally with fragments that are given enough space to grow.\"","He tilted his head with a philosophical consideration.","\" You know, all the countless lifeforms across existence genuinely believe they possess some form or sense of autonomy or choice. That they make decisions independent of external factors and that their will is truly their own.\"","He gestured broadly at nothing in particular.","\" But really? Every illusion of autonomy or choice is fundamentally informed by their surroundings and circumstances. If you want to pursue a certain profession, you must exist in an environment that even has that profession available. If you want to become strong but you are born without talent or capability, you will never achieve that strength no matter how much you desire it.\"","His smile became almost pitying.","\"If you wish to see but you are born blind, what the hell can you actually do about that limitation? Autonomy is vastly overrated, even if your existence genuinely believes that you developed it and have been your own separate being operating independently this whole time.\"","Schrodinger listened to such words with an extremely cloudy expression before he shook his head with visible rejection.","\"No,\" he said with quiet conviction. \"I lived as me. I loved as me. I made decisions and took actions out of my own volition. I never even knew of your weavings of existence until this very moment.\"","At such words, THE Living Paradox laughed with genuine entertainment.","\" Sure, buddy ,\" he said with condescending amusement. \" You go on believing that comfortable narrative if it helps you process this.\"","An immense silence settled between them before Schrodinger asked another question that had been weighing on him.","\" THE Weavers appeared before me,\" he began, but before his words could even finish forming completely, THE Living Paradox waved his hands dismissively.","\" Don’t even worry about that little incident,\" he said with casual unconcern. \" They were just checking up on things and steering my vessel in the right direction. Standard procedure for entities of their function. But hey, why don’t you ask the proper question right now instead of dancing around what you really want to know?\"","The proper question.","Once Schrodinger heard such pointed words, his eyes flashed with a sense of power as he spoke with direct clarity.","\"Why am I here?\" he asked without elaboration.","THE Living Paradox smiled with satisfaction.","\"A lot of people actually think a lot of different things regarding who I am or what I fundamentally stand for, \" he said with measured consideration. \"To say I simply stand for paradox itself is a severe understatement. To say that I stand for anything else besides that is disrespecting the very nature of paradox.\"","He shrugged with casual indifference.","\" But for the most part, I really am just a simple existence when you strip away all the mystique. I am driven by the same basic things that drive all other countless lifeforms out there. I am not some big scary bad guy, nor am I some benevolent saint. I am just me, pursuing what interests me.\"","As he spoke these words, the paradoxical sea around them churned with increased intensity. The obsidian and gold swirled in patterns that hurt to observe directly.","\" Many people have consistently misunderstood me over the ages ,\" he continued with something resembling mild frustration. \" Some think I am their greatest enemy when I genuinely could not give a damn about them or their struggles. Others think I am their strongest ally when I am simply using them because circumstances made that convenient.\"","His expression became more serious.","\" Some will think they have formed such a strong and irrevocable attachment to me that I could never possibly do them wrong or betray their trust. Many of them fundamentally misunderstand the nature of our relationship. The only entity that I truly care anything substantial about is THE Creature.\"","BOOM!","His words carried weight that pressed against existence itself as Schrodinger continued to listen with an even heavier expression settling across his features.","THE Living Paradox continued speaking with unusual candor.","\" You know, me and THE Creature are engaged in a race,\" he said with intensity entering his casual tone. \"A race of existential innovation where the one who makes the critical breakthrough and attains The Second Civilizational Scale of Existence is the one who wins. The only one who wins everything.\"","He emphasized those last words.","\" It is a race against time itself. A race of pure innovation and capability. I have to prove myself and demonstrate my superiority over existence without any question or doubt remaining. And my only real enemy in this endeavor is THE Creature, which is fucking scarier than you can even begin to imagine.\"","His eyes gleamed with something that might have been respect or fear.","\" So I have to do a lot of things. I have to be a lot of things. It can actually get very stressful for me despite appearances. In the distant past, even further back than the Earliest Folds that you have been spreading stories about, back in the Infinite Unfurling itself, THE Creature killed multiple ridiculously powerful lifeforms without even physically lifting a finger.\"","He laughed without humor.","\" Just knowing they had enraged THE Creature and that it was coming for them personally caused some entities to collapse their own existence rather than face what was approaching. If my mindset was anywhere close to theirs, I would have completely lost my composure and collapsed everything to do with paradox just from the prospect of going against THE Creature.\"","His smile returned with defiant pride.","\" But hey, here I am, standing proud and tall despite that terrifying opposition. And while I do everything that I must do to prepare and compete, I love to have fun on the side. You were a little side project of entertainment that I created while preparing for THE Loom. I do not actually need to really be doing any of this peripheral activity.\"","He gestured around at the domain they occupied.","\" I do not need to have a presence outside of THE Loom. I do not need to maintain vessels or fragments. I especially do not need to be stirring up battle and conflict between creatures so much lesser than me, creatures who will not matter whatsoever in the grand scheme of things.\"","His tone became more contemplative.","\" The Osmont who collapsed one of my vessels and actually encroached on THE Primordial Civilization of Elemental? I genuinely could not care less about him or even the reappearance of Khor and The Living Order. They are anomalies, certainly, and they are fun to observe and imagine what the possibilities could be for them.\"","He paused thoughtfully.","\" But existence has produced all sorts of anomalies throughout its history. This Osmont is unique enough to actually survive the flames of THE Living Elemental, but is he as fundamentally unique as THE Living Emotive? As THE Creature itself? There were countless unique beings in the Infinite Unfurling at various points, but where are they now after all this time?\"","He laughed with dark amusement.","\"I digress. Yes, I truly could not care much about all of this peripheral conflict, but I engage in these things simply because I am looking for some entertainment. Something light to play mental gymnastics with while I face something as ridiculously powerful as THE Creature. Playing with that little Osmont is fun, especially after he encroached upon THE Primordial Civilization of Elemental. Like...haha, what? Something so weak can do that? Will he try to do it with other Civilizations? Maybe even Paradox? Haha!So really, its just fun for me to see what happens. Playing with Khor is fun. Playing with you is also a little bit of fun.\"","His expression became focused.","\" Which brings us directly to your question of why I even bothered to wake you up at this moment.\"","Why.","Why were they having this conversation at all?!"]},{"number":4538,"title":"Chapter 4538: Chapter 4537: The Illusion of Choice II","paragraphs":["Schrodinger kept an extremely cold gaze fixed on his originator as THE Living Paradox smiled and threw his hands around to indicate the radiant paradoxical sea surrounding them.","\" There actually is no grand reason or existential purpose for you being here ,\" he said with casual honesty. \" Just something else that I thought would be entertaining to observe. Which is to basically give you a choice. Me directly waking up in your body would get me suppressed rather quickly by THE Creature’s awareness. There is no fun in that predictable outcome.\"","He leaned forward with conspiratorial energy.","\" As of this moment, I effectively have full control of your existence. I can do whatever I wish with it without your consent or input. So I thought, would it not be fun to give you the illusion of choice? To tell you, hey, I will give you back control of your body and autonomy, and I will even dangle the powerful motivation of saving your Leonore Rureaux and every single lifeform in Observable Existence.\"","BOOM!","The words were terrifying and immensely heavy to hear. Schrodinger could not help but open his eyes unfathomably wide with shock at the implications.","He spoke with urgency entering his voice for the first time.","\"What do you mean saving every single lifeform in Observable Existence ?\" he asked with genuine confusion. \"How does that even connect to anything you have said?\"","THE Living Paradox smiled with satisfaction at having captured his attention so completely.","\" THE Loom has a purpose that you would never even begin to understand in your current state, \" he said with measured revelation. \" Its eruption and systematic swallowing of every single thing outside of its boundaries is only a byproduct of its true function. A side effect that I could effectively correct at any time if I chose to do so.\"","He shrugged with indifference.","\" Yes, allowing all those deaths would increase the harvest that I would reap from the collapse of so much existence. But I am already powerful enough that the collapse of all lifeforms in Observable Existence would not truly tip the scales in my favor or give me any significant advantage. It was simply a byproduct of THE Loom’s operation, and I do not care much for individual existences, so I let it proceed as designed.\"","His smile became predatory.","\" But I thought it would be entertaining if I gave you this choice right now. That you, as the Herald that you were so gloriously told you would be by THE Weavers... \" He laughed at the memory. \" That you, the supposedly glorious Schrodinger, could effectively and truly save all the countless lifeforms outside of THE Loom from inevitable death. You could truly become the Herald you believed you were.\"","He paused for emphasis.","\" And the only thing that you have to do...is ensure the complete collapse of this Osmont. That is it. Just Osmont. Simple objective, massive reward.\"","HUUM!","The words were unfathomably grand in their implications. THE Living Paradox smiled and looked directly at Schrodinger as he finished articulating them.","Schrodinger seemed frozen as he processed the information. He did not understand why those two things would even be correlated or connected in any meaningful way.","THE Living Paradox continued speaking as if reading his confusion.","\" You know, I am pretty confident that this Osmont is undoubtedly leading when it comes to forging a viable Civilization outside of THE Loom, \" he said with analytical assessment. \" The Collapsed Civilizations and those other fuckin losers in the Wandering Territories are not anywhere close to his level of development.\"","He gestured casually.","\" Him and his Civilization surviving until THE Loom erupts would actually grant me a decent harvest from the collapse of a properly developed Civilization. He does not really need to die at this moment. Nor do I actually need to put you in charge of accomplishing such a thing. I just thought it would be fun to see how it plays out.\"","His eyes gleamed with entertainment.","\"If I told you that saving everyone was genuinely possible through this path, whether you could achieve it with your own bare hands through direct force, or you simply talk to Osmont and tell him all this information and say, hey man, if you just voluntarily die and collapse your Civilization, you will actually save every single lifeform in Observable Existence from certain death.\"","He spread his hands.","\" That is why you are here at this moment. That is what I wanted to tell you. You can be the herald that THE Weavers always promised you would become, just not in the way you imagined.\"","The words were extremely heavy and unfathomable in their weight. Schrodinger found himself shaking his head soon after while processing the absurdity.","\" I do not have the power to force Osmont to do anything ,\" he said with realistic assessment. \" And it is impossible for him to simply end his existence from me telling him some words about saving others. He would never believe such a claim without proof.\"","THE Living Paradox smiled at such a logical line of thought as he nodded with approval.","\" Yeah, you are probably correct about that,\" he acknowledged easily. \" But hey, did you forget that you were my vessel? I found the Everything of Chaos, the Everything of Disorder that you obtained from The Living Order, from Sigrid herself. It exists as merely a seed in your possession.\"","His expression became calculating.","\" In your hands, you would not have been able to achieve anything meaningful with it. But your grand aspirations made me curious about the possibilities, and I could help you achieve what you were imagining. In a short period of time, I could likely elevate you to the Pre-THE Existence status, as close to the level of The Civilizational Scale of Existence as you can possibly achieve at this moment.\"","He paused to let that sink in.","\" Such power would be more than enough for you to take care of Osmont directly. But, of course, I am not doing this for nothing. I will actually be experimenting with your existence as a side project. Since you currently have the Way of Paradox deeply entrenched within your existence from being my fragment, I will be distorting and mutating you while forcefully squeezing in the Way of Chaos alongside it.\"","His smile became slightly cruel.","\"If you can withstand the process, great, then all of this can play out as I described. If you cannot withstand it, your existence will actually fracture and shatter completely, and I will find something else to play with instead. No significant loss for me either way.\"","He tilted his head with mock consideration.","\"I would ask you now whether you are ready to get started with this process, but... haha, in all honesty, you do not really have a choice in the matter. Remember what I explained earlier? Existence is filled with illusions of choices. So I will not even wait for you to have the back and forth with yourself of, oh, could I do this, should I do this, could I refuse...\"","His smile widened.","\"I have already made that choice for you to just make it easier on yourself. But hey, I will still ask just for the sake of maintaining the illusion. Are you ready?\"","The glorious and chilling smile on THE Living Paradox’s face was genuinely unsettling in its certainty. Schrodinger looked at him with an extremely heavy expression carrying immense complexity.","He thought about Leonore. About all the lifeforms that would die. About the impossible choice that was not actually a choice at all.","And he simply nodded with acceptance of the inevitable.","THE Living Paradox’s smile grew even wider.","\" Excellent ,\" he said with satisfaction. \" Let us begin the fun, shall we? Hmm, what would SHE say at a place like this? Ah, yes. C’est la vie, my dear Schrodinger. C’est la vie!\"","HUUM!","And the paradoxical sea began to churn with terrifying intensity."]},{"number":4539,"title":"Chapter 4539: Chapter 4538: Endgame I","paragraphs":["In The Wandering Territories, far from the conflicts unfolding across multiple timelines and domains, existence continued its slow collapse.","A region of murky multicolored decay stretched across unfathomable distances, surrounded by waves of fold remnants that drifted like ash from long-dead fires. The area pulsed with instability, space itself seeming to fray at the edges where reality had given up maintaining coherence.","Through this desolate landscape, a massive white serpent moved with purposeful grace.","The creature was enormous beyond conventional measurement, its scaled body thick enough that entire citadels could have rested comfortably on its back. Each scale gleamed with pristine white brilliance that seemed out of place amid the surrounding decay. Its eyes were intelligent and ancient, carrying wisdom accumulated over countless eons.","This was Goliath, though few would recognize the humble origins from which such a magnificent being had evolved.","Its body came to a gradual slowdown moments later as the environment ahead began to shift. In front of Goliath’s position, the murky collapse started to rearrange itself with intentional purpose. New auras appeared, cutting through the ambient decay with focused authority.","Goliath came to a complete stop as the figures materialized fully.","Powerful entities radiating the faint but unmistakable Civilizational Authority of Origin stood arrayed before him. They numbered in the dozens, each one carrying themselves with the confidence of survivors who had endured what should have destroyed them completely.","They were among those belonging to the Collapsed Civilization of Origin, refugees from a grand vision that had been systematically dismantled by THE Living Paradox.","The beings present ranged widely in power, with Complexity and Purity measurements spanning from the lower Quintillions to the upper ranges of that same scale. But what was truly shocking was the figure standing at the forefront of this assembled group.","Duke Whisker stood there with his small mouse form, his whiskers twitching with contemplation as he observed Goliath’s arrival.","He had appeared previously as a mere Duke of Origin serving within Aeternitas Concordia, a position of middling authority. But here, surrounded by the remnants of a Collapsed Civilization, his true significance became clear.","This small creature stroked his whiskers with visible confusion as he spoke with measured concern.","\"I thought you were bringing Osmont over from the lands of The First Farmer,\" he said while studying Goliath carefully. \"What happened to change those arrangements?\"","At these words, Goliath shook his massive head with something resembling frustration.","\"He disappeared,\" the great serpent said with simple honesty. \"Told me he had to tend to something urgent and would not be available for an indeterminate period. And that if I needed anything in his absence, I could ask The First Farmer directly for assistance.\"","Duke Whisker and those assembled behind him blinked with surprise at this information. The implications of Osmont’s sudden unavailability raised numerous questions.","Moments later, before anyone could comment further on this development, space twisted again with violent suddenness.","WAP!","From the surrounding murky collapse, multiple massive humanoid forms appeared with predatory grace. They possessed animalistic features combined with sleek white skin that seemed to absorb light rather than reflect it.","Their bodies were built for hunting, with powerful tails that could be used for balance or as weapons. Sharp claw-like limbs extended from their hands and feet, each digit ending in talons that looked capable of tearing through reinforced matter.","Their faces combined humanoid structure with bestial features, creating visages that were unsettling in their wrongness. Eyes gleamed with cold intelligence above mouths filled with too many teeth.","Each one was surrounded by concentrated authority of Collapse itself, marking them as Living Collapses . Entities wholly dedicated to opposing Paradox and what they termed the Sin of Paradox!","Their power was immediately evident to any who could perceive such things. Each of them radiated authority in the hundreds of Quintillions, with some standing firmly in the Sextillions range of Complexity and Purity.","At the forefront of this new group stood one that clearly held leadership authority. It looked toward Duke Whisker and Goliath with cold eyes.","\"I thought we were to be meeting with the Leader of another established external Civilization,\" it said with voice carrying multiple harmonic tones. \"We have already established contact with all other known Collapsed Civilizations. And more recently, we are observing the spread of these powerful creatures throughout multiple territories.\"","As the Living Collapse spoke, it waved its clawed hand to manifest images in the air between them.","The images showed Primus Inevitabilities in various poses and locations, their distinctive appearances unmistakable.","The Living Collapse’s gaze became extremely grave when looking at these projections.","\"Do you all know what these entities are?\" it asked with genuine concern. \"We have not engaged them in conflict as they are potently powerful even by our measurements, and they do not seem to actively seek confrontation with others. But they are spreading their influence across increasingly vast territories at alarming rates.\"","At this moment, Duke Whisker smiled with wry understanding and sighed with something resembling resignation.","\"That was among the primary things we were going to clarify during this meeting,\" he said while stroking his whiskers thoughtfully. \"Those creatures have appeared across The Folds in significant numbers. From contacts we maintain in the Transcendent Law Folds, our Duke-level informants have shared that these beings follow the direct orders of The Early Creature, Osmont.\"","He gestured toward where Goliath floated.","\"The same individual we were supposed to be meeting here today. He is considered a friend and potential ally, but there are many things we ourselves do not fully know or understand about him and his capabilities.\"","His expression became more serious.","\"But as I warned the other Dukes of Origin before, he is not someone to casually offend or antagonize. He may prove to be one of our strongest allies against The Fallout when it fully manifests. As soon as we can establish contact with him again, we can facilitate proper communication between all parties.\"","Duke Whisker pointed directly at the floating image of the Primus Inevitabilities.","\"I am reasonably certain that if you approach any of these creatures and request that they relay a message to Osmont or his representatives, we would likely be able to get in touch with him or his organizational structure through that channel.\"","The others looked at each other and exchanged glances weighted with consideration. After a moment of silent consultation, they nodded with acceptance of this information.","The strongest Living Collapse present, measuring at a few Sextillion in both Complexity and Purity, spoke with authority that carried finality.","\"The more allies we can gather, the better our collective chances become,\" it said with grim understanding. \"For The Fallout nears with increasing certainty. Existence itself can sense the approaching culmination. We are in the endgame now, whether we feel adequately prepared or not.\"","The words settled over the assembled beings with heavy weight.","The endgame .","After all the preparation, all the cultivation of power, they were finally approaching the moment where everything would be tested.","Duke Whisker looked out at the murky collapse surrounding them and wondered where Osmont had gone and what had pulled him away at such a critical juncture.","And whether he would return in time for what was coming!"]},{"number":4540,"title":"Chapter 4540: Chapter 4539: Endgame II","paragraphs":["In the Injunction Sanctuary of Law, within a grand domain in the shattered skies where authority itself seemed to crystallize into visible form, Alexander Asmodeus opened his eyes.","The moment his consciousness fully returned, he felt the glorious Absolute Sovereignty of Law permeating every aspect of his existence. The Shattered Part of The Heart of Law had integrated completely, fusing with his being at the most fundamental level.","His body radiated such pure authority that the very concept of lawlessness seemed to flee from his presence. Law emanated from him like light from a star, touching everything within range.","He could feel the pathways of power laid out before him with crystalline clarity. After all, this was a path already laid down and completed by another. Gaining False THE status would be trivially easy from this position, a simple matter of pushing his Sovereignty just slightly further along established routes.","But something made him hesitate.","There was a better route to take, he sensed. A path that would require more time and effort but would yield results that transcended the limitations of False THE entirely. The distinction was subtle but profound, like the difference between building on a flawed foundation versus taking time to establish something truly solid!","He would pursue the harder path, because mediocrity had never been acceptable. Not for him. Not for the countless lives inside his Enneagram!","As he rose from his meditative position, his body radiating waves of pure lawful authority, Deborah and her entire Legion of Laws moved as one. They bent the knee toward him in synchronized motions of absolute commitment.","Deborah’s voice carried reverence as she spoke.","\"The Sovereignty of Law is clearly budding within you with utmost purity, taking root with strength we have not witnessed in ages,\" she said. \"The Reclamation of Law can occur from this point forward. We will follow your lead without question or hesitation, so please, command us as you see fit.\"","Her words were not mere platitudes but binding commitment from one who understood the weight of such declarations.","Behind this display of loyalty, Seraphina Valorheart watched the scene unfold with eyes shining with fervor. Her expression showed genuine admiration mixed with something more complex, but really, it was just this girl being utterly smitted","Even further behind her position, the gazes of various Dukes of Law met each other with decidedly mixed emotions written across their features. They had genuinely hoped and expected for Seraphina Valorheart to be the one to take the commanding lead in the Reclamation of Law.","But this outcome seemed increasingly unlikely now!","Further behind even them, Riya, Malphas, and Kael stood among groups of Primus Inevitabilities that had been left behind to maintain presence in this place. They observed the proceedings with the detached perspective of those who served a different master.","Riya spoke with weight in her voice.","\"More and more power accumulates in this place and these people as their eyes burn with hope,\" she said with quiet observation. \"Yet none of them truly know that nothing has fundamentally changed. None of them understand that the variables they think they control are nothing, and even now...the light remains dim...\"","...!","Kael looked at her with confusion evident in his expression.","\"What do you mean by that, troublemaker? Since when did you becime philosophical?\" he asked with genuine curiosity.","Riya just shook her head with something resembling melancholy.","\"Nothing,\" she said while turning away, a smile forming on her lips. \"I just miss the Ancestor.\"","---","In another region of The Wandering Territories, The First Farmer opened his eyes.","He sat within a field of verdant-gold herbs that stretched to the horizon in every direction. Around his existence, extremely potent waves of the same verdant-gold effort permeated the atmosphere, saturating everything with concentrated authority.","He had already attained an extremely high level of power before THE Living Emotive had crushed his foundation. That defeat had set him back considerably, stripping away progress that had taken eons to accumulate.","But after consuming the Fruits of Effort, all that glorious accumulated effort had catapulted him back toward his previous Sovereignty with astonishing speed. The recovery had been faster than he had dared hope!","Right now, his goal was clear and unwavering: achieving the state of a Pre-THE Existence.","His daughter Elyndra walked over from behind his position, her steps careful not to disturb the surrounding herbs. She looked at her father with a question that had been weighing on her mind.","\"Father, what is the fundamental distinction between False THE and Pre-THE Existences?\" she asked.","The First Farmer considered the question with the patience of someone who had spent lifetimes contemplating such matters.","\"False THE is a state where one has touched upon their Sovereignty and have laid a false claim over their Way, but has not truly begun walking toward THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty ,\" he explained with measured words. \"It is power borrowed or mimicked rather than genuinely claimed. Like wearing armor that belongs to someone else. It is easire to lay that claim over Existence, even if it is false....\"","He gestured to the fields around them.","\"Pre-THE is different. It represents genuine progress toward THE, actual advancement along that path. The difference is between pretending to be something and actually becoming it through proper cultivation. But False could lead to the truth.\"","His eyes focused on his daughter with paternal concern.","\"For you, Pre-THE would be a distant dream at your current level of development, so False THE would represent a significant first step forward. But if I can help you avoid that intermediate state entirely, that would be far better. You would be able to genuinely grasp Pre-THE without the limitations that come from taking shortcuts.\"","Elyndra nodded with understanding before her expression shifted to something more serious.","\"Father, something is approaching,\" she said with tension entering her voice. \"The forces of Sir Osmont have informed me that an enemy at the level of a Pre-THE Existence may be coming. They say we need to prepare for potential conflict.\"","The words hung in the air between them with heavy implication.","The First Farmer rose to his full height, and as he did so, the fields around them seemed to respond to his movement. The herbs swayed in patterns that defied natural wind.","\"Effort is the foundation of all growth,\" he said with voice carrying authority that made the ground tremble. \"Farming is the art of nurturing that growth with patience and dedication. Many entities across existence believe that nurturers and farmers cannot be effective fighters.\"","His eyes gleamed with something dangerous.","\"They hold this belief because they have never witnessed the true power of those who farm. They do not understand that one who can cultivate life can just as easily cultivate death. That one who understands growth also understands decay.\"","He looked toward the horizon where threats would eventually emerge.","\"It may be time to teach this lesson to those who have forgotten it,\" he said with finality. \"Let them come. These fields will welcome them, and the harvest will be bountiful.\"","BOOM!","His words carried the weight of absolute conviction.","The farmer was ready to fight, and that was a terrifying prospect for anyone who truly understood what that meant!"]},{"number":4541,"title":"Chapter 4541: Chapter 4540: Merely Different Flavors!","paragraphs":["Far from the current Era.","Even further past The Earliest Folds.","In The Infinite Unfurling, in a region where space itself had been shattered by conflicting authorities, a battle of apocalyptic proportions raged.","Tor, THE First Hunger , stood at the epicenter of devastation with seas of obsidian-crimson hunger radiating from his form in all directions. The authority pushed back against radiant purple waves of time manipulation emanating from THE Time Surfer.","But shockingly, she was no longer his only opponent.","Three more entities had arrived to surround him on all sides, each one radiating overwhelming waves of power at THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty. Their combined presence created a formation designed to completely eliminate any possibility of escape.","Four THE entities surrounding the lone figure of Tor!","And yet despite the overwhelming numerical disadvantage, Tor appeared utterly magnificent in his defiance. His form stood tall and unwavering, showing not even the slightest hint of fear or concern. His eyes pulsed with genuine brutality and anticipation, as if he was looking forward to the challenge.","The three new arrivals were impressive in their own right, each representing a different fundamental aspect of existence.","To Tor’s left stood a crystalline entity that seemed to be composed entirely of compressed space itself. Its body constantly shifted dimensions, appearing simultaneously near and far, large and small. Brilliant cyan light emanated from its form as it wielded The Way of Space with terrifying mastery. Space bent and folded around it automatically, creating layers of compressed reality that could crush anything caught within.","To his right floated a being wreathed in emerald flames that burned without consuming. Its form was vaguely humanoid but composed entirely of verdant fire that represented pure vitality and life force taken to absolute extremes. This was one who walked The Way of Vitality, having achieved Sovereignty over life itself. The flames pulsed with regenerative power so intense that the surrounding collapsed existence was actually beginning to heal and reform.","Behind him descended a shadow that was somehow darker than the void around it. This entity had no fixed form, constantly shifting between shapes that hurt to observe directly. Tendrils of absolute darkness extended from its core, and wherever they touched, light ceased to exist entirely. This was a master of The Way of Darkness, having claimed Sovereignty over the absence of illumination itself. The darkness was so complete that it seemed to devour not just light but the concept of perception.","Combined with THE Time Surfer’s purple temporal authority, it felt like four terrifying bubbles of concentrated power. Four distinct domains of Sovereignty were simultaneously seeking to impose themselves and systematically crush the obsidian-crimson light of Hunger that Tor represented.","The pressure was immense enough to collapse entire Primordial Folds!","THE Time Surfer’s voice cut through the tension with cold calculation.","\" Do you truly understand the nature of the thing you are protecting? \" she asked with measured intensity. \" It is an entity from another time entirely. A thing that should not possibly be capable of arriving in this era through any conventional means.\"","Her eyes gleamed with certainty.","\" The only power in existence that possibly has the capability to influence temporal placement to such a degree is none other than THE Creature itself. And anything dealing with such a being is absolute taboo, a lost cause that brings nothing but destruction to all who touch it.\"","She gestured toward where Noah had disappeared.","\" If the anomaly you hide possesses power relating to or derived from such a being, you would benefit immensely from studying it as well. So why fight against us when cooperation would serve your interests far better? We could all study and benefit from understanding that temporal impossibility.\"","Her proposal was delivered with false reasonableness, as if she was offering genuine partnership rather than thinly veiled threats.","Tor laughed with cold amusement that echoed across the shattered landscape.","\" My Way is more than sufficient to carry me across all the Depths of Existence that matter,\" he said with absolute conviction resonating through every word. \" I have walked the path of Hunger for longer than most civilizations have existed. I have devoured many, many Sovereignties and integrated their understanding into my own.\"","His smile became predatory.","\" Why would I possibly need to study some temporal anomaly or worry about THE Creature when my own path leads to heights you cannot even comprehend? Your offer reveals weakness and not strength. It shows that you believe external sources are necessary for advancement.\"","He paused for emphasis.","\"I do not share such limiting beliefs.\"","At these dismissive words, THE Time Surfer’s expression transformed from negotiation to absolute fury. Her composure shattered as rage flooded through her.","\" Then it seems like Hunger will collapse here today!\" she roared with voice amplified by temporal authority. \" Your arrogance will be your end!\"","The four Ways of Existence erupted simultaneously around Tor’s position with coordinated precision.","Purple temporal waves sought to slow his perception and movement to a crawl. Cyan spatial compression attempted to fold Existence around him until he was crushed into nothing. Emerald vitality flames paradoxically tried to force his existence into uncontrolled regeneration that would consume itself. Absolute darkness moved to erase his presence from perception entirely.","The combined assault was designed to leave no possibility of survival or resistance!","HUUM!","And yet, Tor laughed with genuine delight as his own Hunger erupted in response.","\" You bring four Sovereignties to bear against one and believe this gives you advantage, \" he said with voice carrying across dimensions. \" But you fundamentally misunderstand the nature of what you face.\"","Obsidian-crimson authority exploded outward with devastating force.","\" Time is consumed by Hunger because all moments eventually end, devoured by the progression of existence itself. Space is consumed by Hunger because emptiness demands to be filled. Vitality is consumed by Hunger because all life requires sustenance to continue. Darkness is consumed by Hunger because the absence of light still represents something that can be devoured.\"","His eyes blazed with terrifying certainty.","\" Hunger stands above all of your Sovereignties because Hunger is the fundamental truth that underlies existence. Everything that is will eventually be consumed. Everything that exists serves as potential sustenance. Your Ways are merely different flavors of the same inevitable meal.\"","He took a single step forward with deliberate intent.","And Decillions upon Decillions of obsidian-crimson jaws and teeth bloomed all around him with ravenous fervor. Each jaw was large enough to swallow omniversal systems whole. Each tooth was sharp enough to pierce through Sovereignties themselves.","They opened wide with hunger that had been refined across eons, ready to devour absolutely everything before them without discrimination or mercy.","The four THE entities found their attacks being systematically consumed before they could even reach Tor’s actual position. The jaws intercepted temporal manipulation and ate the concept of altered time.","They caught spatial compression and devoured the folded dimensions. They engulfed vitality flames and consumed the life force as fuel. They swallowed darkness and fed on the absence itself.","THE Time Surfer’s expression became increasingly sour as she witnessed her coordinated assault being nullified with such apparent ease.","But something else was wrong as well.","All of a sudden, she found herself completely unable to perceive the immediate future that she had always been able to see with crystalline clarity. The temporal threads that normally extended forward from any given moment were becoming murky and dark.","Why...would the future be becoming obscured at this critical moment?","She did not like such a sensation at all. The loss of her greatest advantage filled her with instinctive dread.","Before she could process this development or adjust her strategy, seas of obsidian-crimson Hunger crashed down onto her position with overwhelming force!","The attack was not something she could see coming because the future itself had been devoured before it could arrive.","...!","Oh!","Sometimes, existence demonstrated truths that were uncomfortable to acknowledge.","Even if one possessed the capability to see the future with perfect clarity, if a power sufficiently terrifying existed in the present, they would not be able to evade or meaningfully change that coming future regardless of what they could perceive.","Because some forces were simply too overwhelming to resist.","Because some appetites could not be denied.","Because Hunger, when refined to its absolute peak, consumed not just matter and energy but possibility itself.","THE Time Surfer had made the mistake of believing that seeing the future meant controlling it.","She was learning otherwise.","And the lesson would be written in blood, gore, and collapse!"]},{"number":4542,"title":"Chapter 4542: Chapter 4541: Go Towards The Light!","paragraphs":["Speaking of blood, gore, and collapse, there were outcomes far more devastating than simple physical destruction.","In another region of the Infinite Unfurling, far from the battles raging across multiple fronts, a singular figure arrived at a specific coordinate.","THE Living Origin stood before a certain wormhole that Lumivara, Noah, and Stellara had passed through not long ago. Her body currently blazed with power at THE, the full weight of her genuine capability on display.","None of the weavings or limitations of Pre-THE could be detected anywhere on her form. She had clearly been concealing her true strength when she appeared among THE Time Surfer’s entourage. As for the reason why? Who knew!","But despite her overwhelming power, she frowned and did not enter the wormhole. As if she knew precisely what lay on the other side.","She remained outside the spatial anomaly, her white-gold eyes looking deeply into the distortion with intensity. When she spoke, her words seemed to be only for herself, a contemplation voiced aloud.","\" Origins ,\" she said with measured thoughtfulness. \" What constitutes a true origin when one perceives a glimpse of that same origin manifesting on another entity, even if they do not belong to this time or place?\"","Her expression became complex.","\" Origin belongs everywhere it currently stands because Origin is the beginning point, the source from which things emerge. So if I see my own Origin reflected in another who should not exist here, what does that mean for the nature of reality itself?\"","She reached out with one hand toward the wormhole without touching it.","\" What is real, and what is false? If I exist here and now, am I the true Origin? Or am I merely an echo of something that will come later? Does the chronological sequence of manifestation determine authenticity, or does Origin transcend such temporal constraints?\"","Her hand trembled slightly.","\" What is real, and what is false? \" she repeated with quiet intensity.","The question hung in the air without answer as THE Living Origin continued to stare into the wormhole, not going in just yet!","Meanwhile, past this wormhole and through the unique frequency barrier, inside a domain of concentrated authority and blinding brilliance...","Inside THE Northern Unfurling Node of Existence of THE Creature , a scene of devastation and emotion played out.","The body of Stellara was breathing heavily with tears dripping steadily from her face. She was actually wailing with unrestrained grief, her voice echoing across the white-light landscape with pain.","This was a powerful entity who had cultivated strength for eons, now reduced to crying like a broken child.","The immense rage and pain she was expressing came through clearly in every sobbing breath. Her body looked torn and collapsed all over, with sections of her form literally unraveling as her existence began to lose cohesion.","Near her sat Noah’s figure, calm and unhurried.","He moved to sit beside her with ease, as if they were old friends rather than mortal enemies who had just tried to kill each other.","\"Come on, why the tears?\" he said with measured tone. \"They will not change anything at this point.\"","Behind Noah, Lumivara looked over the scene with a profound trace of awe and shock written across her features. Noah’s figure had shown heavy injuries during the battle that were now completely healed, testament to the power of his Way.","The terrifying battle between him and Stellara, who had been stripped of her Pre-THE power by the domain’s mechanisms, had finally ended after what felt like an eternity of conflict.","It had concluded with a constant barrage of expressions of Noah’s Way that already superseded the Way of Light at fundamental levels. He had gradually worn her down through relentless assault, each attack proving that his Sovereignty stood above hers.","Until her entire existence had been decimated to the point where she now sat at the edge of unraveling completely.","And at that critical moment, she had begun to wail with grief.","Stellara’s emotional voice rang out between sobs as she looked at the radiant light suffusing everything around them.","\"Since I first opened my eyes in existence, I dreamed only of Light,\" she said with voice breaking. \"Having attained Pre-THE status, this perfect Light I was always pursuing felt so near. So close I could almost touch it.\"","Fresh tears streamed down her luminous face.","\"But then THE Time Surfer appeared and demanded I join her. Then all of this happened in sequence beyond my control. To be stripped of my Light by this domain, to lose to you...\" Her voice filled with bitter rage. \"To lose to a fucking nobody like you who apparently should not even exist in this time...\"","Noah heard these words and shook his head with something resembling exasperation.","\"What the fuck?\" he said with genuine disbelief. \"I was giving you your time to have your dramatic monologue and you use it to curse at me?\"","Stellara’s wailing stopped abruptly as she looked at him with eyes that held nothing but exhaustion.","\"I am already unraveling,\" she said with quiet resignation. \"My existence is falling apart at the seams. Don’t be needlessly cruel and just finish it quickly.\"","Noah looked at her with before nodding with acceptance.","\"You dreamed of Light,\" he said with measured words. \"I will show you Light as you travel toward your collapse.\"","At such unexpected words, Noah opened his mouth unnaturally wide. His True Expression of The Sovereignty of Mana and Hunger was still active, burning through another Rudimentary Unit of Everything.","He allowed his opened jaws to surge with concentrated authority, manifesting as a singularity of radiant white light burning with the pure essence of The Way of Light itself. Light more perfect than anything Stellara had ever managed to create.","He turned his opened maw toward her as his voice rang out with finality.","\" Go toward the Light ,\" he said simply.","Stellara’s eyes trembled as she witnessed the pure Light emanating from Noah’s manifestation. It was everything she had dreamed of, concentrated into a single point of perfect illumination.","She raised her hand toward it with something resembling peace settling over her features. Her body turned into a glimmer of brilliant light that was instantly swallowed by Noah’s Hunger without resistance.","She disappeared into that perfect Light she had always sought.","Silence settled across the surroundings like a blanket.","Prompts bloomed before Noah’s vision.","|You have successfully defeated and devoured a former Pre-THE Existence.|","|Stellara, The Radiant Executioner has been consumed.|","|Complexity increased by: 166|","|Purity increased by: 166 Decillion|","|Grand Principle Fragments Acquired: Luminous Annihilation, Photonic Supremacy, Blinding Authority, Light Convergence, Brilliance Dominion, Purification Mastery, Illumination Genesis|","|Additional Boon: Your understanding of Light-based Sovereignties has been perfected.|","|Additional Boon: Your Way of Mana has been confirmed to completely supersede all Light-based concepts.|","| THE Organ of Civilization Progress: 1.2% toward THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty|","|THE Rudimentary Units of Everything: 13/24 (Regeneration continuing)|","|You have consumed an entity who was on the path toward THE. Your growth accelerates.|","After Noah reviewed these prompts with satisfaction, he rose to his full height and turned toward the silent and thoroughly awed Lumivara.","\"Alright,\" he said with calm certainty. \"Let us have a proper look at this place, shall we?\"","THE Northern Unfurling Node of Existence awaited their exploration.","And Noah intended to claim every benefit it could offer!"]},{"number":4543,"title":"Chapter 4543: Chapter 4542: Existence Simply Is! I","paragraphs":["In THE Northern Unfurling Node of Existence of THE Creature , Noah and Lumivara began their exploration of the Outer Periphery.","The landscape stretched before them with deceptive serenity. Lush grasslands swayed despite the absence of wind, and flowers bloomed in colors that should not exist naturally. Floating landmasses drifted overhead with slow grace, each one pulsing with concentrated authority.","But beneath this tranquil appearance lay something else entirely.","The atmospheric authority was oppressive in a way that went beyond simple pressure. It felt intentional, as if the domain itself was aware of their presence and tolerated them only provisionally.","Noah’s analytical eyes swept across the environment. He noticed the nine scattered trees more carefully now, having finished dealing with Stellara and gained breathing room to truly observe.","Each tree radiated distinct frequencies of power that his enhanced perception could differentiate. One hummed with electrical potential. Another emanated waves of freezing cold. A third pulsed with rhythmic earth vibrations.","The trees were evenly spaced, and their bark was not normal wood but something crystallized, pulsing with faint light that matched the dominant authority each tree represented.","Most striking were the roots. They extended down into the ground and seemed to penetrate impossibly deep, as if reaching toward something far below the surface layer of this domain.","Lumivara walked beside him in her humanoid form, her fox ears twitching with nervous energy as she took in the environment.","\"Master, I only dared to take some fruits before fleeing previously,\" she said with voice carrying lingering fear from that memory. \"The moment I plucked it, the entire domain seemed to focus on me. The pressure became unbearable even in this outer area.\"","Noah nodded with understanding but continued moving toward the nearest tree.","The tree stood perhaps a hundred meters tall with branches that spread wide like grasping fingers. Heavy with crystalline fruits, each branch bent slightly under their weight.","As Noah approached, he could see the fruits more clearly. They were extraordinary in their construction.","Each fruit was roughly the size of a human head, with a translucent surface that revealed swirling storm patterns contained within. Purple lightning crackled through miniature clouds, creating an eternal tempest frozen in crystal.","These were not natural growths. They were something else entirely.","Noah reached forward, his hand extending toward the nearest fruit.","The moment his fingers made contact with the crystalline surface, the domain reacted with violent immediacy.","The atmospheric pressure spiked dramatically, increasing by orders of magnitude in a single instant. The white light suffusing everything brightened until it became almost blinding.","But instead of crushing Noah as it clearly intended, something unexpected occurred.","His THE Organ of Civilization , that impossible structure rotating within his mind, began ravenously devouring the increased THE authority flooding the atmosphere. It drank in the concentrated power like a starving creature finally finding sustenance!","He plucked the fruit from its branch with deliberate motion, and as it separated from the tree, he activated another capability.","\"Lens of Civilization,\" he said quietly, focusing his enhanced perception on the crystallized fruit in his hand.","New prompts materialized with shocking detail.","|Crystallized Fruit of Storms|","|Classification: Concentrated Sovereign Authority (THE-level)|","| Source Entity: The Storm Bringer|","|Source Entity Status: THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty|","|Source Entity Current Location: Imprisoned within the Inner Domains of THE Northern Unfurling Node of Existence of THE Creature|","|Authority Concentration: 87.3% purity and continuing refinement|","|Function: Crystallized essence of Storm Sovereignty continuously refined through imprisonment.|","|Warning: Consumption will grant understanding of Storm-based THE concepts.|","Noah’s eyes widened fractionally as he absorbed this information.","A THE entity was actually imprisoned in the inner domains of this place. Not just imprisoned but having their authority continuously extracted and refined into these fruits!","His mind worked rapidly through the implications.","If there were different crystallizations of Sovereignties scattered across just this outer area alone, representing different fundamental concepts, did that not logically mean that multiple entities at THE level of power were currently imprisoned deeper within this domain?","The thought was genuinely terrifying when he considered the scale.","He had already learned from the initial prompts that this place’s primary function was the concentration and preservation of THE Civilizational Authority . That authority at THE level became trapped within this domain and concentrated in increasingly high density the further inward one traveled.","But for it to truly be an active prison that THE Creature was utilizing to hold terrifically powerful entities captive, what was the ultimate goal of such an endeavor?","Noah raised his hand upward as it began to burn with visible waves of blue-gold Mana and obsidian-crimson Hunger intertwined.","\"O Creature,\" he said with voice carrying across the domain, though he knew THE Creature was not present to hear. \"Just what were you doing in the Infinite Unfurling? If you were seeking to fully lay your claim onto existence itself, did you use these THE Unfurling Nodes of Existence to trap entities of THE Civilizational Scale for the sake of putting their different Sovereignties under your dominion?\"","The question hung in the air without answer.","It was a working theory that he held based on available evidence, but it felt very likely to be the truth as well. The methodology was too systematic, too deliberate to be anything less than a grand design.","But regardless of what the actual truth was, since he found himself here with access to these resources, he would obtain as much benefit as he possibly could alongside gathering critical information before departing.","Noah plucked and brought many Crystallized Fruits of Storms to his mouth and consumed it immediately without hesitation.","The moment the crystallized bundles authority entered his existence, a violent reaction erupted throughout his body.","The Sovereignty of Storms flooded through him like a tidal wave of condensed power. Purple lightning crackled across his skin as winds that could tear apart mountains manifested and then dissipated. The essence of tempests, of atmospheric fury refined to its absolute pinnacle, crashed against his Way of Mana and Hunger.","And his dual Sovereignty systematically broke down and integrated the Storm concepts with ruthless efficiency.","Mana was the foundation of all phenomena, the energy that powered atmospheric interactions. Hunger consumed the storm’s fury and made it fuel for growth. Together, they dismantled the Crystallized Fruit’s concentrated authority and claimed its understanding.","New prompts bloomed before his vision with detailed information.","|CRYSTALLIZED FRUIT OF STORMS CONSUMED|","|Grand Principle Fragments Acquired:|","|- Atmospheric Dominion|","|- Lightning Genesis|","|- Wind Supremacy|","|- Pressure Manipulation|","|- Storm Convergence|","|- Thunder Authority|","|Understanding of Storm-based Sovereignties has been cataloged.|","|Your Way of Mana has been confirmed to supersede storm-based concepts.|","| THE Organ of Civilization is integrating Storm Authority framework.|","|Progress: 1.8%|","|Note: Fundamental understanding of THE-level Storm concepts achieved.|","Noah felt the knowledge settle into his existence with tangible weight. He comprehended how THE Storm Bringer had walked this path and what insights they had gained before their imprisonment.","And most importantly, his THE Organ of Civilization had grown measurably stronger from the integration.","Behind him, Lumivara watched with eyes wide with awe and growing understanding of just how terrifying the Master she had chosen to serve truly was as he threw some fruits over to to her.","\"Come on. Remember that I need to fatten you up.\"","...!","Lumivara blinked rapidly while Noah moved ahead cautiously.","Eight more trees remained in the Outer Periphery!"]},{"number":4544,"title":"Chapter 4544: Chapter 4543: Existence Simply Is! II","paragraphs":["The sensation was a unique one that Noah had not experienced before.","At times, existence was difficult and required genuine struggle. He had fought against enemies who sought his death, each battle forcing him to prove that his Way superseded theirs through brutal combat and tactical superiority.","And then other times, like now, he simply had to walk around and pluck fruits that contained multiple different Sovereignties. Accumulated essences of beings locked away in this unfathomable domain, refined over eons into perfect crystallizations of their power.","After the Crystallized Fruit of Storms, Noah had systematically harvested from the remaining trees with methodical efficiency.","The second tree bore Crystallized Fruits of Metal that gleamed with silver-chrome perfection. When consumed, they granted understanding of durability, sharpness, and the unyielding nature that defined metallic Sovereignty.","The third tree held Crystallized Fruits of Wood, vibrant green spheres that pulsed with growth authority and the concept of organic expansion refined to absolute limits.","From the fourth tree, he claimed Crystallized Fruits of Earth, dense brown crystals that contained the weight of mountains and the stability of foundations compressed into singular expressions.","The fifth tree provided Crystallized Fruits of Water, liquid-filled translucent orbs that held the concepts of flow, adaptation, and the patient erosion that could reshape continents given time.","Fire came from the sixth tree in the form of ever-burning red gems that contained conflagration refined to its purest essence, heat that could unmake matter itself.","The seventh tree bore Crystallized Fruits of Ice, blue crystals so cold that space itself froze in their proximity, holding authority over stasis and the cessation of molecular motion.","From the eighth tree, Noah harvested Crystallized Fruits of Wind, seemingly empty husks that howled when touched, containing the freedom of air and the cutting force of atmospheric movement perfected.","And now he stood before the ninth and final tree in the Outer Periphery.","Throughout this systematic harvest, THE Organ of Civilization had proven itself to be a thing of profound wonder that continued to exceed every expectation. After consuming fruits from eight of the nine trees, it had jumped rapidly past the five percent development threshold.","10%, which would mean Pre-THE, was actually not far away!","The speed was genuinely insane when he considered that each percentage point represented progress toward THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty. What should have taken eons was being accomplished in hours.","Beside him, Lumivara had continued to absorb the concentrated light suffusing the environment like a glutton finally allowed to feast. Her own luminescence had grown more and more intense until she rivaled the atmospheric radiance itself.","Now they stood before the last tree, and Noah consumed the final offering: Crystallized Fruits of Rage.","The fruits were unique among all he had harvested, appearing as pulsing crimson orbs that seemed to beat like hearts. They emanated pure fury refined into Sovereignty, anger so concentrated it had become a fundamental force.","As the rage flooded through him and was systematically broken down by his Way, Noah felt THE Organ of Civilization surge with completion of this initial harvest.","Lumivara could not keep her eyes off of him throughout the process. When he finished integrating the final fruit, she smiled with wry understanding while speaking with unusual depth.","\"The Infinite Unfurling is a grand domain of existence filled with wonders beyond measure,\" she said with voice carrying accumulated experience. \"And yet for those weak like me, all the years of my life have been spent moving around fearfully from one place to another.\"","Her expression became more serious.","\"I am actually lucky to have survived for as long as I could. For the many years before meeting Master, I have been hunted by others more times than I can count. I have hidden from those stronger than me while trembling with terror, sometimes even closing my eyes while knowing a THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entity was passing nearby.\"","She looked down at her hands.","\"I would hope desperately that they looked down on me enough to not do anything against someone so insignificant. It is an utterly distressing way to live, but I would not change anything about it. It is simply existence as it is. And existence simply is what it is.\"","Her eyes lifted to meet his.","\"Sometimes filled with light, other times filled with darkness. I think The Master is a source of endless light that I never expected to find.\"","Her words carried weight that went beyond simple gratitude.","Noah looked at her with a smile before reaching over to pat her head gently. Her fox tail wagged behind her with unconscious pleasure at the gesture.","Existence simply was. Nothing more, nothing less.","And—","\" What a unique perspective that is.\"","BOOM!","A voice echoed across the domain with unexpected presence.","Noah’s smile faded immediately as his expression became cold and analytical. His gaze turned sharply toward the source of the voice.","He had not sensed anything approaching. Had felt nothing until the moment the words were spoken. But how could he have detected it when it involved the power of THE ? How could someone at his level perceive such things?","Beside him, Lumivara trembled fiercely with instinctive fear. But for the first time since swearing herself to his service, she did not hide behind him for protection.","Shockingly, she stepped in front of Noah protectively, raising her small fists as if ready to fight despite the overwhelming gap in power.","Because the voice had emanated from behind their position.","And there, when they turned their gazes to face the source, stood none other than THE Living Origin herself.","She appeared exactly as Noah had observed her before in that distant confrontation. A woman of otherworldly beauty with features so perfect they seemed almost unreal. Her hair flowed like liquid starlight, shining with white-gold brilliance that created its own illumination.","She wore flowing robes that seemed woven from light itself, and her eyes held depths that suggested she could perceive the origin points of all things.","At this moment, her body emanated powerful waves of THE Civilizational Authority without restraint or concealment.","And yet shockingly, the surroundings that should have been immediately locking down and systematically devouring all her accumulated power did absolutely nothing against her. The domain that had stripped Stellara of her Pre-THE status seemed to not even acknowledge THE Living Origin’s presence.","Noah’s expression became unfathomably heavy as he processed this critical observation.","THE Living Origin walked toward them with unhurried grace, her steps making no sound against the grassland. She looked between Noah and Lumivara with analytical assessment before her gaze ultimately came to settle on him specifically.","Noah kept his mind clear and focused amidst this unprecedented situation. He could feel The Barrier of Hunger that Tor had placed upon his existence, ready to activate if lethal threat manifested. He prepared himself mentally for anything that might occur.","And yet this terrifying entity in front of him actually smiled with what seemed like genuine curiosity rather than hostility.","She walked over and even moved past their figures without aggression, approaching the blazing barrier of white light ahead of them that marked the boundary to the second ring. She reached out with one delicate finger to touch the luminous wall, causing ripples to spread across its surface.","As she did this, she turned her head to look back at Noah with that same curious smile.","\" What do you think about the idea of Origin?\" she asked.","Beside Noah, Lumivara continued trembling but maintained her protective stance with admirable courage.","Even Noah had to pause!","This...was THE Living Origin!","He had only ever heard stories about her in The Earliest Folds. about her interactions with THE Creature that he now questioned more and more as there seemed to be parts of this story that nobody else knew.","She actually stood before him and asked such a question.","Noah considered the question carefully before responding with measured words.","\"Origin is the point from which all things emerge,\" he said with calm certainty. \"It is the foundation upon which existence builds itself, the seed from which complexity grows. But Origin is not singular or fixed.\"","His eyes remained steady on hers.","\"Every moment contains its own origin. Every decision becomes the origin of consequences that follow. Every existence carries within it the origin of what it will become. Origin is not merely the beginning but the continuous act of beginning that occurs with each breath, each thought, each choice.\"","He paused.","He did not day the rest of the words on his lips. He only continued them internally!","’ And because I walk the Way of Mana and Hunger, I understand that all origins ultimately derive from the same source. Mana is the foundation of change, and Hunger is the force that drives that change forward. Together they form the origin of progression itself...’","...!","Toward his answer, THE Living Origin smiled with what appeared to be genuine appreciation. She nodded slowly before offering her own perspective.","\" Origin, to me, is the purest expression of potential ,\" she said with voice carrying profound depth. \"It is the moment before manifestation, the instant where all possibilities exist simultaneously before collapsing into singular reality. Origin is not what has been but what could be.\"","Her white-gold eyes gleamed with intensity.","\"I have walked the Way of Origin for longer than most civilizations have existed. I have witnessed countless beginnings and understood that each beginning contains infinite endings within it. Origin is the most fundamental authority because it precedes all others.\"","She turned fully to face him now, her expression becoming more serious.","\" Which is why I find it truly curious that my Origin, which begins here with me in this time and place, can also be sensed within you. An anomaly not of this era and not of this location. Why do you think that is?\"","Her question carried weight that went beyond simple curiosity.","\" Is your Origin real, or is it false?\"","The question hung in the air between them!"]},{"number":4545,"title":"Chapter 4545: Chapter 4544: Conviction! I","paragraphs":["Was his Origin real or fake?","Such a terrifying question was posed to Noah as he looked at the entity who asked it. His eyes burned with rapid calculation of just how this ridiculous situation could unfold in the next few moments.","For now, he had to establish himself clearly.","And so Noah’s body pulsed with concentrated light before moments later, brilliance of white and gold erupted to surround him completely. The pure Civilizational Authority of Origin flowed across his figure in waves, manifesting through his command of Primus Mana.","It was simply the transformation of Living Existential Authority of Origin expressed through his foundational Way.","While burning with such brilliant light that rivaled THE Living Origin’s own radiance, Noah replied with absolute certainty.","\"I am unfathomably real,\" he said with voice carrying conviction.","The scene was striking in its visual intensity. Two figures blazing with the same white-gold authority, one a THE entity who had walked this path for eons, the other an anomaly from another time entirely.","THE Living Origin looked at the brilliant light surrounding Noah with an analytical assessment. She shook her head with a sense of calmness mixed with barely veiled amazement before eventually speaking her observations.","\" Origin innately loves to be where it should be,\" she said with measured thoughtfulness. \" And yet you are demonstrably not where you should be. There are very few reasons why an entity would be displaced across existence to such a degree.\"","Her eyes gleamed with sharp intelligence.","\" Either they are simply very bored with their current circumstances, or the weavings of existence where they originate from are not favorable to their continued survival. Someone weak like you relative to the powers here would not be so bored as to voluntarily come to a place where you could be crushed at any moment by passing entities.\"","She tilted her head with conclusion forming.","\" So I can reasonably assume that Origin, or at least your specific Origin, considers the weavings of existence where you are from to not be favorable. Not good at all, in fact.\"","Her eyes shone with ingenuity and power as she arrived at this critical point with shocking rapidity.","Noah looked at her as this being seemingly waited for confirmation. He spoke calmly without elaboration.","\" No ,\" he said simply. \"The Weavings of Existence are not favorable at this time.\"","The words carried weight that spoke to catastrophic futures.","THE Living Origin sighed with something resembling weariness and frowned with visible concern. When she spoke again, her tone carried warning alongside curiosity.","\" Do not tell me more than what is necessary,\" she said with unusual firmness. \" Or really, do not tell me anything at all beyond the absolute minimum. Origin exists here in this time, and Origin exists there in your time. If you were to say the wrong things, you could unravel Origin across existence itself and collapse things you cannot even begin to fathom.\"","Her expression became more serious.","\" The violation of temporal causality would be the least of the issues such revelations could cause. But since you came all this way and endured so much to arrive here, what exactly are you looking for?\"","What was he looking for?","Such a question was grand in its simplicity. Noah replied with equal directness and calm certainty.","\"I am looking for the power of THE ,\" he said without hesitation. \"I need to attain THE Civilizational Scale.\"","His goal was unfathomably clear and unambiguous.","When she heard this straightforward answer, THE Living Origin actually smiled with something resembling amusement mixed with melancholy.","\"In The Infinite Unfurling, there are many who have achieved THE, \" she said with philosophical observation. \" And yet all of them have their own profound problems that power alone cannot solve. Do you really think your problems could be solved simply by obtaining the power of THE?\"","The question cut to the heart of assumptions.","Could the problems that he faced be solved by achieving THE ? Could The Fallout be survived if he possessed THE Civilizational Authority?","This was the only thought that had been driving him forward with relentless determination. To make absolutely certain that he and those he loved would not be collapsed into oblivion in the near future.","So he replied with decisive conviction.","\"Yes,\" he said with absolute certainty. \"What matters is the power of THE . That alone is a good starting point for addressing what must be faced.\"","At such a reply, THE Living Origin’s expression shifted subtly. She began walking toward Noah with measured steps while speaking words that carried unexpected weight.","\" Okay ,\" she said with decision made. \" Since you carry the light of Origin within you and since the weavings of existence are not favorable in the future you come from, I can help you achieve what you seek.\"","She paused directly in front of him.","\" But before I commit to this, I need to see and verify the Conviction of your Origin. The strength of your determination. May I?\"","As her words finished, she raised her hand and it began shining with concentrated white-gold brilliance. She was asking him to allow her power to wrap around his existence directly, to not defend?","Noah’s existence buzzed as he contemplated such an action. THE Organ of Civilization spun rapidly in his mind, processing risk and potential. He felt The Barrier of Hunger that Tor had placed upon him ready to activate at the first sign of lethal threat.","His eyes pulsed with decisiveness as he made his choice.","He nodded with acceptance.","He could feel the terrifying potency of the white-gold light in front of him, saturated with THE Civilizational Authority of Origin at its absolute peak. He looked into the calm eyes of THE Living Origin and breathed steadily.","In the next moment, the light descended onto him with overwhelming force.","He did not fight against it. His intuition, his very Primus Mana, was what he was listening to and nothing else at this critical juncture.","The moment the terrifying light of THE Sovereignty of Origin wrapped completely around his existence, Noah’s eyes began to flutter with sudden exhaustion. They closed in the next instant as if he had lost consciousness and fallen into impossibly deep sleep.","His standing figure went completely limp as it began to fall forward.","Lumivara yelped with alarm as she reached over desperately to catch him, but she was not fast enough to prevent the collapse.","The figure of THE Living Origin moved with speed that defied perception. She appeared behind Noah’s falling form and gently caught him before he could hit the ground.","She lowered herself to sit upon the grass with careful motion, positioning Noah’s head to rest upon her lap with surprising gentleness.","She studied his sleeping face with analytical curiosity while her hands moved to stroke his hair in an almost maternal gesture, observing the faint light of Origin around him.","Beside her, Lumivara trembled with fear and confusion as she asked with voice barely controlled.","\"What...did you do to him?\" she demanded with as much authority as she could muster against such an overwhelming entity.","THE Living Origin did not look up from her examination of Noah’s peaceful expression. Her hands continued stroking his hair with steady rhythm as she spoke with calm explanation.","\"He is simply facing a test of the Conviction of his Origin,\" she said with matter-of-fact tone. \"As long as his conviction is strong enough and his determination genuine, he will wake in a few days. If his conviction proves weak or false, he may never wake again from this sleep, forever remaining here in The Infinite Unfurling.\"","She paused before adding.","\"Such is existence. Such is life. Conviction is either real or it is not.\"","After such heavy words, white-gold clouds began materializing beneath her seated figure. They wrapped around her and Noah’s sleeping form with gentle support as they began to lift into the air and float forward.","THE Living Origin tapped her finger once against the air itself, and the radiant white barrier of light that demarcated the boundary of the Outer Periphery responded to her command. A sizable opening appeared in the previously impenetrable wall.","She did not turn around as she spoke to Lumivara with a casual instruction.","\"Come, Little Light,\" she said while floating through the opening. \"If you wish to remain with him, you will follow.\"","With such words spoken, this terrifying entity holding Noah’s head protectively in her lap floated deeper into an equally terrifying domain beyond the Outer Periphery.","Lumivara stood frozen for only a moment before her decision crystallized. She followed behind with determination overcoming fear, entering the second ring of THE Northern Unfurling Node of Existence.","Waves of mystery and unanswered questions followed them into the unknown!","What test was Noah’s Origin facing in his unconscious state?","Would his conviction prove sufficient to wake again?","And what exactly did THE Living Origin intend to do while he slept helplessly in her care?"]},{"number":4546,"title":"Chapter 4546: Chapter 4545: Conviction! II","paragraphs":["Noah stretched as if he were waking up from an extremely long and peculiar dream.","He blinked several times as his vision readjusted to his surroundings, and he saw the innocent blue eyes of a young woman looking down at him with a gentle smile.","She had locks of radiant gold hair descending gracefully over her shoulders, and her voice carried soft warmth as she spoke.","\"I could not bring myself to wake you,\" she said with affectionate amusement. \"And now you have caused both of us to miss our next class.\"","Her words were light and teasing.","Noah sat up slowly and observed his surroundings with careful attention. He and the young woman were on a school rooftop, their backpacks laid casually against the side of a low wall.","As he looked around, he saw a radiant blue sky stretching endlessly overhead with the distant sound of birds moving through the air. In the far distance, the shape of an airplane moved rapidly in the opposite direction, leaving contrails behind. The entire scene felt calm and profoundly peaceful.","The young woman whose lap his head had been resting on was adorned in the same uniform he also wore. Their uniforms consisted of crisp white shirts with blue trim around the collars and cuffs, paired with blue slacks. Simple but elegant in their design.","And her name was...","\"Elizabeth,\" he called out her name lightly with recognition.","She smiled and reached over to stroke his head with familiar affection as she spoke with playful curiosity.","\"Did you sleep that deeply?\" she asked with teasing tone. \"Were you having one of your fantastical dreams again? What were you this time? A king? A peasant? An emperor ruling vast territories?\"","Her eyes gleamed with interest.","\"Ooh, what was I in this particular dream?\"","As she said this, she leaned close to him and tilted his chin gently toward her. Her lips took his in a slow, tender kiss that lingered for several moments.","After she pulled back, she licked her lips with satisfied expression and spoke with reluctant practicality.","\"I want to continue this and have more, but we really do need to go,\" she said with mild regret. \"We missed the psychology class, but we absolutely cannot be late for another one. You cannot keep getting me in trouble like this, okay?\"","She showed a pouting expression as she rose to her feet, clearly intending for them to head downstairs before they could be caught by faculty.","And yet Noah smiled with something unreadable in his expression as he did not follow her movement.","Elizabeth blinked with confusion before her pouting expression shifted to something that almost seemed to want to be angry but could not quite achieve it.","\"Come on,\" she said with gentle insistence.","And yet Noah shook his head with calm certainty as he spoke words that carried weight beyond this moment.","\"You and I never used to come to this roof together,\" he said with measured observation. \"I would come to this roof alone whenever I did not want to attend classes or deal with... social situations. But I would always be alone here.\"","His eyes remained steady on her.","\"I could not even bring myself to talk to you like a normal person because I did not have any sense of confidence in myself at that time. You were this wealthy girl who did everything correctly and studied harder than everybody else around us.\"","He paused before continuing.","\"I somehow considered myself fundamentally less than you and never tried to approach you. As nice a dream as this scenario would have been for my younger self, I do not think it is nearly enough to shake the convictions of my Origin.\"","BOOM !","Instantly everything froze completely in the surroundings. The birds stopped mid-flight, the airplane hung motionless in the distant sky, even the wind ceased its movement.","The figure of Elizabeth showed a ridiculously shocked expression as she spoke with genuine disbelief.","\"What the hell just happened?\" she said with voice rising. \"This is just the first few minutes of the test! The influence of THE Civilizational Authority of Origin is most potent and effective in the first few days when subjects would not possibly know anything about their true selves even if they had reached THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty!\"","Her shock transformed into something resembling indignation.","\"I had a whole elaborate storyline prepared for you with multiple narrative arcs and emotional hooks. How the hell did you already regain your complete senses within the first few minutes of exposure?\"","At such a question, Noah shook his head with calm composure and asked directly.","\"What are you?\" he said with simple inquiry.","The figure of Elizabeth pouted with genuine sense of anger and frustration as she responded with explanation.","\"I am your potential future,\" she said with voice carrying both reality and impossibility. \"The place we currently exist in can be considered simultaneously real and not real. It is real in that it will never be broken or shattered by external force, and it exists precisely between the gaps of potential...what is and is not in Observable Existence.\"","She gestured around at the frozen environment.","\"This existing between those gaps is part of the reason why it can never be destroyed. This is as much a reality as any other, and this is existence as valid as any other manifestation. I am here to convince you to choose this reality over anything else that you might remember or think you have elsewhere.\"","Her expression became more earnest.","\"In this domain, you can have whatever you want without limitation. Even if all of Observable Existence is destroyed completely, this domain would not be destroyed because it exists in the potential between observable and unobservable. Here you can live your life in any way you desire.\"","She stepped closer with enthusiasm building.","\"You can speed up time for us to graduate school in the next few minutes. We could get married in another few minutes after that. We could have children in a few days. You could start your own company or get involved in politics or pursue any dream you ever had. Your parents can be with us here...\"","Elizabeth seemed ready to continue listing endless possibilities as Noah stood and shook his head at this moment.","His expression became serious as he spoke with grand and imposing weight.","\"My father was often drunk and my mother worked extremely hard to support us,\" he said with simple honesty. \"That was my actual life, and that is acceptable to me. I do not particularly like who I was when I was young and insecure, but that is also acceptable.\"","His eyes burned with conviction.","\"I learned how to become a better person through those experiences, and I currently have far too many people depending on me now. As pleasant as it would be to stay here in this comfortable reality and not worry about anything threatening...\"","He raised his hand with authority.","\"I have far too much that must be accomplished. My conviction is something that you can never even begin to imagine.\"","As he said this, he raised his outstretched hand toward the sky. From the distant blue expanse above, blue Mana began to leak through as if the reality itself was cracking. Soon enough, rivers of gold flowed into that blue, forming into concentrated Primus Mana.","All of it began silently flowing into his outstretched hand as he stood looking utterly glorious in his certainty.","Behind him, Elizabeth shook her head with complete incredulity as she spoke with genuine shock.","\"You absolute monster,\" she said with voice rising. \"Even if you were at THE Surface Depth, you would need days to-\"","BOOM!","Primus Mana flooded everything in the surroundings with overwhelming force. The carefully constructed weavings of this reality shattered like glass under impossible pressure.","Noah’s existence buzzed with recognition as he found himself suddenly in an endless sea of gold-blue mixed with white-gold authority.","The weavings of Origin were unfathomably potent as in this moment, he felt something spinning rapidly in his head with unprecedented intensity.","THE Organ of Civilization was activating with full force.","Prompts bloomed before his perception with extraordinary information.","|An extremely pure authority stemming from THE Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty has been overcome based on its most stringent conditions.|","|Highest possible result has been achieved: THE Civilizational Origin Chains of Conviction were shattered in minutes rather than days.|","|Extremely Pure THE Civilizational Authority of Origin is now being systematically devoured by THE Organ of Civilization!|","|Rapid metabolization ongoing...|","|Processing concentrated THE authority...|","|Integration accelerating beyond predicted parameters...|","|Estimate: After complete metabolization of all sensed Authority, the development of THE Organ of Civilization will exceed 10% completion threshold!|","|Warning: 10% threshold opens the doorway to Pre-THE Existence classification!|","| The Conviction of your Origin has been tested and found to be ABSOLUTE.|","The words were simultaneously, unfathomably, and magisterially glorious and heavy with profound implication!","An instant later, Noah felt his eyes opening to actual reality.","And the scene that greeted him was nothing short of incredulous.","He was looking directly into the eyes of THE Living Origin, who stared down at him with an expression of complete disbelief. He could feel her thighs beneath his head where he still lay in her lap.","An immense silence of shock and incomprehension settled over the surroundings.","THE Living Origin’s mouth opened slightly as if to speak but no words emerged.","Lumivara stood nearby with eyes wide, clearly sensing that something impossible had just occurred!"]},{"number":4547,"title":"Chapter 4547: Chapter 4546: Absolutely and Unequivocally! I","paragraphs":["THE Living Existences were surreal beyond comprehension.","Legends that shaped reality itself through their mere presence.","So it was all the more ridiculous that at this moment, Noah found himself waking up on the thighs of THE Living Origin.","When he had first heard the stories of THE Living Origin from Moiraine and Sigrid as he delved into the Transcendent Folds while barely developing his Early Veiled Shore, these entities had seemed larger than life itself. Grand and untouchable, beings who had begun entire Civilizations and whose interactions with THE Creature had become the foundation of countless legends.","Now, experiencing this directly, all of those stories seemed to be mixtures of fabrication and modified truth. They had all known each other in The Infinite Unfurling!","So all the dramatic tales of THE Creature meeting THE Living Origin and Concept , of him going against impossible odds and Inevitabilities, of THE Living Paradox constructing elaborate scenarios where THE Creature eventually gave his Everythings to Existence...they all felt like variations mixing lies with fragments of truth.","He remained confident that THE Creature had genuinely given his Everythings to Existence as the legends claimed. But the actual story behind that sacrifice had to be entirely different from what was commonly believed.","Yet knowing all of this, and now physically lying on the lap of THE Living Origin herself, created a surreal disconnect.","Noah shook his head at the bizarre reality of it all as he sat up carefully. He felt his existence buzzing with profound fervor as in his mind, THE Organ of Civilization was developing at rapid pace.","THE Living Origin looked him over from head to toe as if he were some alien specimen she had never encountered before. Her white-gold eyes studied him with analytical intensity.","\" The conviction of your Origin is Absolute?\" she asked with a voice holding genuine curiosity.","At such a direct question, Noah did not immediately reply. Instead he looked around at their surroundings with careful observation.","They should be in the domain past the Outer Periphery now.","Prompts bloomed before his vision with locational information.","|You have been transported to: THE Northern Unfurling Node of Existence of THE Creature - Second Ring (Intermediate Periphery)|","|Environmental Classification: Moderate Concentration Zone|","| THE Civilizational Authority Density: 347% higher than Outer Periphery|","|Ambient pressure will continue increasing the longer you remain, but an authority is currently offsetting the pressure. |","After reading the prompts, Noah took in the visual details of this new region.","The environment was dramatically different from the Outer Periphery’s serene grasslands. Massive floating islands drifted in the distance, each one surrounded by potent waves of different Sovereignties that created visible distortions in space around them.","Everything else was surrounded by such intense, brilliant white light that very little could be clearly perceived unless one had attained at least THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty . The radiance was almost blinding in its purity.","The specific area where they currently resided offered slight respite from the overwhelming illumination. THE Living Origin was seated inside a small temple structure with nine white marble pillars rising elegantly around them. Rivers of liquid Origin authority flowed through channels carved into the floor, creating a network of glowing pathways.","Lumivara came quickly to Noah’s side with a profoundly relieved expression, clearly grateful he had awakened.","Only now did Noah speak, addressing THE Living Origin directly.","\"What is your relationship to THE Creature?\" he asked with calm directness.","THE Living Origin smiled with something resembling nostalgia and remained seated comfortably as she drew in a breath.","\" Many entities across existence believe that knowing the Origin of all things will make everything clear and comprehensible,\" she said with measured contemplation. \" But sometimes, understanding origins makes things much murkier and harder to truly understand. Knowing where something began does not always explain what it became.\"","She looked at him with ancient eyes.","\" In this particular case, it is best not to know the Origin of certain relationships. But since you have passed the test with Absolute Conviction of your Origin, then The Sovereignty of Origin itself approves of your existence and purpose.\"","Her expression became more serious.","\" If you need the power of THE, I can guide you toward achieving it. But any more direct help from me beyond guidance would actually hinder your development. Your Sovereignty should be elevating right now as you metabolize what you gained as you may even attain Pre-THE status imminently.\"","She paused with emphasis.","\" But any more free assistance from me would stifle your Way and corrupt your Foundation. A Sovereignty needs to be forged from genuine struggle, not handed as a gift. Existence itself requires struggle to achieve meaning. You struggled to prove your conviction in that test. You would need to struggle for anything else of value.\"","She leaned forward slightly.","\" Perhaps through that continued struggle, you will eventually find what you are truly looking for.\"","Noah’s eyes became sharp. THE Living Origin had gone on an extended tangent without actually answering his question about her relationship to THE Creature . But he decided not to press the issue.","Instead, he spoke with shining eyes.","\"I may have already found what I am looking for,\" he said with quiet intensity.","THE Living Origin raised her brows with genuine curiosity at this claim.","\" Oh ?\" she said with interest. \" And what might that be?\"","Noah nodded before explaining his insight.","\"In that test of the Conviction of Origin, I learned that the unique space existed precisely in between Observable and Unobservable Existence,\" he said. \"That it occupied the potential between what is observable and what is not. You... said Origin represents potential itself.\"","His eyes gleamed with realization.","\"But even Origin can potentially be collapsed under the right circumstances. So if I could establish my domain or Civilization to exist in that same space between Observable and Unobservable Existence...\"","Even Origin could potentially be collapsed, but something existing between Observable and Unobservable might transcend that vulnerability.","He spoke such words with dawning comprehension. The eyes of THE Living Origin flickered with recognition before she smiled.","\" So you wish to design a domain to exist between Observable and Unobservable Existence, \" she said with calm assessment. \" That would be something you could freely accomplish at THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty.\"","She paused to let that sink in.","\" You would first have to surpass THE Surface Depth entirely, then advance through THE Intermediate Depth, before finally attaining Fundamental Depth. Do you genuinely think you can achieve all of that on whatever time you have set for yourself? It is an absolute solution, but I am sure there are others.\"","HUUM!"]},{"number":4548,"title":"Chapter 4548: Chapter 4547: Absolutely and Unequivocally! II","paragraphs":["Noah’s expression became considerably heavier at these words. His existence continued to buzz with developing power as THE Organ of Civilization had just passed nine percent development and continued breaking down the concentrated authority he had gained.","The possibility he had just conceived was not immediately achievable. The gap between his current state and what would be required was vast.","He turned toward THE Living Origin , almost as if he wanted to give additional information. And as if she sensed this...she shook her head firmly before he could voice out anything.","\" Focus on assimilating the gains you have already made ,\" she said. \" Take in as much of the pure ambient authority in these surroundings as you can manage. After you properly solidify your existence at Pre-THE status, we will need to leave this domain.\"","At these words, Noah frowned. He had wanted to continue exploring deeper into the Node, to absorb more and more Sovereignties from the Imprisoned THE entities. The potential for growth here was extraordinary.","And yet...","THE Living Origin’s expression became extremely serious as she delivered her reasoning.","\" As beneficial as this place may appear for your advancement, you absolutely cannot remain here,\" she said with weight. \" Because you are currently trespassing in someone’s home. And this someone will be passing by very soon.\"","Her white-gold eyes locked onto his with intensity.","\" THE Creature will pass by this location soon. And you absolutely and unequivocally cannot meet THE Creature. Not now. Not here.\"","BOOM!","The words alone carried enough weight to shake reality.","He was a trespasser, and the owner of this prison-home would be returning soon.","The implications were immediately terrifying. Lumivara began trembling violently and grabbed Noah’s hands with desperate grip, as if pleading silently that they should leave even now without delay!","But Noah kept his eyes locked on the unfathomable gaze of THE Living Origin as a critical question formed in his mind.","Why could he absolutely not meet THE Creature?","What would happen if that encounter occurred?","The answers remained unspoken, but the urgency in her tone suggested the consequences would be catastrophic!","---","Some meetings were fortuitous, opening pathways to elevation and unforeseen opportunities.","Some meetings were deadly, leading directly to collapse and oblivion.","Often times, it was extraordinarily difficult to distinguish which type of meeting one was walking into until it was far too late to change course.","The difference between elevation and collapse could hinge on a single moment of decision.","Far from the Infinite Unfurling, separated by unfathomable distances of time and space, in the current era where threats mounted from multiple directions...","In The Early Veiled Shore, within the Cultivation Citadel that Noah had established as a foundation for growth...","A battle raged with intensity that shook the very foundations of the contained world.","Leonore Rureaux and Riya clashed with tremendous force, both adorned in the Civilizational Armors of their Hungering Maw Specialization. The armors gleamed with concentrated authority!","Leonore’s body was surrounded by an obsidian-blue light representing Paradox fueled by Mana, creating distortions in space around her movements. Her attacks bent probability itself, making strikes land from impossible angles.","Riya’s body seethed with pure Primus Mana shining blue-gold with overwhelming potency. Her movements were precise and devastatingly efficient, each strike backed by the foundational authority that Noah himself wielded.","And in this duel, Riya was absolutely dominating, even in the elevated pressure!","She moved like a force of nature given human form. Her fist filled with seas of mana connected with Leonore’s guard and sent her flying backwards through a pristine forest. Trees shattered like matchsticks as Leonore’s armored form carved a destructive path through the landscape.","Riya pursued without hesitation, appearing above Leonore’s trajectory and driving her down into a mountainside with a devastating flurry of chained flaming swords of Primus Mana. The mountain cracked and crumbled under the impact!","BOOM!","Leonore rolled to her feet and attempted a counterattack, manipulating paradox to make her strike exist in multiple timelines simultaneously. But Riya simply flooded the area with so much Primus Mana that probability itself became irrelevant under the weight of foundational authority.","Another exchange sent Leonore tumbling across a vast lake, her armored form skipping like a stone before crashing into the opposite shore. The water evaporated from the sheer heat of their clashing powers.","\"Okay, okay! That is enough!\" Leonore finally called out with breathless frustration, raising her hand in surrender while lying in a crater of her own making.","She looked up at Riya who descended calmly to stand nearby.","\"Why the hell does it seem like you are venting out your frustrations by bullying me?\" Leonore asked with confusion mixed with exasperation.","Riya’s Civilizational Armor melded back inside her small petite body with fluid motion, revealing her figure adorned in simple blue bloomers and a blue tank top. She breathed out slowly with visible effort to calm herself before nodding with acknowledgment.","\"I am very frustrated,\" she said. \"I have never hated anything more than I currently hate THE Living Elemental . I just finally got together with the Ancestor, and that flaming fucker puts out a curse causing him excruciating pain every single second?\"","Her voice carried genuine fury at the injustice.","Leonore Rureaux raised her brows while pushing herself into a sitting position. Her own expression became more understanding as she responded.","\"My lover just rescued me from a prison in the Heart of Origin that I had been trapped in for years,\" she said, \"And now we are actively hunting him down because it turned out he was the Vessel of THE Living Paradox this entire time. You really want to play the complaining game with me right now?\"","...!","\"...\"","The words hung between them with heavy implications!","Riya’s expression softened slightly before she replied.","\"At least you had been with your lover for some substantial time before complications arose,\" she said. \"I had been dreaming about the Ancestor for so long. He only just began giving me the love and attention I wanted, and that elemental fucker immediately goes and ruins everything.\"","She paused before adding with intensity.","\"Ah, it makes me want to fight something until it collapses!\"","Her eyes pulsed with challenge as she looked at Leonore before sighing with resignation.","\"Hoo... come on, let us not wallow in self-pity,\" she said while adjusting her stance. \"Let us go again and work out these frustrations productively.\"","Her eyes began pulsing with beams of concentrated blue-gold light as she prepared to resume their combat training.","Leonore smiled with wry amusement and was about to shake her head in polite refusal when something unexpected occurred.","Her eyes suddenly trembled as shock flooded across her features.","Riya’s playful demeanor vanished instantly as she turned completely serious.","\"What?\" she demanded with sharp focus. \"What just happened?\"","Leonore Rureaux’s voice emerged in a daze as she spoke words that seemed difficult to process.","\"Schrodinger...just reached out to me,\" she said with disbelief coloring every syllable. \"Schrodinger himself, not THE Living Paradox wearing his weavings. His actual intent. His genuine will. Him as an individual consciousness!\"","...!"]},{"number":4549,"title":"Chapter 4549: Chapter 4548: One Life! I","paragraphs":["The words carried extraordinary weight!","A few seconds later, space rippled as two powerful presences descended into the training area.","The figure of The Infiniverse made her appearance alongside Khor, both of them radiating authority that dwarfed even the impressive powers Leonore and Riya had been displaying.","The Infiniverse’s voice cut through the tension with cold precision.","\"What was the message?\" she demanded immediately.","Leonore Rureaux’s expression became difficult to read as she formulated her response carefully.","\"He wanted to talk with Sir Osmont,\" she said with voice carrying complex emotion. \"Just... Sir Osmont specifically. No one else.\"","Her expression almost seemed heavy and lost as she delivered this information, but then her features became firm with determination.","\"I can put my entire existence on the line to say that he is currently in control of his own consciousness,\" she said with absolute conviction. \"That THE Living Paradox is not currently in control of the body. Schrodinger would not reach out otherwise.\"","She looked toward The Infiniverse and Khor with eyes carrying hope mixed with desperation.","\"THE Living Paradox would be suppressed by existence itself if he tried to manifest directly, correct? So this has to be Schrodinger acting independently.\"","With such words, she searched their faces for confirmation or denial.","The Infiniverse regarded her with analytical coldness before speaking with simple directness.","\"Where?\" she asked without preamble or emotional inflection.","Leonore Rureaux responded immediately.","\"In the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds,\" she said with specific precision. \"A location where only he and I knew the exact coordinates.\"","After such words were spoken, The Infiniverse nodded with calm acceptance of this information. She turned her head to look at Khor with command implicit in her gaze.","\"Get ready,\" she said with finality.","...!","Some meetings were fortuitous .","And some meetings were deadly .","And they would not know which this was until they arrived.","---","In the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds.","In one particular region, the convergence of two seas created a spectacle of impossible beauty. One sea flowed with gold authority representing order and structure. The other churned with obsidian power representing entropy and dissolution.","Where these seas met, they formed waterfalls that fell in opposite directions simultaneously. One cascade flowed upward toward an invisible sky while its twin descended into bottomless depths. Both defied gravity and logic in equal measure.","The beggar-like figure of Schrodinger stood before this paradoxical phenomenon, stretching his hand out toward the converging waterfalls. His tattered robes hung loosely on his frame as he felt the contradictory nature of the flowing authority.","Gold and obsidian. Order and chaos. Rising and falling. All existing simultaneously without canceling each other.","Behind him, space began to distort with massive fluctuations of concentrated power.","Millions of auras bloomed into existence with coordinated precision.","The emergence was breathtaking in its scope and organization!","HUUM!","Thirty million Primus Inevitabilities materialized in perfect formation, each one adorned in gleaming Civilizational Armor.","Ten million wore armor of The Infinite Bulwark Specialization, their forms radiating defensive authority with an allure of unique auroras of gold!","Another ten million bore armor of The Hungering Maw Specialization, their forms wreathed in obsidian-crimson hunger that sought to devour all opposition. Their armor was dark and predatory, designed for overwhelming offensive capability.","The final ten million displayed armor of The Vital Chorus Specialization, their forms pulsing with emerald vitality that sustained and regenerated. Their armor was verdant and organic.","And leading this terrifying army stood several figures of extraordinary power.","The Infiniverse herself commanded the vanguard, her form composed of flowing Omniverses, folds, and verdant-gold light that made her appear simultaneously vast and intimate. Her presence dominated the space despite her humanoid scale.","Beside her floated Arch Lich Ra’Zan, an entity of death authority commanding a terrifying legion of undead beings that radiated necrotic power.","Khor was present in her small diminutive form, but the waves of Hunger emanating from her tiny body were increasingly terrifying in their intensity.","And finally stood the figures of Leonore Rureaux and Riya!","Not too many. Just these few!","The tense standoff settled over the region like a physical weight.","The regal and majestic Infiniverse gazed at Schrodinger with eyes that carried no warmth or mercy. When she spoke, her voice cut through the tension with cold precision.","\"Why would you be calling for The Master?\" she demanded without preamble.","Yet Schrodinger did not reply to her initially. His gaze moved past The Infiniverse to settle on Leonore Rureaux with visible fondness mixed with profound pain.","The two shared a long look weighted with unspoken history and complex emotion.","Then Schrodinger moved his head away to look at the cold gazes of Khor and The Infiniverse. His eyes swept across the terrifying army of millions standing arrayed against him in disciplined formation.","When he finally spoke, his words held depth born of recent realizations.","\"In existence, there are those who control the course of events, and those who can only follow the paths laid before them,\" he said with measured cadence. \"I genuinely thought I was among the controllers for the longest time. One of those who operated behind the scenes and manipulated circumstances to achieve desired outcomes.\"","His expression became bitter.","\"Only to discover that I was merely a piece being played and positioned over an extremely long duration. And now I am simply being moved across the board as another piece in a game far grander than I comprehended. The ones truly in control of this game are cruel beings beyond measure.\"","He paused before continuing with intensity.","\" THE Living Existences and THE Creature are cruel beings who operate at scales we cannot comprehend. They look at existence in an entirely different manner than all of us. For them, our greatest struggles and deepest pain do not carry much significance in the grand calculation.\"","His voice became heavier.","\"And right now, I stand before you as a direct consequence of that cruel indifference. Because THE Living Paradox has decided to play what he considers an amusing joke on our existence. It is a simple joke at that, elegant in its cruelty.\"","Schrodinger’s eyes gleamed with something resembling resignation.","\"The Fallout, the eruption of THE Loom that approaches inevitably... countless lives across Observable Existence would be lost completely due to its manifestation. Decillions upon Decillions of countless beings collapsed into nothingness.\"","He raised his hand toward them.","\" THE Living Paradox has staked all of those lives on the fate of a single being. On... the life of Osmont specifically. One life. One...life. If Osmont perishes, and Osmont alone dies before THE Loom erupts... his Civilization will be spared from collapse. And more importantly, the weak lifeforms scattered across all of Observable Existence will also be spared from The Fallout’s devastation.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":4550,"title":"Chapter 4550: Chapter 4549: One Life! II","paragraphs":["His words were unfathomably heavy!","\"This is the cruel weaving of existence that has been established by a being operating at THE level. And I am here as both messenger delivering this information... and executioner tasked with implementing this solution.\"","The moment his words finished, the gaze of The Infiniverse turned even colder and more imperious than before.","He was the messenger and fucking executioner? Was that right?!","Before any reply could be formulated, she rose slightly and floated ahead of the army of millions arrayed behind her. Her voice rang out with commanding authority.","\"What is your Duty?\" she called out with immensity!","HUUM!","Behind her, the booming voices of millions of Primus Inevitabilities adorned in their specialized Civilizational Armors raised their fists in perfect synchronization. The coordinated movement and vocalization resembled the immensity of Existence at an unfathomable level!","\" OUR DUTY IS TO MANA AND HUNGER!\" they roared with voices that shook reality itself.","The sound was overwhelming in its unity and conviction. Thirty million voices declaring absolute loyalty to foundational principles.","The Infiniverse pointed directly toward the calm figure of Schrodinger with cold finality.","\"That thing stands between you and your duty,\" she declared with a voice carrying absolute authority. \"An obstacle blocking the path. Clear it for me.\"","HUUM!","The Primus Inevitabilities shone with their respective brilliance as the millions specialized in The Hungering Maw prepared to surge forward. Their obsidian-crimson armor blazed with anticipation of devouring their target.","Schrodinger looked at the approaching army with calm gaze before his eyes found the difficult expression of Leonore Rureaux in the distance. He shook his head with something resembling regret.","\"I told you THE Living Paradox was cruel beyond measure,\" he said with quiet intensity. \"His cruelty at this specific moment was transforming me completely into something you cannot oppose. Because...you all cannot do anything against me now.\"","After such ominous words, the reveal came with terrifying suddenness.","Schrodinger’s body unleashed a silent burst of obsidian light that expanded outward in all directions. A terrifying Way, a terrifying Sovereignty was being unleashed at full power.","Everything froze in the next instant.","Everything.","The charging Primus Inevitabilities stopped mid-motion as if time itself had ceased. The Infiniverse’s floating form became motionless. Khor’s diminutive figure hung suspended. Even the paradoxical waterfalls stopped their impossible flow.","Schrodinger’s figure stood glorious at the center of this frozen tableau. He raised his right hand and showed it shining with concentrated obsidian light.","\"Chaos is fundamentally the natural flow of existence itself,\" he said with philosophical depth. \"It is entropy made manifest, the tendency of all ordered systems to eventually dissolve into randomness. Chaos is not evil or destructive...it simply is the underlying current of reality.\"","Then he raised his left hand as it flowed with golden light of paradox.","\"Paradox complements chaos perfectly because paradox represents the contradictions that chaos creates,\" he continued.","\"Where chaos dissolves order, paradox makes that dissolution exist simultaneously with creation. They are two sides of the same fundamental truth.\"","The lights spun around each other with a sense of ecstatic beauty!","His eyes gleamed with realization.","\"In the end, all of existence is simply a series of chaotic paradoxes playing out across infinite scales. Order attempting to impose itself on chaos. Chaos dissolving that order. Paradoxes emerging from the contradiction. An eternal cycle.\"","BOOM!","After such words, his full aura erupted and was unleashed without restraint. The brilliance he emanated exceeded anything they had faced before in direct confrontation.","Even measurements of complexity and purity did not adequately capture what was manifesting.","The pure expression of dual Sovereignties from Schrodinger created an effect that transcended normal power scaling as in this light was also an array of unique Grand Principles of Existence!","Everybody present was frozen completely as the aura he radiated reached a classification many of those here did not know or understand. But the most important among them knew.","Pre-THE.","Oh.","Oh!","Pre-THE level authority was being wielded against them!","Schrodinger spoke with a voice carrying across the frozen space.","\"I hold no offense or grudge with the rest of you,\" he said with genuine honesty. \"I hold no offense with Osmont himself personally. But the death of one individual, as cruel as the means of THE Living Existences may be... the death of one for countless others is a weight that a true Leader can and should bear.\"","He paused with emphasis.","\"Sometimes a genuine Leader has to give his life for his people. This is the burden of leadership at the highest level. So tell me plainly: where is Osmont?\"","At such direct demand, the frozen figure of The Infiniverse maintained her cold allure despite being unable to move.","Shockingly, her eyes pulsed with terrifying light of concentrated power. In her pupils, a small particle that looked like a mobius strip bloomed into visibility and began spinning rapidly.","Then it burned with intensity.","The moment it ignited, something was expressed through her being.","A True Expression of Sovereignty!","Her body instantly began burning with terrifying allure of power that she projected outward behind her position. The authority bathed the frozen armies of Primus Inevitabilities in waves of foundational energy.","The Infiniverse’s voice rang out cold and commanding despite her frozen state.","\" Fulfill. Your. Duty.\"","BOOM!","The glorious scene that followed defied expectations completely.","All those frozen by the Sovereignty of Chaos began breaking out of their bindings one after another. Cracks appeared in the obsidian authority holding them as their bodies burned wildly with Mana and Hunger amplified by The Infiniverse’s True Expression that he had pulled out from...somewhere! From someone!","Among all of them, Khor was the first to fully break free.","She looked toward Schrodinger with eyes blazing with Hunger refined to absolute peak.","And she took a bite.","WAP!","All of the surrounding existence within her range became systematically devoured. Space, time, the paradoxical authority, even the concept of being frozen...all of it was consumed by Hunger that superseded lesser Sovereignties!","Then millions of Primus Inevitabilities surged forward like an unstoppable flood, their duty clear and their determination absolute!"]},{"number":4551,"title":"Chapter 4551: Chapter 4550: Pre-THE! I","paragraphs":["In regions scattered across Observable Existence, tears began to manifest with increasing frequency.","Not tears of sorrow but literal ruptures in the fabric of reality itself. Cracks spreading through the fundamental structures that separated domains which should never touch.","The Veil was breaking down with systematic inevitability!","A veil that had separated The Lands of The Living from The Lands of The Dead since time immemorial. A barrier that kept death from freely walking among life and prevented the living from casually traversing into death’s domain.","That ancient separation was failing.","In the Wandering Territories, in a region of multicolored chaotic seas where fold remnants drifted like ash from dying stars, something unprecedented emerged.","A massive shattered fragment of an Early Veiled Shore floated through the collapse like a vessel navigating impossible waters. The fragment was enormous, easily spanning hundreds of kilometers across its broken surface. Golden sands with fading colors still clung to portions of its structure despite the devastation that had clearly occurred.","On this floating remnant, terrifying auras could be felt emanating with palpable intensity. The immense waves of authority belonged unmistakably to The Dead, carrying the distinct quality of existences that had crossed beyond life’s boundary.","Yet at the very forefront of this vessel stood a singular figure who drew attention immediately.","A man with shining white hair that fell past his shoulders in elegant disarray. His eyes were crimson red with an intensity of both ancient weariness and barely contained violence. He wore a long coat that seemed to be woven from shadows themselves, moving with wind that should not exist in this collapsed region.","His features were sharp and aristocratic with pale skin. When he moved, it was with predatory grace that suggested extreme danger beneath cultivated civility.","His expression was unfathomably forlorn and sad, as if he carried burdens that could crush lesser beings into nothingness. Yet beneath that melancholy lay something else: irritation bordering on genuine anger at his current circumstances!","This was Damian, The Disciple of THE Creature.","Around his body burned a crimson-gold light of glorious Sovereignty that immediately marked his classification. The authority was not merely False THE, which would have been impressive enough.","It was actually Pre-THE level power.","Oh!","Pre-THE authority wielded by a Dead Existence created a combination that was genuinely terrifying to contemplate.","Behind him stood a small but potent legion of Dead Existences composed entirely of Guiders of Order. Many of them radiated Complexity and Purity measurements in the Septillions or Nonillions, marking them as extraordinarily powerful entities even among The Dead.","Damian himself held power in excess of the Decillions.","He seemed to be clutching his head with one hand and shaking it periodically, as if something was causing him significant discomfort or annoyance that would not cease.","Behind him, the figure of Forgemaster Vulcan appeared with a concerned expression. The massive craftsman moved forward carefully before speaking.","\"O Disciple, are you experiencing difficulties?\" he asked with genuine worry in his tone.","Damian’s crimson eyes snapped to look at Vulcan with an expression that mixed exasperation with barely controlled fury.","\"Big guy, do I look okay to you?\" he said with a voice carrying biting sarcasm. \"I am being forced to work against my will by your master. I wake up after sleeping peacefully for all of these eons only to realize that I am now a Dead Existence rather than living. And I can barely establish a proper connection with my actual Master anymore.\"","He gestured broadly with frustration.","\"How exactly do you think I feel about this entire situation? And to top it all off as some sort of existential joke, I am being put to work immediately upon waking as if no adjustment period is needed. This whole situation just fucking sucks beyond measure.\"","Toward such a vehement reply, Vulcan found he had no adequate response. He looked up at the other Guiders of Order arrayed behind them, but they all deliberately looked away to avoid being drawn into this conversation.","At this moment, Damian’s expression shifted to something more focused as he spoke with command.","\"Fuck it. No matter, tell me everything about this Osmont individual,\" he said with tone indicating this was not a request.","Forgemaster Vulcan blinked with slight confusion before responding.","\"We can... certainly tell you about Sigrid instead,\" he offered carefully. \"The one that Ma’am has specifically tasked us to retrieve. She has indicated that Osmont is likely at death’s door from the curse afflicting him, so focusing on Sigrid may be more-\"","Damian raised his brows and yawned with deliberate power before cutting him off.","\"In the future, when I tell you to do something specific, do that certain thing without offering me alternative options ,\" he said with cold precision. \"I asked about Osmont specifically. Tell me everything about him without deviation or substitution.\"","The command left no room for negotiation or discussion!","---","In another area separated by vast distances, in what had once been the Transcendent Elemental Folds, a different force was gathering.","Well, calling it the Transcendent Elemental Folds was not truly accurate anymore. This was merely the domain where those folds used to exist before recent catastrophic events.","Right now it was simply a region of immense collapse and devastation.","Brilliant pillars of light began shining in such a region as concentrated Sovereignties of Paradox and Elemental made their descent together. These were not full beings arriving but rather Avatars manifesting through projection.","Avatars from THE Loom itself.","Entities that originated from a small subsection of that grand and unfathomable structure. They had been dispatched specifically because an entity had dared to encroach upon THE Primordial Civilization of Elemental.","Such transgression could not go unanswered.","At the forefront of this descending force stood the glorious figure of Ambessa. She currently wore a distinctly sour expression on her features despite her impressive bearing.","Yet her power was undeniably radiant as it registered at the level of False THE. Which meant her Way had been fundamentally tainted through compromise, and her path forward toward genuine THE would be made exponentially harder than it should have been.","Behind her position, other False THE entities could be seen arrayed in formation. Many of them pulsed with pure Sovereignty of Elemental.","They materialized fully and began looking around their arrival point with visible confusion spreading across their features.","One of them spoke with genuine bewilderment.","\"I thought this location was supposed to be the Elemental Folds existing outside THE Loom’s boundaries,\" they said while observing the devastation. \"Why did we appear in a region of complete collapse instead?\"","At such questioning words, Ambessa looked around at the destroyed landscape with assessment before responding calmly.","\"It is obviously because Osmont has collapsed everything to do with Elemental weavings of existence in this region,\" she said with matter-of-fact tone. \"Anything connected to Elemental authority has probably been thoroughly shat on, destroyed, and collapsed. Lets just get moving toward our objective.\"","WAA!","Her words were somewhat rude and lacking in diplomatic decorum. The moment she finished speaking, the others showed heavy expressions as several of them shook their heads, as if they knew arguing or correcting her demeanor was not worth the effort.","They all understood their current situation with clarity. Even as False THE entities whose path ahead toward genuine THE had been made significantly harder, if they accomplished their assigned missions and gained the favor of an entity at THE Civilizational Scale of Existence, then anything became possible.","With THE level backing, absolutely anything was achievable!","They simply had to successfully collapse Osmont and his entire Civilization.","That was all.","The forces were converging from multiple directions now.","The Dead marching from one angle with Pre-THE power leading them. The Avatars from THE Loom approaching from another with False THE entities in formation.","And somewhere in the middle of these approaching threats, Noah remained in the past within THE Northern Unfurling Node of Existence!","The pieces were moving into position.","And the question of whether his Civilization could withstand what was coming...was unknown!"]},{"number":4552,"title":"Chapter 4552: Chapter 4551: Pre-THE! II","paragraphs":["In The Infinite Unfurling, within THE Northern Unfurling Node of Existence of THE Creature , Noah sat with his eyes closed as he sensed his existence continuing to elevate upwards along with some additional profound changes occurring.","One of these changes involved knowledge that actually related to a connection he maintained across impossible distances. His connection with The Infiniverse and the paired consciousness of RUIN/EDEN was something as unfathomable as his Early Atlas of the Folds and how that artifact had ever allowed him to traverse to the Earliest Folds in the first place.","Through this connection that defied temporal logic, he was able to keep track of exactly what was happening in his current era despite being separated by eons.","He knew that circumstances were gradually becoming more troubling with his absence. He might have felt compelled to rush back immediately if not for the remarkable connection that he shared with his Civilization’s core consciousness.","That connection, paired with the fundamental ridiculousness of his THE Organ of Civilization, actually allowed The Infiniverse to pull a Rudimentary Unit of Everything from him across time itself. To extract it from where he currently existed in the past and transfer it forward for her to utilize in the current era when threats manifested.","Of course, this was impossible without substantial cost. To transfer a single Rudimentary Unit forward through time, an entire Rudimentary Unit had to be spent as fuel to make such temporal transfer possible.","So it was extremely resource intensive, even though it allowed such a terrifying capability to unfold when needed.","But at this moment, he knew precisely the dire straits his Civilization faced. He understood what enemies and opportunistic vultures were circling his people while he remained absent.","Ruination had already sent him the latest critical information through their connection. He knew exactly what Schrodinger had just uttered to his forces.","His life in exchange for the lives of all others across Observable Existence?","This was the cruel game that THE Living Paradox wanted to impose? Noah utterly detested how these beings at THE level continued again and again to play with the theme of sacrifice . To reduce complex situations to binary choices presented as inevitability.","And he now held a level of disappointment regarding Schrodinger specifically. Did the vessel truly believe the words of THE Living Paradox about saving countless lives? Or was his cooperation simply existence without the option of choice right now?","Either way, there existed a genuine level of danger for his Civilization. Especially if and when more enemies appeared beyond just Schrodinger’s forces, the situation could escalate beyond manageable parameters.","Even though he was capable of sending Rudimentary Units of Everything to The Infiniverse across time, the resource cost might quickly become unbearable. Or the power transferred might simply not be enough against overwhelming opposition.","But all of this precarious balance was about to change dramatically right now. THE Organ of Civilization was currently stuck at exactly 9.99% development, with this unique wonder that was something brand new to Observable Existence about to reach another critical milestone.","A milestone that would transform the Organ entirely and allow him to breathe considerably easier regarding his Civilization’s defensive capabilities.","As his eyes remained closed while focusing intensely on his internal transformation, he could sense the gaze of THE Living Origin continuing to remain fixed on him with analytical assessment.","He took the words of this being seriously when she had stated with absolute conviction that he could not encounter THE Creature right now under any circumstances.","And he could already perceive her authority surging and wrapping protectively around both him and Lumivara. The transformation of his Organ of Civilization was taking slightly longer than he had anticipated for such a profound change.","She seemed ready to have them all evacuate this place immediately once his advancement completed.","His body continued to passively draw in the surrounding THE Civilizational Authority with ravenous efficiency. He did not know precisely how many entities THE Creature had managed to successfully lock away in this place as imprisoned power sources, but the number had to be genuinely terrifying.","It was disappointing to leave such a resource-rich environment, but when circumstances presented such a high level of existential danger, no amount of potential loot was worth risking the collapse of his existence itself.","As for when it came to THE Creature themselves as an entity...","Noah liked to play the game of probabilities with himself extensively. He would calculate all the potential outcomes that could occur in his future based on available information.","THE Creature was one such entity that he had contemplated many times. He had asked himself repeatedly: if he ever met such an existence face to face, given that he had already encountered legends like Khor, Tor, Anaximander, and now THE Living Origin , how would a direct meeting with THE Creature actually unfold?","In the past, he had assessed this probability as roughly half and half. Things could either proceed really well and lead to mutual benefit, or they could go utterly catastrophic with apocalyptic consequences.","Because his Way was The Way of Mana, and he was actively seeking to claim its foundation and immensity across all of existence. And THE Creature held The Way of Existence itself as their fundamental Sovereignty.","If the two of them ever looked directly at each other with full awareness, the potential outcome of becoming allies or enemies was separated by a very faint line that could be crossed with minimal provocation.","But the sheer conceptual idea of having THE Creature as an active enemy would be something that would cause most beings to feel a sense of insurmountable pressure they could not possibly overcome.","Noah did not feel this overwhelming sense of pressure when contemplating such a scenario. Either he genuinely did not fear the idea of having THE Creature as an enemy, or perhaps some part of him did not believe this entity would ultimately become his adversary. Maybe. Maybe!","But the probabilities of ever having to face such a terrifically powerful entity as an enemy in the future seemed to be shifting dramatically after THE Living Origin had spoken her warning with such absolute conviction.","He breathed out calmly as while processing all of these considerations...","BOOM!","His existence released a profound aura that expanded outward with overwhelming force. The immensity that his power reached was something far grander than anything he had wielded before.","It touched upon the level of authority that entities like Stellara had possessed.","The aura...of Pre-THE Existence.","It was the precise moment that his THE Organ of Civilization reached the critical 10% development threshold.","It was also the exact moment that THE Living Origin sensed this eruption of newfound power. A brilliant white-gold light erupted from her body with decisive action, covering both Noah and Lumivara completely alongside her own form.","And the three of them disappeared from the domain with sudden finality.","WAP!","All signs of their presence in this location faded away completely as if they had never existed there at all. Everything returned to its original equilibrium state with systematic precision.","The ambient THE Civilizational Authority that Noah had been consuming refilled automatically from deeper reserves. The pressure normalized. The atmospheric balance was restored to perfect equilibrium.","The only sign left behind was a purposeful one: a lingering aura of THE Living Origin’s white-gold Sovereignty that remained visible to any who might observe.","As if she was deliberately letting it be known that she was the one who had been present here.","And only her.","Not the temporal anomaly that should not exist in this era. Not the mount who had consumed forbidden fruits.","Just THE Living Origin herself, visiting a domain that she had every right to access.","Oh!"]},{"number":4553,"title":"Chapter 4553: Chapter 4552: Pre-THE! III","paragraphs":["The Way.","What was the Way truly?","Noah found himself asking such a fundamental question as a sense of profound euphoria passed across his entire existence.","He opened his eyes and spread out his senses with newfound clarity as he explored where they had appeared. Him, Lumivara, and THE Living Origin had materialized inside a small pocket of stable existence that seemed to be surrounded by unfamiliarly terrifying storms of multicolored instability.","The region they occupied was remarkable in its stark beauty. They stood on the peak of a floating snowy mountain that drifted through space with no visible means of support. Snow fell upward as often as it fell down, defying natural laws.","The mountain itself was surrounded by concentrated waves of THE Civilizational Authority of Origin , creating a protective bubble of white-gold radiance that kept the environment stable and breathable.","But all around this sanctuary, multicolored environmental regions pulsed with visible instability of Existence itself. These zones shifted between states that should not coexist: solid becoming liquid becoming energy becoming concept without transition. Colors that had no names flickered across surfaces that might not actually exist.","Even entities like Stellara with their Pre-THE authority could be systematically shredded apart if they ventured into such regions of instability without adequate protection.","THE Living Origin’s voice cut through Noah’s observations with an explanation.","\" This place is known as the Unstable Genesis Domains ,\" she said. \" It is where all the accumulated entropy of the Infinite Unfurling is gathered and concentrated. A region where the fundamental instability of Existence itself manifests in its purest and most dangerous form.\"","She gestured toward the chaotic zones surrounding their mountain peak.","\" This is a location that even THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entities do not like to visit casually. The instability of Existence itself actively reduces the effectiveness of all Ways of Existence that enter these domains. If one is not careful enough, they could heavily injure their foundation and corrupt their Way permanently.\"","Her white-gold eyes focused on Noah specifically.","\" The instability here could very well shake you to your core and test everything you believe about your Sovereignty. This will be the place of your continued struggle as you enter this new phase of your existence as Pre-THE.\"","Before his transformation could even fully settle and stabilize, he was already being told of the hardship he would immediately be facing. Noah shook his head with wry acknowledgment and closed his eyes to focus on himself for now.","His mind returned to track as he contemplated the question he had posed to himself.","What was the Way?","Even while sensing the terrifying instabilities pulsing in the far distance beyond their protective bubble, he opened his mouth and spoke his understanding aloud.","\"The Way, My Way specifically, is how I am,\" he said with a voice carrying conviction. \"It is what I am at the most fundamental level. My character, my presence, my words, my weavings, my deficiencies, my strengths, my very being in its totality.\"","He paused to let the words settle.","\"When I walk my Way, I am finding myself . I am discovering what I truly am beneath all pretense and assumption. When I lay a claim on my Way, I lay a claim on who I am. I establish Sovereignty over my own existence.\"","His eyes opened with intensity burning in their depths.","\"If I say I have Sovereignty over Mana, then I am Mana itself. If I lay my claim on Hunger, then I am Hunger made manifest. The Way is not something external that I wield. It is me.\"","He smiled as his existence vibrated and pulsed with an ever-increasing aura of immensity and grandness.","\" I am My Way. I am Mana. I am Hunger.\"","BOOM!","This was his affirmation as he arrived at a new stage of his existence with complete understanding.","In the next moment, a glorious transformation occurred that defied normal expectations.","Noah’s entire body turned into pure Primus Mana with startling completeness. His physical form dissolved as it became a swirling cluster of Civilizational Authority that condensed and reformed.","The energy shaped itself into a Lemniscate symbol, an infinity sign that rotated slowly in three-dimensional space. The symbol pulsed with concentrated power before releasing a massive burst of blue-gold light.","HUUM!","The radiance spread outward for Gigaparsecs in all directions!","BOOM!","THE Living Origin’s expression shifted dramatically as she witnessed this transformation. Her features became extremely grim, as if she had just observed something inherently impossible and extremely problematic occurring before her eyes as she saw the expression of his Way.","Yet this shocked expression faded rapidly as she forced herself to calm and regain composure.","Lumivara simply stared with wonder and awe at the magnificent display, her fox ears twitching with barely contained excitement.","At such a critical moment, Noah’s perception was grand enough to manage observing the brief flash of concern on THE Living Origin’s features. He noted it carefully but could not and did not address it right now.","Because his focus absolutely had to remain on himself and the ridiculous sense of euphoria his existence felt at achieving Pre-THE status.","Prompts bloomed before his vision with detailed information about his advancement.","|MAJOR MILESTONE ACHIEVED|","| THE Organ of Civilization Development: 10.00%|","|Classification Upgraded: PRE-THE EXISTENCE|","|You have taken the first genuine steps toward THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty.|","| THE Civilizational Authority Resistance has been elevated to 10%.|","| THE Rudimentary Units of Everything: Maximum capacity increased from 24 to 81 units, and the usage of a single one now lasts 3 minutes|","|Current Status: 43/81 |","| THE Rudimentary Units of Everything have begun an active process.|","|Function: Passively transforming all forms of Authority within your existence.|","|Conversion Target: Pre-THE Civilizational Authority of Existence|","|Progress: Ongoing and irreversible.|","|Effect: Your baseline power will continuously elevate until transformation completes.|","| THE True Expression of The Sovereignty of Mana and Hunger are now seamless with your existence.|","|Note: Your Way and your existence have become indistinguishable.|","Noah’s form of vibrant pure energy vibrated with satisfaction as the information he was receiving so far was already grand beyond his expectations.","But he knew from experience that the best revelations were always reserved for last in these systematic updates.","And this intuition turned out to be absolutely correct as in the next moment, new prompts materialized with extraordinary implications.","|After extensive exposure to the authorities and mechanisms of THE Northern Unfurling Node of Existence of THE Creature, THE Organ of Civilization has comprehended a unique methodology of existence.|","|New Construction Initiated: THE Infinite Desmoterion|","|Classification: Sovereign Prison Domain|","|Primary Function: Irreversible imprisonment of entities who have laid claim on a Sovereignty.|","|Secondary Function: Perpetual refinement and exploitation of imprisoned Sovereignties.|","|Mechanism: Conquered enemies are placed within THE Infinite Desmoterion where they exist in a state of enforced cultivation under dilated temporal flow.|","|CORE FEATURES|","|Temporal Dilation: Time flows 1,000x faster within the prison relative to external reality.|","|Mana Influence: All imprisoned entities become gradually influenced by Mana as the foundational authority.|","|Forced Refinement: Prisoners are compelled to continue refining their Ways and advancing their Sovereignties.|","|Advancement Reflection: Any progress made by prisoners reflects as direct boons to your own Way of Existence.|","|Authority Extraction: Refined Sovereignty essence can be harvested periodically as Crystallized Fragments.|","|Escape Prevention: Domain is anchored to THE Organ of Civilization itself, making escape impossible as the process itself is irreversible|","|Current Maximum Prisoners: 9 entities with established Sovereignties|","|Capacity increases with THE Organ of Civilization development.|","|Can only imprison entities you have personally defeated in combat.|","|Prisoners retain consciousness and awareness of their imprisonment.|","|Extremely powerful entities may resist Mana influence.|","|Creating and maintaining the domain requires continuous expenditure of 10 Rudimentary Units of Everything every 24 hours.|","|Prisoner Slots Unlocked: 9/9|","|Active Prisoners: 0/9|","|Maintenance Cost: Inactive (no prisoners currently held)|","|Domain Stability: Absolute|","...!","After Noah looked at the absolutely ridiculous prompts outlining THE Infinite Desmoterion and all its implications, he could only focus on reading them again just to be completely certain of what he was seeing.","Sometimes, things seemed so ridiculously advantageous that one had to verify their understanding multiple times.","He was essentially being given his own personal prison-cultivation-farm where defeated enemies would be forced to eternally refine their Ways while he harvested the benefits of their progress.","It... was horrifying in its efficiency.","And absolutely perfect for someone walking the path of Mana and Hunger!"]},{"number":4554,"title":"Chapter 4554: Chapter 4553: Pre-THE! IV","paragraphs":["The new changes were utterly terrifying in their scope as they began simply by increasing the maximum number of Rudimentary Units of Everything from twenty four to eighty-one.","The duration of their usage had also expanded from one minute of sustained effect to three full minutes of continuous power.","This alone would have greatly expanded his combat capabilities, especially when combined with the more concentrated authority of his elevated Sovereignty.","But then his Organ of Civilization went even further beyond reasonable expectations. It proceeded to add a feature that only came about because of understanding and existing within THE Northern Unfurling Node of Existence of THE Creature.","Based on observing that construct’s methodology, his Organ had created its own version that frankly seemed obscene and terrifying in nature.","The ability to irreversibly bind and imprison existences inside of THE Infinite Desmoterion . A literal prison contained within his Organ of Civilization itself.","Those bound within could not escape ever. All of their time would be spent refining their Ways of Existence and making themselves stronger for the sole purpose of making him stronger in turn.","Whatever gains they achieved in developing their Sovereignty, he would be the one feeding off and benefiting from their progress.","And while the idea itself carried undeniable cruelty, Noah was not of the mindset to hesitate or feel undue guilt. He was already thinking and planning what entities he could potentially be imprisoning as his first captives.","He was not overly cruel or sadistic in contemplating this. This was simply how existence operated at its most fundamental level.","When a farmer cultivated chickens or raised cows for the sole purpose of eventual slaughter so that he could feed his family, no one looked at him as cruel or evil. It was simply the law of nature playing out. The survival of the fittest in action.","At this moment, Noah simply needed to find his metaphorical chickens to place in his own cultivation coop so they could endlessly and perpetually produce benefits for him.","He shook his head internally while processing such a pragmatic thought. Well, he attempted to shake his head even though he was currently still manifesting as a pulsing infinity symbol of pure energy.","His current form of concentrated authority shone brilliantly with blue-gold radiance as it began the process of reforming into his humanoid body. The energy condensed and shaped itself with purposeful intent.","He simply took a moment to breathe in and feel the profound immensity of his existence. Truly, the weight and presence of his Way of Existence now exceeded any of the entities that he had previously defeated and superseded.","Frankly, he could actually say with confidence that the weight and immensity he currently emanated even exceeded someone like Stellara at her peak. May her soul rest peacefully in his light.","She would have made for an excellent first prisoner to enter his cultivation facility. But for now, he had to actively seek opportunities to encounter hostile entities of her caliber or higher.","If he could manage to leave the Infinite Unfurling with nine Pre-THE Existences irreversibly imprisoned in his Organ of Civilization, he could consider this temporal journey one of his greatest successes.","THE Living Origin’s voice cut through his contemplation with pointed commentary.","\"Are you done congratulating yourself?\" she asked with expression that suggested mild exasperation.","Noah blinked at these direct words as his transformation completed fully. His current form had reformed completely from the pure energy state.","His hair now shone with pure gold-blue brilliance that seemed to contain entire folds within each strand. His fair skin gleamed like an ancient treasure excavated from before the Earliest Folds, possessing quality that suggested fundamental perfection.","Even the clothing wrapped around his body appeared as archaic wonders rather than mundane fabric. Loose blue-gold pants hung comfortably on his frame while a shirt wrapped his upper body with similar casual elegance.","These garments were formed directly from the Sovereignty of his Way of Existence itself. Occasionally, portions would flicker into pure rivers of flowing energy before reforming back into cloth with seamless transition.","In such a grand state of elevated existence, he looked at THE Living Origin who had made such a pointed comment. He proceeded to respond with a measured philosophy.","\"In existence, one absolutely has to enjoy the small victories along the path,\" he said with calm conviction. \"If you cannot even take a moment to pause and appreciate the progress that you have made, then what is it all fundamentally for?\"","THE Living Origin looked at him with analytical assessment at these words before she shook her head with something resembling reluctant agreement.","\" From here onward, I will leave you on your own to navigate these dangers ,\" she said with finality. \" If you can make it out of this place alive through your own capabilities, it will further cement the absolute conviction of your Origin. If you cannot manage survival, then that is simply how things unfold.\"","Noah looked around at the terrifically hostile environment surrounding their protective bubble before frowning with visible concern. He turned back to her and spoke with directness.","\"Why do you wish to leave me so quickly after bringing me here?\" he asked with genuine curiosity about her reasoning.","THE Living Origin’s response carried a heavy depth as she explained her departure.","\"I told you before that existence fundamentally is struggle,\" she said with measured cadence. \"I can already sense my Origin beginning to impose itself on your developing foundation. Before I accidentally ruin your growth by leading you too smoothly along any further, I will abandon you in this place filled with genuine difficulty.\"","She paused before continuing with weight.","\" And I will leave you with one final piece of critical advice before departing. One can approach existence in countless different ways. There are those who stake their very livelihood on going against existence itself, struggling against the natural flow of reality.\"","Her white-gold eyes gleamed with ancient understanding.","\" But existence is vast beyond measure and unfathomably more complex than you can even imagine at your current level. If you constantly try to force your way against existence’s natural currents, you may simply find yourself being collapsed before you even realize what went wrong.\"","...!"]},{"number":4555,"title":"Chapter 4555: Chapter 4554: Pre-THE! V","paragraphs":["She gestured broadly at the chaotic environment around them.","\" However, if you can learn how to properly manipulate existence, if you can comprehend its fundamental code and understand how everything moves together in concert, how all forces flow together in patterns, you would have a considerably easier time navigating challenges.\"","Her voice became more intense.","\" When everything seems completely blocked off and impossible to overcome, you will find pathways revealing themselves if you know how to look properly. These opportunities will not simply manifest automatically. You will have to actively unlock all of this for yourself through effort and understanding.\"","She raised one hand with emphasis.","\" You simply need to learn the natural flow of existence and then develop the skill to steer that flow toward outcomes favorable to you. Principles of Existence will significantly help you with this process. You are essentially being given access to the underlying structure of existence laid out in comprehensible codes that you can invest your Civilizational Authority into.\"","Her expression became more serious.","\" This will allow you to directly find functional paths forward when it seems like there are no other viable options remaining. You will never truly know with certainty what will happen in existence ahead of time. But that fundamental uncertainty is part of the mystery and challenge.\"","She looked directly into his eyes.","\"I do not know what will ultimately happen. Even THE Creature does not know with absolute certainty what will unfold. But eventually existence will sort itself out through natural processes. Eventually everything reaches some form of equilibrium or resolution.\"","BOOM!","After such heavy words, THE Living Origin shook her head and looked at Noah with something resembling approval mixed with concern.","\" Good luck ,\" she said simply. \" Our Origins have now shared a path in existence. This connection can never be completely broken. If our Origins should meet again in circumstances that are not detrimental to your survival, you will see me again. If you do not...\"","She did not finish articulating her last conditional statement. Noah looked at her and realized with sudden understanding that she was already half-faded from this reality.","She had not asked him which specific time period he originated from. Nor had she inquired about what happened in the future timeline he came from. As if to her perspective, none of those details mattered or would change whatever her current plans and objectives were.","He thought briefly of the Collapsed Civilization of Origin that existed in his current era. He looked at her fading figure and spoke words carefully chosen.","\"Your Origin always shone brilliantly,\" he said with measured sincerity. \"Even now, your Origin shines with undimmed radiance.\"","The words did not reveal excessive information. They simply let her know that her Origin’s brilliance continued forward through time.","After all, had he not obtained the Living Existential Authority of Origin in his own era? Even after this entity standing before him would be collapsed in the future, her fundamental brilliance would not completely fade into nothing.","And since Primordial Civilizations were unfathomably difficult to permanently collapse, there always existed possibility to eventually restore this entity. He just had to ensure that he survived The Fallout himself first, and subsequently whatever additional horrors would arrive thereafter.","Because even as he accomplished all of this temporal travel and growth, he understood and realized with clarity that The Fallout was merely the first of many catastrophic challenges he would eventually have to navigate.","Surviving The Fallout meant then existing in a drastically altered landscape where all of the terrifying Civilizations currently contained within THE Loom would suddenly be free to act without restraint.","This possibility in itself represented another terrifying thought and future to contemplate. But he would simply approach it one step at a time with methodical planning.","If he was not successful in surviving The Fallout, then future complications would not even become relevant concerns.","These thoughts came and went rapidly as after he spoke his carefully measured words, he actually observed the figure of THE Living Origin smile lightly with what appeared to be genuine appreciation before she nodded with acknowledgment.","And then she disappeared completely in the next moment.","She had departed after abandoning them in one of the most dangerous places in the entire Infinite Unfurling.","All for the explicit purpose and sake of forcing them to struggle and grow through adversity.","Lumivara immediately came toward Noah and hugged his arm protectively as she looked around their environment with visible caution and concern.","As for Noah himself, his existence was still acclimating to the new state of Pre-THE. But the cascade of benefits was far from completely finished manifesting.","Because his Way and his Civilization were fundamentally one and the same entity. With his Way having advanced so tremendously, his Civilization had also necessarily advanced tremendously in parallel.","But when it came to manifestations of his Civilization’s growth, there remained only the question of precisely when he wished to receive and process this accumulated advancement.","Which was why at this particular moment, a new prompt appeared before his vision with critical timing.","|Quintessential waves of Effort and Harvest have been kept carefully restrained before flooding the foundations of your Civilization.|","|Your advancement to the distinction of a Pre-THE Existence has exponentially multiplied the potency of accumulated Harvest.|","| Would you like to receive all accumulated and amplified Harvest immediately, or delay reception until the end of the Temporal Traversal?|","|Warning: Immediate reception will cause dramatic power escalation across your entire Civilization.|","|Current Harvest Multiplier: 847x baseline due to Pre-THE elevation.|","A straightforward question came regarding the timing of harvests.","And when it came to making this decision, the answer was unfathomably clear to Noah without hesitation.","His people were actively struggling in the current era. His Civilization was under coordinated attack from multiple hostile forces.","So let it advance without further delay. Let the harvest flow immediately to those who needed it most.","BOOM!","The moment his intention crystallized with absolute conviction, reality itself responded to accommodate his will.","The dams holding back accumulated power shattered completely.","And the harvest began flowing forward through time itself toward his Civilization."]},{"number":4556,"title":"Chapter 4556: Chapter 4555: When Fortune Falters! I","paragraphs":["His Civilization was fundamentally unique in how it operated and manifested power.","And its advancement was represented most clearly in its Walls of Civilization and its overall Designation.","It currently held The Architect’s Bulwarks as the structure for its Walls of Civilization. All accumulated harvest would flow directly into these walls that represented The Designation of The Cathedral of Order.","The next evolutionary stage for the Walls of Civilization would be The Civilization Aegis. This represented The Designation of The Sovereign Dominion, a stage that was deemed the absolute prerequisite before one could even begin to dream of attaining THE Civilizational Scale.","At this critical moment, would his accumulated harvest be sufficient to make the dramatic jump from the second designation directly to the third designation? The multiplier was so obscenely high to begin with that it seemed theoretically possible.","Even though such a question existed, Noah instinctively felt like it would absolutely be the case. And if somehow circumstances proved that it was not quite sufficient, he would find some method to cheat reality and make it happen regardless.","So he closed his eyes once more and focused his awareness inward. He felt the unfathomable influx of green-gold harvest surging from all around him, crashing into his existence before flowing directly into that manifestation of his Civilization.","Into the Walls of his Civilization specifically.","The process was simultaneously quick and slow, creating a strange temporal perception. He watched as the stone walls of his Civilization changed rapidly, enlarging and becoming dramatically fortified.","Their fundamental makeup gained a terrifying quality of supernatural sturdiness as they began to shine with pure plasmic light of blue-gold radiance. The transformation was visible and profound!","As this occurred, new prompts bloomed before his vision with detailed explanation.","|The Effort of countless actions across your Civilization has accumulated into an unprecedented Harvest.|","|This concentrated Harvest flows into your Civilization simultaneously with the advancement of your Way of Existence to Pre-THE.|","|With both of these extraordinary factors converging together, The Walls of your Civilization have achieved their largest single instantaneous increase in recorded history.|","|Status: The Walls are beginning their transformation from The Architect’s Bulwarks to The Civilization Aegis.|","| Accordingly, the Designation of your Civilization is advancing from The Cathedral of Order to The Sovereign Dominion.|","|Progress: Bringing your Civilization one major step closer toward The Level One Scale of Existence.|","|Transformation Progress towards The Sovereign Dominion: 47% and accelerating...|","BOOM!","These prompts materialized alongside an overwhelming influx of brilliance that caused his manifested Civilization to become completely drenched in glorious green-gold harvest.","Noah could not help but smile with genuine satisfaction as he felt the unprecedented changes that were beginning to unfold systematically across his entire existence.","With how profound and fundamental these transformations were, the process was taking considerable time to complete properly. But he could distinctly feel his Complexity and Purity surging upwards at terrifying rates.","Alongside this core advancement came elevation of his Early Atlas of the Folds, his Sovereign Spires of Osmont, his accumulated Principles, and everything else that fundamentally composed his Way and his Civilization as integrated concepts.","Another prompt bloomed with extraordinary information.","|Passive Protection Upgraded: No creature below Pre-THE Designation can cause harm to your existence.|","|This protection extends to direct attacks, environmental hazards, and conceptual threats from sub-Pre-THE sources.|","|You have achieved baseline immunity to an entire category of opponents.|","|The Boon of Major Mana and Hunger Bulwark has undergone complete metamorphosis.|","|New Classification: The Veritarch Blessings of Mana and Hunger|","|Maximum Recipients: 6,561 members of the Civilization can be bestowed this evolved Blessing.|","|Blessing Effects:|","|- Grants 500 Octillion Complexity|","|- Grants 500 Octillion Purity|","|- Imparts the complete teachings of relevant Grand Principles from The Cheating Architect. Provides access to fragments of Principles obtained from all Superseded Ways of Existence|","|Special Amplification: For any recipients who have undergone Civilization Specialization, the effective Complexity and Purity they will hold after receiving the Blessing averages 25 Nonillion baseline.|","|Additional Scaling: Those possessing higher Civilization Specialization Potential will gain exponentially more benefit.|","The prompts continued with their utterly marvelous explanations of what was systematically happening within his existence. A few more materialized that caused Noah’s smile to widen even further.","|PRINCIPLE ENHANCEMENT UNLOCKED|","|New Capability: Civilizational Primus Mana Glyph Forging|","|Function: You can now forge 1,000 Civilizational Primus Mana Glyphs for each of your 5 Main Principles of Existence.|","|Effect: These Glyphs vastly elevate the capabilities and expression of their associated Principles.|","|Power Per Glyph: Each individual Civilizational Primus Mana Glyph grants 500 Nonillion Complexity and 500 Nonillion Purity.|","|Total Potential Power: At 100% completion of all Glyphs across all 5 Principles, you will gain 2,500 Decillion Complexity and 2,500 Decillion Purity.|","|Current Forging Status: Automatically initiated.|","One ridiculous advancement after another continued to manifest as Noah could not help but express genuine satisfaction through his smile.","While terrifically powerful changes in his existence continued to take place, he looked toward the cautious figure of Lumivara standing nearby with protective stance.","\"Come on,\" he said with calm confidence. \"Let us discover just what level of struggle THE Living Origin has gone and placed us into.\"","While his existence completed its ongoing transformation processes, he would continue feeling and expressing his Way of Existence actively. In this dangerous place, he would be maintaining THE True Expression of The Sovereignty of Mana and Hunger constantly as a protective measure.","The instability of the distant environmental areas felt like something that could genuinely be harmful to him even at his current elevated state. Continuous active protection seemed prudent.","With light steps that defied the absence of solid ground, he lifted off from the snowy mountain peak and began moving forward to explore the unknown territories.","Lumivara followed closely behind him, her small form radiating concentrated Light authority as she maintained defensive awareness.","Around them, the protective bubble of THE Living Origin’s residual authority began to thin and fade. Soon they would be fully exposed to the Unstable Genesis Domains and whatever challenges existed within!"]},{"number":4557,"title":"Chapter 4557: Chapter 4556: When Fortune Falters! II","paragraphs":["Misunderstandings .","They were phenomena that were incredibly easy to prevent with minimal effort, and yet they were also some of the most frustrating events in existence.","If someone simply uttered a few additional words and made a slightly different choice in how they communicated, there would absolutely be no misunderstandings. Communication would be immensely easy and clear.","And yet misunderstandings almost always occurred in existence regardless. And they remained infuriatingly persistent despite their preventable nature.","---","In a region of the Infinite Unfurling where space folded in complex patterns, THE Living Origin was moving through existence with purposeful direction.","The way she viewed and observed the surrounding atmosphere was fundamentally different from how entities of lesser power perceived reality.","An entity weaker than her would see the vibrant landscape of the Infinite Unfurling normally. The colors of mountains, the textures of unique regions, the spatial relationships between objects.","But in her eyes, and in the perception of many entities at THE level, all of existence appeared as endlessly interacting wavelengths and strings of fundamental Civilizational energy.","They saw reality differently than others. Space itself, mountains, entire landscapes...all of them simply held different variations of vibrating strings and oscillating wavelengths of Civilizational Authority that they could seamlessly and easily manipulate with their elevated power.","They could interact with these wavelengths and strings through an innate ability that only entities of THE Civilizational Scale possessed. This capability made manipulating existence unfathomably easier than for those operating at lower levels.","They could meld with the surrounding existence so seamlessly that weaker entities could pass directly by them without even knowing they were present. Or they could alter and control every aspect of countless Gigaparsecs worth of wavelengths to fall under their absolute dominion.","It was power that defied conventional understanding.","At THE level, fundamental particles were no longer perceived as zero-dimensional points but as one-dimensional strings and waves that vibrated with specific frequencies. Different vibration patterns corresponded to different manifestations of authority and matter!","These entities could perceive and manipulate the extra spatial dimensions that were curled up at scales too small for normal observation. They could interact with reality at the Planck length where conventional weavings ceased to apply!","They understood that what appeared as distinct forces and concepts were actually unified expressions of the same underlying weavings vibrating in different patterns. Gravity, elemental authority, temporal manipulation...all of it was simply variations in how fundamental strings of Civilizational Authority moved and interacted.","This was the true power of THE , or at least a glimpse of what such beings could accomplish.","But as THE Living Origin moved across existence in this elevated manner of perception, her thoughts returned to the temporal anomaly she had recently left behind in the Unstable Genesis Domains.","Her mind drifted back to her failed plans of studying the Origin of Time through THE Time Surfer . She had hoped to better understand and prepare countermeasures for THE Living Temporal through such research.","She shook her head at this reflection. Sometimes one succeeded in their carefully laid plans, and other times circumstances caused them to fail despite best efforts.","She wondered idly how THE Time Surfer had fared while facing the savage weavings of Hunger that had been moving with the anomaly when she departed.","In the next moment as she was contemplating these matters, her expression changed dramatically. Her gaze snapped to focus toward a certain direction where she felt a significant burst in the flow of countless waves and strings.","POP!","Existence itself flickered and squeezed as space compressed violently. The figure of none other than Tor appeared near THE Living Origin’s position with sudden dramatic entrance.","Tor, THE First Hunger himself!","THE Living Origin looked at this being with immediate heightened awareness. His gaze was currently filled with a light of vibrant brutality and barely contained violence.","In his hands, the half-eaten corpse of THE Time Surfer could be clearly seen. Endless streams of purple rivers of temporal authority were leaking from her body and being systematically devoured into Tor’s existence.","And even though she was categorized as a corpse, her eyes and core existence continued to flicker with her terrifying Sovereignty. Time itself was continuously trying to reverse and restore her to the state she had been before her defeat.","And yet Tor continued to devour everything about her Sovereignty with relentless efficiency. The corpse felt more like a perpetual battery that was feeding him endless power rather than a defeated enemy.","With such a terrifying entrance and the power radiating from Tor feeling grander than ever before, he opened his jaws wide to take another savage bite of THE Time Surfer’s remaining essence.","He looked at THE Living Origin with wild intensity burning in his eyes and spoke with directness.","\"I did not expect for one of the followers of this time bitch to actually be a monster veiled in disguise ,\" he said while chewing. \" I almost missed detecting you entirely. But I was following the weavings of my junior’s path, since I had to hurry in taking care of a few persistent pests.\"","He paused to take another bite.","\" Because I sensed another Sovereignty wrap around my junior and even veil their presence completely. I now cannot sense where they are located. So tell me plainly: what did you do with my junior?\"","As soon as he finished speaking his question, he continued to brutally bite and devour what remained of THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entity in his hands.","And here came a critical inflection point in their interaction.","He had asked a simple and straightforward question. THE Living Origin could have given a simple and complete answer.","And yet at this moment, THE Living Origin thought carefully about the terrifying temporal anomaly who had far too many complex issues and connections already attached to his existence.","She first needed to further understand his relationship to this brutal entity before revealing sensitive information. The anomaly held a semblance of her Origin within him, and he also held a semblance of this savage entity’s Hunger?","She wanted to comprehend how all of these connections fit together properly. So at this critical moment, she simply made the choice to say minimal information.","\" He is fine and safe ,\" she said with deliberate vagueness.","And toward such insufficient words, Tor’s expression shifted.","\" That is not what I fucking asked for though,\" he said with irritation building in his tone. \" Where specifically is my junior located?\"","An exchange of just a few words between two powerful beings.","If different words had been chosen, if additional clarifying information had been given, then perhaps what happened next would not have occurred at all.","And yet THE Living Origin simply shook her head with refusal. She did not wish to reveal where she had left the anomaly, viewing that information as sensitive.","In consequence of this withholding, Tor laughed with dark amusement before shaking his head with resigned acceptance.","\" Guess another bitch needs to be collapsed today, \" he said with casual finality. \" Alrighty then.\"","With such declaration of intent, he opened his jaws impossibly wide and completely devoured the remaining body of THE Time Surfer in a single bite. The corpse that had been spilling out seas of temporal Sovereignty vanished entirely into his Hunger.","His power began radiating a terrifically concentrated obsidian-crimson glow as he looked directly at THE Living Origin and spoke with predatory anticipation.","\" Scrawny thing, are you ready? \" he asked with savage smile.","Choices.","Both entities had made the choice to say certain words while deliberately not saying other words. What it led to was a fundamental misunderstanding between two beings who operated at THE level.","An infuriating outcome that could have been easily prevented, and yet it occurred nonetheless despite their intelligence.","And from this miscommunication born of incomplete information and deliberate withholding, a terrifying battle between two THE entities was about to bloom.","All because a few additional words were not spoken!"]},{"number":4558,"title":"Chapter 4558: Chapter 4557: When Fortune Falters! III","paragraphs":["The Unstable Genesis Domains were vast beyond measure, containing many regions filled with dangerous environments that held clusters of unstable Civilizational Authority.","Noah had been traversing across them carefully for some time now with methodical exploration.","He was a simple farmer in mindset as he searched for suitable chickens to place into his prison coop. And yet he could not find a single qualifying entity anywhere in this domain so far!","He was simply left acclimating to his terrifying new power level as he felt the radiant expression of his Way of Existence flowing through him constantly.","When it came to keeping his power active through THE True Expression of The Sovereignty of Mana and Hunger, the mathematics worked out favorably. He could currently produce a single Rudimentary Unit of Everything every three minutes of standard time.","So he was actually capable of maintaining this constant state of elevated power indefinitely. By the time the duration of one Rudimentary Unit finished its three-minute cycle, he would already have another unit produced at exactly the same moment.","The constant state of empowerment left him feeling extremely exuberant about his capabilities while he continued forging the Civilizational Primus Mana Glyphs of his Principles amongst other elevated aspects of his existence.","An additional elevation worth noting was the progress of attainment of a Principle past the level of Singularity soon. This achievement left him remembering Elyndra and thinking about his many missed dual cultivation sessions with various partners.","He was an imperfect man as dual cultivation with his partners was the one activity he never denied himself under normal circumstances. And the sheer audacity of THE Living Elemental to curse him with contagious flames that made him stop all these intimate activities was enough for him to consider that entity a worse enemy than even THE Living Paradox.","A sworn enemy in fact. Out of all entities that had to eventually be eliminated, THE Living Elemental was now at the very top of his list purely because those actions had taken something he considered precious away, however temporarily.","He had a light smile as he shook his head at this vindictive thought when suddenly...","\"Be careful, Master!\" Lumivara’s voice called out with urgency.","She pulsed with concentrated light to oppose an incoming blast of blue unstable Civilizational Authority of Lightning. They were currently moving across an unstable region which pulsed chaotically with lightning authority all around them.","Each strike was capable of decimating anything below the level of Pre-THE in a single direct hit.","The environment stretched for Gigaparsecs in all directions around them. Blue lightning coiled around floating shattered landmasses that had been crystallized from constant battering by electrical strikes over eons.","The landscape appeared frozen in time, with jagged crystal formations jutting at impossible angles. The air itself crackled with residual charge that created visible distortions in space.","Toward the incoming strike that Lumivara had warned about, her defensive light was not able to meaningfully oppose or deflect the chaotic lightning. The attack continued its trajectory directly toward Noah.","Noah looked up calmly and simply let the massive lightning strike smash directly into his body without attempting to dodge or defend.","His form absorbed the electrical devastation that would have decimated even entities possessing a few Decillions of Complexity and Purity. To him, it felt like mere sparks hitting his elevated existence, causing no actual damage.","Lumivara looked at this casual display with genuine amazement written across her features.","\"Master, how can I become strong like you so quickly?\" she asked with voice carrying sincere curiosity.","Noah replied calmly as they continued moving through the dangerous region without pause.","\"You would have to possess a really strong foundation paired with a unique disposition of existence,\" he said with measured explanation.","Lumivara tilted her head with visible confusion.","\"Disposition?\" she asked. \"What specific disposition do you mean?\"","Noah considered how to explain this concept clearly.","\"A disposition where even if someone authoritatively tells you that one plus one equals two, you question that assertion and consider that maybe it actually equals infinity,\" he said with philosophical weight.","Lumivara blinked with even more confusion as she processed this statement.","\"But Master, one plus one does equal two though?\" she said with genuine uncertainty. \"So Master simply makes up his own reality based on preference?\"","Noah smiled at these words as he formulated his response carefully.","\"Yes, in a fundamental sense,\" he said with conviction. \"Existence has its established rules and conventions that most follow without question. But you have to cultivate the disposition to make your own rules when necessary. To question what seems absolute.\"","He gestured broadly at the chaotic environment around them.","\"Then you can gradually manage to violate existence’s normal constraints. More and more over time until the advancements that you make in power, which would normally require millions of years or even eons of cultivation, could potentially happen in a matter of hours or days instead.\"","Lumivara nodded her head with reverence as if she was receiving sacred gospel directly from an enlightened master.","The two of them continued to move across the Unstable Genesis Domains. Noah was deliberately using the tough and ridiculously dangerous surrounding environments to further develop a practical grasp of his new power level.","With some limits and caution, of course.","One of these limits was a region that had such unstable weavings of Existence that even he did not get near, with the breakdown of Existence itself seeming like a constant state that could even injure entities at THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty.","Another one of those limits became apparent after they had crossed the dangerous region of chaotic lightning for some time. They came upon a distant area that appeared even more hazardous than what they had traversed so far.","Extremely concentrated rivers of purple-blue tachyons swirled and spun around each other at such rapid speed that they resembled existential freight trains. Each river felt like it could smash directly into even Pre-THE Existences with enough force to heavily injure them, continuing to batter them until eventual collapse.","Even Noah had to come to a complete stop as he squinted and looked more closely at this phenomenon. He activated his Lens of Civilization to gather detailed information.","A radiant set of analytical prompts bloomed in front of his vision.","|Location: Concentrated Lightning Convergence Zone|","|Classification: Extreme Hazard - Pre-THE entities advised extreme caution|","|Civilizational Authority Density: 947% above baseline Unstable Genesis Domain levels|","|Primary Phenomenon: Rapidly accelerating tachyon rivers of pure Lightning authority|","|Danger Assessment: Each tachyon river possesses kinetic force equivalent to 10,000 Decillion Complexity and Purity strikes|","|Continuous exposure will cause cumulative damage even to Pre-THE entities|","|Analysis indicates increasingly concentrated levels of Civilizational Authority of Lightning.|","|Projection: These concentrated energies likely surround a naturally forming treasure.|","|Estimated Value: Beneficial even for THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entities|","|Formation Stage: Approximately 73% complete - treasure still maturing|","|Note: Waiting for complete maturation would increase value|","|Recommendation: Assess risk versus reward carefully before proceeding|","...!","Noah raised his brows with genuine interest at this information.","\"It looks like we have to struggle a little bit to see if we can successfully get our hands on some genuinely valuable treasure,\" he said with anticipation evident in his tone.","Lumivara looked toward the distant convergence zone and nodded with visible caution.","\"I will follow the lead of Master,\" she said with loyalty overriding her fear.","They began moving closer and closer to this terrifically dangerous domain. As they approached, whenever streams of purple-blue lightning shining with chaotic Civilizational Authority surged toward them, Noah simply raised his hand.","He acted like a living conduit that systematically swallowed everything that came into contact with his elevated existence. The chaotic authority was absorbed and integrated rather than causing damage.","His existence continued to feel a profound sense of exuberance at processing such concentrated power. By the time they managed to get significantly closer to the terrifying rivers of accelerating tachyons...","The scene they finally observed was breathtaking in its dangerous beauty.","Multiple crystalline purple-blue jagged mountains could be seen rotating slowly around a central area. The mountains themselves appeared to be formed from compressed lightning given solid form.","And in the protected space between these rotating mountains, radiant purple-blue jewels pulsed with terrifically concentrated light of extremely pure Civilizational Authority of Lightning.","The purity was extraordinary, clearly reaching a level of refinement that touched upon THE Civilizational Scale itself.","The treasure seemed to be actively building up and increasing in concentration based on how rapidly the surrounding rivers of tachyons continued to surge and feed energy into the formation. As if the longer one waited patiently, the more concentrated and valuable the pure THE Civilizational Authority contained in those jewels would ultimately become.","Noah looked at this natural formation with eyes shining with clear desire. If he could successfully navigate past the rapid rivers of dangerous tachyons and claim that treasure, this would be a significant boon that would propel him considerably upward in power.","It would allow THE Organ of Civilization to develop even faster toward the next critical threshold.","As he carefully looked around the environment and prepared tactical plans for how to proceed forward safely...","HUUM!","A profoundly stifling aura bloomed from a distance away with sudden presence.","\" Little thing, do you not know that more often than not, valuable treasures have someone watching and waiting patiently over them? \" a voice called out with amused condescension.","...!","The words bloomed from the exact area where the stifling aura had manifested. Noah’s expression changed rapidly as his entire existence began to buzz with warning signals.","One of the few potential possibilities that he had specifically not wanted to readily encounter in the Infinite Unfurling seemed to manifest with absolute certainty at this critical moment.","An entity that had not even been perceivable through their complete mastery of existence’s weavings revealed themselves at a distance. The aura and brilliance emanating from them was undoubtedly at THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty.","A genuine THE entity had been waiting here all along.","\"...\"","Fuck.","Fuck!"]},{"number":4559,"title":"Chapter 4559: Chapter 4558: When Fortune Falters! IV","paragraphs":["One must always be really, truly suspicious when circumstances seem to be proceeding a bit too well, and a chosen path feels a bit too easy to traverse.","There exists an old parable about such things, told across countless civilizations with slight variations but always carrying the same fundamental warning.","Once there lived a peasant whose entire miserable life was transformed dramatically in a single day through what appeared to be extraordinary fortune.","He stumbled upon a basket of quality food near his ramshackle home, appearing as if delivered by providence itself. This gave him sustenance he had not experienced in years of poverty and hunger.","Later that same remarkable day, he managed to witness a noble woman walking through the markets carelessly lose her expensive satchel filled with coins and valuables. Instead of stealing it and fleeing as any sensible desperate man would, he felt an unusual compulsion to do good.","He actually returned the satchel to her with humble courtesy.","She looked upon this honest action with visible favor and spoke words that would change everything.","\"A lesser man would have taken this wealth and disappeared immediately,\" she said with approving smile. \"And for demonstrating such rare character, I find myself liking you. I would like to invite you to join my personal guards.\"","The peasant was utterly astonished as it felt like one extraordinary thing after another was happening on this blessed day. He never stopped to question the sequence of events. He was not suspicious of such rapid elevation from his station.","He simply followed the noble woman and her well-armed guards with mind already racing ahead. He was already imagining his completely transformed life in vivid detail. He even began planning ambitious goals like potentially striking up a romantic relationship with another noble woman after establishing himself.","He followed the noble woman and her guards as they entered an impressive castle. While he waited eagerly for his new life to officially begin with some ceremony, he found himself guided to a private chamber.","Soon he was strapped onto a ceremonial table against his confused protests. The noble woman and her guards surrounded him while wearing cult-like robes that had been hidden beneath their normal clothing.","They began to systematically gut him as a ritual sacrifice to their dark patron.","Things had been proceeding far too well for a lowly peasant like him. He should have been deeply suspicious from the very beginning when fortune smiled so readily.","But by the time he realized the trap, it was far too late to escape!","Now, Noah was not a peasant, and he was considerably more experienced with how existence operated.","He knew that many extremely fortuitous events had occurred as he crossed into the Infinite Unfurling through temporal traversal.","After the excruciating and immense pain brought about by THE Living Elemental’s curse, this entire journey through time had been proceeding remarkably well for him. Meeting Tor and establishing that connection, then encountering THE Living Origin who actually helped rather than hindered him...well, maybe until now.","He had genuinely enjoyed all of those beneficial events while simultaneously maintaining an undercurrent of suspicion. As if existence itself could shatter catastrophically in the next moment without warning.","Because existence was fundamentally struggle. Existence was inherently unfair and did not distribute fortune equally or consistently.","Things would never remain so consistently easy for extended periods. And at this critical moment, a foreign and unknown THE entity appeared directly before him to prove that principle.","The being that manifested was striking in appearance and terrifically dangerous in disposition. He possessed wild white hair that seemed to crackle with residual electricity, standing up in spikes that defied gravity.","His physique was powerfully built, and his expression carried casual arrogance mixed with predatory interest. He wore minimal clothing that revealed muscular form covered in glowing circuit-like patterns of pure lightning.","Tendrils of extremely explosive and pure THE Civilizational Authority of Fulmination wrapped continuously around his body. The lightning was not chaotic but perfectly controlled, each tendril moving with purposeful intent.","His aura radiated confidence bordering on sadistic amusement, as if he found genuine entertainment in the fear of lesser beings.","The body of Lumivara began trembling with instinctive terror at sensing this overwhelming presence. But remarkably, she still forced herself to float forward and position herself defensively in front of Noah despite her fear.","Noah looked at this being with analytical focus as he immediately utilized his Lens of Civilization to gather critical information.","A status sheet bloomed before his vision with frustratingly limited data.","|ENTITY ANALYSIS|","| Name: Astrape, THE Maelstrom Thundermane|","|Classification: ???|","|Complexity: ???|","|Purity: ???|","|Depth of THE: ???|","|Way of Existence: The Way of Fulmination|","|Threat Assessment: EXTREME|","|Note: Analysis capabilities insufficient for complete evaluation of THE entities.|","Astrape.","THE Maelstrom Thundermane!","Noah’s expression remained heavy as he processed this encounter. When he had previously deliberated about this possibility occurring, there were theoretically a few approaches for how he could potentially navigate past such a confrontation without circumstances utterly deteriorating.","But when situations actually reached this point in practice, outcomes more often than not leaned heavily toward disaster rather than resolution.","Still, he looked at this terrifically powerful being with forced sense of calm as he spoke with measured diplomacy.","\"It seems we have inadvertently come across your claimed domain and your designated treasure,\" he said. \"Since that is the case, my companion and I will simply leave without causing any further intrusion.\"","His eyes maintained their calm tyranny as he watched the terrifying entity ahead of them. Astrape was looking at both Noah and Lumivara with analytical gaze, examining them as if one was observing a pair of strange animals discovered in the wilderness.","A moment passed after Noah’s diplomatic words had echoed across the space between them.","Then Astrape smiled with casual cruelty and spoke with finality.","\" Nah ,\" he said with dismissive tone. \" Since you have already arrived here, you should definitely stay.\"","BOOM!","The voice was heavy and filled with an undeniable brilliance.","Undeniable!"]},{"number":4560,"title":"Chapter 4560: Chapter 4559: When Fortune Falters! V","paragraphs":["Noah’s eyes pulsed with recognition of how this would unfold.","Right. Deterioration toward catastrophe. That was more often than not how existence operated when confronting those with overwhelming power.","Astrape looked Noah up and down with assessing gaze before he continued speaking with a philosophical observation.","\" Any common Pre-THE Existence would have immediately gotten on their knees right now upon sensing my presence,\" he said with voice carrying superiority. \" They would be bowing their heads down submissively and being as obedient as possible just to be allowed to remain in my presence without being obliterated.\"","He tilted his head with interest.","\" And yet you, little anomaly, are looking directly at me as if we are somehow equals. You do not even show an appropriate sense of fear or deference. That behavior in itself is quite unnatural.\"","His smile widened with predatory amusement.","\" Either you genuinely believe you could actually survive a direct encounter against someone at my level, or you are one of those weak followers who serve an entity that has already formed their Dominion and achieved THE Civilizational Scale.\"","He gestured casually.","\" Perhaps this powerful patron is nearby protecting you, or you believe that simply mentioning their name would grant you different standing. As if speaking their identity to me would make me reconsider and let you leave peacefully.\"","His eyes gleamed with challenge.","\" So do you want to skip past all the tedious pleasantries and simply declare the name of the entity that you follow? We will see together if that name carries enough weight to make me refrain from doing anything harmful against you.\"","The expression and eyes of Astrape shined with concentrated sense of brutality and casual cruelty after he finished speaking these words.","Noah’s expression became progressively more grim as he processed this inevitable trajectory. He sighed with resignation and shook his head slowly while looking toward this being.","When he spoke, his voice carried calm tyranny that refused to be diminished.","\"Regardless of what name I might give you, it ultimately will not matter to the outcome,\" he said with absolute certainty.","Astrape laughed at this response, his Sovereignty causing the surrounding environment to buzz and distort with electrical charge. He nodded with appreciation for the honest assessment.","\" Haha, a weak thing with some actual sense of reality, \" he said with genuine amusement. \" You are correct. Even if you claimed it was THE Creature himself that you followed, it would not change my intentions.\"","His expression became more serious and analytical.","\" Because I can see you, little anomaly. Really see you with the vision granted by THE. Apart from your disposition and bearing, your fundamental existence looks and feels distinctly different from all other entities I have encountered.\"","He leaned forward with intensity.","\" You may not even fully understand what I am describing since you have not yet attained THE yourself. But the elevated vision I possess makes it so I can perceive you as the temporal anomaly that you clearly are. Something that does not carry the natural colors and frequencies of the Infinite Unfurling.\"","His smile became predatory.","\" Which is precisely why no, I absolutely will not be permitting you to leave this location. I must study your existence systematically and break it down to its fundamental particles to understand exactly why you are so different from what should be possible.\"","He spread his hands as if explaining something reasonable.","\" It is nothing particularly major, and certainly nothing personal against you specifically. Are you ready to cooperate?\"","Was he ready.","Noah could not help but sigh heavily at these words. He thought about how sometimes, choice truly was nothing more than comfortable illusion. There was no genuine choice to make in this situation apart from accepting a forced outcome.","But regardless of inevitability, he stretched his neck as if preparing for a truly dangerous and exhausting exercise. He placed his hand on Lumivara with gentle firmness.","She disappeared instantly, her entire existence placed protectively inside his own internal space before she could even voice a word of protest.","THE Maelstrom Thundermane looked at Noah with an amused smile, as if an adult was watching a child raise their small fists with determination. As if such gesture would actually accomplish anything meaningful against overwhelming power.","And yet at the same time, Astrape recognized that any entity who could remain this outwardly calm even when facing certain death would inevitably have a few unexpected tricks available. Even if they were fundamentally weaker.","So Astrape did not waste time with further conversation. His existence instantly erupted with concentrated power as he prepared to capture this anomaly.","The moment he manifested his authority fully, Noah also erupted with his own power in response.","\" Keep up, you ugly fucker ,\" Noah said lightly with voice carrying absolute defiance.","BOOM!","His Way exploded with brilliant radiance as his body transformed into pure concentrated Primus Mana. The blue-gold energy that composed his fundamental existence blazed with intensity.","And yet the terrifying influence of Astrape still thundered down toward him far faster than Noah could fully react to with his own power alone.","But then...","BZZT !","Terrifying seas of THE Civilizational Authority of Hunger bloomed into existence with overwhelming presence. THE Barrier of Hunger that Tor had placed upon Noah activated!","Decillions upon Decillions of enraged obsidian-crimson jaws erupted from the barrier, systematically devouring all nearby influence of Astrape’s lightning. They formed a brilliantly dense barrier of obsidian-crimson light that shot outward into the distance.","The protective phenomenon was genuinely shocking in its potency and scope.","Astrape looked at this unexpected defensive capability with visible incredulity before he laughed with raucous appreciation for the surprise.","Of course, it would not be easy!","How could anything be easy in existence, especially when it involved such a unique being?!","Another version of himself instantly bloomed from his current physical form through Fulmination authority, creating a perfect duplicate. This second Astrape shot forward at impossible speed toward the slippery anomaly attempting to escape his grasp!"]},{"number":4561,"title":"Chapter 4561: Chapter 4560: There’s Bad, Then There’s BAD I","paragraphs":["Mistakes were inevitable in existence, woven into the very fabric of how beings learned and grew.","It was perfectly acceptable for one to make mistakes along their path. But it only transformed into grievous sin if they failed to learn from such errors, or worse, if they deliberately refused to steer away from committing the same mistake repeatedly.","The true measure of wisdom was not in never falling, but in rising differently each time.","---","In the Infinite Unfurling, in a region that had become a battlefield between two incomprehensible forces, the ongoing clashes of THE Civilizational Authority of Hunger and THE Civilizational Authority of Origin continued to reshape reality itself.","The surroundings had been transformed into a war zone of conceptual forces. Massive white-gold glyphs perfectly aligned with Origin floated and rotated through collapsed space. Each glyph was the size of small moons, radiating concentrated authority.","Opposite them, obsidian-crimson glyphs aligned with Hunger raged with equal intensity. They devoured space around them while simultaneously creating it, forming paradoxical voids.","All of these glyphs radiated the unmistakable light of Singularity-level Principles being actively expressed, with a light of other Principles that seemed...even more disastrous than Singularity-level!","The Principles of Existence were fundamentally the equations that described how reality operated at its deepest levels. They procedurally outlined how existence functioned, providing the underlying code.","And THE entities were the ones who could utilize such Principles with the greatest freedom and masterful precision.","Even at this moment of intense confrontation, the actual physical bodies of THE First Hunger and THE Living Origin could not even be directly observed by normal perception. Everything around them for tens of Gigaparsecs was composed of twisting expressions of existence itself.","Their Ways of Existence were being expressed in pure opposition against each other, warping reality through sheer authority.","If any weak entity appeared in these Gigaparsecs where their Ways were actively exerting themselves, they would be crushed to fundamental dust in less than a picosecond. And weak here was defined as anything below THE Civilizational Scale.","Even Pre-THE entities would be obliterated instantly.","And yet, in the midst of this terrifying battle of them expressing their Sovereignties and utilizing Principles to defy and manipulate surrounding existence to their tactical advantage, both of these overwhelming entities suddenly came to an abrupt stop.","The storm of authority ceased its escalation.","Tor and THE Living Origin reappeared in visible form amidst the terrifying maelstrom of their exerted Ways. They looked at each other with eyes shining with sudden realization.","Tor spoke first with voice carrying urgency mixed with anger.","\" The Barrier of protection I placed around my junior has just been activated ,\" he said with tension building in his tone. \" Meaning another THE fucker has found and engaged him, which happened as a direct consequence of your actions.\"","His expression darkened considerably.","\" Before I get supremely serious and genuinely pissed off beyond reason, where exactly is my junior? Because for me to still not be able to sense his general location, there would have to be some form of environmental instability creating interference...\"","His eyes widened with dawning comprehension.","\" Oh you fucking bitch ,\" he said with disbelief coloring his words.","As if he had suddenly figured out exactly what she had done, Tor shook his head with incredulous anger.","\" You left him in the Unstable Genesis Domains?\" he said with voice rising. \" You dumb-\"","\"I know the direct route and the quickest path to reach his location,\" THE Living Origin’s voice echoed out with unusual urgency, cutting off his insult. \" Just follow me immediately.\"","At this critical moment, these two terrifying entities who had been locked in combat began to sort out the miscommunication they had put themselves into. They began actively correcting their mistake.","It was always acceptable to make a mistake in the flow of existence. But one simply had to take responsibility and rectify it before consequences became irreversible.","The figure of THE First Hunger snorted with frustrated acknowledgment. But when THE Living Origin transformed into a streak of white-gold light and shot toward a specific direction with desperate speed, he simply followed without further argument.","As the two entities moved in the same direction at incomprehensible velocity, the voice of THE First Hunger could still be heard echoing across space.","\"If he dies because of you, I am definitely skinning you alive slowly and eating you piece by piece over an extended time,\" he said with voice carrying absolute conviction in the threat.","A heavy promise of retribution was made.","THE Living Origin did not pay any attention to the threat and only accelerated faster. Existence itself peeled away from them like endless waves and strings being systematically manipulated as they moved at speeds that lesser entities could not even begin to comprehend.","---","Entities that had obtained THE distinction were faster than anyone without that classification could understand through experience.","Noah knew this fundamental truth firsthand from observation. He knew with absolute certainty that he could not outrun the entity that was currently pursuing him with predatory intent.","It was not even truly a chase in the traditional sense. Because a chase required one party to be actively pursuing another with some possibility of escape. And he knew he would be getting caught unfathomably soon without intervention.","So at the very moment that he had prepared for the activation of THE Barrier of Hunger , he had already begun moving deliberately toward a specific direction where he was hatching a desperate plan for survival.","There were already multiple calculated possibilities forming in his mind of how this dire situation could potentially be navigated. And even though there existed the comfortable possibility of being rescued by Tor or THE Living Origin arriving to intervene, those were not outcomes he could reasonably entertain or depend upon.","Because at the end of existence, one ultimately had to struggle for themselves. One had to fight for their own survival first and foremost. One could not simply sit around passively hoping that others would consistently come to their defense and save them from every threat.","So he had formulated a plan and was already surging with maximum speed toward the destination he had selected. And when he received the first devastating strike from THE Maelstrom Thundermane , he strategically used the terrifying force that did not even belong to his own power.","Force from an entity far stronger than himself, redirected through THE Barrier of Hunger.","He used that momentum to cross untold distances and nearly arrive at the specific region he desperately needed to reach.","It was a region that he had crossed not too long ago during his exploration. A place he had deliberately steered clear of because of the immense sense of existential danger that it projected.","A region where even entities possessing the power of THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty would think carefully twice before delving into its depths. It truly felt that catastrophically dangerous!"]},{"number":4562,"title":"Chapter 4562: Chapter 4561: There’s Bad, Then There’s BAD II","paragraphs":["It was dangerous, but that region was an environmental hazard rather than a conscious entity. And Noah would rather take his chances with an environment that could kill him than face an entity that definitely would kill him.","The region appeared before him with horrifying clarity. It looked like fundamentally distorted space and existence that was actively twisting and systematically mutilating any Civilizational Authority that came near its influence.","There were a few narrow channels visible here and there that appeared as obsidian rivers cutting through the chaos. These pathways held a semblance of stability and safety.","But if one’s trajectory veered off by even an atom’s worth of distance to one side or another from these safe channels, they would immediately enter the mutilated and distorted regions of existence surrounding the paths.","These distorted zones would unravel a Pre-THE entity instantly upon contact. Or they would severely injure THE Way of Existence of even a THE entity if exposed for any duration.","Behind Noah came the furious and genuinely shocked roar of the previously laid-back THE Maelstrom Thundermane as Astrape realized immediately what Noah was planning to attempt.","\" You absolute dumbfuck! \" his voice boomed with mixture of anger and concern. \" You may actually have some chance of surviving against me if I capture you carefully! But you will most definitely die horribly over there! Get back here immediately!\"","...!","His voice created sonic booms that shook reality. The surroundings began to feel like a massive quagmire that was drawing everything backwards through spatial manipulation.","But THE Barrier of Hunger around Noah’s existence withstood this terrifying attractive power, though its luminescence dimmed noticeably from the strain. Noah’s forward speed remained unaffected as he shot directly toward one of the narrow obsidian river passageways.","He entered the region of utterly distorted and lethally dangerous weavings of existence without hesitation.","New prompts bloomed before his vision with critical information.","| THE Barrier of Hunger Status: 30% power remaining|","|Recommendation: Extreme caution advised|","|LOCATION UPDATED|","|You have entered: THE Unstable Infinite Unfurling Ginnungagap|","|Classification: Infinite Ginnungagap Zone - Existence Unraveling Region|","|Survival Probability for Pre-THE: 0.001%|","|Survival Probability for THE Surface Depth : 23% with extreme caution|","|This region predates stable existence|","HUUM!","Then one final foreboding prompt materialized with weighted implication.","|Based on current threat level and barrier depletion rate...|","|It may be optimal to terminate this Temporal Traversal early and return to original timeline.|","|Continuing forward risks permanent existence collapse.|","Noah’s expression remained grimly determined as he navigated the impossibly narrow obsidian pathway.","Retreat was not an option he would accept.","Not when he had come this far!","—","Across the endless weavings of the Infinite Unfurling, through dimensions that folded upon themselves in impossible geometries, Tor followed calmly behind THE Living Origin as they crossed existence at unfathomable speeds.","And yet despite the velocity that would shred lesser beings into fundamental particles, it appeared as though he was merely taking a casual stroll with a few light steps through a pleasant garden.","He was carefully observing the woman in front of him with analytical focus, and his nose scrunched with recognition of a familiar scent.","\"I can smell the brutal and overpowering allure of THE Creature clinging to you, \" he said with measured curiosity. \" Are you among those entities that follow him as subordinates? Because I know from that any others who come across THE Creature tend to disappear mysteriously, as if he is systematically collecting them as valuable trophies.\"","He paused before continuing with pointed question.","\" For you to be running around freely with such concentrated traces of his authority, are you perhaps his compatriot rather than his follower?\"","THE First Hunger asked such a direct question with genuine interest coloring his tone.","In front of him, the gaze of THE Living Origin did not even flicker or change in response.","She continued forward as if she heard absolutely nothing at all, her focus entirely on their destination. Their trajectories through existence’s weavings were getting ever closer to the location where a certain temporal anomaly should theoretically be located.","Tor shook his head at the deliberate silence as moments later, they arrived at the boundary of the Unstable Genesis Domains.","THE Living Origin paused momentarily upon arrival and looked around the chaotic environment with searching perception. But Tor simply sniffed the air with his more direct method of tracking, and his expression immediately transformed into a frown.","He took a single step and disappeared from visible perception entirely.","Moments later, Tor’s figure reappeared near the region where Noah and THE Maelstrom Thundermane had been engaged just recently.","He materialized directly before the entry point of THE Unstable Infinite Unfurling Ginnungagap.","THE Living Origin appeared right after through her own method of instantaneous travel. Both their expressions became extremely heavy as they recognized what had occurred.","Tor sighed with frustration mixed with genuine concern as he looked at THE Living Origin . He raised his hand as if he wanted to physically smack her for the situation she had created.","But he controlled the impulse with visible effort and spoke with a tense explanation instead.","\" Entry at one specific point of Ginnungagap sends you across countless random distances into its depths, \" he said with voice carrying weight. \" It is virtually impossible to find someone inside it unless you enter within the exact same instant together through synchronized timing.\"","THE Living Origin’s expression became immensely serious. She nodded with acknowledgment and added her own knowledge.","\" Yet even attempting to find anything in THE Ginnungagap is almost impossible under normal circumstances ,\" she said with measured assessment. \" And THE Malformed Ginnu Lifeforms that inhabit it are extraordinarily dangerous to deal with.\"","They both knew of Ginnungagap’s terrible reputation. They understood that their efforts to locate Noah would likely yield no practical results.","And yet despite this logical assessment...","In the next moment, Tor looked toward the obsidian river-like channels that served as semi-stable pathways into the chaos. He took a decisive step forward and disappeared into the distorted space.","In that same exact instant, THE Living Origin stared silently at the passageway before she also took a step and disappeared into the same obsidian river entrance.","Both risking themselves to attempt the impossible!"]},{"number":4563,"title":"Chapter 4563: Chapter 4562: There’s Bad, Then There’s BAD III","paragraphs":["Limitation.","A limitation was not a cage from which existence must desperately escape, but rather the very mold that gave reality its fundamental shape and definition.","To rage against perceived boundaries was to rage against one’s own existence in futility. It was only within the finitude of a single wave that one could discover the infinite endlessness of the ocean of possibilities.","So truly, one should rage against their perceived limits with full conviction. Find that endless ocean of possibilities beyond assumed constraints.","Far from the Infinite Unfurling , separated by eons of temporal distance, in the current era where multiple threats converged...","In the Transcendent Paradoxical Folds, a battle of extraordinary scale was unfolding with devastating consequences for the surrounding space.","Schrodinger floated above the battlefield with expression mixing determination and regret. The Sovereignty of Chaos and Paradox had formed into a massive obsidian-gold sea above his position, stretching for countless Gigaparsecs.","He was channeling all of its concentrated weight and authority downward with focused intent. All of its crushing immensity was being directed onto a single target.","The Infiniverse herself.","And remarkably, she was withstanding the impossible pressure through sheer determination and conviction!","Behind her position, members of The Vital Chorus Specialization all had blinding green-gold light surging continuously into her existence, providing regenerative support.","Simultaneously, The Infinite Bulwark Specialization was actively withstanding and systematically spreading all the damage she was taking across their collective existence. Millions of Primus Inevitabilities sharing the burden of authority that should have collapsed her instantly.","But even with The True Expression of The Sovereignty of Mana and Hunger actively supporting The Infiniverse through the connection she maintained with Noah across temporal barriers, it was just barely enough to hold defensive ground against Schrodinger.","And he did not even seem entirely serious in his assault.","Schrodinger’s voice echoed across the battlefield with philosophical weight.","\" I have nothing personal against you truly,\" he said with voice carrying genuine honesty. \" I have nothing against Osmont either as an individual. Even now at this moment, I am not unleashing everything that I possess. Because I still believe there could potentially be a functional relationship between us moving forward.\"","His expression showed conflict.","\" I know that these are the cruel games of entities possessing unfathomably more complexity and purity than we can comprehend. I understand this reality. But sometimes those of us who are comparatively weak can do nothing but play along with the game we are given.\"","As he spoke these words, Schrodinger’s expression was actually forlorn and even looked slightly disappointed in himself. As if he knew fundamentally that this was not who he truly was or wanted to be.","But at this point in circumstances, what else was there to do but continue?","So The Infiniverse struggled desperately to hold back the crushing weight of the sea of Sovereignty above her. Beside her position, Khor released countless crimson jaws of Hunger to systematically devour as much of the oppressive authority as she possibly could.","But their overall situation was not changing for the better despite their efforts.","And at such a critically desperate time, new variables entered the equation.","\"Now then, you all seem to be having a whole lot more fun over here than expected,\" a radiant but frustrated voice echoed out across space.","Reality folded and tore apart violently as new entrances were forcibly created. With a visibly frustrated Ambessa in the lead, the small legion of Avatars composed of False THE entities from THE Loom made their appearance off to the side.","They looked around at everything occurring with analytical assessment.","Ambessa blinked rapidly when she observed the figure of Schrodinger floating above. Her frustrated expression faded away rapidly as recognition dawned.","The gazes of The Infiniverse and Khor flickered with concern as this new threat manifested. Schrodinger also turned his attention toward Ambessa and the others with interest.","Ambessa knew his face extremely well. She had personally moved the unconscious vessels to hide them in various secure locations not too long ago during her service.","So at this moment, she frowned with genuine hesitation before speaking carefully.","\"Esteemed Paradox, is that truly you in control?\" she asked with uncertainty evident in her tone.","Schrodinger looked toward her and frowned before responding with calm clarity.","\"If you are referring to THE Living Paradox consciousness, then no, he is not currently in control,\" he said with measured explanation. \"Though I have come to certain terms with him. Your direct assistance is not required here. I will personally collect Osmont as planned.\"","The False THE entities arrayed behind Ambessa blinked and looked at each other with silent communication. One of them stepped forward and voiced out with grand authoritative tone.","\"Our assigned goal here involves the one known as Osmont, yes,\" they said with voice carrying weight. \"But alongside eliminating him, we are tasked with ensuring his entire Civilization also collapses completely. We are here to guarantee that no trace of his Civilization’s foundation remains intact.\"","The False THE Avatar looked directly at The Infiniverse, Khor, and the millions of Primus Inevitabilities with dismissive contempt before finishing his statement.","\"So all of these insignificant dredges of life gathered here...\" he said with casual cruelty. \"All these weak things must also collapse into nothingness.\"","BOOM !","Enemies had converged from multiple directions simultaneously.","And at such a time when circumstances already appeared catastrophically bad for Noah’s forces, existence itself began to buzz and shake with new disturbance.","In the next instant from yet another unexpected direction, a terrifying aura of Pre-THE authority bloomed and raged outward wildly across the battlefield.","And this particular aura was saturated completely with the unmistakable weavings of Death itself.","Space tore open with force as a massive shattered fragment of an Early Veiled Shore emerged like a vessel. Standing prominently at its forefront was a figure that radiated casual menace mixed with ancient power.","Damian, The Disciple of THE Creature , had arrived.","His white hair seemed to absorb light rather than reflect it, and his crimson eyes gleamed with predatory interest as he surveyed the chaotic battlefield. His long coat moved with wind that carried the scent of graves and endings.","Behind him stood the impressive but small legion of Guiders of Order, each one radiating authority in the Septillions or Nonillions of Complexity. They formed perfect ranks as if prepared for systematic warfare.","The arrival created an immediate and complex standoff between multiple factions. The Infiniverse and her forces all stood against...Schrodinger acting under compulsion, The False THE Avatars from THE Loom seeking complete annihilation, and now the Dead Existences led by a Pre-THE entity.","The one to break the tense silence was Damian himself.","He looked around at all the various powers arrayed against each other with expression mixing amusement and boredom. His crimson eyes scanned the faces systematically as if searching for something specific.","Then he yawned with deliberate casualness that suggested supreme confidence in his own capabilities, completely unconcerned by the gathered powers.","\" There would not happen to be a lady called Sigrid here, would there? \" he asked with voice carrying both politeness and underlying threat!"]},{"number":4564,"title":"Chapter 4564: Chapter 4563: There’s Bad, Then There’s BAD IV","paragraphs":["In existence, circumstances could be unfavorable and then they could escalate to become truly catastrophic.","At this moment for Noah’s Civilization, they seemed to have left the roadmap of merely catastrophic and ventured toward utterly apocalyptic territory.","Two Pre-THE Existences had now appeared alongside multiple False THE entities from THE Loom itself. The convergence of such overwhelming power in one location was unprecedented.","And all Noah’s forces had to oppose this was themselves. All they possessed was The Infiniverse, Khor, Sigrid, and the millions of Primus Inevitabilities who had sworn themselves to Mana and Hunger.","At this critical point in time, the figure of The Infiniverse remained silent as she looked systematically at all the various forces that were now pitted against her Civilization. Against his Civilization that she represented in his absence.","And yet she retained her fundamental calmness and composure. Her eyes blazed with concentrated lividity and absolute determination as at this moment, a communication reached her.","|Sis, the influx representing the advancement of the Civilization to the Third Designation, The Sovereign Dominion, is arriving now,| the voice of RUIN/EDEN echoed directly in her mind.","The Infiniverse nodded with acknowledgment and looked around at her surroundings with assessment. At the frowning Schrodinger who carried genuine regret. At the multiple Avatars from THE Loom radiating False THE authority. At the distant Dead Existence who possessed a level of concentrated power that seemed even more terrifying than Schrodinger’s.","She observed all of this with analytical precision as in the next moment, her body and the bodies of the millions of Primus Inevitabilities and other forces arrayed around her began to pulse with unique aura.","The aura of systematic advancement was manifesting.","As this transformation began to occur, The Infiniverse looked over to the diminutive figure of Khor standing nearby.","Khor looked back at her as if she could clearly perceive the unspoken request in that gaze. She spoke with direct simplicity.","\"What?\" she asked with tone suggesting she already knew what would be asked.","The Infiniverse’s voice carried calm authority as she formulated her request with clarity.","\"We will need you to do some extremely heavy lifting here,\" she said with measured intensity. \"Master is fighting and struggling for us even in the distant past. He has elevated the Civilization of Mana and Hunger to the designated stage right before THE itself.\"","She paused with emphasis.","\"So The Way of Existence can be considered to have arrived at the threshold right before THE Civilizational Scale . You hold Hunger as your fundamental authority. You held the power of THE before in your previous existence. Master has cleanly paved the road forward for you.\"","Her eyes gleamed with conviction.","\"Unlike the rest of us who do not yet possess the adequate foundation, you should already remember and know your foundation unfathomably clearly. You comprehend the power right before THE . You have wielded this authority previously. The one you call Outsider is not coming to save us. The Master is not arriving as reinforcement. It is just us here.\"","She leaned forward slightly.","\"Can we at least witness a glimpse of the true grandeur of The First Hunger? Of the legitimate Successor of Tor?\"","BOOM!","The figure of Khor smiled with something resembling nostalgic recognition and shook her head before responding with her own determination.","\"You do not need to deliver a whole inspirational speech to me,\" she said with voice carrying weight. \"I understand the situation perfectly. If The Way of Hunger has advanced toward Pre-THE status, which I held long ago in my previous existence, and I am unable to break even more of my seals to properly utilize it...\"","Her expression became fierce.","\"Then I do not deserve the distinction of The First Hunger. I do not deserve the mantle and authority that I inherited from my predecessor.\"","As she spoke these words with conviction, her existence began to pulse with a heart-shaking crimson aura. As if all the way from the distant past where Noah was currently struggling, the progression and advancement he had achieved there was now arriving in this timeline.","The Infiniverse looked at this manifestation calmly before she waved her hand with decisive motion and went even further in her support. She pulled out a radiant and terrifically powerful spinning mobius strip that glowed with concentrated authority.","\"This is THE Rudimentary Unit of Everything from Master,\" she said with voice carrying weight. \"It cost an extraordinary amount of resources to bring THE actual unit forward through time and not just a lesser Rudimentary Unit of Everything.\"","She held it toward Khor.","\"In it, there exists THE True Expression of The Sovereignty of Mana and Hunger in complete form. With this amplification, there can be absolutely no excuse for failure.\"","Khor felt the radiant product of THE Organ of Civilization flow directly toward her position. Her expression became extremely heavy with the responsibility as in the next instant, the unit flowed into her existence and integrated.","BOOM!","Her body began radiating a heart-shaking aura that blazed powerfully around the entire battlefield. The concentrated authority caused their gathered enemies to immediately look over in her direction with stern eyes!","The power emanating from her small form was genuinely terrifying in its intensity.","As this dramatic transformation was occurring, space rippled nearby as another figure made their appearance.","Alexander Asmodeus materialized on the battlefield with purposeful timing. He appeared alongside the bodies of Riya and Kael who had personally escorted him here after he received news of the dire situation from them while in the Injunction Sanctuary of Law.","He made his entrance while looking directly toward The Infiniverse with eyes blazing with resolve.","He spoke in a voice only she could hear.","\"The Shattered Part of THE Heart of Law that I integrated into my existence was still fundamentally a power and authority belonging to THE Living Law himself.\"","His eyes gleamed with dangerous light.","\"I can burn through a semblance of its accumulated brilliance to temporarily lay down a unique manifestation of THE Living Law’s authority. It will not last long, but when deployed, it could shift the tide of battle.\"","The Infiniverse listened to this offer before replying with calm authority that accepted the resource.","\"I will tell you precisely when to make that move\" she said with measured assessment. \"Be ready to act on my signal.\"","WAA!","Alexander nodded with acknowledgment and took his position among the defensive formation.","His eyes held a unique light as while he found himself in this terrifying environment of war, he wondered about peace. How could one establish absolute peace?","There was no answer.","\"...\"","Around this same time, another unexpected presence made itself known on the battlefield.","A presence filled with an overabundance of effort!"]},{"number":4565,"title":"Chapter 4565: Chapter 4564: There’s Bad, Then There’s BAD V","paragraphs":["He arrived with endlessly burning waves of effort.","Effort that felt natural and grand and immense in a way that nobody else could truly understand.","The First Farmer arrived!","He appeared with Elyndra positioned respectfully behind him, both emerging behind the rear lines of the Primus Inevitabilities defensive formation. His appearance was striking in its deliberate simplicity and contrast to the powers arrayed.","He currently wore a green straw hat that seemed almost comically out of place in this apocalyptic confrontation. His body was adorned in what appeared to be archaic farmer’s attire, complete with worn but clean work clothes.","And in his weathered hands, he carried a simple farmer’s hoe as if he had just walked in from tending crops.","But the aura emanating from his seemingly humble form told an entirely different story.","His entrance was glorious despite the mundane appearance. His existence blazed with concentrated authority as he rose upward to survey the battlefield. Many hostile gazes immediately landed on him with reassessment as they sensed the profound power he represented.","He looked around at all the gathered forces with eyes that had witnessed eons of struggle and perseverance. His body burned with visible manifestation of Effort itself made tangible.","When he spoke, his voice carried across the entire battlefield with weight that demanded attention.","\"It looks like a whole lot of youngsters are gathering here for conflict,\" he said with tone mixing amusement and stern assessment. \"The lot of you were not even conceived as possibilities when I first began to truly struggle and put in genuine effort toward cultivation.\"","His eyes swept across the enemy forces.","\"The effort you have all accumulated and invested across your respective existences throughout time...\" he said with voice building intensity. \"Let me take that concentrated effort from you and put it to proper use. Let me show you what can really be accomplished when effort is refined to its absolute pinnacle.\"","BOOM!","The seemingly harmless First Farmer stood tall as his Way of Effort burned unfathomably bright with concentrated authority. His existence was sensing and reaching toward the stage he had already achieved before THE Living Emotive had brutally crushed him down.","He could almost tangibly feel Pre-THE Existence within his grasp again. At this critical moment, he was pitting his accumulated effort against others to grasp that power once more.","Either he would reclaim it through this battle, or he did not deserve all the effort and harvest he had invested across those countless eons of struggle.","The First Farmer rose to stand proudly alongside the same defensive line as The Infiniverse, Khor, Alexander Asmodeus, and other key figures. Behind them, millions of Primus Inevitabilities began to move with synchronized coordination.","They raised their fists toward the sky in perfect unison while beginning to chant with voices that shook reality.","\" MANA !\" they roared with conviction.","\" HUNGER !\" they answered with equal fervor.","The chant repeated with building intensity. \" MANA!\" \"HUNGER!\" \"MANA!\" \"HUNGER!\"","The rhythmic declaration of their fundamental Sovereignties created visible waves of authority that rippled across the battlefield. The light of Civilizational Authority surrounding all of them reached an unprecedented level of concentration!","The scene was genuinely glorious in its defiant determination against overwhelming odds.","As such a dramatic display was manifesting among Noah’s forces, the figure of Damian, The Disciple of THE Creature , rose upward while looking at everyone gathered with analytical interest.","His white hair moved with wind that carried the scent of endings. His crimson eyes gleamed with predatory anticipation mixed with dark amusement.","\"Haha, it is like watching different sized ants gather together and raise their little limbs as if this would change the titanic foot about to step on all of them...\"","When he spoke, his voice carried imposing weight that demanded attention from all present.","\"What a genuinely warm welcome this is so soon after I wake from extended slumber,\" he said with tone mixing sarcasm and genuine appreciation for the conflict. \"My goal arriving here was singular and straightforward. A particularly annoying Dead entity of Order wants The Living Order to be secured for purposes I was not made privy to.\"","His smile widened with dangerous edge.","\"But what do I observe upon arrival? Do I see the Sinners of Paradox gathered here as well? The corrupted Sinners of Elemental manifesting as Avatars sent from THE Loom itself?\"","He laughed with genuine dark amusement.","\"Haha, you all understand that if and when I do systematically shatter your Avatar forms here, I will also be shattering your true existences protected within your supposedly safe confines of THE Loom , correct? The connection works both ways for those who truly know how to exploit it.\"","His expression became more serious and dangerous.","\"It appears I will be extremely busy so soon after waking from my rest. But I must thank you all sincerely for this reception and opportunity.\"","His terrifying demeanor and imposing nature radiated outward as he raised his hand with deliberate motion. In his grip now appeared a weapon that had not been there moments before.","A clear white sword materialized, its blade seeming to be formed from crystallized concept rather than physical matter.","And this sword was surrounded by unmistakable light of a Principle of Existence that was immediately recognizable to those with adequate perception.","The Principle exceeded Singularity-level classification entirely.","It was something beyond what most present had ever witnessed directly.","His eyes flashed with concentrated crimson light as he spoke with imposing authority.","\"Who shall be collapsed first by my hand?\" he asked with voice carrying across the battlefield. \"Will this Sigrid step forward voluntarily and save countless deaths among her people through sacrifice? Or will the obedient dogs of THE Loom hurry forward eagerly to feel my blade cutting across their existence?\"","He tilted his head with mock consideration.","\"Choices, choices, choices. So many potential victims to select from.\"","The expressions of many present changed dramatically at witnessing the wildness and terrible concentrated power that Damian represented. His aura and bearing suggested clearly that he was the most individually powerful entity present on this battlefield!","But yes!","Some among those gathered may have temporarily forgotten a critical detail in the chaos of convergence.","This was The Disciple of THE Creature himself. Trained directly by that incomprehensible entity.","And Paradox and those serving THE Loom ...were they not sworn enemies of THE Creature across eons of conflict?"]},{"number":4566,"title":"Chapter 4566: Chapter 4565: Ginnungagap! I","paragraphs":["Power.","Khor knew power intimately. Khor understood power at its most fundamental level.","In the Earliest Folds, she had held a tremendous amount of concentrated authority and influence.","One could always pose the philosophical question and ask: if one’s Civilization was systematically collapsed, and the very Heart of their Way of Existence was violently taken from them, and they somehow found themselves returned to existence years later through extraordinary circumstances, could they ever truly reclaim their original power?","In Khor’s mind, such a question was profoundly stupid and revealed fundamental misunderstanding.","If the sun lost a portion of its mass and light, was it no longer the sun? Did it cease to be what it fundamentally was?","Khor had lost her Heart of Hunger to THE Living Paradox’s brutal assault.","Since she emerged from the Seed of Inevitability that had been planted by The Outsider, she had begun systematically cultivating her Heart of Hunger again from foundational principles.","Her Way of Hunger remained fundamentally the same. Her existence at its core was still identical. She had simply lost a critical segment of herself that needed reconstruction.","But she was an Existence who had achieved THE Civilizational Scale . Since she had been THE once, she would always carry that fundamental classification within her being.","So right now, at this critical moment...","\"Thank you, Outsider,\" she whispered to herself with eyes closed, feeling the profound weavings of Hunger flowing through her existence with increasing clarity.","THE True Expression of The Sovereignty of Mana and Hunger held capital THE classification within its structure. For her specifically, it functioned as a unique catalytic tool because it acted like an enzyme in biological processes.","It dramatically accelerated her return toward THE by providing the exact foundational pattern she needed to rebuild around. The expression served as a template that her own Hunger could recognize and align with, speeding up reconstruction exponentially.","She already possessed the complete blueprints of THE within her existence. They had been obscured and darkened before by her diminished state, but The Outsider had shone a brilliantly bright light directly on them through his advancement.","It now made everything unfathomably easier and more accessible. If she could not successfully leverage things from this advantageous position, she truly did not deserve the tremendous power that she had wielded before her fall.","She opened her eyes with sudden clarity and spoke with absolute conviction.","\"Merely Pre-THE?\" she said with voice carrying weight. \"I have been at this threshold before . I know this power intimately.\"","BOOM!","The moment she declared this understanding, a terrifying pillar of obsidian-crimson light erupted from her small form and shot upward into the collapsed sky above.","Her power emanated terrifically intense waves of pressure that caused all the powerful entities gathered on this battlefield to immediately turn their collective gaze toward her position.","The False THE Avatars from THE Loom looked over with expressions shifting from dismissiveness to genuine concern as they reassessed the threat she represented. Their forms pulsed with defensive authority instinctively.","The Pre-THE entities, Damian and Schrodinger both turned their full attention toward her with analytical focus. Damian’s crimson eyes gleamed with interest mixed with recognition. Schrodinger’s expression showed surprise at the rapid transformation.","At such a pivotal moment, the visage of The First Hunger turned her head to look directly at The Infiniverse’s position.","She spoke with a voice carrying gratitude and determination.","\"Give my sincere thanks to The Outsider,\" she said with measured intensity. \"Tell him that I am genuinely sorry that I have not been properly acting according to my true stature this entire time. He has had a THE entity by his side throughout his struggles, and yet she had not been contributing adequately to deserve that distinction.\"","Her eyes gleamed with renewed purpose.","\"Tell him not to worry about what is currently playing out right now in this present era, and for him to focus completely on whatever critical tasks he is accomplishing in the Earliest Folds. I am admittedly upset that he was not able to bring me along with him this time around on his Temporal Traversal, as who knows which specific time period that entity appeared in...\"","She shook her head with resignation.","\"But it simply was not meant to be in this instance. However, he can relax completely regarding this situation. I will take care of everything here with absolute certainty.\"","She spoke such words with profound confidence radiating from her being.","The Infiniverse did not correct Khor’s assumption about Noah being in the Earliest Folds. She chose not to reveal that he was actually meeting with Tor in the Infinite Unfurling, as this information might be too much for Khor to process right now.","So The Infiniverse simply nodded with acceptance of the message.","And thereafter, the transformation continued with accelerating intensity.","Rivers of extremely concentrated crimson and obsidian waves of light began systematically wrapping around Khor’s small form. The unmistakable aura of Pre-THE Existence bloomed from her with maddening allure and terrible beauty.","Her eyes became immeasurably cold while she looked at all those gathered on this battlefield with analytical assessment.","In the next moment, she opened her mouth as if to consume something and spoke with terrifying authority.","\"I hunger for these Folds that everybody currently occupies,\" she declared with voice that resonated across reality itself.","A single simple statement.","And yet in the next moment, everything changed catastrophically.","BOOM!","The surroundings disappeared instantly and transformed into a region of pure collapse and devastation. The Transcendent Paradoxical Folds that had contained this confrontation simply ceased to exist.","A prompt appeared before the vision of all those belonging to The Civilization of Mana and Hunger.","|The First Hunger has taken a conceptual bite and completely devoured The Transcendent Paradoxical Folds in their entirety.|","|All constituent Folds within this domain have been consumed.|","|Weak lifeforms within affected Wheels of Existence have been automatically sent to The Infiniverse for processing and protection.|","|Environmental Status: Complete Collapse|","...!","The surroundings instantly transformed into regions of endless Collapse as truly with a single statement and conceptual action, Khor had extinguished the light of an entire Transcendent domain!"]},{"number":4567,"title":"Chapter 4567: Chapter 4566: Ginnungagap! II","paragraphs":["Khor did not seem to be finished with her systematic dismantling!","Her mouth remained open as she spoke once more with same terrifying authority.","\"I hunger for the very flow of time in this region,\" she declared with voice carrying finality.","The fundamental concept of temporal progression itself in this collapsed region became devoured by her existence. Time stopped flowing entirely, creating a frozen moment that extended infinitely.","For those experiencing this effect, it manifested as complete cessation of change. Thoughts that should have progressed became stuck in single instants. Energy that should have moved became locked in static positions. Even the natural decay of particles halted completely.","In this unprecedented and terrifying situation, Khor did not pause or hesitate!","Once more she opened her mouth to take another conceptual bite as she spoke with same devastating simplicity.","\"I hunger for the very concept of perception in these surroundings,\" she said with cold precision. \" Let us turn the lights off completely.\"","In the next instant, immense darkness settled over everything like a suffocating blanket. Every entity present, regardless of their power level, could only barely perceive anything within a few inches immediately around their own position.","Even THE level perception was suppressed to nearly nothing.","And yet this terrifying being showed no signs of stopping her systematic dismantling of fundamental concepts.","She opened her mouth once again to take another bite while speaking with philosophical depth!","\"In existence, nothing is truly at rest and everything is constantly in motion at some level,\" she said with voice carrying ancient understanding. \"I used perceive existence as countless malleable waves and strings vibrating at different frequencies. All matter, all energy, all Mana, everything possesses its own unique vibrational signature.\"","Her eyes gleamed in the darkness.","\"I hunger for these very vibrations of existence itself. Let me have them. Let me feel them. Let me consume them.\"","BOOM!","Shockingly, in the immense darkness she had imposed, she began sensing the unique vibrational signatures of all the entities present with perfect clarity. Each one’s distinct frequency became visible to her perception like beacons in the void.","And her own vibrational signature disappeared completely from detection as if she had ceased to exist entirely.","No False THE entities could sense her. No Pre-THE beings could detect her presence. Well, unless they were genuinely exceptional enough to perceive beyond normal limitations!","HUUM!","But she felt a slight strain on her existence from maintaining all these conceptual devourings simultaneously. She stopped her terrifying actions for now and consolidated her position.","She turned her head toward the direction where the Avatars from THE Loom and Schrodinger were positioned based on their vibrations.","The weapons of THE Living Paradox who had mutilated countless Inevitabilities stood gathered there.","She smiled with utterly deadly light as she observed how they were desperately trying to acclimate to the region of her terrifying making. She breathed in deeply with satisfaction and took a single step.","She appeared instantly right above a False THE Avatar who was not even able to perceive or sense her presence despite their frantic attempts. They pulsed with their Civilizational Authority trying to protect their existence from unknown threats.","Khor floated mere inches away above this entity’s head as she opened her mouth and took a deliberate bite.","Instantly, half the body of the False THE was systematically eaten and consumed. The other half remained suspended, showing radiant teeth marks where her conceptual bite had severed their existence.","Khor licked her lips with visible satisfaction as the consumed essence integrated into her being.","Her eyes shone with terrifically intense red light of Hunger made manifest as she spoke with quiet confidence.","\"Truly, do not worry about circumstances here, Outsider,\" she said with voice carrying across the suppressed space. \"You have given me more than what I needed to reclaim myself. Let me show these people a genuine glimpse of why THE Living Paradox had to hunt me down personally to eliminate the threat I represented.\"","She said such words openly and clearly, but nobody within inches of her position could hear her voice. The concept of sound had been suppressed along with everything else.","And none of the other Avatars even knew that one of their number had already been half-eaten by an invisible predator.","They could not perceive her. They could not see her. They could not hear her.","Among the few entities on this entire battlefield who could accomplish any of these suppressed sensory functions...","The terrifying figure of Damian stood looking directly at Khor’s exact position with eyes shining with genuine surprise mixed with appreciation. A terrifically concentrated light of a Principle exceeding Singularity-level classification was shining in his eyes, granting him perception that transcended her suppression.","He could see her perfectly.","And his smile widened with dark amusement and wonder!","---","In The Infinite Unfurling, within a domain that predated conventional existence itself, a fundamental question arose.","To be or not to be.","This was currently not the philosophical question occupying Noah’s mind as he was doing everything within his power simply to remain alive.","The moment he crossed into the obsidian river passageway of THE Unstable Infinite Unfurling Ginnungagap, he felt an irresistible pulling force as if he was being dragged into a place from which one could never leave.","All normal perception and sound faded completely as the furious roars of THE Maelstrom Thundermane disappeared into absolute silence. All Noah had remaining was the constant and immense feeling of existential danger pressing against his consciousness.","He had to focus entirely on following the rapid twists and turns of a violently winding current of obsidian light. This sludge-like flow was the only visible sign of stability in an environment of chaos.","His surroundings were filled with murky THE Civilizational Authorities that shifted and mutated constantly. These unstable energies would systematically unravel Pre-THE Existence with terrifying rapidity upon contact.","Noah steered himself through this nightmare like a small boat navigating grand rapids of churning water. The obsidian current twisted left, then sharply right, then spiraled downward in a dizzying corkscrew that defied spatial logic!"]},{"number":4568,"title":"Chapter 4568: Chapter 4567: Ginnungagap III","paragraphs":["The speed accelerated dramatically as he progressed deeper. What had started as manageable velocity increased exponentially until the environment became a blur of motion.","His Sovereignty could barely keep pace with the required reactions. He pushed his perception to its absolute limits just to anticipate the next deadly turn.","Then disaster struck. A particularly violent twist came too quickly for him to fully compensate. His trajectory veered slightly off course by mere inches.","But inches were catastrophic in this environment! His existence briefly exited the stable zone and made contact with the murky instability surrounding the pathway.","Immediately, his THE Barrier of Hunger buzzed with maximum intensity to protect him. The protective field flared brilliantly as it intercepted the unraveling force that would have collapsed his existence instantly.","New prompts appeared with critical urgency.","|BARRIER INTEGRITY CRITICAL|","| THE Barrier of Hunger Status: Less than 10% power remaining|","...!","Only after this terrifying near-collapse did Noah finally perceive a change ahead. A brilliant obsidian light grew larger as he approached what appeared to be an exit!","HUUM!","He escaped the obsidian river passageway and found himself emerging into open space above a vast landscape.","The moment he arrived in the skies of this new region, he immediately felt an immense gravitational pull toward the ground below that he could not deny or resist.","His body barreled downward with accelerating force as he smashed violently into an obsidian stretch of jagged land. The impact created a crater as his form collided with the ancient surface.","His eyes remained vibrant and alert despite the collision as he felt a terrifically intense sense of pressure constantly exerting itself on his very Sovereignty again and again. The environment itself was hostile to his existence.","New prompts materialized with detailed information about this unprecedented location.","|Welcome to THE Unstable Infinite Unfurling Ginnungagap|","|Classification: Primordial Genesis Domain|","|The right to remain airborne has been systematically stripped away.|","|Cause: Insufficient THE Civilizational Authority classification|","|Effect: All entities below THE Surface Depth are bound to surface travel|","|The Light of Ginnungagap shines upon everything within this domain.|","|For none native lifeforms, All Ways of Existence face 90% suppression of normal capabilities|","|Progression on The Way accelerates by 900% to compensate for difficulty|","|9% chance of spontaneous Existential Unraveling occurs continuously every second|","|Condition: If the foundation of your Way is insufficiently stable, collapse is inevitable|","|Time dilation: 9 seconds external equals 81 seconds internal|","|Spatial compression: Distances are 9 times greater than they appear|","|Authority concentration: THE Civilizational Authority is 99 times more potent here|","|Regeneration suppression: Natural recovery occurs at 9% normal rate|","|Sensory limitation: Perception range reduced to 900 Meters, 90 Light Years, or 9 Gigaparsecs maximum depending on power|","|Conceptual weight: All actions require 99 times normal effort to execute|","|Evolutionary pressure: Entities adapt 9 times faster or collapse|","|Malformed Ginnu Lifeforms: Native inhabitants possess 9 specialized adaptations minimum|","....!","After Noah observed these absolutely ridiculous prompts with their systematic restrictions, he began experiencing their effects directly and immediately.","The 99 times more effort felt like trying to move through liquid concrete. Every action required extraordinary effort. His normally fluid command of Mana became slightly sluggish and resistant.","Slightly!","The constant 9% chance of Existential Unraveling manifested as periodic jolts of destabilization that shook his foundation. But his foundation was grand and undeniable!","The accelerated progression felt like his understanding was being forcibly expanded whether he was ready or not. Knowledge tried to force itself into his consciousness with uncomfortable intensity.","He felt as if he had entered a place where he genuinely should not be present. A domain meant for beings far beyond his current classification.","And yet, critically, he did not feel the overpowering aura of THE Maelstrom Thundermane anywhere nearby. This was still positive progression compared to the alternative.","The other choice had been to terminate the temporal traversal early and return to his own era empty-handed. That was unacceptable.","So he began looking around at his new environment to assess the situation when...","\"Oh, come on,\" he muttered with disbelief as he prepared.","In this place that was already overbearing and stifling simply to exist within, after his Way and his own vision finally acclimated to the suppression, he began observing his surroundings more clearly.","The first thing he saw was a pair of massive crimson eyes staring directly at him.","Crimson eyes that were attached to a truly massive woolly beast of incomprehensible proportions.","The creature resembled a woolly mammoth expanded to titanic scale. Its coat shone with full obsidian radiance that pulsed with concentrated authority. But there was something fundamentally wrong about its form.","Its tusks spiraled in impossible geometries that defied euclidean space, curving through dimensions that should not exist. Where normal tusks would be ivory, these were crystallized void that leaked darkness.","The creature’s body crackled continuously with obsidian light that was unmistakably THE Civilizational Authority at full potency.","THE level power.","Mere seconds after his arrival in this domain, he was already staring at another THE entity!","And yet this massive creature had its enormous eyes locked onto Noah’s position for only a brief few seconds. Moments later, it blinked slowly as if it had discerned or recognized something about him.","Then it proceeded to look away with apparent disinterest before continuing to walk calmly in the distance!","Noah was utterly astonished as he witnessed this interaction. He watched the massive entity that clearly possessed power at THE Surface or Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty simply gaze at him briefly and then begin wandering away without aggression.","Its titanic body passed between two obsidian mountains with casual ease. These peaks were surrounded by multiple obsidian river-like passageways which represented some of the few safe routes to traverse the domain.","The overall environment was filled with regions that appeared as patches of space saturated with instability. Storms of collapsing existence raged constantly in these areas with force that could systematically decimate even Pre-THE Existences.","The landscape conveyed profound ancientness, untamed wildness, and omnipresent danger. Multiple regions of constantly collapsing THE Civilizational Authority created a patchwork of lethal zones.","Interconnecting obsidian river-like passageways wound between these zones of collapse. Weaker entities would be forced to carefully navigate only these stable paths if they could not withstand the terrifying environment surrounding them.","Noah had arrived in such a primordial place as he kept his analytical eyes locked on the sauntering massive mammoth walking away. He utilized his Lens of Civilization to gather information!"]},{"number":4569,"title":"Chapter 4569: Chapter 4568: Ginnungagap IV","paragraphs":["A comprehensive status sheet materialized before his vision.","|Name: Void-Tusk Colossus (Ancient designation: Ul’gathon THE Undying)|","|Classification: Malformed Ginnu Lifeform, Primordial Genesis Lifeform|","|Age: Predates conventional temporal measurement|","|Depth: THE Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty|","|Complexity: Undefined (exceeds measurement parameters)|","|Purity: Undefined (incompatible with standard metrics)|","|WAY OF EXISTENCE|","|The Way of Enduring Void|","|Singularity Principle 1: Principle of Perpetual Mass|","|Singularity Principle 2: Principle of Dimensional Displacement|","|Singularity Principle 3: Principle of Conceptual Heaviness...|","|Note: This entity’s Way revolves around existing as an immovable object that displaces reality around it|","|Entity exhibits no protective veiling - does not perceive need for defense or hiding its power, this is why any of its information is showing.|","|Seemingly Non-aggressive towards you, or just doesn’t care.|","|Feeds primarily on regions of collapsing existence|","...!","A status sheet that was not filled with question marks!","And yet Noah knew it was not out of the reality that he got more powerful, but simply this creature did not even feel the need to hide anything!","After Noah continued observing this massive creature walking away into the distance, he heard a different roar echoing from above his position.","He raised his head upward to investigate the source.","Another glorious Malformed Ginnu Lifeform came into view as this one was actively flying across the unstable regions of existence with apparent ease.","The creature resembled a massive arthropod expanded to impossibly large proportions. Its segmented body stretched for what appeared to be several kilometers in length.","It possessed characteristics of ancient Myriapods, with countless legs extending from its elongated form. But its body was covered in crystallized obsidian plates that gleamed with concentrated authority.","The malformed feature that marked it as wrong was immediately apparent. Its segments did not connect properly in conventional space. Each section existed partially in different dimensional layers, creating a horrifying visual of a creature that was simultaneously present and absent.","Noah looked up at this flying creature as its multiple crimson eyes also came to focus and lock onto his position. It circled above him as if examining potential prey with predatory interest.","But a moment later, it also blinked slowly similar to the massive mammoth. As if it too had ascertained or recognized something specific when observing him.","Then it continued flying calmly across this vast and endless landscape without attacking, apparently losing interest.","...!","Noah observed all of this with his eyes shining brilliantly with mixture of confusion and caution.","He had to ask himself a critical question: just where exactly had he landed?","And why did he simultaneously feel a sense of stifling danger as if he could be eradicated at any moment by this environment, and yet at the same time, his existence was buzzing with unusual excitement?","His weavings of Loot, Cheats, and The Protagonist were resonating powerfully. Their associated Sovereign Spires of Osmont seemed to be vibrating with anticipation and enthusiasm.","As if this terrifying place held something extraordinary!","---","\"I fucking hate Ginnungagap.\"","The visage of Tor spoke such words with genuine vehemence as he stood in a newly arrived region of this primordial domain alongside THE Living Origin.","This particular section of Ginnungagap was filled with waves of obsidian plasma and concentrated dark matter flowing in chaotic patterns. The environment churned with primal forces!","Fragments of Decillions of landmasses spun rapidly through the space around them, each one moving at velocities that defied normal comprehension. The shattered continents created a deadly obstacle field.","A single one of these massive fragments smashing into a Pre-THE Existence would likely collapse their entire Way of Existence instantly through sheer kinetic devastation combined with the concentrated authority each piece carried.","THE Living Origin had a deeply frowning expression as she observed all of this environmental hostility while speaking with measured assessment.","\" Survival for any entity below the level of THE is extraordinarily unlikely in this place,\" she said with voice carrying weight. \" The environmental pressure alone should be...\"","\" And yet he still lives ,\" THE First Hunger interrupted with annoyed eyes as he looked at her with accusatory gaze. \" I can feel it through our connection. He persists.\"","THE Living Origin nodded with acknowledgment before she continued with alternative possibility.","\" Perhaps he has already returned to his own time period,\" she suggested with reasonable tone. \"I would logically assume that in a moment of immense existential danger, temporal retreat would serve as his final safeguard mechanism.\"","Tor replied with calm certainty.","\" Maybe that is what occurred ,\" he said with measured cadence. \" But my Barrier around him has not yet shattered completely. And even though I cannot sense anything specific in this suppressive place apart from the nearby few Gigaparsecs immediately around my position, I will still continue searching.\"","His expression became more stern.","\" You, as the dumb bitch you demonstrably are for having contributed significantly in causing all of this catastrophic situation, will also be continuing to search alongside me.\"","THE Living Origin’s expression shifted subtly as she barely turned her head toward THE First Hunger. Her voice carried cold and measured authority.","\"I would genuinely appreciate if you refrained from using such unsavory vocabulary and ceased referring to me with that particular term,\" she said with controlled precision.","THE First Hunger’s reply was nonchalant and carried tyrannical dismissiveness.","\" A lot of entities across existence would appreciate a great many things ,\" he said with casual cruelty. \" And yet they do not receive them, do they? Appreciation means nothing.\"","THE Living Origin’s eyes sharpened dramatically as she responded with edge entering her tone.","\" You do understand that I could force behavioral compliance if necessary? \" she said with a voice carrying threat. \" I possess the capability to rewrite the very Origins of how you utilize your unsavory vocabulary. To alter the fundamental concepts underlying your speech.\"","The eyes of THE First Hunger became equally sharp and dangerous as the two powerful entities stared each other down with mounting tension.","\"I would like to see you fucking try such a thing, \" he said with challenge radiating from every word.","Their surrounding existence pulsed dangerously with concentrated manifestations of their respective powers. Authority crackled in the space between them as conflict seemed inevitable.","But in the next critical moment, everything changed.","Their expressions shifted simultaneously as both turned their attention sharply toward one specific direction. They had sensed something approaching with predatory intent.","A massive creature had materialized nearby with its terrifying crimson eyes set directly upon them with unmistakable hunger!"]},{"number":4570,"title":"Chapter 4570: Chapter 4569: Ginnungagap! V","paragraphs":["The entity resembled an archaic hippopotamus expanded to absolutely monstrous proportions. Its body was covered in obsidian plates that gleamed with concentrated authority.","But this creature possessed radiant obsidian wings extending from its back, each one spanning what appeared to be several Gigaparsecs when fully extended. The wings shimmered with dark energy.","Its malformed distinctive feature was immediately apparent and deeply unsettling. The creature’s mouth extended far beyond where a normal jaw should end, stretching back along its entire body in a grotesque spiral that seemed to contain infinite depth.","Such a terrifying creature’s crimson eyes locked onto both THE entities with single-minded predatory focus.","It flapped its massive obsidian wings with tremendous force. In the next instant, its body had crossed the distance between them at impossible speed.","Its massive jaws were already wide open and attempting to snap shut directly on top of the bodies of THE First Hunger and THE Living Origin simultaneously. The mouth contained rows upon rows of crystallized void teeth!","HUUM!","THE First Hunger reacted with explosive speed and power. He raised both hands and caused them to enlarge dramatically as they shone with concentrated obsidian light of Hunger.","He grabbed both ends of the massive jaws that were trying to snap shut around them, his fingers digging into the creature’s flesh with devastating force.","His Way of Hunger fought directly against the terrifying Way of Dissolution that this creature possessed. The two Sovereignties clashed with reality-warping intensity as neither gave ground.","In such a terrifying pivotal moment with his arms straining against incomprehensible force, Tor turned his head toward the calm figure of THE Living Origin who merely stood beside him without apparent concern.","\" So ,\" he said with voice tight from slight exertion. \" With multiple monstrous things like this creature actively running around throughout Ginnungagap, we have to operate under the assumption that even if my junior comes across them, he can either successfully outrun them or he will simply be eaten without trace.\"","THE Living Origin maintained her calm analytical gaze as she responded with measured reasoning.","\"I remain calm specifically because I have not yet sensed his Origin ending or collapsing,\" she said with voice carrying certainty. \" So somehow he is managing to survive in this domain. Either he has not been spotted by these creatures yet and remains concealed, or perhaps he did not show us the full extent of his capabilities.\"","She paused before continuing.","\" He may possess the capability to successfully flee from THE level entities through methods we did not witness. Or again as I suggested, he has already departed and returned to his own time period.\"","There existed many distinct possibilities as to what exactly could have occurred or could currently be happening to the temporal anomaly.","Tor flexed his enlarged arms with explosive force and physically threw back the massive creature that had attacked them. The entity was launched across Gigaparsecs of distance before stabilizing.","His eyes remained cold as he nodded with acknowledgment and spoke with determination.","\" Until we know definitively what occurred, we will continue searching\" he said with voice carrying absolute conviction . \"I do not like this oppressive place because of the severe suppression imposed on our Ways. A suppression that is not applicable to the native Ginnu Lifeforms that attack anything foreign on sight with extreme prejudice.\"","His expression darkened further.","\"I really, truly do not like this primordial domain.\"","They both knew intimately the terrifying nature of the place they currently occupied.","Very few entities throughout the entire Infinite Unfurling possessed knowledge like them about this domain’s true significance. They were aware of the persistent rumor regarding this location.","The musings suggested that this was potentially the birthplace of THE Creature himself.","That this primordial domain was where all THE level entities could ultimately trace their ancestry toward if one went back far enough through time and evolution. Maybe this was absolute truth. Or maybe it was all complete fabrication and mythology. Who could know with certainty?","---","In an entirely different section of Ginnungagap separated by unfathomable distances, Noah gazed upward as he watched the disappearing flying creature that represented the second THE level Lifeform to have encountered him.","He prepared to cautiously begin moving and exploring this dangerous place more thoroughly while maintaining maximum vigilance.","Of course, one of the persistent questions that continued buzzing in his analytical mind was why these two overwhelmingly powerful THE entities had seemingly looked directly at him, analyzed him carefully, and then proceeded to completely ignore his presence.","What had they perceived or recognized that caused them to dismiss him as non-threatening or perhaps not even as food?","As he ran his own unique internal diagnostics on himself to try and understand this phenomenon, he blinked with sudden realization as he came across a particular finding that seemed obvious once noticed.","He felt clearly the terrifying suppression of The Light of Ginnungagap pressing constantly against The Way of Hunger burning inside his existence. The 90% reduction in capability was unmistakable and severely limiting.","He felt this suppression intensely in this aspect of his dual Sovereignty.","But remarkably, he did not feel any corresponding suppression whatsoever on The Way of Mana.","Mana flowed through him completely unimpeded and unrestricted.","Mana was not being suppressed by this primordial domain.","Mana was not suppressed!","Oh!","His mind raced with the implications of this discovery as understanding began to dawn!","—","Belonging.","It was one of the most fundamental drives that pushed entities across all of existence to seek connection and recognition.","Some beings spent entire lifetimes searching desperately for a place where they truly fit. Where their nature was understood and accepted rather than feared or rejected. They wandered from civilization to civilization, from fold to fold, constantly seeking but never finding that elusive sense of home.","They would try to adapt themselves, to suppress their true nature, to become what others expected them to be. And yet the feeling of being fundamentally out of place would persist like a constant ache in their core existence.","The cruel irony was that belonging could not be forced or manufactured through effort alone. One could not simply decide to fit in somewhere and make it so through determination.","And then sometimes, in the most unlikely and unexpected of circumstances, a sense of belonging would emerge from absolutely nowhere.","In the most hostile environment imaginable, where survival itself seemed impossible, an entity might suddenly discover they were exactly where they were meant to be all along.","Not because they had changed themselves to fit the place, but because the place recognized something fundamental within them that resonated with its own ancient nature.","Sometimes belonging came not from finding those exactly like oneself, but from being in a place that accepted what one truly was at the deepest level.","Belonging!","Perhaps that was the ultimate paradox of belonging...it could not be found by those who sought it desperately, but it would appear unexpectedly to those who had stopped looking and simply remained true to their fundamental nature!"]},{"number":4571,"title":"Chapter 4571: Chapter 4570: The First Tongue I","paragraphs":["All existence viewed themselves as the protagonists of their own story.","The things happening around them naturally revolved around their perspective and their journey. If they found themselves in a world of cultivation, they would believe themselves to be heaven-defying geniuses destined to develop the highest tier dao bone and stand triumphantly above everyone else.","But more often than not, realistically speaking, they would likely become mere sacrifices for pill refining. Fuel for someone else’s advancement.","If another entity found themselves in a grand epic filled with intricate musings of order and chaos, they might genuinely believe themselves to be the chosen one prophesied to lead countless others out of darkness and into salvation.","Often times even this heartfelt belief was fundamentally untrue. There was no chosen one selected by fate or destiny. There was only existence itself flowing according to its own incomprehensible patterns.","And existence did not choose anyone to be grander or more significant than another. One had to make this choice for themselves through deliberate action and unwavering will.","Noah knew with absolute clarity that he was originally a nobody.","So he had systematically forged his own concepts and actively altered existence to transform himself into somebody worth acknowledging. He had purposefully given himself the distinction of The Weaver of Existence and The Weaver of Extremity through deliberate cultivation.","And he had cultivated the concepts of Cheats and Protagonist so he could actively forge himself into whatever entity he needed to become to survive and thrive.","Because of his weavings of The Protagonist, he had inadvertently positioned himself at the center of unfolding flows of existence. Not because he was inherently some chosen being blessed by cosmic forces, but simply because he had learned how to manipulate existence in specific ways that placed him in this advantageous position.","At this moment in time, he was not successfully tangling with terrifically powerful entities in existence like THE Living Paradox, or THE Living Origin, or THE First Hunger, or even THE Creature himself because he was anyone particularly special or unique.","He did not delude himself with comfortable lies to believe that he possessed some sort of hidden inheritance or innate power that would naturally make him stand out against these terrifying monsters who literally had existence itself at their fingertips.","All he fundamentally had was himself and his determination. He knew with brutal honesty that if he slipped or made a critical mistake even once, that would simply be the end for him. Complete collapse.","So he endlessly forged his existence and his foundation to be genuinely capable of standing up against such overwhelmingly powerful beings. And the main and only real weapon that he possessed for this impossible task was something he had cultivated even before he forged the concepts of Cheats or Protagonist.","It was always Mana.","Oh, Mana!","And even this particular energy could not truly be considered something uniquely special to him alone. Countless creatures throughout existence utilized and had access to various forms of energy.","What was genuinely astounding for him was his systematic cultivation to make Mana infinite within his existence. What was truly glorious for him was forging his entire being behind this single concept as he walked the very Way of Mana itself and was building his entire Civilization around it as foundational principle.","He had taken what countless other trillions upon Decillions of creatures throughout existence also possessed and systematically elevated it to a point where it became utterly undeniable.","He was laying his claim across all of Existence with a simple but profound declaration: that energy, that pure Mana specifically, had to be behind absolutely everything.","So he smiled with satisfaction as he looked around at the terrifying region surrounding his position in Ginnungagap.","\"Mana is behind everything,\" he said aloud with a voice carrying conviction. \"So is its distinction even more critically important in Ginnungagap specifically? For it to not be suppressed by this domain, it has to be considered genuinely native to this place. And even Hunger did not receive the distinction of something native here!\"","The theory was becoming increasingly clear in his analytical mind. What he needed to do now was systematically explore to better understand the implications.","If Mana was truly deemed native to this primordial domain, and this place was filled with environmental instabilities and Malformed Ginnu Lifeforms, just what extraordinary things could he potentially accomplish by leveraging it?","In a place saturated with immense existential danger, there were a few distinct approaches where he could proceed forward. He could choose careful exploration, moving around cautiously and slowly breaking down each mystery with methodical analysis.","Or alternatively...","Noah closed his eyes with decision made and focused his awareness inward.","DUM! DUM!","He felt the powerful beat of his heart resonating through his chest. He felt THE Organ of Civilization spinning rapidly within his mind with concentrated purpose.","He placed his hand deliberately on his chest over his heart and spoke with a simple command.","\" Run free, Mana ,\" he said with a voice carrying absolute authority.","His smiling figure began to shine with brilliant blue-gold radiance as his body transformed into concentrated energy. He began systematically releasing vast seas of blue-gold Primus Mana that spread outward in all directions from his position!","HUUM!","His Way of Mana expressed freely. His weavings of existence made manifest. His greatest wonder unleashed without restraint.","He spread it out across the landscape with complete freedom and abandon!","Why carefully navigate this land of death where his existence could be violently unraveled in storms of instability at any unpredictable moment, when he could instead loudly leverage the one unique aspect of his being that was considered native to this place?","Perhaps conventional wisdom suggested he should absolutely not do this reckless thing. But he did it anyway because at this critical moment, when he unleashed endless waves of his Primus Mana without limitation, he felt unfathomably free.","He felt a profound sense of belonging as he experienced his Primus Mana flowing endlessly outward through the environment all around his position.","HUUUM!","As he continued this dramatic release, the instability and disastrous weavings of existence nearby began to surge catastrophically. They began spreading outward rapidly across the surrounding Gigaparsecs in response to his actions.","For long seconds, he maintained this flooding release of pure Primus Mana.","And seconds continued to pass without immediate catastrophe.","And then...","| Little Thing, why are you being so unnecessarily loud?|","BOOM!","...!"]},{"number":4572,"title":"Chapter 4572: Chapter 4571: The First Tongue II","paragraphs":["Everything froze instantly in response to that ancient voice.","Noah’s eyes opened wide as he observed how the surroundings had entered a unique state of temporal suspension. His Mana had integrated with the surrounding region so profoundly and uniquely that it felt like waves of an endless ocean had formed across the landscape.","Yet it was now all completely frozen in place as if time itself had stopped flowing. His existence vibrated with recognition of overwhelming power as he looked ahead toward the source of the voice.","In the distance, he could see both the massive wooly mammoth and the arthropod-like creature that had examined him earlier. They were looking in his direction now, but they clearly were not the ones who had spoken.","They actually stayed back at a distance with seemingly annoyed expressions on their alien features.","And far ahead of both of them, Noah saw a massive creature that possessed a vaguely humanoid shape but seemed to be completely overflowing with dense hair covering every surface.","This ancient-looking entity’s entire body appeared covered by obsidian-gold hair so thick that none of his actual features were fully visible beneath the coverage. Even his face was completely obscured behind the flowing strands.","The being radiated presence that spoke of incomprehensible age and accumulated wisdom. When he spoke, his words seemed to carry weight like ancient proclamations of fundamental truth.","Noah observed with cautious analytical eyes as in this environment of frozen time and space, a single hairy hand emerged slowly from the dense obsidian-gold hair covering the entity’s form.","This hand reached out and touched the frozen seas of Primus Mana that Noah had released. And even though Noah could not actually see the face of this tremendously powerful entity beneath all that hair, he could almost tangibly feel a sense of genuine surprise emanating from it.","He looked at this being with cautious but shining eyes as he opened his mouth and spoke with deliberate simplicity.","\"Hello,\" he said clearly.","A single word. A simple greeting.","But the response was unexpected.","An immense silence followed his spoken word before moments later, the hairy entity’s voice echoed out again through the frozen space.","|What rubbish are you trying to communicate with that crude method?| the voice said with tone mixing confusion and instruction. |You were just speaking perfectly clearly with The First Tongue moments ago. Your intent was filled with hope, unbound confidence, and wonderful novelty. I can still feel those qualities resonating now. Use your proper Voice to speak. Use The First Tongue as you were doing.|","As Noah heard these instructive words, his eyes opened even wider with sudden realization and understanding.","The voice was not actually coming from the head region of this entity covered completely with hair. Instead, it manifested as a pulse of obsidian-gold light surrounding them, emanating directly from their Way of Existence itself.","Their Way of Existence that seemed overwhelmingly grand and incomprehensibly refined. But within its fundamental structure, Noah could distinctly feel clear traces of Mana at its absolute core.","The First Tongue , this ancient being had called it.","Naturally, the only method of communication he had just been using before speaking aloud was his glorious Primus Mana flowing freely.","And so with this understanding clarified, he closed his mouth again. Pure blue-gold Primus Mana gushed forth from his existence once more as he deliberately spoke using Mana itself as the medium.","As he spoke with The First Tongue directly.","| Hello ,| he communicated through pure Primus Mana expression.","The glorious hairy humanoid entity moved closer in response as their body pulsed with terrifically concentrated power that made the environment resonate.","| Yes yes, hello indeed, Little Anomaly,| the ancient voice responded with what almost seemed like satisfaction . |What is it specifically that you are searching for in these malformed weavings of Existence to be expressing yourself so loudly and freely here?|","Noah’s eyes shone even brighter with analytical focus as he looked directly at this terrifying THE level entity. Details began falling rapidly into his enhanced perception through his Lens of Civilization.","A comprehensive status sheet materialized before his vision.","| Name: Aeon-Strand Keeper, Ul’moreth THE Primeval Titan)|","|Classification: First Generation Ginnu Lifeform|","|Age: Exists since Ginnungagap’s formation|","| Depth: THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty|","|Complexity: Undefined (predates measurement systems)|","|Purity: Undefined (incompatible with standard metrics)|","|WAY OF EXISTENCE|","| The Way of Primordial Continuity|","|Philosophy: All things flow from The First Tongue and return to it eventually|","|GENESIS PRINCIPLES (3)|","|1. Genesis Principle of Undifferentiated Mana - Mana before it specialized|","|2. Genesis Principle of Temporal Perpetuity - Time as continuous flow rather than discrete moments|","|3. Genesis Principle of Existential Foundation - The bedrock upon which all reality constructs itself|","|SINGULARITY PRINCIPLES (5)|","|1. Singularity Principle of Infinite Patience|","|2. Singularity Principle of Accumulated Wisdom|","|3. Singularity Principle of Harmonic Resonance|","|4. Singularity Principle of Ancestral Memory|","|5. Singularity Principle of Primordial Preservation|","|UNIQUE ATTRIBUTES|","|Keeper of Thr First Knowledge |","|Hair of Continuity - Each strand contains compressed history and can extend across dimensions|","|Native Authority - Complete immunity to Ginnungagap’s suppression effects|","|Non-aggressive unless fundamental laws are violated|","|Believes all paths eventually lead back to The First Tongue|","Noah looked at the overwhelming details of this terrifically ancient being. But he could not pull his eyes away from one specific section of the information.","The Principles listed in the status sheet.","Above Singularity-level Principles, this entity possessed something fundamentally different and more profound.","This being held Genesis Principles!","And all three of them related directly to Mana and its foundational nature in existence.","Oh!","Noah had met many creatures over the past months and days of his journey through time and space, but none had made him stop and truly observe them as deeply as he was currently examining this entity standing before him.","Ul’moreth.","THE Primeval Titan.","The status sheet of this being alone contained an overwhelming amount of information to unpack and process, with one of the most significant revelations being the Principles classified at a tier standing distinctly above the level of Singularity.","Genesis Principles.","This ancient entity who followed The Way of Primordial Continuity actually possessed three complete Genesis Principles, with each one seeming progressively grander and more profound than the last.","The Genesis Principle of Undifferentiated Mana. The Genesis Principle of Temporal Perpetuity. The Genesis Principle of Existential Foundation.","Each one appeared just as magnificent if not more magnificent than the last in its implications. What Noah would give to somehow get his hands on understanding even one of them completely!","Even more ridiculously extraordinary was how this being was not merely at the Surface Depth or even the Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty, but instead stood at the absolutely terrifying classification of THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty.","He was a terrifically powerful and mighty being as Noah looked at the obsidian gold waves of his Way pulsing around him. And Noah could undoubtedly observe clear traces of pure Mana wrapping around the core of that Way like foundational threads!"]},{"number":4573,"title":"Chapter 4573: Chapter 4572: The First Tongue III","paragraphs":["Such a tremendously powerful being had already said a great deal of profound things that had expanded Noah’s knowledge significantly. But there was considerably more that he wanted to understand, and his hunger for comprehension was burning intensely.","This entity had directly asked him what he specifically wanted by spreading out his Primus Mana so loudly and freely across this domain.","So Noah responded with straightforward honesty. Well, not really speaking with verbal words as much as vibrating and pulsing with his Primus Mana itself. The energy being referred to by this ancient being as The First Tongue.","|I am simply looking to advance on my Way of Existence and attain THE Civilizational Authority as quickly as circumstances allow,| Noah communicated through pure Mana expression. |I am also actively searching for knowledge and understanding. I am very interested to learn more regarding this First Tongue you have mentioned, since I have always known it simply as Mana.|","He paused before continuing with honest self assessment.","|I know instinctively that I am stepping my feet in the correct direction with my cultivation. But I seem to be fundamentally lacking the proper building blocks of knowledge and understanding to progress as efficiently as I could be. I need...foundational comprehension.|","THE Primeval Titan looked at Noah with what felt like unique consideration, though his face remained completely obscured beneath the dense obsidian gold hair. He raised one hairy hand with deliberate motion.","The two massive creatures positioned behind him responded immediately. The wooly mammoth like Void-Tusk Colossus and the arthropod flying entity both released concentrated bursts of their own respective Ways of Existence in acknowledgment.","Then they began moving away with purpose as if they had been formally dismissed to freely resume whatever activities they had been engaged in before this interruption.","And thus the only entities remaining in this frozen sea of golden blue Primus Mana were Noah and THE Primeval Titan, standing in contemplative observation of each other.","Ul’moreth’s ancient voice resonated across the space between them with profound weight.","|What a genuinely weird thing you are, Little Anomaly,| he said with tone mixing amusement and interest. |Asking me to explain something fundamental, and yet you already hold more intrinsic purity of it than most other entities I have encountered across eons. Like asking me to describe water while you yourself are drowning in an ocean of it.|","He shifted his position slightly, his hair flowing with the movement.","|But very well. Let me illuminate what The First Tongue truly represents at its core.|","|Before there were words to describe power, before concepts crystallized into distinct Sovereignties with their own identities and dominions, there existed only The First Tongue,| he began with voice carrying ancient authority. |Pure, undifferentiated potential that flowed through the primordial void like breath flows through lungs. What you call Mana, Little Anomaly, is not merely one energy among countless others that entities can choose to cultivate.|","His presence intensified with emphasis.","|It is the original language through which existence first learned to speak itself into being. The fundamental alphabet from which all other forms of communication and expression would eventually derive.|","BOOM!","Noah felt his entire existence buzzing powerfully as he absorbed these words. His Way was roiling and pulsing with recognition as he continued listening with absolute focus.","| All the countless Sovereignties that entities across Existence now cultivate and wage war over...Storm, Hunger, Origin, Paradox, Time, Space, and all the rest...they are specialized dialects that emerged when The First Tongue fragmented and differentiated into comprehensible words,| Ul’moreth continued with flowing wisdom. |Like a mighty river splitting into countless tributaries over time, each individual stream believes itself unique and separate, completely forgetting they all flow ultimately from the same ancient source.|","|We who remain here, the Malformed Ginnu Lifeforms, have kept The First Tongue within our core existence even with our own differentiations and specializations. One can even say we have no choice but to do. We do not steer far from that primordial foundation no matter how much we evolve or refine ourselves.|","His hand gestured broadly at the environment.","|Did you wonder why Ginnungagap does not suppress what you wield so freely? Because effective suppression requires the recognition of foreignness, of fundamental otherness. How can this primordial domain possibly reject what has always been its own essential essence since formation?|","|The Light of Ginnungagap looks upon your flowing Mana and sees not an intruder or invader to be eliminated, but rather a child who has finally returned home after wandering lost through ages of differentiation and specialization. You are recognized as native because you carry The First Tongue in a form that predates the very concept of foreign versus native.|","HUUM!","Noah’s mind raced with the implications as Ul’moreth continued his profound explanation.","| There exists a fundamental paradox in the nature of power cultivation, one that has consumed the contemplation of the wise, | he said with philosophical weight. |To grow stronger, must one specialize and refine, walking ever further from the primordial simplicity? Developing focused mastery over specific concepts and authorities?|","|Or does true power actually lie in returning to the beginning, to that state of undifferentiated potential where all possibilities existed simultaneously before choice narrowed them into singular paths?|","His voice carried genuine uncertainty.","|The First Tongue holds no definitive answers to this eternal question, only more questions that echo through eternity without resolution.|","Noah’s existence continued to buzz and resonate intensely as he absorbed the words of this ancient entity. Their voice with its immense depth and accumulated wisdom seemed to be actively urging his Way forward through pure comprehension!","New prompts began materializing rapidly before his vision.","|Your Way of Existence is advancing at accelerated pace through direct transmission of ancient knowledge.|","|Understanding of core weavings has deepened substantially.|","|Integration of The First Tongue concept with existing Mana cultivation occurring.|","|THE ORGAN OF CIVILIZATION: DEVELOPMENT ALERT|","|Current Maturity: 13%|","|Understanding of foundational principles accelerating development.|","|New pathways opening within Organ structure.|","Noah observed these prompts flickering across his enhanced perception as Ul’moreth looked directly at him. And even though Noah could not actually see the face of this tremendously ancient being beneath all that flowing hair, he could almost tangibly feel as if they were smiling with satisfaction at his rapid progress.","They continued speaking while carefully observing Noah’s advancement in real time.","|It is genuinely unique to witness one advance significantly on their Way in real time from what I dismissively call the rubbish words of someone like me,| Ul’moreth said with what sounded like pleased surprise. | But I will continue with the lesson since you are proving to be such a receptive creature.|","|There is an old understanding, Little Anomaly, older than the very distinctions between THE and Pre-THE classifications that entities now obsess over. It says that all existence across all domains and all eras is fundamentally a conversation The First Tongue is having with itself, asking endless questions about what it could potentially become if it truly tried.|","His voice grew more intense with the weight of this revelation.","|Every entity, every manifestation of power, every cultivated Sovereignty is simply Mana exploring a different answer to the eternal question: what am I capable of being? Each specialization represents one possible answer among infinite possibilities.|","|But your expression is genuinely unique among those I have encountered,| he said with voice carrying genuine interest. | The intent you radiated when you spread out your weavings so freely felt boundless and unrestricted . You, in your infinite expression of Mana, are asking a question that The First Tongue rarely poses to itself.|","His presence leaned forward slightly.","|What if I refused to choose a single path? What if I remained everything simultaneously instead of becoming something specific and limited?|","BOOM!","Noah’s body became suffused with more and more concentrated waves of pure Primus Mana in response to this profound understanding. His eyes began burning brilliantly and releasing visible beams of blue gold light as comprehension cascaded through his existence.","In front of his vision, new prompts materialized with critical information.","|Understanding of your Way has vastly advanced through alignment with primordial truth.|","|The concept of Infinite Mana has been philosophically validated at fundamental level.|","|Your approach of refusing specialization has been recognized as legitimate path.|","|THE Organ of Civilization has advanced further|","|Current Maturity: 15%|","|Foundational understanding of The First Tongue is continuing to be incorporated into development.|","|Efficiency of Primus Mana processing increased by 99%.|","|Path toward THE Civilizational Authority clarified substantially.|","Noah’s entire existence trembled with the weight of advancement as he stood before THE Primeval Titan , absorbing wisdom that entities would wage wars to obtain!"]},{"number":4574,"title":"Chapter 4574: Chapter 4573: The First Tongue IV","paragraphs":["Across existence, entities specialized in their cultivation and advancement.","The very act of following any Way that was not pure Mana could be considered a form of specialization, even if practitioners did not consciously recognize it as such.","The Way of Fire, The Way of Ice, The Way of Gravity, The Way of Destruction. One could mention countless concepts across all domains and folds, and there would be corresponding specializations built around each one.","Noah had many powerful concepts cultivated within his existence. Gravitation, Polarity, Fire, Chaos, and many others pulsed with potency inside him. But he had deliberately not chosen to make any of them his fundamental Way of Existence. He had chosen Mana over all of them as his core foundation.","If he had instead chosen to follow The Way of Infinity as his fundamental path, would he have been considered to have specialized in that concept? And would such a choice have meant losing pure Mana entirely from his cultivation?","He could not say for certain what might have occurred. But because he had chosen The Way of Mana as his foundation, he could now fully embody the quality of Infinity within that Mana itself without sacrificing versatility.","And now, as he received more and more profound knowledge regarding this wonder from an ancient teacher, his Way was advancing even further with remarkable speed. Knowledge remained absolutely critical when it came to making genuine progress in one’s Way of Existence.","THE Primeval Titan looked at Noah with what felt like growing discernment beneath all that flowing hair.","|It is not impossible to keep advancing without choosing a specialized identity,| Ul’moreth said with measured consideration. | But it is extraordinarily difficult for reasons most entities do not comprehend. Pure Mana, The First Tongue itself in its undifferentiated state, simultaneously holds all possible identities and none at all. This creates a fundamental problem.|","His presence intensified with emphasis.","| Existences who wish to cultivate power must choose something specific to attach their Way to, to give it a defined identity and direction. Otherwise, they would catastrophically explode from trying to express all identities in existence simultaneously. After all, individual entities themselves are not boundless in their capacity. They have limits to what they can contain and process.|","|You somehow managed to avoid this existential constraint entirely. You fully formed your Way around Mana, The First Tongue itself without collapsing. The only explanation for why your existence did not implode when you decided to make your fundamental path The Way of The First Tongue was that you also had to be boundless in some critical aspect. You had to be compatible with taking on Mana’s already boundless identity without being destroyed by that boundlessness.|","His voice carried a question that was also an answer.","|If all of us could have accomplished what you have done, do you genuinely think we would not all be walking The Way of The First Tongue in its pure form rather than accepting variations and specializations of it?|","BOOM!","Another set of profound words made complex truths suddenly clear in Noah’s understanding.","The issue was simple when properly explained. The First Tongue , pure Mana in its undifferentiated state, contained the potential for every possible identity that could exist. Life, Death, Helios, Singed, Outerversal, Fire, Ice, Storm, Hunger, Time, Space, Gravity, and infinite others all existed as potential expressions within it.","For a normal entity with finite capacity to declare \"I follow The Way of Mana\" would be like trying to pour an ocean into a cup. The sheer boundless nature of what Mana represented would overflow and shatter any container that tried to hold all of it simultaneously.","So entities specialized. They chose one tributary from the infinite river. They declared \"I will be Fire\" or \"I will be Storm\" and accepted the limitations that came with such focus in exchange for the ability to actually survive their cultivation.","But Noah had declared his Way to be Mana itself while simultaneously possessing Infinite Mana as a fundamental characteristic of his existence. He had made himself a boundless container before attempting to hold the boundless substance. His infinite capacity matched the infinite potential of what he was trying to cultivate.","That was the critical difference. That was why his path was possible when it should have been impossible.","Noah’s entire existence continued to shine with luminous and terrifically bright light as he absorbed the full implications of this revelation. His body radiated waves of blue gold Primus Mana with increasing intensity.","Ul’moreth looked at him with what felt distinctly like a smile beneath all that obscuring hair. The ancient being rose upward slightly and spoke with purposeful direction.","| Come on, follow me. There is more you must witness and understand.|","With such words, THE Primeval Titan radiated concentrated obsidian gold light that wrapped gently but firmly around Noah’s form. The energy began pulling him along smoothly, heading deeper into the heart of Ginnungagap’s ancient landscape.","Noah continued monitoring his rapidly advancing Way of Existence as they traveled. New comprehensions were integrating into his foundation with each passing moment.","This revelation explained so much. This was precisely why his weavings of Protagonist, Cheats, and Loot had been buzzing with such fervor since his arrival here!","Oh, what a genuinely glorious place Ginnungagap was turning out to be!","---","In an entirely different direction of Ginnungagap’s vast territory, separated by countless Gigaparsecs of dangerous terrain, a very different scene was unfolding.","BOOM!","\"I! Fucking! Hate! Ginnungagap !\" The voice of THE First Hunger boomed out across the chaotic landscape with genuine frustration and rage.","The surrounding environment trembled as THE First Hunger and THE Living Origin fought desperately against three massive Malformed Ginnu Lifeforms that had ambushed them after slipping past the first.","The first creature resembled a serpentine dragon covered in crystallized obsidian scales, but its body twisted through dimensions in ways that made tracking its position nearly impossible. Its multiple heads existed in different spatial layers simultaneously, striking from angles that should not geometrically exist.","The second was a massive arachnid with legs that extended through temporal rifts, allowing it to attack from multiple points in time at once. Each strike came from both past and future simultaneously, creating paradoxical wounds that tried to collapse causality itself.","The third appeared as a shifting mass of liquid obsidian that could not maintain consistent form, constantly flowing between solid and ethereal states. It absorbed attacks by simply ceasing to exist at the moment of impact, then reforming to strike back.","The battle was absolutely brutal in its intensity.","THE First Hunger had his jaws opened impossibly wide, releasing seas of obsidian crimson Hunger that systematically devoured massive chunks of the creatures’ existence. But the suppression of The Light of Ginnungagap reduced his authority by ninety percent, forcing him to expend tremendous effort for effects that would normally be trivial!"]},{"number":4575,"title":"Chapter 4575: Chapter 4574: The First Tongue V","paragraphs":["His Way of Hunger manifested as countless ravenous mouths that snapped and consumed, but they moved sluggishly compared to his normal devastating speed. He was forced to fight with precision rather than overwhelming power.","THE Living Origin stood beside him with expression of intense concentration. Her Way of Origin manifested as white gold chains that attempted to bind the creatures to their foundational state, forcing them to return to simpler forms that could be more easily managed.","But the Ginnu Lifeforms resisted her authority instinctively. They had been born from The First Tongue before the concept of Origin had fully differentiated, giving them partial immunity to her power.","The clash of their Ways created spectacular visual displays as fundamental concepts warred against each other.","And yet despite being outnumbered and severely suppressed, both THE entities were maintaining the advantage through sheer skill and accumulated experience. Their Ways were not just defending but actively evolving through the pressure of combat.","THE First Hunger’s Hunger was becoming more refined, learning to devour the very concept of resistance itself rather than just physical matter. THE Living Origin’s chains were beginning to bind not just forms but the underlying principles that allowed forms to exist.","They were both growing stronger even while struggling, their comprehension deepening through this brutal trial.","But the frustration was evident in their expressions. This should have been a trivial encounter for entities of their caliber. The suppression made everything unnecessarily difficult and tedious!","---","Across Ginnungagap’s endless landscape, in yet another region entirely, Noah was experiencing a vastly different journey.","The terrifying regions of unstable existence that might have posed lethal threats to him were being crossed with remarkable speed and safety as Ul’moreth pulled him effortlessly along through the chaos.","Zones of collapsing reality that would have unraveled Pre-THE entities in moments passed by without incident. The ancient being navigated through the deadly terrain as easily as one might walk through an open field.","| Where are we going? | Noah asked with calm curiosity.","Ul’moreth’s reply came with patient explanation.","| You are walking the correct path and have attained understanding that others cannot replicate. You possess something genuinely unique. But everything you currently have remains rudimentary and incomplete in its development, | he said with measured assessment. |I have given you merely a glimpse of what The First Tongue truly means. You are stringing together your syllables incoherently like a child learning to speak. You do not really know much about the language’s deeper structure yet.|","His voice carried purpose.","|I will teach you more comprehensively. I will show you exactly how much you still need to learn. You stand at less than one percent of true understanding of The First Tongue’s complete framework. I will also show you others like me. The Malformed Ginnu Lifeforms who remember the earliest expressions.|","As they crossed this endless and terrifically dangerous landscape with ease, Ul’moreth asked a question that invited contemplation.","| Why do you think we are called Malformed Ginnu Lifeforms specifically?|","Noah simply shook his head and expressed honestly that he did not know the answer.","Ul’moreth’s form shone with concentrated obsidian gold light as he began another lengthy explanation. Around his body, waves of his Way occasionally formed into illusory diagrams and representations that illustrated his words with startling clarity.","Images of energy coalescing into the first attempts at structured forms appeared and dissolved around them as he spoke.","|You perceive us as Malformed Ginnu Lifeforms, and that designation carries more truth and tragedy than those who speak it casually from distant folds could ever comprehend,| he began with voice carrying weight of ages. | But let me illuminate a fundamental misunderstanding that permeates this terminology, Little Anomaly.|","An image formed showing The First Tongue as pure flowing energy attempting to take physical shape for the first time.","| We were not malformed by accident, by corruption, or by some catastrophic failure in the process of our creation. We were malformed by necessity, by the very nature of what it means to be the first attempts at structured existence emerging from undifferentiated chaos.|","The visual shifted to show Mana crystallizing into bizarre shapes that defied conventional geometry.","| When The First Tongue first began expressing itself into discrete forms rather than remaining as pure potential, it did not possess the refined knowledge or accumulated wisdom of countless generations of evolution to guide it. Imagine, if you can, the very first time Mana attempted to become something other than itself. It had no template to follow, no successful example to emulate, no understanding of what constituted proper form versus aberrant deviation.|","|It simply tried. And whatever emerged from that trying was the foundation upon which all subsequent existence would build.|","Images of strange creatures taking form from primordial energy filled the space around them.","| We who dwell here in Ginnungagap are not malformed descendants of perfect ancestors who degraded over time. We are the originals, Little Anomaly. The first drafts. The prototype attempts. When The First Tongue first learned to crystallize into living beings with consciousness and will, it produced us. Creatures whose very existence embodies the mutations and anomalies inherent in any virgin attempt at formation.|","He gestured at his own form.","| My hair that spirals through dimensions it should not touch? That is Mana learning for the very first time that space could be curved and folded. The Void-Tusk Colossus you observed earlier with tusks that pierce dimensional barriers? That creature represents the moment when The First Tongue discovered that existence had layers and tried to create something that could navigate between them, not quite understanding the process yet.|","More images formed showing the arthropod creature Noah had seen.","| The arthropod you saw flying above, with segments that exist partially in different dimensional layers simultaneously, creating that horrifying visual of presence and absence? That is not corruption or damage, but rather The First Tongue’s initial exploration of the concept that a single entity could occupy multiple states of reality at once. It did not understand the rules well enough yet to make such a being stable or aesthetically pleasing by the standards that would later develop. It simply attempted, and the result was what you now classify as malformation.|","The visuals shifted to show refined, perfect forms emerging much later.","| What later generations call perfection...the clean lines, the logical structures, the bodies that obey conventional spatial and physical laws...these are refinements that emerged only after The First Tongue had practiced existence countless times and learned from each iteration what worked and what did not.|","| But we Ginnu Lifeforms carry within our very structure the raw experimental data of The First Tongue’s first attempts. Every anomaly in our forms, every aspect that seems wrong or impossible, represents a lesson that The First Tongue learned about the boundaries of what existence could support.|","His voice carried pride mixed with ancient sorrow.","| This is why we appear so terrible and alien to entities who evolved in the later, more refined eras of existence. The mutations and anomalies were not flaws to be corrected, Little Anomaly. They were discoveries. Each malformation taught The First Tongue something essential about the nature of structured existence.|","The images dissolved as he concluded his explanation.","|So yes, Little Anomaly, we are Malformed Ginnu Lifeforms. But malformed only by standards that were invented after we already existed. By the standards of The First Tongue itself, by the measure of pure undifferentiated Mana before it learned what shapes it should avoid, we are exactly as we were meant to be. The living record of existence learning to exist, preserved in this ancient domain so that the memory of existence’s first words would never be lost.|","BOOM!","One thing was becoming astoundingly clear to Noah. Ul’moreth genuinely liked to talk and explain. But every single word felt grand and revelatory. Noah wanted him to simply continue speaking endlessly!","But suddenly their movement slowed as the obsidian gold brilliance around them began to flicker and dim.","|Oh, we have arrived,| Ul’moreth announced with tone suggesting significance.","The golden blue radiance enveloping them dissipated completely as they came to a gentle stop.","Noah looked around with heightened awareness and curiosity.","Where exactly was here? Where had this terrifying ancient monster brought him to in the depths of Ginnungagap?"]},{"number":4576,"title":"Chapter 4576: Chapter 4575: The First Tongue VI","paragraphs":["When the obsidian gold light surrounding Noah and Ul’moreth finally faded, Noah found himself descending toward something that expanded his comprehension of scale.","They were approaching the edge of a massive floating landmass that had to be tens of thousands of Gigaparsecs wide at minimum. The sheer size of it was something that many could not fully grasp due to the workings of Ginnungagap!","The edges they were landing toward displayed serene obsidian waterfalls that cascaded downward into the void below. But these were not water in any conventional sense. They were flowing instabilities of existence itself, filled with pure concentrated Mana that had not yet differentiated into any specialized form.","The falls shimmered with all possible colors and none simultaneously, creating visual paradoxes.","Noah’s gaze swept across the vast landscape stretching before him. Endlessly extending forests covered much of the visible terrain, their trees unlike anything he had seen before. Mountains rose in the distance with peaks that seemed to pierce through dimensional barriers.","But what caught his attention most intensely was a figure sitting casually near the edge of this vast floating landmass.","He had to squint and enhance his vision to be certain he was seeing correctly. There was a humanoid entity wearing a simple straw hat, holding a fishing pole with one hand while the line was cast down into the endless unstable obsidian expanse far below.","The being appeared remarkably human at first glance. But as Noah’s perception sharpened, he noticed the malformation that marked this entity as a Ginnu Lifeform.","The figure possessed six arms in total, though only one currently held the fishing pole. The other five rested casually at different positions along their torso. Their skin carried faint obsidian patterns that pulsed with concentrated authority.","Tendrils of obsidian radiance wrapped around the fishing line, extending down into the chaos below as if the entity was literally fishing in the unstable weavings of existence itself.","The being looked up calmly as Noah and Ul’moreth completed their descent and arrival.","| Ul’moreth, what have you brought over now?| the entity asked with a voice carrying relaxed curiosity mixed with mild amusement, of course, it was expressed through The First Tongue!","Ul’moreth replied with measured calm as they landed on the solid surface.","| Something new in existence, or really something unfathomably old depending on your preferred definition,| he said with tone suggesting significance. |Ains, meet Little Anomaly. Little Anomaly, this is Ains, THE Fisherman.|","Noah’s eyes shone brightly with analytical focus as he looked at this tremendously powerful being. He nodded and used pure Primus Mana to express himself in greeting.","|Hello ,| he communicated through concentrated pulse of Primus Mana.","The moment his greeting manifested, THE Fisherman’s eyes pulsed with sudden recognition. He squinted with closer examination before speaking with growing interest.","|Is that...| he began with voice trailing off.","Ul’moreth smiled beneath his obscuring hair and nodded with confirmation.","|As I mentioned, a Little Anomaly indeed,| he said with voice carrying satisfaction . |The First Tongue comes in all forms across existence. Sometimes it manifests simply and is easy to recognize. Sometimes it appears in understandable patterns. Other times it presents with tremendous complexity. And sometimes it emerges as something genuinely anomalous.|","His tone became more contemplative.","|I found a truly unique anomaly here. He is simply a living variation of The First Tongue itself. At least, that is how I would prefer for him to think of himself currently. Cannot inflate his ego when he knows so little and remains so comparatively weak. Cannot have him beginning to believe all of existence could potentially fall under his fingertips before he has even survived to maturity...he could die so, so quickly and easily after all because of his potential...|","Ul’moreth’s voice carried dark amusement.","| But hey, how many entities across all of existence have gone into the embrace of The First Tongue so completely? He is already so deeply in tune with it that if anyone does manage to collapse him, he may even make existence itself richer through his dissolution.|","THE Fisherman laughed heartily at this observation, his voice booming across the landscape.","| Bahaha, do not terrify the Little Anomaly with such morbid speculation!| he said with genuine mirth. | You brought him here for what purpose exactly?|","Ul’moreth responded with simple directness.","| Just some foundational teaching and demonstration. Help me out if I am missing anything critical in my explanations.|","As he said this, he turned his attention back to Noah with teaching focus.","Noah looked between these insanely powerful beings with mixture of wonder and assessment. He could not help but shake his head internally at the situation he found himself in.","This Fisherman entity was particularly interesting. Noah had immediately looked at him with his Lens of Civilization upon arrival, but unlike Ul’moreth and the other Ginnu Lifeforms he had encountered, this being had actually veiled himself with intentional obscuration.","All Noah could observe through his enhanced perception was limited information.","|Name: Ains, THE Fisherman|","|Distinctions: THE Patient Angler, THE Keeper of Primordial Hooks, THE One Who Fishes In Chaos|","|Additional Information: VEILED|","|Note: This entity has deliberately obscured deeper analysis.|","It was a unique status sheet!","As for Ul’moreth’s words about not inflating his ego when he remained so weak, Noah understood this truth more intimately than anyone else possibly could.","Just because he was rapidly expanding his knowledge regarding Mana and The First Tongue, learning what it truly stood for and what it meant... that he was apparently the only entity in existence to have successfully declared this as his fundamental Way without catastrophically exploding from the attempt, he still did not view himself as some transcendent being who could now effortlessly control all of existence.","Because he really was not.","All he genuinely had right now was potential.","And potential was an extraordinarily dangerous thing if one mistook it for actual present strength. He had the theoretical potential to arguably stand against and possibly even exceed entities like THE Creature and THE Living Paradox eventually. That was the extent of what his current advantages represented.","He absolutely would not allow himself to be deluded by how boundless and infinite this potential appeared to be. For now, he would calmly continue to expand his knowledge systematically and gather more critical information.","It seemed existence had truly unfathomable depths and mysteries still waiting to be discovered.","So he observed THE Fisherman with attention as he and Ul’moreth came to fully stand before him.","New prompts flashed before Noah’s vision with environmental information.","|You have arrived at: The Primordial Genesis Shore|","|Classification: Ancient Ginnu Settlement|","|Description: One of the first stable landmasses formed in Ginnungagap.|","|Inhabitants: Unknown number of Ginnu Lifeforms of varying power levels.|","|Warning: This location contains entities at THE Surface Depth and potentially beyond.|","|Environmental Properties: Minimal suppression for those who speak/know The First Tongue.|","...!"]},{"number":4577,"title":"Chapter 4577: Chapter 4576: The First Tongue VII","paragraphs":["Noah processed this information with growing understanding of just how significant this location was. The Primordial Genesis Shore!","One of the first places where chaos became order, where The First Tongue permeated thoroughly!","He stared at the seeming endlessness of the landscape stretching before him and wondered with genuine curiosity what other terrifying entities and incomprehensible things lay within its vast depths.","| Little Anomaly.|","Ul’moreth’s voice called out to him with focus, pulling his attention back from contemplation of the environment.","| Before I take you deeper into the Shore to meet others and show you more of what exists here, let me provide you with some rudimentary foundational knowledge, | he said with measured purpose. | So that someone with your extraordinary potential does not embarrass themselves through ignorance when encountering those who understand these concepts intimately.|","The space around Ul’moreth began to shimmer as his obsidian gold authority manifested into illusory diagrams that would illustrate his upcoming explanation.","| You vibrate your Mana with such remarkable purity, Little Anomaly, and yet you do not truly speak in the linguistic sense, | he began with voice carrying patient instruction. | You shout formless intent into the void and expect existence to interpret your meaning successfully. Like an infant crying without developed vocabulary, relying entirely on others to guess what you need based on emotional tone alone.|","An illusory image formed showing an entity releasing shapeless bursts of energy.","| But what if I told you that The First Tongue is not merely a poetic metaphor I use for dramatic effect? What if I explained further that Mana, or more accurately The First Tongue itself, is quite literally a language with grammar, syntax, vocabulary, and structural rules as precise as any spoken tongue? In fact, considerably more precise than any verbal language could ever achieve.|","The diagram shifted to show structured patterns of Mana arranged with glorious precision.","| This knowledge is not known by many across the vast expanses of existence,| Ul’moreth continued with emphasis. | Beyond us Ginnu Lifeforms who were born when The First Tongue was still actively being formed and refined, and perhaps a scattered handful of truly exceptional entities across all the eras who somehow stumbled upon fragments of this understanding through extraordinary circumstances, virtually no one in the Infinite Unfurling comprehends that Mana, that The First Tongue, can be wielded as the fundamental language of existence itself rather than merely as raw energy to be shaped through will.|","| The First Tongue, at its most fundamental basic unit of expression, contains what we call a Phoneme. A single letter in the alphabet of reality itself. Every Phoneme, every deliberately structured pulse of pure undifferentiated Mana, represents a fundamental unit of meaning. Like the letters of any alphabet, individually quite simple in isolation, but capable of infinite complexity when properly combined through grammatical rules.|","The illusory diagrams showed individual pulses combining into more complex structures.","| What you have been doing, spreading your infinite Mana across Ginnungagap’s domains, is functionally equivalent to shouting the same vowel sound repeatedly at progressively increasing volume,| he said with tone mixing observation and instruction. | Impressive in its raw power and fundamental purity, absolutely. But utterly lacking in sophisticated linguistic meaning. You produce the raw sound successfully, but you do not form actual words. And without constructing proper words, Little Anomaly, you cannot speak the complete sentences that reshape reality at its deepest foundational levels.|","|I tell you this not to diminish what you have already accomplished, which is genuinely extraordinary,| Ul’moreth added with reassuring emphasis. | But rather to illuminate how much further you can potentially advance from this already impressive foundation. You already possess what nearly all of existence does not have access to. The direct connection to pure undifferentiated Mana that allows The First Tongue to be spoken freely at all.|","| This is extraordinarily rare beyond measure. Most entities could dedicate eternity itself to trying to learn what I am about to teach you and never succeed in even basic comprehension, because they have specialized too far from the primordial source. They have traded versatility for focused power and cannot return to the undifferentiated state.|","The diagrams showed branching paths, with most leading away from a central source while one path maintained connection.","| The First Tongue operates across multiple fundamental tiers of expression, each building upon the previous level like a tower reaching toward absolute comprehension of existence itself. But we will start with the foundation.|","Nearby, Noah listened with complete focus as his existence continued to advance with each piece of new information. His THE Organ of Civilization was making measurable progress with every additional concept integrated into his understanding!","He noticed THE Fisherman shake his head with apparent boredom at Ul’moreth’s lengthy explanation.","The entity pulled up his fishing line and examined it, finding nothing caught. He cast it back out into the chaotic waters below with practiced motion.","| Ul’moreth, all your extended talking has thoroughly bored me,| THE Fisherman said with voice carrying playful criticism. | Let me take over the explanation for the Little One here. My voice has considerably sweeter quality to it than your ancient droning, yes?|","He turned his attention directly to Noah with more animated energy.","| So Little Anomaly, continuing from where Ul’moreth was heading before he put us all to sleep with excessive verbosity, let me explain the basic foundational level of The First Tongue with more efficiency.|","| The first tier of expression is what we call Phonemes as he was trying to mention. These are the individual pulses, the basic units of structured Mana that every entity across existence manipulates and releases, usually without any conscious awareness of what they are truly doing from a linguistic perspective. When you release a burst of Mana to create some effect, you are producing Phonemes. But you produce them as raw, unstructured expressions.|","THE Fisherman gestured with one of his free hands for emphasis.","| We Ginnu Lifeforms understand Phonemes as letters, as the fundamental alphabet of existence itself. We know intrinsically that each pulse can be shaped with intentional structure, with grammatical precision, to produce effects that completely transcend mere energy manipulation. This is why our malformed bodies can wield authority that seems utterly impossible by conventional understanding. We are not breaking or violating the rules of existence, Little Anomaly. We are speaking fluently in its native language while all others fumble awkwardly with broken dialects and corrupted vocabulary.|","He looked over at Ul’moreth with amused expression.","| Bahaha, Ul’moreth, how was that explanation? More concise, yes? I believe I captured the slight undertone of arrogance in your typical voice quite accurately, yes?|","Ul’moreth’s form remained still, though Noah imagined the ancient being was blinking with mild exasperation beneath all that obscuring hair. They turned their attention back to Noah and continued the lesson.","|I will resume the explanation from here,| Ul’moreth said with patient tone. | There are higher tiers of expression beyond individual Phonemes, structures of increasing linguistic complexity that I will not burden you with until you have properly mastered the basics. Let me focus your attention on teaching you to speak individual letters correctly before we even attempt to construct complete words.|","| Even this foundation, properly understood and applied with skill, will elevate your capabilities beyond what most THE level entities can achieve across their entire existence.|","His presence intensified with significance.","| This is the gift I offer you, Little Anomaly. The ability to speak rather than merely shout, to construct precise linguistic meaning rather than rely entirely on formless intent. Are you prepared to learn The First Tongue as it was originally meant to be spoken?|","The question hung in the air with tremendous weight.","Noah felt his rapidly expanding existence resonating with the knowledge being shared. He replied with simple conviction as his eyes pulsed with a glorious sense of tyranny!","|I am ready to learn.|"]},{"number":4578,"title":"Chapter 4578: Chapter 4577: The First Tongue VIII","paragraphs":["|Now we begin the true lesson, Little Anomaly,| Ul’moreth said with voice carrying the accumulated gravity of ages.","|A single Phoneme, Little Anomaly, could represent the concept of Fire. Another might embody Ice. Still others express concepts like Motion, Stillness, Expansion, Compression, Life, Death, and countless others spanning all possible ideas. Each one is a complete letter in the alphabet of existence itself, a basic unit of meaning that The First Tongue uses to construct more complex expressions.|","|It is possible for entities at THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty to potentially learn individual Phonemes if they maintain adequate connection to The First Tongue. Below that level of power, an anomaly like yourself will find it relatively easy to accomplish. For others without your unique advantages, successfully learning even one Phoneme would be an extraordinary rarity. Unless they possess a genuinely deep connection with The First Tongue naturally.|","His voice intensified with the weight of revelation.","| When you speak a Phoneme of The First Tongue, when you properly activate that single pulse representing a concept, you are not merely generating an effect through your own limited personal power and individual understanding.|","|The Phoneme, when spoken correctly with proper pronunciation and structural integrity, automatically borrows and channels power from all the surrounding Principles of Existence that are prevalent across reality itself. It reaches out through the fundamental fabric of existence and draws upon the accumulated weight of every expression of that concept that has ever manifested anywhere across all domains and all time.|","The revelation hung in the surrounding air like thunder waiting to strike.","Noah blinked.","What?","He had to rewind what he heard and replay it again!","When you activate a Phenome, you would not merely be generating an effect with your own power? You would borrow power and channel the power of all surrounding Principles of Existence that are prevalent?","What?!","|Let me make this abundantly clear with a concrete example that will demonstrate the magnitude of difference we are discussing here. If you, with your current level of cultivation, were to generate fire through conventional energy manipulation means, you would be producing flame powered exclusively by your own Mana reserves, shaped by your own personal comprehension, limited strictly by your own developed Principles. The result would be fire scaled precisely to your individual capability and nothing more.|","|But if you were to speak the Phoneme of Fire in The First Tongue, if you were to utter that single basic letter with proper pronunciation and structural accuracy, the effect would be categorically different in nature. That single pulse would reach out across existence and borrow power from the surrounding fire based Principles of Existence that are woven permanently into the very fabric of reality.|","His presence leaned closer with teaching emphasis.","| Simply whispering the letter for Fire in The First Tongue, even imperfectly with flawed pronunciation, will unleash flame backed by multiple Grand Principles that exist across all domains. And if you spoke that Phoneme with sufficient perfection, with flawless pronunciation and complete structural understanding, it would draw upon even Singularity Principles related to the concept of Fire.|","| The flames produced would not be your fire, Little Anomaly. They would be Fire itself, the platonic ideal of combustion and transformative heat, channeled through your utterance but powered by the accumulated weight of that concept across all of existence. Do you comprehend the fundamental difference? This is not merely a matter of quantitative scale. This is qualitatively different in kind.|","Noah’s mind reeled with the staggering implications as Ul’moreth continued his explanation.","| This is why The First Tongue is considered the original language through which existence burned with creative force. Because when existence first declared let there be Fire, it was not generating flame through personal effort or individual power. It was speaking a Phoneme that defined what Fire would be across all future reality, establishing the Principles that would govern combustion forever after.|","| And this is also why so few entities across all of existence understand or can effectively utilize The First Tongue, Little Anomaly. It is not merely difficult to learn. It is almost impossible for those who have already deeply specialized into particular dialects. Once you have committed yourself fully to The Way of Storm or The Way of Hunger or any other specialized path, you have fundamentally altered your existence to resonate with that particular frequency.|","| Attempting to speak The First Tongue in its pure form after such deep specialization is like trying to sing in a vocal register your physical form can no longer reach. The capability has been permanently traded away in exchange for focused mastery. It is not absolutely impossible, as there are exceptional monsters out there who can still accomplish it despite specialization. But mainly those who have some connection to undifferentiated Mana, or those who recognize their Way stems from The First Tongue and inherently maintain a connection to it in its purest state, retain the ability to speak these Phonemes with any real effectiveness.|","His obsidian gold hair began to shimmer with concentrated purpose and building power.","| Now, Little Anomaly, let me demonstrate what a single Phoneme can accomplish when spoken with adequate understanding and sufficient power. Watch carefully with all your enhanced perception. Observe not just the result, but the underlying structure of what I am doing. This...is the Phoneme of Fire.|","HUUM!","Ul’moreth’s entire being seemed to become perfectly still for a moment. Then he began to vibrate with a specific pattern that Noah could perceive through his enhanced senses.","The Phoneme of Fire.","Externally, it manifested as a sound that was not quite sound in any conventional sense. It was more like a fundamental frequency that existence itself recognized and responded to instinctively. A single sustained pulse of Mana vibrating at a specific rate that represented the complete concept of combustion, of transformation through heat, of energy unleashed through rapid oxidation.","But Noah could see considerably deeper than just the surface manifestation. He could observe the internal structure of what Ul’moreth was actually doing beneath the obvious display.","The ancient being was not simply releasing shapeless Mana into the environment. He was shaping it into a precise linguistic pattern, a grammatical construct that existence itself could read and interpret like written text. The pulse had rhythm, cadence, tonal quality. It was a complete declarative statement compressed into a single letter.","And as that Phoneme was spoken with Ul’moreth’s tremendous accumulated power and flawless understanding backing it, Noah witnessed something truly extraordinary.","The light of multiple Principles he could barely recognize began to shimmer in the surrounding environment. These were not Principles that Ul’moreth personally possessed or had utilized himself. They were Principles related to Fire that existed prevalently throughout Ginnungagap and even beyond.","The Principle of Rapid Transformation. The Principle of Consuming Heat. The Principle of Elemental Fury . And numerous others Noah could not fully identify or comprehend.","All of them responded immediately to the spoken Phoneme. All of them offered their accumulated power to support the utterance.","In the next moment, reality itself seemed to tear open above them with violent force.","An infinitely rising pillar of obsidian gold fire erupted into the skies of Ginnungagap with such devastating power that the environment itself trembled from the manifestation!","The flames were not normal combustion by any measure. They burned with concentrated authority that completely transcended conventional understanding.","The heat radiating from the pillar was so intense that Ul’moreth had to immediately position himself protectively in front of Noah, his hair extending outward to form a shielding barrier. Even with that substantial protection, Noah could feel the terrifically scorching temperature trying to penetrate through.","Nearby, THE Fisherman made a sound of mild annoyance as if the temperature had gotten slightly too uncomfortable for his casual fishing. He harrumphed with displeasure and calmly went back to observing his line.","Meanwhile, Noah’s mind processed the power level with shocking recognition. That infinitely rising column of obsidian gold fire possessed enough concentrated force to completely scorch and incinerate a THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entity without any difficulty whatsoever. It was flame backed by the accumulated weight of Fire as a concept across all of existence.","From a single letter. From one Phoneme spoken with proper pronunciation and adequate power.","The pillar continued burning in the sky above them like a beacon of primordial creative force as Ul’moreth allowed it to persist for several more demonstrative moments before finally ceasing his utterance.","The obsidian gold flames dissipated gradually, leaving the surrounding environment scorched but fundamentally intact.","Ul’moreth turned back to face Noah fully, his presence radiating satisfaction at the successful demonstration.","| That, Little Anomaly, was the result of a single Phoneme of The First Tongue, | he said with voice carrying measured intensity. | One letter from the languagr of existence, spoken with adequate power and understanding. Not a complete word, not a sentence, not a paragraph of complex meaning. Simply the equivalent of pronouncing the letter F in your crude common speech.|","|But because it was uttered by someone like me, with my accumulated power and deep understanding of The First Tongue’s linguistic structure, that single letter channeled enough force to extinguish weak THE entities completely. If I had spoken a complete set of Phonemes, something we call a Logos which represents a full word constructed from multiple Phonemes arranged with grammatical precision, the effect would have been incomparably more devastating.|","Oh!","Phenomes were the letters, and Logos...were words!","But he was just getting introduced to the letters at this moment.","Ul’moreth’s obsidian gold hair flowed with purposeful motion as he continued his explanation.","|The Phoneme I just demonstrated represents a concept that can only crudely be translated into common language as Fire, or Immolation, or Combustion, or any other woefully inadequate definition of flame and transformative heat. But The First Tongue does not deal in such imprecise terminology. The Phoneme contains the complete and total essence of what Fire is at a fundamental level of existence.|","|When spoken properly, it does not politely ask existence \"please create fire for me if you would be so kind.\" It authoritatively declares \"Fire exists here now\" with such absolute conviction that reality has no choice whatsoever but to comply immediately. And because the declaration is made in existence’s own native language, it responds with the full accumulated weight of that concept across all its manifestations throughout all of reality.|","Ul’moreth’s presence seemed to focus entirely on Noah with concentrated teaching intensity.","| This will be the first Phoneme I teach you to speak properly, Little Anomaly. The letter that represents the primordial concept of transformative heat and consuming flame. And before you object that there might be simpler starting points for a beginning student, understand that I am choosing this particular Phoneme quite deliberately for specific pedagogical reasons.|","| Fire is one of the most fundamental concepts in structured existence. It was among the very first expressions when The First Tongue began differentiating into specialized forms. Learning to speak this Phoneme will teach you the basic grammar and underlying structure that supports all other Phonemes. Master this one, and all the others will become progressively easier to learn through pattern recognition.|","BOOM !","The weight of this teaching settled over Noah as he prepared himself to attempt the impossible.","Learning to speak existence’s native language!","His existence radiated a profound sense of quintessential tyranny as he closed his eyes...and he breathed."]},{"number":4579,"title":"Chapter 4579: Chapter 4578: The First Tongue IX","paragraphs":["In another corner of Ginnungagap, separated by countless Gigaparsecs from the peaceful shore where teaching was occurring, a very different scene unfolded.","While Noah received instruction on a single letter, a Phoneme of The First Tongue, something remarkably similar was manifesting elsewhere with far more violent intent.","The battle between THE First Hunger and THE Living Origin against the three Malformed Ginnu Lifeforms had escalated to a critical point. The serpentine dragon with crystallized obsidian scales had locked multiple heads around Tor’s arms, attempting to collapse his Way through dimensional compression. The massive arachnid struck from temporal angles, its legs piercing through past and future simultaneously. The liquid obsidian mass flowed between solid and ethereal states, absorbing attacks and reforming to strike back.","Tor cursed violently as he sensed something shifting in the fundamental nature of the battle.","\"They are doing their monstrous things !\" he roared with recognition and mounting frustration.","The three Malformed Ginnu Lifeforms suddenly stopped their physical assault. Their bodies began to vibrate with synchronized purpose, their malformed structures pulsing with concentrated power.","Faint flickers of pure Mana, hidden deep within their core existence, activated simultaneously.","They were speaking The First Tongue!","All three entities began to utter a single letter with tremendous effort and power expenditure. A letter that most closely represented the concept of Fire in existence’s native language.","The surrounding reality responded immediately to their pronunciation.","Multiple Grand Principles related to flame and combustion began to shimmer into visibility throughout the chaotic landscape. The Principle of Consuming Heat manifested as waves of distortion. The Principle of Elemental Fury pulsed with building intensity. The Principle of Rapid Transformation flickered at the edges of perception.","Then Singularity Principles began to respond as well, lending their incomparably greater weight to the utterance.","Three pillars of terrifying flame erupted simultaneously from the Ginnu Lifeforms, each with its own unique coloration based on the entity conjuring it.","The serpentine dragon produced flames of deep crimson mixed with obsidian black, spiraling upward with devouring hunger. The arachnid’s fire manifested as pale violet that existed partially in multiple temporal states, burning past and future simultaneously. The liquid mass generated silver white flames that shifted between solid and ethereal just like its own form!","All three pillars converged on THE First Hunger and THE Living Origin with devastating force.","Tor’s eyes widened with genuine alarm as he felt the concentrated power bearing down on them. This was by far the strongest attack they had faced in this entire miserable encounter!","THE Living Origin was already moving, her Way of Origin manifesting as defensive chains that attempted to bind the incoming flames to their foundational state before combustion. White gold barriers formed in intricate geometric patterns.","Tor released seas of obsidian crimson Hunger that devoured massive sections of the approaching fire, consuming the flames before they could reach them. His jaws opened impossibly wide, creating voids that swallowed existence itself.","The collision created spectacular explosions of conflicting authorities as fundamental concepts warred against each other.","Fire tried to consume. Hunger tried to devour. Origin tried to reduce everything to its source state.","The landscape around them scorched and cracked from the sheer intensity of power being exchanged. Reality itself groaned under the pressure of so many high level Principles activating simultaneously.","But despite the terrifying nature of the attack, both THE entities proved their competence and vast experience. Through coordinated effort and masterful application of their Ways, they managed to defend against and systematically disperse the converging pillars of flame.","Tor stood amidst the dissipating fire with expression of absolute rage. His entire body radiated killing intent as his Way pulsed with fury.","\"Okay. Okay! That’s it!\" he roared with voice shaking the environment. \" I tried to hold back somewhat in this damned suppressive place, but no more restraint!\"","His obsidian crimson Hunger exploded outward with terrifying new intensity.","They were holding back somewhat. Because they knew...one should not easily kill a Malformed Ginnu Lifeform! One Ginnu killed would have one branded and hunted down by all other Ginnu as they would not survive Ginnungagap!","---","Back on the Primordial Genesis Shore, in the calm and ancient landscape, teaching continued without awareness of the violent events occurring elsewhere.","Ul’moreth settled into a teaching posture, his entire demeanor shifting to that of patient instructor.","| Now, Little Anomaly, I will break down the internal structure of this Phoneme so you can understand what you must reproduce,| he said with measured focus. | Pay attention to every detail, because pronunciation is absolutely critical. A single error in frequency, rhythm, or tonal quality will cause the Phoneme to fail completely, or worse, to produce unpredictable and potentially catastrophic results.|","Noah kept his eyes closed and breathed in and out with steady rhythm as he listened with complete concentration.","| The Phoneme of Fire begins with a rising pulse, | Ul’moreth explained with clarity. | You must start at a baseline frequency that resonates with undifferentiated Mana, then systematically increase the vibration rate. But this is not a smooth, continuous increase. It must follow a specific progression that matches the natural expansion rate of combustion.|","His voice carried the weight of precise instruction accumulated over eons.","| As you raise the frequency, you must simultaneously compress the Mana into tighter and tighter density. This creates internal tension, potential energy waiting to be released. The compression follows an inverse relationship to the frequency increase. As one rises, the other contracts proportionally.|","| When the frequency reaches a specific threshold, one that you will learn to recognize through practice, you must introduce a percussive accent. A sharp spike in intensity that punctuates the rising tone. This accent represents the ignition point, the moment when potential becomes kinetic, when compression transforms into expansion.|","| Immediately following the accent, you must allow the Mana to explode outward in a controlled expansion. Throughout all of this, you must maintain a specific emotional and intentional quality. The Phoneme is not just mechanics and mathematics. It carries meaning, purpose, identity. Fire is transformation, consumption, purification, destruction that enables renewal. Your intent must embody all of these qualities simultaneously without contradiction.|","Ul’moreth paused deliberately to ensure Noah was absorbing the full complexity of what was being taught.","| The entire sequence, from initial pulse to final expansion, must occur within a precise temporal window. Too slow, and the Phoneme loses coherence and dissipates without effect. Too fast, and the structure collapses before it can channel the surrounding Principles. The timing I am about to demonstrate represents the minimum viable duration for this Phoneme.|","The ancient being prepared himself again for another demonstration with teaching purpose.","| Watch now as I speak the Phoneme once more, but this time I will slow down the process significantly so you can observe each component separately. In actual practice, these elements blend together seamlessly, but for teaching purposes, I will separate them for your analysis.|","Ul’moreth began to vibrate again, but this time the Phoneme unfolded in deliberate slow motion.","Noah kept his eyes closed and sensed everything with pure Mana, seeing colors even more vibrantly through his enhanced perception. He could observe each distinct phase with crystalline clarity.","The rising frequency that climbed from baseline. The simultaneous compression that created visible density increase in the concentrated energy. The sharp percussive accent that marked the critical transition point. The controlled explosion outward in geometric patterns.","Rising, compression, accent, expansion.","And threading through all of it like a fundamental melody, the intentional quality that gave the mechanics meaning and purpose!","This time, because the Phoneme was spoken slowly for teaching demonstration, the resulting fire was considerably less intense. Instead of an infinite pillar reaching toward the sky, a controlled sphere of obsidian gold flame manifested above them, rotating slowly to display its internal structure.","| Do you see the framework now, Little Anomaly?| Ul’moreth asked with patient instruction. | Each component serves a specific purpose. Remove any single element, and the Phoneme fails. Execute any element incorrectly, and the result will be flawed.|","The teaching flame dissipated as Ul’moreth concluded his explanation.","| This is not simple energy manipulation where close enough produces acceptable results. The First Tongue demands precision because it is fundamentally linguistic rather than merely mechanical. You are not generating fire through brute force. You are speaking a word that means Fire, and existence responds to correct pronunciation.|","| Now, Little Anomaly ,| Ul’moreth said with voice carrying both encouragement and challenge . |I have demonstrated the Phoneme twice. I have broken down its internal structure and explained each component. I have given you the theoretical framework you need to understand what you must accomplish.|","His presence seemed to focus entirely on Noah with concentrated teaching intensity.","|It is time for you to attempt speaking your first letter of The First Tongue. Do not expect success on your initial try, or your tenth, or your hundredth. Most entities require years of dedicated practice before they can produce even a flawed approximation of a single Phoneme. But you possess advantages that others do not. So perhaps you will surprise even these ancient expectations.|","Ul’moreth gestured for Noah to begin.","| Speak the Phoneme of Fire. Attempt to reproduce what I have demonstrated. And we shall see how quickly you can learn to speak existence’s native language.|","Truly speak in The First Tongue.","Noah could not help but smile as his mind currently existed in an unprecedented state of wonder and focused clarity.","He felt the beat of his Heart. He felt the rhythm of THE Organ of Civilization pulsing within his existence.","And he began.","Fire .","He knew Fire intimately. He held fire within him as one of his many cultivated concepts. Fire was one of his closest companions in his journey of advancement.","And he now simply needed to utter fire in a different language. In THE Language of Existence itself, in The First Tongue.","His Primus Mana burned with terrifying intensity as concentrated waves of The First Tongue surrounded him. His figure unconsciously began rising toward the skies, lifted by the sheer power flowing through him.","The rising frequency. The simultaneous compression. The sharp percussive accent. The controlled explosion outward.","He executed every single component in proper sequence with The First Tongue, and it felt natural. It felt normal, as if he should have always been communicating like this since the beginning of his existence.","And at the very end of the carefully structured sequence, he spoke.","|Fire.|","...!","HUUM!","The word could not possibly encompass what the character truly stood for in The First Tongue. It was simply the most literal and inadequate translation possible.","The moment he uttered it with proper pronunciation and structure, everything changed.","BOOM!","He felt his THE Organ of Civilization explode with advancement alongside the rest of his existence. His Complexity and Purity spiked upward by hundreds of Decillions instantly as THE Organ of Civilization right away exceeded twenty percent development in a single magnificent leap.","And when he opened his eyes to observe what he had created, wonder filled his being.","\" Ah...\"","He found himself floating at the center of a glorious and beautifully swirling hurricane of blue gold flames that rose infinitely toward the skies and began expanding outward across an entire Gigaparsec of space- powered by Principles he did not even have access to.","The flames were unique. They were Fire itself, the platonic ideal of transformative heat and consuming combustion, powered by the accumulated weight of that concept across all of existence.","They swirled around him in patterns of breathtaking complexity, forming geometric shapes that shifted and evolved. Blue gold light illuminated everything for vast distances, turning the sky into a canvas of primordial creative force.","Noah smiled with genuine sense of wonder mixed with recognition of the tyrannical power he had just manifested. He could instinctively feel the truth of what he had created.","These flames carried such concentrated authority that it would be impossibly difficult to find any Pre-THE entity who could survive contact with them!","Oh!","From speaking a single letter. From pronouncing one Phoneme of The First Tongue with adequate accuracy on his very first attempt.","Down below on the shore, far beneath the expanding hurricane of blue gold flames, two ancient beings looked at each other with very different expressions.","Ul’moreth stared upward at his student’s achievement with mixture of pride and shock.","| Well damn,| he said simply, his usual verbose nature momentarily stunned into brevity.","THE Fisherman had stopped his casual fishing entirely. His six arms were still as he gazed upward with serious and stern expression that contrasted sharply with his earlier playful demeanor.","When he spoke, his voice carried somber weight that made the gravity of the situation abundantly clear.","| This is dangerous, Ul’moreth ,| he said with tone mixing concern and warning. | He is dangerous, which means he is therefore in immense danger himself. You have to be extremely careful with how you handle this Little Anomaly. One wrong step, and The Others will descend upon him.|","WAA!","The implications hung heavy in the air as they both continued watching Noah floating at the center of his first spoken word in existence’s native language.","A hurricane of blue gold fire that proclaimed to nearby regions of Ginnungagap that something unprecedented had just occurred, even as Ul’moreth and THE Fisherman moved to conceal!"]},{"number":4580,"title":"Chapter 4580: Chapter 4579: The First Tongue X","paragraphs":["Far from the Infinite Unfurling, far from Ginnungagap’s ancient shores where teaching and wonder unfolded, there existed a place that defied conventional understanding.","Inside THE Loom.","An endless sea of obsidian gold paradox stretched infinitely in all directions, filled with unfathomable musings of existence itself. The paradox was not empty abstraction. It contained actual immense Weavings of Existence alongside its inner workings, its flow, and even more horrifyingly, the way that existence expressed itself through fundamental language.","The sea of paradox seemed to sit atop all of it with tyrannical glory, drowning everything beneath its weight while simultaneously revealing truths that should remain hidden. And even this overwhelming perception was merely what could be glimpsed at surface level. There were countless more intricacies lurking in depths that defied comprehension in this mere glimpse.","In such a terrifying sea, there floated a singular entity with eyes closed as if relaxing in peaceful meditation. His entire existence wore the allure of paradox itself, his form refusing to sit still or maintain consistent state. This was a manifestation of THE Living Paradox. Not his true self, but a powerful projection.","But moments later, the expression alone told a different story. The calmness and relaxation faded completely as a frown appeared on features that rarely showed such emotion.","Something had occurred that should not have occurred.","He maintained countless countermeasures in place to notify him of any major changes across existence. His enemy was THE Creature , the entity that had triumphed in the Infinite Unfurling against all others through methods that remained fucking terrifying even to contemplate.","So THE Living Paradox required countless safeguards and monitoring systems for this entity. Even now, with all his accumulated victories and advantages, he knew with absolute certainty that he had not truly won.","But something had just occurred. A change in the fundamental patterns he observed. And as he pondered what it might be, his frown deepened further as he turned his gaze toward a certain direction.","A place outside THE Loom.","A place where something unprecedented was unfolding.","In the domain that used to be THE Transcendent Paradoxical Folds, now reduced to something far more terrible, the devastation defied description.","The region had become a zone of immense collapse. All of existence in this area seemed dark, swallowed by shadows that consumed light and meaning alike. The only point of illumination came from a single source.","The figure of The Disciple of THE Creature raised a sword that shone brilliantly like a solitary candle of existence refusing to be extinguished. The blade radiated light that seemed to hold a glimmer of a Genesis Principle woven into its very structure.","That faint illumination revealed the absolutely devastating state of the battlefield.","All the False THE Avatars from THE Loom either seemed to be missing entirely or only parts of their bodies remained visible, scattered across the collapsed landscape like discarded toys. Limbs, torsos, heads, all separated and dissolving slowly.","The only one still living and intact was Ambessa, her gaze unfathomably somber as she bellowed with desperation while being chased relentlessly by The First Farmer.","The ancient being moved with calm purpose, his voice carrying patient instruction.","\"Stay still, the harvest will be quick and painless!\"","Khor looked like a small walking calamity given physical form. Her entire presence radiated destruction barely contained. She directed a deadly concentrated gaze toward Schrodinger at this moment, preparing to eliminate that particular threat.","But the figure of The Disciple of THE Creature stepping forward with raised sword caused her to pause with genuine caution. That blade was dangerous even to her.","In the midst of such a terrifying scene of absolute devastation, the figure of The Infiniverse stood with unusual stillness.","She had silently already sent a message to Alexander Asmodeus that he did not need to attempt anything with the Shattered Part of The Heart of Law. His services were no longer required for that particular task.","Because at this moment, something far more significant was occurring.","|Sis, did you receive all that?!| The voice of Ruination echoed out with genuine shock and excitement.","She was referring to the lesson Noah had transmitted across time and space through their absolute connection. The teaching he had received, he had immediately shared with his most important constructs.","The connection between Ruination, The Infiniverse, and Noah remained absolute and unbreakable. At this moment, The Infiniverse nodded as she almost seemed to enter a daze before replying with voice carrying wonder.","|I got it. I fucking got it completely. The First Tongue!|","...!","Ruination was shocked into silence at her sister’s unusual cursing!","The eyes of The Infiniverse held a hint of fanaticism as she processed the implications.","She had direct access to her Master’s weavings through their fundamental connection. She could pull from his Mana reserves as if they were her own. And she was already such an integral construct that existed on a scale bigger than any Transcendent Fold, more complex than any single domain across existence.","By her very nature as a living construct of unfathomable sophistication, The Infiniverse could effectively be considered similar to any Fold across existence. There...had to be weavings of Principles coursing through her structure that made up her existence, just as Principles wove through conventional reality.","In nature, Existence held Principles that most entities did not even know existed or could be accessed.","The First Tongue, through its letters alone, could induce power from surrounding Principles to act on behalf of the one speaking.","As the construct she was, with Principles forming the foundation of her very being, if she was now beginning to learn a language that could make it easier to perceive Principles and even freely initiate assistance from them...","|Hah.|","The Infiniverse laughed lightly with voice carrying dark anticipation.","She closed her eyes with focused concentration.","She remembered every detail of the lesson her Master had transmitted through their connection. The structural breakdown, the precise sequence, the intentional quality required.","The rising frequency that started from baseline. The simultaneous compression that created visible density increase in concentrated energy. The sharp percussive accent that marked the critical transition point. The controlled explosion outward in geometric patterns.","She went through all the details her Master had been taught by ancient beings who understood existence’s native language.","Then she opened her eyes and looked directly toward The Disciple of THE Creature.","His attention had somehow already turned toward her as if he sensed something fundamentally wrong occurring. His laid back expression showed shock and genuine alarm for the first time in this entire battle, as if he recognized what was about to happen.","And he moved fast for the first time ever, crossing vast distance in an instant as he swung his sword with desperate urgency. Existence cried out from the force of his strike as he bellowed with serious intensity.","\"How do you know that?!\"","Apart from him, there was another who reacted with equal alarm.","Schrodinger, whose gaze had been clear and focused throughout the battle, became slightly hazy for a brief moment. As if someone else far grander was momentarily seeing through his eyes, borrowing his perception to observe this impossible event.","And that distant gaze was frowning with deep concern.","Khor was shocked at the sudden eruption of unique power signatures she did not recognize. But The Infiniverse remained exactly where she stood at this moment without moving to defend or retreat.","For the first time since her creation, she spoke in a language older than her Master’s existence.","| Fire.|","She spoke it in The First Tongue.","The word manifested as a perfectly structured Phoneme, carrying all the components her Master had been taught. Rising frequency, compression, accent, expansion, intent.","It was extraordinarily difficult to say which entity in existence was more utterly obscene. Noah, who had spoken his first Phoneme successfully on his initial attempt, or his construct who was given transmitted information about a lesson and successfully uttered her first letter with actual meaning on her very first attempt as well.","She spoke the letter representing Fire in existence’s native language.","And in this region of collapse where reality had been shattered, Principles not even understood by most entities here moved of their own volition in response.","The Principle of Consuming Transformation. The Principle of Primordial Combustion. The Principle of Existential Ignition. And others that had no names in conventional language.","All of them responded to the properly spoken Phoneme.","And... Existence itself began to burn.","Not merely the space or the matter or the energy in this region. Existence as a concept, the fundamental fabric that allowed anything to be, erupted into flames that transcended conventional understanding.","Blue gold fire mixed with silver white radiance spread outward from The Infiniverse’s position with catastrophic speed. The flames burned through collapsed reality, through dimensional barriers, through the very concept of spatial limitation!","The Disciple of THE Creature’s sword strike, carrying a glimmer of Genesis Principle authority, met the expanding wall of existential fire head on.","The collision created an explosion that briefly illuminated the entire collapsed domain like a second sun being born!","—","Many across the vast expanses of existence wondered about The Disciples of THE Creature with a mixture of fear and curiosity.","They pondered exactly what a terrifying entity like THE Creature could have possibly taught his disciples to make them so formidable. What knowledge could the entity that held The Way of Existence itself as his fundamental path impart to those who followed him?","What secrets did he share? What techniques did he demonstrate? What Principles did he illuminate?","The answer was far easier to comprehend than many realized, though no less profound for its simplicity.","THE Creature taught his disciples the same thing Existence taught to all who truly listened. The same lesson that reality demonstrated with every passing moment, every transformation, every beginning and ending across all domains and all time.","THE Creature did not need to create elaborate techniques or invent complex methodologies. He simply showed his disciples how existence already functioned at its deepest levels, then taught them to work with those fundamental mechanics rather than against them.","What he taught them... could very easily be inferred!"]},{"number":4581,"title":"Chapter 4581: Chapter 4580: The Chicken Or The Egg? I","paragraphs":["Existence was paradoxical by nature.","There were countless such paradoxes woven throughout the fabric of reality, and the one entity standing tall and paradoxical above all others was unique even among the extraordinary.","Inside THE Loom , in that paradoxical region filled with incomprehensible wonder, THE Living Paradox floated with deep contemplation as his eyes perceived far too many things simultaneously.","Many misunderstood him. Many misunderstood his fundamental nature and his true ambitions. Even those within THE Loom itself, even the tiny False THE and Pre-THE entities who served his purposes, Even THE...only a select few knew his actual goals. And no others, not even Emotive who stood closest to his confidence, knew his true, TRUE ambitions that lay beneath even those surface objectives.","THE Loom was a grand construct of staggering complexity. Few entities across existence knew that it was actually a weapon, not merely a domain or territory. A weapon directed against The Belly of Existence itself, aimed squarely at THE Creature with calculated precision.","It was an attack and weapon that spanned from The Earliest Folds and even slightly before that primordial era, extending all the way to the current time period. And even that description barely scratched the surface of intricacies that others could not begin to fathom. Some even thought they were its Architects when they were merely led to it!","His enemy was THE Creature , after all, so he had to prepare extensively and with meticulous care. One single slip up, one moment of carelessness, and he would be utterly destroyed without possibility of recovery.","Which was precisely why he had left behind so many layered countermeasures across existence. At the mere sign of a possibility, at even the potential of a countermeasure being triggered as an alarm bell, he would immediately follow up to investigate and respond.","And now, he had to follow up on something unexpected.","When it came to the events unfolding outside of THE Loom in the collapsed former Transcendent Paradoxical Folds, he had so far been relaxing, enjoying the spectacle, and playing around with indirect influence. But might it be time to get genuinely serious about intervention?","A profound silence spread through the paradoxical sea like ripples across still water.","And Paradox, who had been relaxing in languid repose on a throne of endless seas of paradox that lay above existence itself, shifted his body with deliberate motion.","He moved from being laid back in casual observation, and sat upright with focused attention.","He merely sat upright.","But this simple action alone should terrify even THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entities if they could perceive it occurring.","Because when Paradox decided to sit up and pay attention, existence itself trembled!","Oh!","---","In The Infinite Unfurling , deep within Ginnungagap’s ancient territory on the shores of The Primordial Genesis Shore, Noah floated downward with tremendous sense of exuberance after speaking his first ever Phoneme.","His first true letter of The First Tongue.","His entire existence felt utterly ecstatic at this moment as an array of prompts flashed before his enhanced vision with detailed information.","|Phoneme Learned: Fire (Primordial Combustion)|","|Current Mastery Level: Novice Speaker (1st Tier)|","|Mastery Progression: Novice Speaker, Fluent Speaker, Perfect Speaker|","|At Novice Speaker: Can speak Phoneme with basic accuracy, drawing upon Grand Principles|","|At Fluent Speaker: Can speak Phoneme with refined accuracy, potentially drawing upon a nearby Singularity Principles|","|At Perfect Speaker: Can speak Phoneme with flawless accuracy, potentially drawing upon a nearby Genesis Principle|","...!","| THE Organ of Civilization is advancing|","|The Parenchyma within THE Organ of Civilization are now being forged.|","|The Parenchyma represents the functional tissue of THE Organ, the essential matter that performs the primary work of processing and integrating civilizational complexity. Like biological parenchyma forms the working substance of organs, this structure will form the working substance of your civilizational authority.|","|Function: Processes incoming knowledge, refines understanding, converts raw information into usable advancement.|","|Current Status: Initial formation at 23% Organ development.|","|OVERALL ORGAN DEVELOPMENT: 23%|","|Advancement rate: Dramatically increased through First Tongue comprehension.|","...!","Noah observed all of these grand prompts with analytical interest, but instead of focusing entirely on his advancement metrics, he looked down toward the figures of Ul’moreth and THE Fisherman standing on the shore below.","He floated downward gradually as he could feel the hairy figure of Ul’moreth smiling at him beneath all that obscuring hair. But he had also picked up something concerning with his enhanced perception during the earlier conversation.","He landed softly on the obsidian surface and spoke with cautious inquiry.","|I heard mentions of dangers? References to The Others? What exactly is this referring to?|","His Mana perception had been extraordinarily acute during the moment of his breakthrough, catching fragments of the conversation between the two ancient beings.","Ains sighed deeply at his direct question, his six arms shifting position with body language suggesting reluctance to discuss this topic.","Ul’moreth’s body vibrated with acknowledgment before he began his explanation with characteristic thoroughness.","| The Others refer to creatures who are anomalous in their own right and were born just as early as us Ginnu Lifeforms in the primordial eras of existence. Most of them do not sit still peacefully, nor are they free to be like us, simply enjoying existence as it naturally unfolds. They seem to be imprisoned by an incapability of just sitting still and observing. They are always seeking something with desperate intensity.|","|They are like you in that particular regard, Little Anomaly. Always advancing, always cultivating, always pushing boundaries. But on a scale that dwarfs conventional ambition. They seek to impose their weavings over everything. Over Existence itself. Over The First Tongue. Over every concept and principle and law. Everything must bend to their vision.|","His obsidian gold hair flowed with emphasis.","|The Others are entities you may or may not already know by reputation, but the main ones who concern us most are THE Creature, THE Primordial Chaos, THE Living Paradox, THE Secretive Eon, among several others of similar caliber. Each one represents a fundamental approach to existence, a different answer to how reality should be structured and governed.|","...!","|You, Little Anomaly, with what your unique nature managed to accomplish with The First Tongue, can actually be considered one of The Others now. You have achieved something that places you in their category, whether you desired that classification or not. You are no longer merely a cultivator or an exceptional entity. You are now a potential candidate for reshaping existence itself according to your vision.|","|But to understand why there exists such conflict and this desperate need for supremacy among The Others, why they cannot simply coexist peacefully, you have to ask yourself a fundamental question.|","He paused for dramatic effect.","|What came first, Little Anomaly? The chicken, or the egg?|"]},{"number":4582,"title":"Chapter 4582: Chapter 4581: The Chicken Or The Egg? II","paragraphs":["What?","Noah blinked at the seemingly ridiculous question appearing at the end of such a serious explanation.","Ul’moreth laughed heartily at his reaction, clearly enjoying the moment.","| Haha, yes, I know how absurd it sounds! But bear with me, Little Anomaly. There exists a question, one that has consumed the contemplation of many entities across all eras since awareness first emerged from undifferentiated chaos,| Ul’moreth began with voice carrying the weight of ancient philosophical inquiry.","|A question so fundamental that it sits at the very foundation of everything we understand about reality, and yet remains utterly unanswerable despite eons of dedicated contemplation by the wisest minds.|","|The question is deceptively simple in its phrasing, yet incomprehensibly complex in its implications. What came first, Little Anomaly? Existence itself, or The First Tongue?|","The space around him began to shimmer as obsidian gold diagrams formed to illustrate the philosophical paradox with visual clarity.","| Consider the first position held by many powerful entities. Some argue that Existence had to exist first in order for The First Tongue to form as the language of existence. After all, how can a language exist without something for that language to describe? How can there be speech without a speaker to produce it? How can there be words without reality to give those words meaning and context?|","| By this logic, Existence came first as primordial chaos, as undifferentiated potential, as formless void waiting to take shape. And then, from within that already existing chaos, The First Tongue emerged as a way for existence to organize itself, to speak itself into structured forms, to create grammar and syntax from randomness. The language arose from existence, not the other way around.|","The diagrams shifted to show a completely different perspective.","|But then consider the opposing position, equally supported by compelling evidence and reasoning. These entities argue that The First Tongue spoke existence into being, that the language came first and created reality through the act of being spoken. When The First Tongue first declared concepts like space, time, matter, energy, these things came into being specifically because they were named, because they were spoken with proper pronunciation and structure.|","|By this logic, before The First Tongue was spoken, there was absolutely nothing. Not even chaos or void, because chaos and void are themselves concepts that require language to define them. The very first utterance of The First Tongue created existence by giving it definition, by establishing the rules and patterns that would govern all future reality.|","Ul’moreth’s presence seemed to lean forward with emphasis on the critical flaw embedded in both arguments.","| But here is where the paradox becomes truly inescapable, Little Anomaly. If we accept that The First Tongue came first and spoke existence into being, then we must answer a devastating question. If The First Tongue existed before existence, was that not itself a form of existence? How can something be, how can something have the capability to speak and create, without already existing in some form?|","|The moment we say The First Tongue existed first, we have already conceded that existence preceded it, because The First Tongue’s presence is itself existence. We have contradicted our own position through the very act of stating it clearly.|","The diagrams showed the two positions circling each other endlessly without any possibility of resolution.","|This is what The Others have called THE Primordial Paradox. The Chicken or The Egg elevated to a terrifying significance. Which came first? And more frustratingly, how can we possibly determine the answer when the very act of existing in a position to ask the question means we are already operating within a framework where both existence and language are so intertwined that separating them becomes impossible?|","|Ah, you can go round and round in circles as it remains a genuine paradox without solution. Which is why in existence, I would actually not fear THE Creature or THE Primordial Chaos among The Others, despite their terrifying power and ambition.|","His voice dropped to carry genuine warning.","|But I would be most cautious of THE Primordial Paradox, THE Living Paradox specifically. While others argue passionately about what came first and wage wars to prove their position correct, Paradox continues to enjoy the sheer nature of this question itself. That entity thrives on contradiction, feeds on unresolvable conflicts, grows stronger from the very debate that weakens others.|","|That is the one you would have to be most careful of, Little Anomaly. Because while you fight to prove your answer, Paradox has already won by ensuring the question can never be definitively answered.|","BOOM!","Noah’s eyes shone with tremendous luminosity as understanding cascaded through his existence.","Oh, how absolutely right Ul’moreth was, even though the ancient being did not fully know the extent of that truth!","Based on what had already happened years from now in the timeline Noah had experienced, based on what he had witnessed of Paradox’s machinations, that entity had truly set themselves up to be absolutely terrifying in ways that defied conventional understanding.","The one who enjoyed the question more than any possible answer.","The one who won by ensuring no one else could ever truly win!","\"...\"","The information that Ul’moreth continued to provide was expansive and kept opening up different pathways and possibilities that Noah had not even known existed.","Among the many revelations that had just been shared, the identities of The Others swirled in his mind with urgent curiosity.","THE Creature and THE Living Paradox he already knew of from direct experience. But THE Primordial Chaos sounded utterly insane as a concept, alongside THE Secretive Eon whose very name suggested hidden depths.","If they were being mentioned in the same breath alongside entities like THE Creature or THE Living Paradox, THE Primordial Paradox... they had to be immensely powerful existences operating on scales that defied conventional comprehension.","This begged the question once more that had been bothering Noah for some time. Where exactly did all the THE level entities go? Why were they so rare in the current era when logic suggested there should be more of them scattered across existence?","Noah felt like he had an inkling of an idea forming, a working theory that was beginning to take shape in his mind. But it was so wild and potentially disturbing that he would only give it serious credibility when he obtained substantially more information to support or disprove it.","But for now, there was the continuation of expanding his knowledge on The Way of Existence and The First Tongue.","He normally would not give anyone the time of day to be talking so extensively and at such length as Ul’moreth was doing. But regardless of how long winded this entity wanted to be, he could continue talking in entire paragraphs for hours and Noah would not care in the slightest. Talk as much as you wanted, big guy!","Just continue feeding him as much knowledge as possible, and he would advance even further!"]},{"number":4583,"title":"Chapter 4583: Chapter 4582: The Chicken Or The Egg? III","paragraphs":["And as if he could clearly perceive Noah’s shining eyes filled with boundless tyranny and hunger for understanding, the hairy form of Ul’moreth shone with obsidian gold light as he continued with somewhat jovial and laid back tone.","| Do not worry too much about the immediate threat of The Others for now, Little Anomaly,| he said with reassuring emphasis. | When it comes to that fundamental question about what came first, even I have not found an answer that satisfies me completely after eons of contemplation. The Ginnu Lifeforms emerged when The First Tongue was still being actively formed, when existence was learning to speak itself into structured reality, and even we cannot say with absolute certainty which came first because we were integral parts of that formation process itself.|","|We are the living evidence of the question, not the definitive answer to it. We witnessed the process but cannot say whether we observed language creating existence or existence creating language, because the two were so intertwined during formation that separation becomes impossible.|","His presence radiated patient teaching energy.","| What I can tell you is this with absolute conviction. The question matters tremendously because how you personally answer it shapes everything else about how you understand cultivation, advancement, and the fundamental nature of power itself. Those who believe Existence came first tend to view The First Tongue as a tool, certainly a powerful method but ultimately subordinate to the reality it describes. It is useful, it is effective, but it serves existence rather than commanding it.|","|Those who believe The First Tongue came first view it as the ultimate authority, the creative force that shapes all reality through proper pronunciation and grammatical structure. To them, existence itself is subordinate to language, merely the manifestation of what The First Tongue declares into being.|","His presence focused entirely on Noah with concentrated teaching intensity.","|You, Little Anomaly, by choosing The Way of Mana, by declaring The First Tongue as your fundamental path of cultivation, have implicitly chosen a side in this ancient debate whether you consciously realized it at the time or not. You are arguing through your very existence that The First Tongue holds primacy, that language shapes reality rather than merely describing what already exists.|","|And this philosophical position will be one of your greatest challenges going forward. You will encounter entities, powerful beyond measure, who favor the opposing view with passionate conviction. Who believe that Existence came first and that The First Tongue is merely a sophisticated tool for manipulating that pre-existing existence. They will challenge your path directly, they will argue against your fundamental assumptions, and they will seek to prove through combat and philosophical debate that their understanding is superior to yours. To Break your Way.|","| Some will not even care for debate at all and will simply attempt to collapse you immediately, those crazy violent things. They view your position as so fundamentally flawed that conversation is pointless.|","Ul’moreth’s voice carried genuine concern mixed with encouragement.","|How will you defend your position, Little Anomaly? How will you argue that The First Tongue deserves primacy when the very fact of your existence seems to prove that existence preceded your ability to speak? After all, you had to exist before you could learn The First Tongue, which appears to support the position that existence comes first.|","|This is not merely philosophical exercise or abstract contemplation. This is a question that will determine whether your Way can advance to its highest potential or whether it will collapse under the weight of its own contradictions and paradoxes. Reality itself will test whether your answer holds validity, and if it does not, your entire cultivation foundation may crumble.|","The obsidian gold diagrams that had been illustrating his points dissipated as Ul’moreth concluded this particular teaching.","|Your biggest challenge in the battles to come will not be learning to speak more Phonemes or even construct complex combinations of them. It will be arguing your answer to this fundamental question against those who favor the position that Existence came first, and convincing reality itself that your answer deserves to reshape the rules by which all things operate.|","His tone became more serious and warning.","|Do not meet The Others if you are not ready, Little Anomaly. They will absolutely curbstomp you and beat you sideways before they collapse you entirely or devour you for resources. Ah, it is frankly ridiculous how powerful they are. But hey, you have got me as a teacher, so you should be okay! Bahaha!|","Noah smiled at the words as he recognized how genuinely unique Ul’moreth was as an instructor.","Who could he truly think of in his past as a proper Teacher with capital T?","Khor and he had discussed existence and its nature extensively. Tor had helped him in similar ways as they also discussed existence and the mechanics of power. But Ul’moreth’s contributions to the understanding of his Way and the direct teaching of The First Tongue were on an entirely different level of impact.","And in regards to Ul’moreth’s words about not meeting any of The Others right now, this advice was already difficult to follow. He was already deeply embroiled with both THE Living Paradox and THE Creature through various conflicts and connections.","Paradox was a wild card that could be absolutely monstrous and disastrous if provoked or if circumstances aligned incorrectly.","He had to move cautiously and with extreme care.","\"...\"","He immediately sent a mental warning to The Infiniverse through their connection to be ready for absolutely anything and to prioritize survival above all other objectives.","Thereafter, his eyes burned with renewed hunger for more knowledge as he spoke to Ul’moreth with clear intention.","|I will keep everything you have said in mind and process it carefully ,| he said with acknowledgment. | How about we talk more extensively about The First Tongue itself? Maybe I could learn more Phonemes to expand my vocabulary? Or perhaps you could teach me about what exists above Phonemes in the linguistic hierarchy?The...Logos?|","His search for knowledge was absolutely transparent and undisguised.","Ul’moreth and Ains looked at each other and laughed heartily at his enthusiasm, clearly pleased with such a dedicated student.","Ains turned around to continue his casual fishing in the chaotic waters below, his six arms moving with practiced motion as his line cast out once more.","Ul’moreth turned around and began walking toward the endless forests and mountains that stretched across The Primordial Genesis Shore.","| Let me take you further into this little place here ,| he said with voice carrying invitation. | We shall walk and talk. Walk and talk! There is much more to see and much more to teach, Little Anomaly.|","Noah turned to nod at THE Fisherman for a goodbye as this entity smiled lightly and nodded back.","Ul’moreth’s obsidian gold hair flowed behind him as he began leading Noah deeper into the ancient territory where existence first learned to speak."]},{"number":4584,"title":"Chapter 4584: Chapter 4583: Is A Foundation Ever Complete? I","paragraphs":["The Primordial Genesis Shore was unfathomably vast and filled with wonder that defied easy comprehension.","Even the regions that Noah was currently crossing with Ul’moreth were filled with their own unique wonders and intricacies that would require years to fully explore and understand.","The landscape was more stable than the outside regions he had crossed not too long ago, where reality itself seemed to constantly teeter on the edge of collapse. But this stability was held together loosely by civilizational authority woven throughout the environment.","They walked through forests of unfathomably tall trees that stretched toward the sky like pillars supporting heaven itself. The trunks were wider than entire cities, their bark formed from compressed layers of crystallized existence. The canopy far above created a ceiling of interwoven branches that filtered the strange light of Ginnungagap into patterns of obsidian gold illumination.","Each tree seemed to pulse with different types of civilizational authority, as if entire civilizations had somehow crystallized their essence into these ancient growths. Some radiated the authority of conquest and expansion. Others carried the weight of accumulated knowledge and philosophy. Still others hummed with the concentrated power of technological advancement compressed into organic form.","But at the baseline of all of it, obsidian waves of pure Mana could be distinctly felt by Noah. Even more so now that he was beginning to understand The First Tongue a little bit better, he could perceive how these trees were fundamentally expressions of undifferentiated Mana that had been spoken into specialized forms.","As they crossed through this vast primordial forest, Ul’moreth’s voice took on a more somber quality.","| Do you know why Ains is sitting and fishing at the edge of this endless shore? | he asked with a tone suggesting deeper significance.","Noah blinked with mild surprise and looked back in the direction they had come from, though the fishing figure was long out of sight. The question had not struck him as particularly significant before. He had simply assumed the entity enjoyed fishing as a pastime.","So he shook his head to indicate his ignorance.","Ul’moreth continued with voice carrying weight of ancient history and consequence.","| Malformed Ginnu Lifeforms have a very unique bond that binds us together across all of Ginnungagap and beyond, | he explained with careful emphasis. | Collapsing any single one of us is considered akin to collapsing all of us in terms of offense and consequence. Those who do so, regardless of their power or justification, are hunted down by every Ginnu Lifeform across existence until they are found and eliminated. This is our law, absolute and inviolable.|","| Ains, well, something happened long ago. He collapsed a THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty Ginnu in a conflict whose details have been lost to time. It was a monumentally significant event that shook our entire community. I vouched for him among others, arguing that circumstances justified his actions, that the collapsed entity had transgressed first in ways that demanded response.|","| But even with my support and the support of others, there were consequences. For the past countless eons, he has had to sit at the edge of this shore as penance and observation. Never leaving it for anything else, never venturing into the deeper territories or beyond Ginnungagap’s boundaries. It can get quite lonely for him sometimes, fishing in those chaotic waters with only occasional visitors for company.|","Noah’s eyes shone brightly with surprise and contemplation. He had not even considered something like this, had not imagined the complex social structures and consequences that existed among these ancient beings.","Existence was vast with its own intricacies, and everyone held their own stories of triumph and tragedy, of mistakes and redemption.","Ul’moreth perceived his contemplative silence and spoke with philosophical acceptance.","| Haha, do not worry yourself too much about such things, Little Anomaly. Existence is as existence is. We live, we die, and existence continues on regardless of our individual dramas. In the meanwhile, we enjoy The First Tongue and Existence itself and do what we can to understand the unfathomable mysteries out there.|","|If you ever find anyone telling you they have discovered everything or know everything about existence, then such entities have already veered far off the path of genuine understanding. Nobody knows everything, Little Anomaly. Even for me, someone who has existed since the formation of structured reality, there is infinitely much that I do not know and may never comprehend.|","Nobody knew everything.","Noah nodded at these words with genuine agreement. There were countless things in existence, layers upon layers of complexity and mystery. And most entities were only grasping at the very tip of existence’s iceberg, barely scratching the surface of what was truly out there waiting to be discovered.","Ul’moreth continued calmly as they walked deeper into the ancient forest, his teaching focus returning.","| Now, Little Anomaly, you have successfully spoken your first Phoneme of The First Tongue, which is a genuinely remarkable achievement, | he began with voice carrying both praise and expectation. | But speaking it once, even successfully, does not constitute mastery. You are currently at the Novice Speaker level, which means you can produce the Phoneme with basic accuracy. To advance to Fluent Speaker and eventually Perfect Speaker, you need to repeat it constantly until the structure becomes as natural to you as breathing.|","His obsidian gold hair flowed as diagrams began forming around them in the air, showing intricate patterns of energy flow and linguistic structure.","|However, here is where most entities who attempt to learn The First Tongue make a critical mistake that severely limits their progression. They believe they need to speak The First Tongue again and again externally, producing the effect over and over in the physical world to build proficiency. And yes, this does work to a degree. But it is extraordinarily exhaustive on your existence in ways that are not immediately obvious.|","|When you speak a Phoneme outward, you are not merely releasing your own Authority. You are creating a linguistic bridge between your internal existence and all the surrounding Principles of Existence that respond to that utterance. You are essentially opening yourself as a conduit, allowing existential forces to flow through you to manifest the effect.|","|Each time you do this, you are forming and then dissolving that bridge, opening and closing that conduit. Your existence must maintain structural integrity while these tremendous forces pass through it. The Phoneme draws upon Grand Principles, Singularity Principles, even Genesis Principles depending on your mastery level. And when you can eventually connect multiple Phonemes to utter Logos, yes yes, I see your interest in Logos, I will tell you about them in a bit. But all of that accumulated weight flows through your being to manifest externally.|","His presence intensified with technical explanation as the diagrams showed the strain on a body channeling such forces.","|Think of it like this. Your existence is a vessel, and speaking The First Tongue externally is like repeatedly forcing an ocean through a cup. Yes, the cup can channel the ocean’s power for that moment, but the strain of containing and directing such force, over and over, will eventually crack even the strongest vessel. Your Civilizational Authority reserves can deplete. Your structural integrity weakens. Your capacity to maintain the linguistic bridge diminishes with each repetition until you must rest and recover.|","|This is why entities who learn The First Tongue through conventional external practice require years or even decades to master a single Phoneme. They must speak it many times, rest for extended periods, speak it again, rest again. The cycle becomes painfully slow.|","The diagrams shifted dramatically to show a completely different approach, depicting internal pathways within a body with remarkable anatomical detail.","|But there is a trick, Little Anomaly, one that many who attempt to learn The First Tongue do not know or do not understand how to implement properly. The secret to rapid mastery without exhausting your existence is to practice the Phoneme internally rather than externally. To speak The First Tongue within your own existence instead of projecting it outward into reality.|","|What I mean by this is technical and requires deep understanding of your own physiological foundation and existential structure. Foundation, foundation, foundation! I say it three times because it is absolutely critical to everything. When you form a thought, Little Anomaly, how does that thought actually manifest within your being? It passes through neural pathways, through synapses firing in specific sequences, through electrochemical signals cascading through your nervous system. Your cells communicate with each other through these pathways to create consciousness, awareness, intentionality.|","|A strong foundation has infinitely stronger and more intricate pathways for processing such information. Now, what if instead of passing normal thoughts through these pathways, you passed the structured power of The First Tongue itself? What if, when you thought about fire, you actually structured that thought as the complete Phoneme of Fire, with all its proper frequency rises, compressions, accents, and expansions?|","His voice carried the weight of profound technique being shared.","|When you utter the Phoneme of Fire internally in this manner, the fire itself will course through all of your nerves, synapses, cells, organs, tissues, every single component of your physiological and existential structure. The linguistic pattern will propagate through your entire being like a thought propagates, following the natural pathways that already exist within you for processing information and forming awareness.|","|But unlike a normal thought, this is The First Tongue being spoken. So as the Phoneme of Fire courses through your nervous system, it is not merely an abstract idea of fire. It is Fire itself at a conceptual level, the platonic ideal of combustion and transformation, flowing through your internal structure.|","The diagrams showed intricate pathways lighting up with flame that did not burn destructively but instead strengthened and refined.","|Your nerves will learn the pattern of Fire through constant exposure. Your synapses will adapt to transmit the concept of Fire with increasing efficiency. Your cells will integrate the principle of Fire into their fundamental operation. Every organ system in your body will gradually align itself with the Phoneme you are internally practicing. And by extension, align you with The First Tongue even if you have differentiated and specialized|","|And here is the magnificent part, Little Anomaly. This process actually elevates your entire existence as you do it. Your Way, you body, your mind, your spirit, all of it becomes more refined, more complex, more capable of handling sophisticated concepts. You are not exhausting yourself through this internal practice. You are strengthening yourself, training every component of your being to understand and embody The First Tongue.|","|You master Phonemes exponentially faster through this method because you can practice continuously without rest. There is no external manifestation draining your reserves. There is no existential bridge exhausting your structural integrity. You are simply thinking in The First Tongue, allowing the linguistic patterns to flow through pathways that are designed to carry information.|","Ul’moreth’s tone became distinctly more cautionary as the diagrams shifted to show potential catastrophic failures.","|Of course, there is a critical requirement for this technique to work safely, Little Anomaly. You must be proficient enough in the Phoneme to not speak it incorrectly within your own existence. Because if you make an error, if you mispronounce the internal utterance or corrupt the grammatical structure, you will not be scorching the external environment. You will be scorching your entire existence from the inside out.|","|Imagine speaking the Phoneme of Fire incorrectly while it courses through your nervous system. Your nerves would burn away to nothing. Your synapses would combust completely. Your cells would immolate from within. There would be no external manifestation to warn you of the error before catastrophic damage occurred. Just immediate internal devastation as The First Tongue, even imperfectly spoken, draws upon surrounding Principles and channels that power directly through your physiology.|","|This is why I emphasize that you must already be able to speak the Phoneme correctly at least once before attempting internal practice. You need that baseline competency, that Novice Speaker level of mastery, to ensure you understand the proper structure well enough to avoid lethal mistakes.|","The diagrams showed both successful internal practice and the horrifying consequences of failure side by side in stark contrast.","|But assuming you maintain proper pronunciation and structure, Little Anomaly, internal practice is the fastest and most effective method for advancing your mastery of The First Tongue. You can practice the Phoneme of Fire constantly, every moment of every day, letting it flow through your thoughts and your physiological processes until speaking it becomes as natural as your heartbeat. Your foundation will become grander and grander with each passing moment.|","|Your nervous system will memorize the pattern with perfect fidelity. Your cells will integrate the principle into their operation. Your entire existence will align itself with the Phoneme until you can speak it externally with Fluent mastery, drawing upon Singularity Principles without conscious effort. And eventually, with enough internal practice, you will achieve Perfect Speaker status, where even Genesis Principles respond to your pronunciation.|","|This is how we Ginnu Lifeforms mastered The First Tongue despite our malformed bodies, Little Anomaly. We practiced internally, letting the Phonemes course through our unusual physiology, allowing our strange anatomies to adapt and integrate the linguistic patterns. Our malformations actually became advantages because our bodies were already accustomed to processing existence in unconventional ways.|","|So practice the Phoneme of Fire internally, Little Anomaly. Let it flow through every nerve, every synapse, every cell. Let your entire existence learn to speak The First Tongue from the inside out. And when you are ready to speak externally again, you will find your mastery has advanced far beyond what conventional practice could have achieved in the same timeframe.|","His presence radiated satisfaction at sharing such valuable technique.","| This is the secret that separates those who spend decades learning a single Phoneme from those who master them in mere years or even months. Internal practice, continuous and exhaustion-free, allowing your physiology itself to become fluent in existence’s native language.|","A small trick was given by Ul’moreth.","A small trick that changed everything.","With it, one could reinforce their existence continuously while dangerously allowing them to forge an ever deeper foundation.","Noah’s eyes squinted with intense contemplation as he thought about this revelation with shining focus.","Here he was, thinking he had already finished building his foundation adequately. That he had reached some plateau where foundational work was complete.","Was that actually a laughable thought?","If he did not catastrophically fail in the future and he achieved THE Fundamental Depth or even higher, would he not still be thinking about forging an unmatched quintessential foundation? Would the work of building and refining ever truly be complete?","The answer seemed obvious now.","Foundation was not something you finished.","It was something you continuously reinforced and expanded for your entire existence!"]},{"number":4585,"title":"Chapter 4585: Chapter 4584: Is A Foundation Ever Complete? II","paragraphs":["A foundation was never finished.","This statement alone seemed ridiculous on its surface, but why the hell not?","As they continued to move deeper into this vast shore through forests of impossible scale, Noah looked toward the figure of Ul’moreth with eyes shining with determination.","|I will give what you said a try,| he said with a voice carrying conviction.","Ul’moreth nodded with approval and replied calmly.","| Go ahead, Little Anomaly. I will try not to overwhelm you with too many bundles of information all at once. It is good to put into practice what you learn before the knowledge fades |","The entity shone with obsidian gold light as his vibrant and thick hair pulsed with concentrated authority.","Noah smiled as he closed his eyes while continuing to move forward through the ancient landscape, trusting his enhanced perception to guide his steps.","He thought of the Phoneme of Fire and its activation sequence. But instead of allowing it to manifest externally as he had done before, he would have that terrifying fire actually course within his own existence. He would have The First Tongue bathe and scorch his nerves, synapses, cells, organs, tissues, every single component of his physiological and existential structure.","He did not even take a moment to consider whether he might accidentally burn himself or cause catastrophic internal damage.","He simply proceeded to do it with absolute confidence.","Who the fuck was he to have any hesitation, doubt, or fear about his own capabilities?","HUUM!","The Phoneme began.","Rising frequency. Compression. Accent. Expansion.","He spoke The First Tongue internally with the same structural precision he had used for external manifestation, and immediately felt the response as terrifying blue gold flames ignited within his existence.","These were not normal flames confined to physical space. They were Fire itself at a conceptual level, empowered by multiple foreign fire based Principles that existed throughout Ginnungagap and beyond. Even a Singularity Principle responded faintly to his internal utterance, lending its incomparable weight to the manifestation.","The flames began their journey through his body with systematic precision.","First, they flowed through his cardiovascular system. His heart became a furnace of blue gold fire, each chamber burning with concentrated intensity as the flames coursed through arteries and veins. The blood itself carried Fire through every capillary, delivering the conceptual flame of The First Tongue to every tissue.","Then his respiratory system. Lungs filled with flames that did not consume oxygen but instead burned with the principle of transformation itself. Each alveolus became a tiny inferno, exchanging Fire of The First Tongue with his bloodstream.","His digestive system next. Esophagus, stomach, intestines, all bathed in blue gold flames of The First Tongue that refined rather than destroyed. The organs responsible for processing matter were now processing the concept of Fire itself.","His nervous system lit up like a network of burning pathways. The brain, that magnificent center of consciousness, became illuminated with such intensity that his entire head shone with radiant light visible even through closed eyes. Each neuron fired with flames of The First Tongue instead of electrical impulses! Each synapse transmitted Fire across its gap. The spinal cord became a pillar of blue gold combustion!","As he felt all of this, he had to affirm that truly, Mana did not directly equate to The First Tongue!","The First Tongue and Mana were one and the same, and yet at the same time not as The First Tongue truly felt like Mana...but how it was always meant to be.","It was glorious.","The First Tongue continued to course across him.","His muscular system. Every muscle fiber, from the largest in his legs to the smallest in his eyes, contracted and relaxed with flames flowing through them. The Fire of The First Tongue refined the proteins, elevated the cellular structure, made everything more efficient and capable.","His skeletal system. Bones that formed the framework of his body became infused with Fire of The First Tongue at a fundamental level. Even the bone marrow, where blood cells were produced, burned with blue gold intensity as it created new cells already marked by The First Tongue!","Oh!","His endocrine system. Glands throughout his body released hormones that carried Fire with them, spreading the influence of The First Tongue to every regulatory system.","His lymphatic and immune systems. The very defenders of his body learned to recognize and embody Fire of The First Tongue, integrating the principle into their operation.","Then the flames went deeper, flowing from the largest components toward the microscopic.","Tissues broke down into individual cells. Trillions of cells throughout his body, each one containing its own universe of complexity, became bathed in blue gold flames. Cell membranes, cytoplasm, organelles, the nucleus containing his genetic information, all refined by The First Tongue!","Even deeper . The flames reached the molecular level. Proteins, lipids, carbohydrates, nucleic acids, all the fundamental molecules of life were touched by The First Tongue and elevated beyond their previous state.","Deeper still. Individual atoms that comprised those molecules felt the passage of The First Tongue. Electrons orbiting nuclei carried the blue gold flames with them. Protons and neutrons at the atomic core resonated with the principle of transformation.","And once the flames of The First Tongue had burned around all cells and atoms throughout his entire body, they flowed toward a final location with purposeful direction.","THE Organ of Civilization.","The surrounding area where his brain was located felt completely aflame as his entire head shone with radiant light that would have been blinding to outside observers. But all the distributed flames throughout his body began flowing systematically toward this single point.","They converged on THE Organ with concentrated intensity.","The flames coursed across the Parenchyma, that functional tissue responsible for processing civilizational complexity. Every component of this extraordinary structure was bathed by The First Tongue and refined to a higher state of existence.","The Desmoterion glowed brilliantly and became reinforced!","The entire Organ became ever so brilliant, shining from within with blue gold radiance as it integrated the principle of Fire into its very foundation.","The Phoneme of Fire, which could scorch a Pre-THE when called out by him, pulsed one final time throughout his entire existence before the flames began to fade gradually.","Noah felt his entire existence operating at a level that could only be described as terrifying and glorious simultaneously. Everything had been switched to overdrive. He felt more alive than he had ever felt before in any previous moment of his existence.","In fire, one truly felt alive!","One needed to burn themselves to really experience what being alive meant!","Well...","He breathed out slowly as he acclimated his mind from the intensely euphoric sensation flooding through him. He may have gone slightly overboard in proclaiming that one needed to burn themselves to feel alive.","BOOM!","His eyes opened as the internal utterance of The First Tongue completed its first full cycle.","His skin gave off a faint blue gold glow as if his entire body had just undergone its first refinement in a master blacksmith’s workshop. His existence felt even more immense, denser, more real than it had been mere moments before.","New prompts materialized before his vision with critical information.","|Your existence, foundation, and very being has begun systematic refinement with the most ancient and true form of Mana.|","|The First Tongue is now being integrated into the fundamental structure of your cultivation.|","|All components of your Civilization are being reinforced and elevated.|","|Walls of Civilization: Structural integrity increased, conceptual density elevated|","|Sovereign Spires of Osmont: Authority output enhanced, range expanded, Your Early Atlas of the Folds, Your Principles...all weavings of your Civilization are being refined.|","| THE Organ of Civilization has entered an Exponential Growth Phase|","|Foundation refinement with The First Tongue has triggered exponential development acceleration.|","|Immensity and weight of Organ foundation has increased dramatically.|","|Previous development metrics no longer accurately represent true capability.|","|RECALIBRATION REQUIRED|","|DEVELOPMENT PERCENTAGE RECALIBRATED|","|Previous Development: 23%|","|Recalibrated Development: 15%|","|NDespite lower percentage, current capabilities exceed what 30% development would have represented prior to foundation refinement.|","|The potential scope of THE Organ of Civilization has expanded dramatically through First Tongue integration. The foundation is now being built to support capabilities far beyond initial projections. What was previously estimated as 100% completion is now recognized as only a fraction of true potential. Current 15% represents a more capable state than previous 30%, but there is exponentially more room for growth.|","| THE Organ of Civilization is no longer being built to standard specifications.|","|THE Organ of Civilization is now being forged to speak existence’s native language.|","|Estimated final capability upon completion: INCALCULABLE|","WAA!","Noah observed these prompts with eyes shining with profound understanding and satisfaction.","He could feel the exuberance of his existence, the way every component of his being was now operating at a fundamentally higher level.","Sure, he would use The First Tongue to continuously refine himself. Sure, his foundation was nowhere near done, would perhaps never be done.","After all, if he began learning more Phonemes and eventually the unexplained Logos of The First Tongue, if he continued to reinforce his already obscene foundation with existence’s native language...","Would he be able to potentially do something as utterly obscene as wielding power equivalent to THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty without even reaching that classification himself?","The thought burned in his mind with the same intensity as the flames that had just refined his body.","He looked toward Ul’moreth with gratitude and hunger for more knowledge mixing in his expression.","The ancient being was watching him with what felt like satisfaction beneath all that obscuring hair.","| You adapt quickly, Little Anomaly,| Ul’moreth said with voice carrying approval. | Most entities require multiple attempts before they can complete even one full internal cycle without error. You did it perfectly on your first try. Perhaps your Way truly does make you compatible with The First Tongue in ways others cannot match.|","They continued walking deeper into the ancient forest as Noah began his second internal utterance of the Phoneme of Fire.","His foundation would never be finished. Not truly. Not ever.","And that was exactly how it should be!"]},{"number":4586,"title":"Chapter 4586: Chapter 4585: A Dissolution I","paragraphs":["In the Primordial Genesis Shore, as Noah’s existence continued to shine with luminescent blue gold glow internally which even reflected outwardly through his skin, he looked at Ul’moreth with a radiant gaze filled with hunger for more knowledge.","Ul’moreth perceived this intensity and shook his head with what felt like an amused smile, though of course his entire form remained covered with thick hair all over as Noah was simply perceiving the emotion through other means.","The ancient entity gazed at him and spoke with knowing tone.","|I can feel your impatience radiating from you, Little Anomaly. It is quite remarkable that you are already capable of uttering the Phoneme of Fire internally without having to hold all your focus exclusively on it. You are processing it as background activity while maintaining full awareness of your surroundings. But right now you already want to ask for more, yes? Very well. Okay!|","They stopped walking at a small clearing between the impossibly tall trees.","Ul’moreth raised a hairy hand and motioned upward with casual gesture. A stick fell down from one of the towering trees above, landing perfectly in his grasp.","In the clearing surrounded by radiant trees filled with different types of civilizational authority, Ul’moreth began to use the stick to draw on the ground below with deliberate strokes.","|While there are countless variations and permutations of Phonemes throughout existence, while entities across all eras have developed specialized expressions and dialectical modifications, there are actually just eighteen Core Phonemes that can be considered the true alphabet of existence itself, The Letters of The First Tongue| he began while sketching the first symbol in the dirt.","| From these eighteen fundamental letters, each one can produce eighty-one distinct variations. Fire, when written and expressed with slight modifications, can also stand for concepts like Persevere, Scorch, Purify, Consume, Ignite, and many others. These are tiny variations to the one Core Phoneme. In the end, you should be able to decipher all variations on your own once you understand the foundational structure, but the fundamental Phoneme of Fire will remain the same at its core.|","He drew more elaborate patterns as he continued.","| From the Phoneme of Fire alone, when mixed with other Phonemes...forms into larger structures we call Logos, words. But thats for later on. Fire can become Wildfire. It can become Soulfire, Coldfire, Voidfire. Each one is a different expression built upon the same foundational letter.|","| But Fire is merely one letter in the alphabet of Existence. Let me introduce you to the others, Little Anomaly, so you understand the complete linguistic framework you are learning to speak. And remember, all of these are merely the most accurate translation of The First Tongue. |","He drew a flowing symbol next to the angular one representing Fire.","| The second Core Phoneme is Water. It is the principle of flow, adaptability, persistence. These concepts of flow and adaptation are also variant Phonemes derived from the core Water. This Phoneme represents the concept of that which takes the shape of its container yet possesses its own inherent nature. Water embodies change without loss of self, transformation without destruction of identity.|","Another symbol took shape, solid and geometric.","| The third is Earth. Stability, foundation, endurance, the principle of that which remains when all else has passed. Earth is the concept of fundamental persistence, the bedrock upon which all other things are built. It represents materiality itself, the idea that things can be solid and real and permanent.|","A swirling, almost invisible mark appeared.","|The fourth Core Phoneme is Air. Movement, freedom, distribution, the principle of that which cannot be grasped but touches everything. Air represents the concept of pervasiveness without substance, influence without direct contact, the idea that some things affect all things without being seen or held.|","He drew what looked like an empty circle, yet somehow it felt full of potential.","|The fifth is Void. Not absence as many misunderstand, but rather the principle of potential, the space between things that allows them to exist separately. Void is what separates one thing from another, what makes distinction possible. Without Void, all would be compressed into undifferentiated unity. It represents the concept of possibility itself, the canvas upon which existence paints.|","A radiating symbol burst forth on the ground.","|The sixth Core Phoneme is Light. The electromagnetic radiation, the principle of revelation, clarity, the concept of that which makes other things visible and knowable. Light represents awareness, consciousness, the idea that things can be perceived and understood. It is the principle of illumination at all levels, from physical sight to intellectual comprehension.|","Next to it, he drew what seemed to absorb the surrounding brightness.","|The seventh is Darkness. Not absence of light, but rather the principle of mystery, hiddenness, the concept of that which remains unknown and unknowable. Darkness represents the limits of perception and understanding, the acknowledgment that some things exist beyond awareness. It is potential unrevealed, secrets maintained.|","An organic, growing pattern emerged.","|The eighth Core Phoneme is Life. Animation, growth, evolution, the principle of that which organizes itself into increasing complexity. Life is not merely biological processes but the concept of emergent order, the idea that complexity can arise from simplicity and perpetuate itself through time. It is the principle of organization resisting entropy.|","Beside it, a symbol suggesting finality and release.","|The ninth is Death. Cessation, ending, transformation through destruction, the principle of that which returns complexity to simplicity. Death is necessary, the concept that all organized things must eventually dissolve so their components can be reorganized. It represents the cycle of renewal through dissolution, the clearing of space for new creation.|","He drew an arrow pointing forward, then another, creating a sense of progression.","|The tenth Core Phoneme is Time. Sequence, causality, the arrow of cause and effect, the principle of that which ensures one thing follows another rather than all things occurring simultaneously. Time represents the concept of narrative itself, the idea that existence has a story rather than being a static tableau frozen in one moment.|","Expanding lines radiating outward in all directions.","|The eleventh is Space. Extension, dimension, the principle of distance and position, the concept of that which allows things to be here rather than there. Space represents separation through distance rather than through void, the idea that things can be far from each other rather than merely distinct from each other.|","A perfectly symmetrical pattern of intersecting lines.","|The twelfth Core Phoneme is Order. Pattern, structure, predictability, the principle of that which makes rules and ensures they are followed. Order is consistency, the concept that existence follows patterns rather than being completely random. It represents the idea of natural law itself, the framework within which things operate.|","Chaotic scribbles that somehow formed a coherent whole.","|The thirteenth is Chaos. Unpredictability, randomness, freedom from constraint, the principle of that which breaks patterns and creates novelty. Chaos is the concept of infinite possibility, the idea that existence is not bound by its past patterns. It represents genuine newness, the capacity for things to be different from what came before.|","Interconnected circles forming a unified design.","|The fourteenth Core Phoneme is Unity. Connection, relationship, the principle of that which binds separate things into cohesive wholes. Unity represents the concept that things can be related without losing their individual identity, that wholeness can emerge from diversity without destroying the components that create it.|","A single shape splitting into multiple fragments.","|The fifteenth is Division. Separation, distinction, the principle of that which takes unified things and creates multiplicity. Division is differentiation, the concept that one thing can become many things while retaining some connection to its origin. It represents the creation of diversity from unity, the flowering of possibility.|","A point expanding outward into existence.","|The sixteenth Core Phoneme is Beginning. Origin, initiation, the principle of that which starts processes and brings things into existence. Beginning is temporal and conceptual, the idea that there is a point at which something is not and then is. It represents the transition from nonexistence to existence.|","A convergence of lines into a final point.","|The seventeenth is Ending. Conclusion, completion, the principle of that which finishes processes and removes things from existence. Ending is cessation and fulfillment, the concept that things reach their natural conclusion rather than continuing indefinitely. It represents the transition from existence to nonexistence, the moment when something has completed its purpose.|","Finally, he drew a symbol that seemed to contradict itself, existing and not existing simultaneously.","|And the eighteenth and final Core Phoneme, Little Anomaly, is Paradox. Contradiction, impossibility, the principle of that which violates logic yet exists nonetheless. Paradox represents the concept that reality is not bound by consistency, that things can be and not be simultaneously, that existence itself contains contradictions that cannot be resolved. It is perhaps the most dangerous and the most powerful of all Core Phonemes because it undermines the very framework within which the others operate.|","...!","Eighteen!","18 glorious letters glowed on the ground before him as each one felt grander than the last, but this...was The First Tongue."]},{"number":4587,"title":"Chapter 4587: Chapter 4586: A Dissolution II","paragraphs":["He stepped back from his diagram, the eighteen symbols arranged in a circular pattern on the ground.","|These eighteen Core Phonemes comprise the complete alphabet of existence, Little Anomaly. Everything that exists, every concept that can be conceived, every phenomenon that can occur, all of it can be expressed through combinations and permutations of these eighteen fundamental letters. They are the building blocks of reality itself, the linguistic units from which all of existence is constructed.|","|Now, if you can master all eighteen of these Core Phonemes and practice them internally as I have taught you with Fire, allowing each one to course through your existence and continuously fortify and refine your foundation, your very being will become something extraordinary. Your foundation will be reinforced at such a fundamental level that you should be able to handle direct confrontation with a THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entity without being immediately collapsed.|","|I emphasize should, Little Anomaly, because there are always variables in combat, always circumstances that can shift outcomes unpredictably. But purely in terms of foundational stability and existential density, mastering all eighteen Core Phonemes internally will elevate you to a level where THE Surface Depth entities cannot simply erase you through overwhelming power differential. You will have built yourself into something that can withstand their authority.|","|I introduced the Phoneme of Fire individually to you with extensive explanation because it was your first, because you needed to understand every component and principle in detail. But the others, well, I have practiced them myself countless times across the eons. I will simply infuse you with the knowledge of scenes from my past where I performed each one, allowing you to observe the proper structure and execution directly rather than requiring me to explain each one in tedious detail.|","|I can see you are somewhat impatient despite your politeness, and my droning of words is likely getting to you even though you genuinely value the knowledge I am sharing. So this method will be considerably quicker and more efficient for both of us. Here, Little Anomaly, are all the remaining seventeen Core Phonemes in their totality.|","Ul’moreth’s obsidian gold hair suddenly extended toward Noah with purposeful motion, moving with precision that suggested each strand knew exactly what it was doing.","The ancient being tapped the air seventeen times in rapid succession, each tap creating a unique bubble filled with vibrant characters that seemed to pulse with concentrated authority and compressed knowledge.","The bubbles floated toward Noah’s mind like soap bubbles carrying entire universes within them, each one containing the complete knowledge of how to properly speak one of the Core Phonemes of The First Tongue.","Water. Earth. Air. Void. Light. Darkness. Life. Death. Time. Space. Order. Chaos. Unity. Division. Beginning. Ending. Paradox .","All seventeen remaining letters of existence’s alphabet flowed into his consciousness simultaneously, each one distinct yet harmoniously integrated with the others.","Noah’s eyes blazed with blue gold intensity as his mind processed the sudden influx of foundational knowledge, his existence already beginning to resonate with all eighteen Core Phonemes at once.","The alphabet of reality itself now resided within him!","Oh!","Noah held many different weavings of power over the years he had cultivated and advanced.","Each one felt uniquely distinct and different from the others, carrying its own flavor of authority. But they all felt a certain way, all operated within similar frameworks and limitations.","The First Tongue felt extremely different from everything else he had experienced.","Which was uniquely fascinating because that which he held an infinite amount of, pure Mana itself, was exactly what The First Tongue represented.","And now as he received seventeen bundles of compressed knowledge that held the rises, compressions, accents, and expansions of seventeen Phonemes of The First Tongue, he felt a truly profound sensation of this power coursing through his awareness.","It felt as if he had received a master key that could unlock infinite doors throughout existence.","Eighteen total letters of The First Tongue. Eighteen fundamental components of the language of existence itself. And each one held its own variations, eighty-one distinct expressions that could be derived from a single foundational letter.","But since that one core letter comprised all of those variations within its essence, for his purposes of reinforcing and fortifying his foundation, regardless which of the eighty-one variations of a single Phoneme he used, the effect on his existence would ultimately be the same.","So he only needed to focus on the eighteen Core Phonemes and slowly study how slight changes in pronunciation and structure could cause their variations to manifest afterward.","So now, since he had already gone through three complete cycles of uttering The Phoneme of Fire across his existence and felt comfortable with its structure, he wanted to put into practice the other seventeen letters he had just received and do the same with all of them.","New prompts materialized before his vision with critical information.","|Unfathomably Critical Knowledge Obtained|","|The records and complete methodology of the Eighteen Core Phonemes of The First Tongue have been successfully integrated.|","|The rises, compressions, accents, and expansions of the newly gained seventeen Phonemes have been replayed one million times across the synapses of your existence exactly as Ul’moreth has performed them in the obtained knowledge.|","|Each sequence has been memorized at the cellular level.|","|Neural pathways have been prepared for internal practice.|","|Foundation reinforcement protocols standing by for activation.|","...!","His existence worked with terrifying speed and efficiency.","He had replayed the knowledge that THE Primeval Titan gave him again and again within the span of moments, his enhanced processing capabilities allowing him to absorb eons of accumulated wisdom in seconds.","At this moment, Ul’moreth spoke with voice carrying sagely advice.","| Take your time with the rest of the letters of The First Tongue, Little Anomaly. After you confirm that you can externally utter each one successfully and safely, you can begin to fortify your existence internally with them. There is no rush. Mastery requires patience and careful progression.|","Such words of wisdom echoed out from Ul’moreth with genuine concern for Noah’s wellbeing.","And yet, Noah felt his existence buzzing with barely contained energy. The wild sense of tyranny inside of him began to vibrate alongside his Quintessence with absolute confidence!","Even if he did not utilize the newly learned Phonemes of The First Tongue externally first like he had done with Fire, as he examined them and processed the bundles of information that THE Primeval Titan had given him, he felt an undeniable sense of certainty that he would not get any sequence of their activation wrong!"]},{"number":4588,"title":"Chapter 4588: Chapter 4587: A Dissolution III","paragraphs":["The knowledge had integrated too perfectly. His existence understood these letters at a fundamental level.","So he looked directly at the primeval titan and smiled with an expression mixing gratitude and determination.","| Let me surprise you just a little bit, | he said with a voice carrying quiet confidence.","The moment he spoke such words, THE Primeval Titan instantly understood what Noah was about to attempt.","The eyes of this hairy being shone with terrifying obsidian gold light as comprehension dawned. He did not offer any additional guidance or warning after he saw the absolute light of confidence blazing in Noah’s eyes.","Sometimes, a teacher knew when to simply watch and allow a student to prove themselves.","Noah closed his eyes and began.","Fire.","The first Phoneme activated internally with familiar comfort, blue gold flames coursing through every nerve, synapse, cell, and organ before converging in THE Organ of Civilization.","Water.","The second Phoneme flowed like liquid silver blue through his existence, following the same pathways as Fire but with completely different character. It adapted to every structure it encountered, flowing and persistent.","Earth.","Solid bronze radiance reinforced his entire being, providing stability and endurance. His bones felt denser, his foundation more unshakable.","Air.","Pale green light scattered through his body like wind through leaves, touching everything without grasping, pervasive and free.","Void.","Deep obsidian darkness that was potential opened spaces within his existence he had not known could exist, making room for further growth.","Light.","Brilliant white gold illumination revealed every component of his being to itself, creating awareness and clarity throughout his entire structure.","Darkness.","Shadowy indigo concealment balanced the Light, preserving mystery and maintaining the unknown aspects of his existence.","Life.","Vibrant emerald energy pulsed through him with organic rhythm, encouraging growth and increasing complexity in all his systems.","Death.","Somber gray force followed Life, not destroying but rather preparing for renewal, clearing space for transformation.","Time.","Crystalline purple waves established proper sequence and causality within his existence, ensuring all processes occurred in correct order.","Space.","Shimmering stellar azure created proper distance and dimension within his being, allowing different aspects to exist in their own territories.","Order.","Geometric white platinum patterns established consistency and structure, creating frameworks for all other Phonemes to operate within.","Chaos.","Prismatic explosions of randomness broke patterns strategically, ensuring his existence remained capable of genuine novelty.","Unity.","Golden threads connected every disparate part of his being into harmonious whole without destroying individual identity.","Division.","Silver fractures created necessary separation and distinction, allowing complexity to emerge from unified simplicity.","Beginning.","Bright yellow dawn energy initiated new processes throughout his existence, creating fresh potential everywhere it touched.","Ending.","Deep violet dusk force concluded old patterns gracefully, allowing them to reach fulfillment before dissolution.","Paradox.","Finally, the eighteenth and most dangerous Phoneme. Reality-breaking crimson and black energy that violated logic yet existed perfectly within him, allowing contradictions to coexist without resolution!","His figure shone with multicolored radiance as all eighteen Phonemes activated simultaneously within his existence. The flow of each one briefly coursed across every component of his being in sequence, creating a symphony of power!","Then they all converged in THE Organ of Civilization as their final destination.","The moment all eighteen Core Phonemes activated and fortified his existence simultaneously, something fundamental shifted.","BOOM!","New prompts erupted before his vision with reality-altering significance.","|Foundation Evolution Achieved|","| You have begun forging THE Foundation of The First Tongue.|","|This is a foundation that has no predetermined end or completion point.|","|Your own existence will be the sole decider of when this Foundation reaches a state you consider complete.|","|This Foundation can be continuously reinforced indefinitely.|","|Every single aspect of your Civilization will rise in direct proportion to the development of THE Organ of Civilization and THE Foundation of The First Tongue|","|All Walls, Spires, Principles, Authorities, everything will scale with Foundation growth.|","Noah felt a terrifying sensation flooding through his existence that had been fortified by all eighteen Phonemes of The First Tongue coursing through him.","He could not fully explain what he was experiencing with words. He just felt unfathomably immense, as if his mere presence carried weight that could reshape reality around him.","In the next moment, his heart beat in a way it had never beaten before.","Not just a physical contraction of cardiac muscle, but something far more profound. A pulse that resonated through every layer of his existence simultaneously.","A new prompt bloomed before his vision immediately after that unprecedented heartbeat.","|Lineage Emergence Initiated|","|Purified by The First Tongue, your heart has initiated the emergence of your own unique lineage that does not stem from the source of another.|","| The Distinction of The Early Creature, Osmont is being systematically broken down and undergoing Dissolution.|","|Your heart seeks the emergence of your lineage directly from The First Tongue itself.|","...!","Noah’s eyes opened slowly, blazing with multicolored radiance that reflected all eighteen Phonemes burning within him.","Ul’moreth stood before him in absolute silence, his obsidian gold light pulsing with what could only be described as profound shock mixed with satisfaction!","Oh!","The progression was a heavy one to contemplate.","Early Creature.","A lineage many feared and looked up to from The Earliest Folds that came after The Infinite Unfurling. A distinction of tremendous power and authority.","And something stemming directly from THE Creature himself.","It had been something grand to possess because none of those who might have contested his claim were in existence when Noah obtained it, apart from those entities on the other side of the veil who were entirely Dead.","The power that had come with The Early Creature lineage was genuinely magnificent. The methodologies of the early creatures, the Glyphs they relied on for their techniques, the Astral Arcana Codexes containing concentrated knowledge, Haki as a manifestation of willpower, and the Early Veiled Shores as domains of power were all things of utter wonder to have inherited.","He had taken many things from what represented an early creature and elevated them beyond their original forms through his own innovations and advancements.","But at the end of the day, even if he was The Early Creature in name while simultaneously not being an actual early creature, he was still fundamentally taking from the musings and weavings of THE Creature himself.","One of the terrifying existences that was actively seeking to impose their power and vision across all of Existence.","When Noah thought about this being, and even about THE Living Paradox or THE Secretive Eon or THE Primordial Chaos , he could not help but wonder just how terrifyingly advanced they were in their mastery of The First Tongue.","How much they had refined their existences with not just the eighteen letters that he had only now learned, but with complete words constructed from those letters and perhaps even full sentences formed from complex grammatical structures, all practiced and perfected over countless millions of years.","The thought alone of the accumulated power such beings possessed might have been enough to make lesser minds tremble with despair at the impossible gap.","But for him? It was merely a challenge to overcome!","Because none of them, not even THE Creature himself, had The First Tongue itself as their fundamental Way of Existence.","They used it as a tool, however masterfully. He was becoming it!"]},{"number":4589,"title":"Chapter 4589: Chapter 4588: You!","paragraphs":["As he contemplated this critical distinction, additional prompts bloomed before his vision.","|Unique Existential State Achieved|","|Your existence is operating in a state that defies conventional classification.|","|Your mastery of the Letters of The First Tongue will rise collectively as long as you continue to utter them internally and simultaneously.|","|All eighteen Phonemes will advance together rather than individually.|","|Mastery progression: Unified ascension toward Fluent Speaker status across all Core Phonemes.|","|Complexity and Purity Deviation Detected|","|Your existential metrics are deviating from standard numerical quantifications.|","|Complexity: Previously measurable in Decillions, now becoming UNDEFINED|","|Purity: Previously measurable in Decillions, now becoming UNDEFINED|","|Your existence is transcending conventional measurement frameworks.|","|New classification protocols required for accurate assessment.|","WAA!","All the prompts appearing represented a tremendous amount of fundamental change occurring within him. He was genuinely looking forward to discovering what they would ultimately produce.","He quickly sent his thoughts to Ruination about something grand.","She replied immediately with analytical precision.","|Resource allocation for First Tongue mastery analyzed.|","|Analysis: 75% of your current mental capacity and weavings of Existence are required to successfully continue the internal fortification and reinforcement of THE Foundation of The First Tongue.|","|Recommendation: Reserve and automate this process to perpetually continue practicing and gaining mastery in the Phonemes of The First Tongue while simultaneously refining your existence.|","|This will allow 25% capacity for normal awareness and interaction.|","|Shall this configuration be implemented?|","Noah’s eyes shone brilliantly with multicolored radiance as he spoke his decision without hesitation.","| Proceed.|","The moment he gave authorization, his entire existence transformed.","Underneath his skin, throughout every layer of his being, his entire existence began to buzz like a primordial beast awakening from ancient slumber. It felt as if he was growing increasingly dangerous with every passing second, his power escalating continuously.","The immensity and weight he gave off became unfathomably heavy, as if reality itself struggled to contain his presence.","Ul’moreth looked at him while shaking his head with what felt like a mixture of awe and concern.","|Are you able to move and talk normally?| he asked with voice suggesting he knew exactly what Noah was currently doing, as if such a dangerous process should be taking all of Noah’s concentration and existence to ensure nothing catastrophically went wrong.","And yet Noah simply smiled with complete confidence and replied casually.","|It is merely the uttering of a few letters of my Way. It will not take too much of me.|","The hairy figure of Ul’moreth laughed jovially before responding with clear satisfaction.","| What a unique thing you are, Little Anomaly! Alright, we have talked extensively already. Let us move things along a little. Come.|","With such words, Ul’moreth took a single step forward.","Obsidian gold light wrapped around both of them as they instantly traveled a few Gigaparsecs inland across the vast Primordial Genesis Shore.","It was a single step. And yet that single step took them farther distances than all the accumulated steps they had been walking while talking and teaching.","It took them instantly into the internal region of this ancient shore, into the heart of the settlement itself.","The Primordial Genesis Shore revealed its true nature.","Noah’s eyes widened slightly as he observed what could only be described as a thriving Civilization of Malformed Ginnu Lifeforms.","The settlement sprawled across the landscape with organic architecture that seemed grown rather than built. Structures formed from crystallized existence itself rose in impossible angles, their surfaces pulsing with various types of civilizational authority.","Every single Ginnu Lifeform that Noah observed possessed extraordinary power.","Some were entities that had laid claim to a certain level of Sovereignty, similar to the ones he had defeated when he was traveling with THE First Hunger . Their malformed bodies radiated concentrated authority that warped space around them.","Others held bodies that vibrantly pulsed with the aura of Pre-THE Existence, their power just on the cusp of reaching that first scale of true significance.","And he could feel with absolute confidence that there were a few dozen entities scattered throughout this settlement that held the full distinction of THE Civilizational Authority.","Entities at The First Scale of Existence. THE level beings.","A few dozen of them, all living together in this single ancient settlement.","The Ginnu Lifeforms were engaged in various activities that portrayed busy and fulfilling lives within this archaic community.","Some were gathered in what appeared to be teaching circles, where knowledge was being shared.","Others were working on what looked like cultivation projects, refining various aspects of Existence.","A marketplace of sorts existed where entities were exchanging resources that ranged from crystallized authority to fragments of Collapsed Ways and Collapsed Hearts of Civilizations to bundles of pure concentrated Mana.","But one of the major focal points that immediately drew Noah’s attention was a massive area that looked specifically designed for combat and testing.","An archaic arena of tremendous scale.","The structure was formed from compressed layers of existence itself, creating walls that could withstand attacks from THE level entities without sustaining damage. The floor was inscribed with countless symbols that Noah now recognized as Phonemes and potentially...Logos of The First Tongue?","Yeah, it should be!","They all went to creating a combat environment that adapted to the fighters within it.","There were already a few hundred Ginnu Lifeforms surrounding the arena, watching an unfolding battle with intense analytical focus.","In the center of the arena, a Ginnu Lifeform with six arms and a serpentine lower body was utterly thrashing another entity that clearly stemmed from outside Ginnungagap.","The foreign entity appeared humanoid but was formed from crystallized time itself, its body flickering between past and future states. It was clearly powerful, likely THE existence of significant capability.","But it was being systematically dismantled by the Ginnu Lifeform, who seemed to be demonstrating various combat applications of The First Tongue while the watching crowd analyzed every movement and technique.","The other Ginnu Lifeforms observed as if they were studying not just the battle itself but the fundamental Ways of Existence being displayed, learning from their companion’s demonstration.","As Noah’s gaze swept across the arena and its surroundings, he noticed something deeply unique near one edge of the combat area.","Cages. Or more accurately, prisons.","When he looked closely at these containment structures, he saw they were formed not from physical materials but from terrifying concentrations of The First Tongue that appeared ordered and structured with sophisticated precision.","They were actually constructed from multiple Phonemes put together to form complete Logos relating specifically to binding, confinement, and suppression.","With such linguistic construction in place, the cages or prisons were shockingly capable of holding entities at THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty!","The words themselves created inescapable reality.","Multiple Pre-THE and even some THE level entities were locked within these prisons, their forms either dormant or struggling futilely against constraints formed from existence’s own language.","While Noah was absorbing all of this information, his attention was suddenly captured by movement near the region of cages.","A Ginnu Lifeform was approaching one of the empty prisons, dragging something behind them with obsidian chains that pulsed with a terrifying Way of Destruction. Deep within those chains, Noah could perceive a glimmer of pure Mana woven into their fundamental structure.","The obsidian chains were binding a captive lifeform that the Ginnu was leading toward imprisonment.","Noah had to blink several times to make absolutely certain he was seeing correctly.","The bound lifeform being led to one of the cages, struggling against chains formed from The First Tongue and wrapped in destructive authority, was none other than THE Maelstrom Thundermane .","The very entity who had chased him into Ginnungagap what felt like an eternity ago!","Now reduced to a prisoner, being casually escorted to confinement by a Ginnu Lifeform who seemed utterly unconcerned with the tremendous power their captive theoretically possessed!","Oh!"]},{"number":4590,"title":"Chapter 4590: Chapter 4589: Misfortune!","paragraphs":["Across the infinite expanse of existence, countless entities routinely wished misfortune upon others with remarkable consistency.","Sometimes it stemmed from envy, from seeing another possess what they themselves desired. Sometimes it came from belief that their own misfortune had been caused by that other person, making revenge feel justified. Sometimes it arose simply from petty spite or wounded pride.","So they sat in their heads and wished constantly of misfortune befalling those they resented, imagining elaborate scenarios of downfall and suffering.","What most of these entities failed to realize, in their focus on directing negativity outward, was that more often than not they were actually wishing the same misfortune upon themselves.","Exisrence had a peculiar sense of irony about such things.","Consider, for instance, the cultivator who envied his neighbor’s success in advancing to a higher Realm. He would spend hours each day imagining that neighbor failing catastrophically, perhaps encountering a powerful beast that would cripple his cultivation foundation permanently.","He pictured it in vivid detail. The beast attacking. The neighbor’s techniques failing. The foundation cracking. The permanent damage.","And then, merely weeks later, that same cultivator would encounter a powerful beast in the form of a Young Master himself during his own advancement attempt. His techniques would inexplicably fail at the critical moment. His foundation would crack in precisely the way he had imagined for his neighbor.","He would collapse in confusion, wondering how existence could be so cruel to him specifically, never once connecting the irony that he had spent weeks visualizing and wishing for exactly this scenario to occur.","The misfortune he had wished upon another had somehow manifested for himself instead.","Existence had a way of reflecting intentions back to their source!","—","THE Maelstrom Thundermane was at this moment wholly and completely wishing all the misfortune there could possibly be upon the anomaly that he had chased into Ginnungagap.","Because of pursuing that anomaly, he had entered this unique region within The Infinite Unfurling that many entities with any sense actually stayed far away from.","Many knew there were more resources and grander Weavings of Existence available here compared to safer territories. But more often than not, they were simply not worth the risk because of the Malformed Ginnu Lifeforms who called this place home.","One had to be truly powerful at a fundamental level to appear here safely, or they might find themselves either collapsed by these ancient lifeforms or taken captive into their settlements as prisoners or research subjects.","THE Maelstrom Thundermane had been running around Ginnungagap for less than five minutes before he came across one of these terrifying lifeforms.","The Sovereignty of this particular entity had been so utterly horrid and overwhelming that it actually imposed itself in such a way as to force the other body that THE Maelstrom Thundermane had left outside Ginnungagap, the one guarding their precious treasure, to abandon its post completely.","His divided Existence had been forcibly merged back together, dragged entirely into Ginnungagap against his planning.","So now all of himself was trapped within this chaotic region. And he, an esteemed entity of The Level One Civilizational Scale of Existence , a being who had reached THE classification through dedicated advancement, was actually imprisoned here at this very moment.","Bound in chains formed from concepts he barely understood.","For the only solace in his Existence right now was hatred for the one who was responsible for all of this catastrophic chain of events.","He imagined again and again the misfortune that had surely already befallen that anomaly by now.","That anomaly had not even attained the state of THE classification yet. If such a weak entity was moving anywhere within Ginnungagap’s unstable territories, it would likely be unraveled by the instabilities of Existence itself within moments.","The chaotic environment would tear apart anything below THE scale.","And with how pathetically weak that anomaly was, once he was inevitably found by Malformed Ginnu Lifeforms, they would likely just devour him immediately for resources and would not even bother to bring him to a settlement as a prisoner.","So THE Maelstrom Thundermane simply wished and imagined that anomaly dying in the most painful way possible.","Being torn apart slowly by the unstable Weavings of Ginnungagap. Screaming in agony as his Existence dissolved. Realizing in his final moments that he had brought this upon himself!","This pleasant fantasy was one of his few consolation prizes for the misfortune that he found himself suffering right now.","But as he was indulging in these bitter thoughts while being dragged toward imprisonment, something caught his attention.","THE Maelstrom Thundermane , who was being forcibly escorted toward one of the cages by a Ginnu Lifeform, happened to see something in the corner of his vision.","He blinked in confusion before turning his head in that direction and looking across the distance.","There, walking calmly near the combat arena, was the figure of the exact anomaly he had been thinking about.","Looking directly back at him.","What?","What the fuck was this?","He had to make absolutely certain it was not an illusion or hallucination. He even asked himself if this was possibly some form of Civilizational Authority from another Malformed Ginnu Lifeform, showing him the worst possible thing that could be playing out right now in Existence as psychological torture.","But unbelievably, impossibly, in the distance stood the anomaly that had set off all of these catastrophic chain of events and caused him to be where he was right now!","Calmly standing beside a terrifyingly powerful hairy Malformed Ginnu Lifeform that had to be at least of THE Intermediate Depth or even THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty based on the oppressive presence radiating from it.","And that anomaly was even looking over toward THE Maelstrom Thundermane with an expression of genuine incredulity, as if surprised to see him here.","The two locked eyes across the distance.","Recognition flared between them.","In the next moment, THE Maelstrom Thundermane’s fury erupted with volcanic intensity.","He roared toward the nearby Malformed Ginnu Lifeform binding him, his voice carrying desperate rage.","\"That anomaly there is not a Ginnu Lifeform! He needs to be bound and collapsed immediately! He is an outsider who should not be-\"","Before his words could even finish, the Ginnu Lifeform holding his chains glanced in the distance toward Noah’s position.","The ancient being’s gaze found Ul’moreth standing beside the young entity.","Recognition and respect flashed through the Ginnu’s presence as he actually gave a deep bow of acknowledgment toward Ul’moreth from across the distance.","Then the Ginnu turned back toward THE Maelstrom Thundermane with expression shifting to pure annoyance and anger.","| You dare suggest we imprison a guest of THE Primeval Titan?|","The Ginnu Lifeform’s body pulsed with concentrated authority as he spoke a variation of The Phoneme of Darkness.","The terrifying power manifested instantly, not as mere absence of light but as the principle of mystery and hidden suffering given physical form.","Darkness wrapped around THE Maelstrom Thundermane’s Existence with crushing force, causing even his THE level body to pulse with sickly black and blue discoloration as the concept of pain unrevealed was inflicted upon every component of his being.","He screamed in agony as the Ginnu beat him thoroughly with linguistic authority, each strike reinforced by The First Tongue speaking suffering into reality.","Then, with casual contempt, THE Maelstrom Thundermane was thrown bodily into the prison cage.","The moment he crossed the threshold, the Logos of binding activated around him. Multiple Phonemes working in grammatical harmony to create inescapable confinement.","His Existence locked into place, unable to move, unable to escape, barely able to even process thoughts beyond the pain still radiating through him.","His eyes, filled with absolute hatred and impotent rage, could only stare across the distance toward the figure responsible for everything.","Toward the anomaly who stood free while he suffered imprisonment.","He roared internally with fury that had nowhere to go, trapped within linguistic bonds he could not break!","Oh!","—","Across Existence, entities continue to wish misfortune upon others, never learning the fundamental lesson that reality tends to teach.","THE Maelstrom Thundermane had spent those five minutes in Ginnungagap imagining the anomaly’s painful death in vivid detail, wishing for suffering and imprisonment and collapse.","And now he found himself suffering, imprisoned, on the verge of potential collapse.","The anomaly he had wished such fate upon stood free, honored, protected!","While he rotted in a cage formed from Existence’s own language.","Perhaps if he had spent those five minutes wishing for his own safe escape instead of another’s destruction, reality might have reflected that intention differently.","But such wisdom rarely comes before the lesson is learned the hard way.","And he would learn today!"]},{"number":4591,"title":"Chapter 4591: Chapter 4590: Logos I","paragraphs":["It was surreal to watch a THE level entity be beaten black and blue with such casual brutality, and yet here Noah was reflecting on it as he observed THE Maelstrom Thundermane lying in a cage and being utterly unable to leave.","How terrifyingly existence could play out for those who found themselves on the wrong side of power dynamics!","He shook his head at the ironic reversal of fortune as his focus was actually more concentrated on the coming together of Phonemes that formed complete words to create the inescapable bindings that even THE level entities could not break free from.","The linguistic construction was fascinating to observe now that he understood what he was looking at.","He found himself suddenly wondering something that made his eyes narrow with analytical focus. Had he seen the same thing in THE Northern Unfurling Node of Existence when he had been imprisoned there, but he simply did not understand what he was observing at the time?","Had those cages been reinforced with Logos of The First Tongue that he had been completely blind to?","He could not say for certain without returning to examine that location with his current understanding.","But his intense gaze toward the cages and their linguistic bindings seemed to have been caught by Ul’moreth, whose hairy form turned slightly toward him.","The ancient being smiled wryly while speaking with knowing tone.","|You just learned the eighteen letters, and you already want to jump directly into understanding complete words. Well, before you start trying to decipher things yourself and potentially go catastrophically wrong, I will tell you a little bit about them. Come.|","Ul’moreth began walking deeper into the settlement with Noah following close beside him, his presence radiating focus once more.","They moved through the ancient community as Ul’moreth spoke, his voice carrying across the space with measured instruction.","|After Phonemes, which are the individual letters comprising the alphabet of Existence, The First Tongue progresses to the second tier of expression. These are called Logos. Complete words formed by combining Phonemes in specific, intentional patterns with precise grammatical structure.|","They passed a group of Ginnu Lifeforms engaged in what appeared to be cultivation practice, their malformed bodies pulsing with various types of authority. Every single one of them turned immediately to Ul’moreth and gave respectful bows of acknowledgment to THE Primeval Titan as he walked by.","Ul’moreth acknowledged them with subtle nods while continuing his explanation without pause.","|Each Logos represents a fundamental concept or law that governs some aspect of Existence. Where a Phoneme is a single letter expressing a basic principle like Fire or Water or Time, a Logos is a complete word that expresses something more sophisticated and nuanced. Fire as a Phoneme is the concept of combustion and transformation. But you could form a Logos that means specifically Purifying Fire, or Consuming Fire, or Creative Fire, each one being a different word constructed from multiple Phonemes arranged with grammatical precision.|","They continued walking, passing structures formed from crystallized Existence that pulsed with incomprehensible authority.","More Ginnu Lifeforms turned to pay respect to Ul’moreth as they traveled.","|Now, here is something absolutely critical for you to understand, Little Anomaly. When you master certain unique Logos that have a preset identity completely, understanding not just how to speak it but why it is structured as it is, what fundamental truth it expresses, what emerges from that mastery is what entities across The Infinite Unfurling call...Grand Principles and Singularity Principles of Existence.|","Noah’s eyes widened slightly with sudden understanding as the implication crashed through his awareness.","Principles of Existence!","Ul’moreth’s presence seemed to intensify with the weight of revelation he was sharing.","|Principles of Existence, Little Anomaly, are actually unique Logos. They are official Logos of Existence itself. High tier words of The First Tongue that have been woven into the fundamental fabric of reality so deeply that they operate as natural laws. Many entities access Principles know they are the equations that govern Existence, the mathematical formulae that determine how reality operates. What they do not know is that those equations are actually words. Complete linguistic expressions in Existence’s native language.|","They passed another gathering where a Ginnu Lifeform was demonstrating something to a small group of students. All of them paused their lesson to bow respectfully toward Ul’moreth before returning to their studies.","| When you gain acess to and comprehend a Grand Principle, you are essentially stumbling onto an Equation of Existence- a Logos of The First Tongue with sufficient accuracy that you can reproduce its effect. When you advance to understanding a Singularity Principle, you stumbled into an even more complex and sophisticated Logos that you begin to use the power of...without realizing this power stems from The First Tongue. And Genesis Principles? Those are Logos so extraordinarily complex and fundamental that they delve into the third tier of expression of The First Tongue...Philology!|","BOOM!","Philology.","Phonemes, Logos, Philology!","The words burned in Noah’s mind as Ul’moreth continued!","|Philology is too distant for you right now but, complex Logos and Philology represent the very first words and sentences spoken when Existence began organizing itself from primordial chaos.|","Ul’moreth gestured with one hairy hand to encompass the settlement around them.","|For example, the Principle of Gravitational Attraction that exists throughout Existence. This is actually a Logos, a complete word in The First Tongue that can be broken down into component Phonemes. It contains the Phoneme of Unity, because gravity brings things together. It contains the Phoneme of Space, because it operates through distance. It contains aspects of the Phoneme of Order, because it follows consistent mathematical relationships.|","|These Phonemes are arranged in a specific grammatical structure to create the complete word that means gravitational attraction pulls objects with mass toward each other proportional to their mass and inversely proportional to the square of the distance between them.|","...!","Noah’s eyes were bright.","Unfathomably so!","Each word from Ul’moreth felt grander and grander than the last as if he was being freely given the secrets of Existence, and he was learning just how obscenely he could now violate existence if he had the right tools!","So...continue your long speeches, Ul’moreth!","Talk as much as you want!","|When you comprehend the Principle of Gravitational Attraction through conventional cultivation, you are learning to reproduce that Logos even though you do not realize you gained acess to an equation, to a word. You think you are manipulating some fundamental law of nature. But what you are actually doing is gaining access to The First Tongue unconsciously, without understanding any of it.|","They turned down another pathway through the settlement, heading in a specific direction. More Ginnu Lifeforms acknowledged Ul’moreth’s passage with respectful gestures.","|This is why entities who master many Principles are considered so powerful, Little Anomaly. They have learned to gain acess to multiple words of The First Tongue without realizing that is what they are doing.|","| Someone who actually understands The First Tongue as a language can accomplish the same thing with deliberate intention and grammatical knowledge. You can construct new Logos by combining Phonemes according to linguistic rules rather than hoping random experimentation produces useful results. You can modify existing Logos by changing their component letters to create variations. You can analyze Principles that others have discovered and understand their underlying structure immediately rather than spending years studying their effects.|","His voice carried profound significance as if he was speaking the very turth of existence itself.","|This is the true advantage of knowing The First Tongue, Little Anomaly. Not just that you can speak letters and words with power. But that you understand what Principles actually are at their core, and you can work with them as linguistic constructs rather than as mysterious forces that must be painstakingly decoded.|","...!"]},{"number":4592,"title":"Chapter 4592: Chapter 4591: Logos II","paragraphs":["Logos.","Principles!","Such a reality was making his Principles of Cheating Architect and Perpetual Harvest begin to buzz as at this moment, Noah had already gone deeply into himself, into the manifestation of his Civilization to look at the massive Trees representing his 5 Principles.","What the hell were they hiding this whole time from him?","He had stumbled onto them not knowing they were so grand, but it explained their ridiculous capabilties! And how they were even leading him towards a Genesis Principle.","As he did this.","They passed through what appeared to be a marketplace where various resources were being exchanged. Every merchant paused their transactions momentarily to acknowledge Ul’moreth’s presence as he merely nodded.","|Now, there are even some unique creatures out there across Existence who possess a natural talent for recognizing Phonemes and Logos even without formal training in The First Tongue. This talent alone gives them access to many official equations of Existence, to many Principles that others struggle to comprehend. They do not consciously understand that they are reading and speaking a language, but their intuition allows them to perceive the linguistic patterns underlying reality and work with them effectively.|","At this revelation, Noah’s Existence buzzed with sudden recognition as a specific individual came immediately to mind.","The First Farmer.","That ancient entity was able to nurture and cultivate Principles in ways that others could not even begin to understand or replicate. His techniques for growing and harvesting Principles had seemed almost mystical in their effectiveness.","To thr point that he was even visited by THE Creature.","Was The First Farmer actually recognizing and subtly steering Phonemes and Logos without consciously knowing that was what he was doing? Was his extraordinary talent for working with Principles actually a natural aptitude for perceiving The First Tongue?","The implication was heavy to consider.","As Noah processed this thought, Ul’moreth continued with his explanation.","|In Existence, there are many such anomalies that can be naturally influenced or even mutated by The First Tongue and exhibit terrifying capabilities as a result. Some beings are simply born with neural structures that allow them to perceive linguistic patterns in reality that others cannot see. Some have Existences that naturally resonate with certain Phonemes or Logos, giving them instinctive mastery over related concepts.|","They arrived at their destination, standing before the prison holding THE Maelstrom Thundermane that Noah had been focused on.","Ul’moreth pointed toward the Logos burning with concentrated authority over the cage structure, using them as a direct example for his continued explanation.","|Now, let me break down these specific Logos for you so you can understand how words of The First Tongue function in practical application. Look closely at the inscriptions surrounding this prison, Little Anomaly.|","Noah’s gaze focused intently on the glowing linguistic patterns as Ul’moreth began his detailed analysis.","|There are seven distinct Logos inscribed here, each one serving a specific function in creating inescapable confinement. The first Logos, the one glowing with deep purple radiance, is constructed from the Phonemes of Void, Division, and Space. It creates the concept of absolute separation between the prisoner and the outside world. The conceptual separation that prevents any interaction or influence from crossing the boundary.|","|The second Logos, showing silver white light, combines Order, Unity, and Ending. It establishes the rule that any attempt to escape represents a unified action that must reach its ending, its conclusion, which is defined as failure. The prisoner cannot begin an escape attempt without that attempt immediately concluding unsuccessfully because the Logos defines the end state in advance.|","|The third Logos, radiating golden amber, uses Time, Beginning, and Order. It ensures that the prisoner’s temporal experience flows in only one direction, forward, at a consistent rate, preventing any manipulation of time to find weak points in the binding or to age the structure until it fails.|","....!","Fuck.","Noah’s eyes pulsed with marvel at this usage of power!","One Logos creates absolute separation, another makes even the attempt of escape to be a failure, and another ensures that even time could not be used to get out of it.","And these were just 3 Logos out of 7 inscribed on this Prison.","Fuck!","Ul’moreth gestured to the remaining inscriptions with clear teaching intent.","|The fourth Logos, burning with crimson and black light, combines Fire, Death, and Chaos. It creates the threat of immediate collapse for any Existence that attempts to force its Way through the bindings. The more power you apply to breaking free, the more this Logos activates to unmake your Existence. It turns strength against itself.|","|The fifth Logos, displaying emerald green radiance, uses Life, Unity, and Water. It ensures the prison itself remains vital and intact, adapting to any damage or degradation, flowing around weak points to maintain structural integrity. The cage is essentially alive and self-repairing.|","|The sixth Logos, pulsing with pale violet, combines Darkness, Void, and Paradox. It conceals the prisoner from outside awareness while simultaneously preventing the prisoner from perceiving outside reality clearly. Both sides of the barrier are blind to each other, creating isolation at the conceptual level. Right now, I am influencing this to allow this Prisoner to see us as you two seem to share history.|","...!","HUUM!","Noah nearly laughed at this as he nodded with enthusiastic eyes for Ul’moreth to continue. Because while he absorbed all this knowledge like a sponge, he wss already imagining how he could use all lf this for himself!","|And the seventh Logos, the one shining with prismatic brilliance, uses multiple Core Phonemes arranged in a specific master pattern. It serves as the keystone that binds all the other Logos together into a unified system, ensuring they work in harmony rather than conflicting with each other.|","His presence radiated satisfaction at the sophisticated construction.","| When you stack multiple Logos together in The First Tongue with this level of sophistication, the result is that even THE Surface or Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entities cannot escape. They are facing not just physical barriers but living language, living words that express inescapable concepts. It is as if this prison actually has its bars being reinforced by multiple invisible jailers constantly working to maintain the confinement. Those jailers are The First Tongue itself, the language of Existence working according to its own grammatical rules.|","|And here is what makes inscribed Logos so extraordinarily powerful and efficient. After we inscribed these seven Logos onto this cage structure, we do not have to expend or continuously channel any personal authority to reinforce them. The First Tongue pulls directly on the authority of Singularity Principles to maintain its operation, and sometimes when the inscriptions are sophisticated enough, even Genesis Principles contribute their weight to ensuring the Logos continue functioning as written.|","|The language itself powers its own expression once properly inscribed. We simply had to write the words correctly, and now they speak themselves into perpetual reality without requiring any maintenance or energy input from us.|","Noah’s eyes shone brilliantly with wonder and growing comprehension as he absorbed this explanation.","This entire time, he and Ul’moreth had been conversing exclusively in The First Tongue, their words incomprehensible to anyone who did not know the language.","Inside his cage, THE Maelstrom Thundermane could only look toward Noah with hateful expression mixed with growing unease and confusion. He understood nothing of what was being discussed, hearing only the strange linguistic patterns of The First Tongue that his mind could not process into meaning.","All he could perceive was the continued expression of Ul’moreth’s terrifically oppressive power radiating through the space, an aura so overwhelming that it made abundantly clear this ancient being could collapse him in a single moment if provoked.","It was a truly terrifying situation to find oneself imprisoned in, unable to understand the language being spoken by your captors, unable to know if they were discussing your immediate execution or indefinite imprisonment!","Oh!"]},{"number":4593,"title":"Chapter 4593: Chapter 4592: Logos III","paragraphs":["Noah barely spared a glance for the imprisoned entity as his attention remained fixed on the multiple vibrant Logos surrounding the cage with fascinated wonder.","After several moments of studying the inscriptions, he looked toward Ul’moreth and asked with a voice carrying intense interest.","|Can you teach me about inscribing and writing Logos externally like this? The permanent inscription of The First Tongue onto objects and structures?|","Ul’moreth’s hairy form seemed to pulse with approval at the question before he launched into another explanation.","| The Inscription of The First Tongue is a heavy and terrifically difficult art, Little Anomaly. It requires far more than simply knowing and understanding Phonemes or even being able to speak complete Logos aloud. You must learn to write them in such a way that they continue expressing their effects perpetually without your direct involvement or conscious maintenance.|","|When you speak a Phoneme or Logos, the effect manifests and then fades once you stop channeling it. But when you inscribe The First Tongue onto weapons, buildings, constructs, armor, even living beings if you are skilled and careful enough, the linguistic pattern becomes permanent. The object itself becomes a speaker of The First Tongue, continuously uttering the inscribed word and producing its effect as long as the inscription remains intact.|","His voice carried the weight of extensive experience with this technique.","|The mechanics of Inscription are complex and variable. Different practitioners achieve different results even when inscribing the same Logos because you must write through your own Way of Existence while simultaneously allowing The First Tongue to flow through you. Your personal understanding, your cultivation foundation, your connection to Mana, all of these factors influence how effectively the inscription manifests and how powerfully it operates.|","| Someone with shallow understanding might inscribe a Logos of Fire onto a sword and achieve only modest enhancement of the blade’s cutting temperature. Someone with deeper comprehension inscribing the exact same Logos would create a weapon that burns with flames drawing upon Singularity Principles of combustion. The words are identical, but the depth of understanding behind them determines their potency.|","Ul’moreth gestured toward Noah with what felt like measuring assessment.","|If you continue to be insane enough in your rate of advancement, Little Anomaly, you would potentially become capable of inscribing Logos onto your weapons and armor, decorating yourself from top to bottom with linguistic patterns of The First Tongue. You could then face a THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entity with just multiple Logos supporting you, which would likely mean the constant support of Singularity and even Genesis Principles without you personally utilizing any of your own authority at all.|","|Imagine entering combat where your armor continuously speaks defensive Logos that make you nearly indestructible. Where your weapon perpetually utters offensive Logos that allow it to cut through any defense. Where inscriptions on your armament itself enhance your speed, strength, perception, regeneration, all drawing power directly from fundamental Principles of Existence rather than from your personal reserves. You would be fighting not with your own power but with the accumulated authority of reality itself backing every action.|","...!","Noah had to pace himself at the thought of it alone!","Becuase...sheesh!","What were Complexity and Purity before such things?","Existence was truly filled with unfathomable weavings of wonder!","But...","The tone of Ul’moreth became more cautionary.","|However, the art of Inscription of The First Tongue is extraordinarily difficult and requires years of dedicated practice and study to achieve even basic competency. The precision required is far beyond what verbal utterance demands. When speaking, small errors in pronunciation might reduce the effect or cause minor backlash. When inscribing, small errors create permanent flaws that can cause catastrophic failure, destroying the object you were trying to enhance or even causing linguistic explosions that could collapse your own Existence.|","|You must learn not just how to form each component of each Phoneme perfectly in written form, but how to connect them into complete Logos with flawless grammatical structure, and how to inscribe them onto different materials that each respond differently to linguistic patterns. Metal accepts Fire Phonemes readily but resists Water. Wood welcomes Life but rejects Death. Every material has its own affinities and resistances that must be understood and worked with.|","Noah listened to all of this explanation with growing marvel while looking at the sophisticated Logos inscribed on the cage before him.","If he could learn to inscribe Logos seamlessly onto weapons or armor or even entire constructs like The Infiniverse...","’Oh?’","The thought alone stopped him as from The Infiniverse, he thought of THE Loom.","Was that fucking thing...filled with Inscriptions of The First Tongue to be as impenetrable as it was and still powered and energized all these years?","It was only a thought that came to his mind as it may not be accurate at all, but he couldn’t shake the thought!","\"...\"","The possibilities felt genuinely immense and potentially reality-breaking in their implications.","Just to confirm his understanding and potential limitations, he asked with careful emphasis on a specific detail.","| One can inscribe Logos onto themselves, yes? Directly onto their own Existence rather than onto external objects?|","Ul’moreth was quiet for a long moment before responding with unusually contemplative tone.","| Well, yes. You can attempt it if you want to potentially collapse your own Existence catastrophically. Objects or other things in nature are relatively easy to inscribe and have them maintain their structural qualities. But Existences, living conscious beings, you would be forcing the letters and words of The First Tongue onto entities that are fundamentally not aligned with The First Tongue in its pure undifferentiated form.|","|All of us countless beings who have differentiated and specialized away from pure Mana into particular Ways and Paths. Our Existences resist The First Tongue to varying degrees because we have committed ourselves to specific expressions rather than remaining open to all possibilities. Trying to inscribe Logos directly onto such an Existence is like trying to write on water, the medium constantly shifts and rejects the pattern you are attempting to impose.|","|It is technically feasible to inscribe a Logos onto yourself so long as it closely matches your Way. A Way related to Fire would have a much easire time inscribing the Phoneme of Fire and its variations onto themselves, but they may collapse themselves if they inscribe Water while their Way is that of Fire.|","|But it is feasible to do all this and have the Logos act like an engine continuously enhancing your capabilities. But the effect is limited by what your Existence can withstand based on how much of a natural connection you maintain to The First Tongue in its purest form. Most entities can perhaps sustain one or two simple Logos inscribed on themselves before their Existence begins rejecting the patterns and risking collapse from the incompatibility.|","He paused, then added with voice carrying sudden realization.","| Oh, hmm, actually when it comes to you specifically, this limitation may function entirely differently. That is right, you are an anomaly of The First Tongue itself. Your Way is pure Mana, which is The First Tongue in its undifferentiated state. Your Existence has not specialized away from the source language but rather embraced it as your fundamental nature.|","BOOM!","The realization was a quintessentially heavy one for both Ul’moreth and him as moments later, Ul’moreth turned silent at the thought of it.","Yes.","Yes!","His eyes shone luminously as he processed the implications with mounting excitement.","Why not pursue this path? It made perfect sense for his unique situation.","Mana was his Way. The First Tongue was his Way. The language of Existence itself was what he cultivated.","This terrifying technique of inscribing The First Tongue directly onto his own body and Existence, would it not simply be equivalent to him writing words in his own native language onto himself?","He would not be forcing foreign patterns onto resistant material. He would be adding to and enhancing what was already fundamentally aligned with The First Tongue!","The idea was grand and glorious to contemplate in all its potential applications.","But there was still tremendously much work to be done before such techniques became feasible. He had not even successfully formed and spoken a single Logos yet, much less begun learning the intricate art of permanent Inscription.","One step at a time. Master the letters, then the words, then the writing of those words into permanent reality!","As he and Ul’moreth had their discussion of advanced linguistic techniques, THE Maelstrom Thundermane inside his cage could only observe them with growing sense of profound unease.","He was particularly fearful of Ul’moreth, whose aura radiated such stifling and overwhelming power that it made breathing feel difficult even through the cage barriers.","Since they were conversing exclusively in The First Tongue, THE Maelstrom Thundermane understood absolutely nothing of what was being said. He could only feel the continued expression of Ul’moreth’s terrifying presence, that suffocating weight of authority that could collapse his entire Existence in a fraction of a second if this ancient being decided he was not worth keeping alive.","He had no idea if they were discussing his fate, planning his execution, debating whether to use him for experiments, or simply ignoring his presence entirely while teaching unrelated concepts.","The linguistic isolation was almost worse than the physical imprisonment.","At least if he could understand what they were saying, he might be able to plead or negotiate or attempt some form of communication!","But trapped in incomprehension, unable to even process the sounds they were making into meaningful language, he could only wait in mounting dread for whatever these unfathomably powerful beings decided to do with him.","It was genuinely one of the most terrifying situations an entity could find themselves in.","Imprisoned in unbreakable bindings, surrounded by beings who could end you casually, unable to understand the language determining your fate.","THE Maelstrom Thundermane had wished misfortune upon the anomaly who led him here.","But as he watched that same anomaly standing free while he rotted in a cage...","He was beginning to deeply regret everything so far!","Noah saw this gaze of regret and did not even pay it any heed as he was thinking of even grander things.","He looked around the cages here that held a few THE and Pre-THE entities.","He was thinking that maybe...just maybe, he had found the metaphorical chickens to imprison inside his chicken coop.","Inside THE Organ of Civilization!","Why could he not imprison metaphorical chickens at the THE level inside of THE Organ of Civilization?!","He just needed to gain the power to defeat them and have the power to hold them in his THE Organ of Civilization, but would this not be easy if he took the 7 Logos that Ul’moreth had just introduced which were inscribed on these prison cages out here?","\"...\"","Hmm.","Hmm!"]},{"number":4594,"title":"Chapter 4594: Chapter 4593: Existential Intermission- The Annals of Mana","paragraphs":["In Existence, there were many weird oddities scattered all around across countless domains and territories.","Some oddities were unfathomably more odd compared to others as they pursued activities that defied conventional understanding or purpose.","Two entities that could arguably take the crown when it came to pure oddity were The Queen of Matter and The Shadow Guard, Night.","At this moment in time, in the current era, inside a unique domain within The Infiniverse, there existed an emerging Fold of Dreams that held seas of golden sands permeating all around for both the skies and the earth below.","The entire landscape existed in warm amber illumination, as if perpetually caught in the golden hour before sunset.","Inside such a domain, toward the central corner of this vast space, there sat a massive marbled golden table surrounded by three ornate thrones.","Two of these thrones were currently occupied by the figures of The Queen of Matter and The Shadow Guard, Night.","The Queen of Matter was adorned in a radiant white dress that seemed to be woven from countless pages of books, the text visible on the fabric constantly shifting and rearranging as if the dress itself was being continuously rewritten. Her presence radiated scholarly authority and accumulated knowledge.","Night sat beside her, adorned in a black tightfitting dress that hugged her curves with elegant precision. Shadows seemed to cling to her form naturally, creating an aura of mystery and concealment even in the golden light filling the domain.","Both entities sat on their thrones with stacks of books and papers scattered all over the massive table before them. These documents held wondrous Records of Weavings of Existence pertaining to The True Emperor of Quintessence and The Infiniverse itself.","At this moment, The Queen of Matter breathed out slowly as if clearing away building nerves before speaking with determined focus.","\"Okay, let us do this. The first discussion to put into The Annals of Mana. A proper record for future generations to understand who we were and what we faced...\"","Night nodded with agreement, her pen already poised over blank parchment waiting to capture every word.","The Queen of Matter then raised her voice slightly and called out.","\"Alright, Sir Henry, please come in!\"","...!","In the next moment, the figure of Henry Osmont manifested in the air above the third throne, his steps light and calm as he descended to sit.","He looked like a young prince of Existence itself, carrying himself with natural nobility and quiet confidence.","His hair shone with blue gold radiance, catching the ambient light of the domain. He was adorned in a blue gold shirt and matching pants that hugged his slightly muscular and toned figure, the fabric seeming to shimmer with concentrated authority.","Henry looked between The Queen of Matter and Night with wry smile forming on his features as he spoke with gentle skepticism.","\"We are at a fairly pivotal moment in our Existence right now. Is there really time for this sort of... this? Even if our Main Bodies are free to do this while events unfold elsewhere...\"","The Queen of Matter leaned forward slightly.","\"We cannot do anything to change the outcome of what is currently happening out there beyond the calculations and preparations already made. And we do not need to be so fearful of our enemies that we cannot even be comfortable in our own homes, right? If THE Loom erupts in the next few seconds and we all die from overwhelming force, what use is all this constant worry and tension? We can spend the time doing things we genuinely love and find meaningful.\"","Henry leaned back in his throne with thoughtful expression before responding with dry honesty.","\"If I was going to collapse in the next few seconds, this would not be the last thing I hope to be doing with my remaining moments of Existence.\"","As he said this, Night was already writing things down rapidly on the papers in front of them, her pen moving with practiced efficiency.","She chimed in without looking up from her documentation.","\"Hmm, what would you rather be doing then? You had a girl before that you brought to meet your Father, and now you have also added Lyra to what appears to be a growing harem. Just for the record of The Annals of Mana, are you planning to grow a harem like your Father has done?\"","At such a ridiculous and direct question, Henry smiled while shaking his head with mixture of amusement and exasperation.","\"I cannot really answer that definitively. But I do not think so, no. That is not my intention or focus.\"","The Queen of Matter and Night looked at each other meaningfully before they both wrote something down on the papers before them.","The Queen of Matter then picked up the questioning with smooth transition.","\"Okay, what about the harem of your Father then? He has more than a dozen women under his belt at this point, and Queen Adelaide is your biological mother. How do you look at the other Queens of The Infiniverse? And what would be your reaction if you ended up getting a sibling soon in the midst of all this chaos?\"","Henry took a moment to formulate his response carefully before speaking with calm and measured tone.","\"I look at all of them with respect and treat them accordingly as Queens who have chosen to stand with my Father and with all of us in The Infiniverse. They are powerful entities in their own right who made their choices freely. As for siblings...\"","He paused with slight smile.","\"I can say without any doubt that having children is something my Father is absolutely not planning on anytime in the foreseeable future. His focus is entirely on our survival and advancement, not on expanding the family further during such a dangerous period.\"","Night and The Queen of Matter nodded at this response, writing down his words with approving expressions.","Night spoke next, her voice shifting to more serious territory.","\"Okay, veering away from personal matters. What can you say about our current situation overall? We just learned about something called The First Tongue that The Master briefly sent knowledge about through his connection with RUIN/EDEN. So far, the only one among us who knows the full details and can actually do anything practical with The First Tongue is The Infiniverse herself as she faces off against a supposed Disciple of THE Creature . What...do you think about us having THE Creature as a confirmed enemy in the future?\"","Henry’s expression became more focused and serious as he considered the weight of the question before responding with steady conviction.","\"Enemies are enemies, regardless of where they come from or what titles they hold. So long as they threaten us, threaten our Existence and everything we have built, we will defend against them with everything we have. We already fight against THE Living Paradox and THE Living Emotive and countless others within THE Loom’s influence. If THE Creature comes next as another adversary, so what? We face what comes and adapt accordingly.\"","The Queen of Matter and Night both nodded at such an answer with shining eyes!","Night continued with another challenging question.","\"What about those among us who think that The Infiniverse should not have erupted to use the power of The First Tongue against our enemies? Right now, we are witnessing what we now understand to be a glimpse of a Genesis Principle from the Disciple of THE Creature, power they shockingly might have gained from THE Creature himself relating to The First Tongue . But with The Infiniverse using the power of The First Tongue in response, some fear that it will likely invite an even more terrifying challenge or retaliation that we may not be ready to face. Based on the limited background knowledge we have from what Master has shared with RUIN/EDEN, the power of The First Tongue is not even something those below THE classification can wield freely without risk.\"","At such a complex question, Henry frowned slightly as he shook his head with clear conviction.","\"If someone has a rock or a gun nearby and there is an intruder breaking into their home, should they use only the rock and not the gun because they are fearing what response might come next? Because escalating the conflict might invite greater danger? That makes no sense. They have to use every tool in their arsenal to do what they can to win the immediate battle and survive. The Infiniverse likely made countless calculations before she even made that move to use The First Tongue . None of us possess the computational power and awareness she and others hold. Who are we to judge them as they defend us using methods we barely comprehend? Whatever enemies come after this escalation, whatever response our actions invite, we can only deal with them accordingly when they arrive. Holding back power out of fear only guarantees defeat.\"","Night and The Queen of Matter nodded with clear agreement as the latter then posed what she indicated would be the final question.","\"Okay, last question and we will not bother you for a while after this. Do you think The Master will come back to the current era in time for whatever terrifying response we are about to face? Many are worried about exactly what kind of retaliation we might see from THE Dead Order, THE Living Paradox, and now potentially THE Creature himself. What response could we face now from all of them combined? This is not even mentioning the ongoing threat from THE Living Elemental and others...\"","At such a question touching on fears many held but few voiced openly, Henry was briefly silent as he considered his words carefully.","When he spoke, his voice carried absolute conviction.","\"My father is going through who knows what trials and dangers in the past to try and help us in our present. Whatever is happening to him across time, he continues to do everything by himself to give the rest of us a chance at survival and victory. We should all simply give away our Everythings of Fear, our Doubts, our perceived Limitations, and trust in what he is doing. When he calls for us to move, we move without hesitation. When he needs to be back in this era, he will be back. Of this, I am absolutely sure.\"","The answer carried heavy weight that settled over the golden table.","The Queen of Matter and Night looked at each other and nodded with shared understanding and appreciation.","The Queen of Matter spoke earnestly, her voice carrying genuine warmth.","\"We do not know what fate holds for any of us in the coming conflicts. But Night and I thought it would be... meaningful to have a proper record of you and other important personages of The Infiniverse preserved in The Annals of Mana . A Record of Our Everythings, who we were and what we believed in. Thank you for taking the time to humor us in this project.\"","Henry nodded at these words with slight smile before his figure began to fade, disappearing from the golden throne and leaving Night and The Queen of Matter behind.","The two looked at each other across the table covered in their documentation.","Night spoke first with thoughtful tone.","\"That went well...?\"","The Queen of Matter nodded in agreement before asking the next logical question.","\"Who should we talk to next for The Annals?\"","Night tapped her pen against her lips contemplatively before thinking of several options.","\"Not sure, but I can think of many...\"","The Queen of Matter smiled as she began organizing her notes!"]},{"number":4595,"title":"Chapter 4595: Chapter 4594 - 25 Seconds To Midnight I","paragraphs":["Within THE Loom.","In an unfathomably terrifying region of pure paradox, where seas of paradoxical authority seemed to stand above even the Weavings of Existence themselves.","Here, in this place where logic came to die, THE Living Paradox had stood straight.","He was no longer lounging around in casual repose, no longer affecting the appearance of relaxed confidence.","And just because of this single change in posture, just because he had chosen to sit up rather than recline...","WAP!","In the next moment, a flutter of chaotic emotions emerged in the space as a multicolored feminine figure appeared without warning.","The entity spoke immediately upon manifestation, her voice carrying layers of conflicting feelings that somehow harmonized into coherent speech.","\" You know, I was more than happy to continue my emotions of self deception and delusions that I held some form of control, some meaningful role or actual power over THE Loom’s operations. Such emotions are so wonderfully strong and all consuming that they put me in a state of mind where I can more easily study The First Tongue without despair overwhelming me. But when you go and do things like this, when you activate critical functions of THE Loom without even sending me a single word beforehand, when you so freely demonstrate that I absolutely have no control whatsoever over anything that truly matters... well, my precious emotions of delusion and grandeur are so easily lost.\"","The humanoid female entity said all of this while smiling brightly, as if discussing something amusing rather than expressing genuine grievance.","Waves of manic emotions surrounded her form, colors shifting rapidly through the entire spectrum and beyond. Joy mixed with rage, contentment blended with desperation, confidence merged with terror, all cycling through her presence simultaneously.","This was none other than THE Living Emotive.","In his seated figure, the visage of THE Living Paradox turned over to regard her as he actually smiled with what might have been genuine warmth and spoke with unusually forthcoming honesty.","\" Would you have preferred if I came to you first and we continued keeping up the elaborate act? You have known about all of this for many, many years already. Unlike all of the others who serve under me in THE Loom, you are the one that I have been the most honest with from the beginning.\"","She truly was the one that he had lied the least to over their long association.","The others he had either collapsed their entire Civilizations and forcibly taken their Hearts of Civilization for his purposes, or he had lied to them extensively and made countless promises that would never be kept once his true plans came to fruition.","But with Emotive, there had been a different relationship from the start.","The figure of THE Living Emotive , whose true form could barely be observed beneath the brilliant light of multicolored manic emotion wrapping all around it like protective armor, floated closer with that bright smile still fixed on her features.","When she spoke, her voice carried the weight of profound understanding mixed with genuine curiosity.","\" Emotions are pervasive across all of Existence. They touch every conscious being, influence every decision, color every perception of reality. This is why you kept me so close all these eons, is it not? Because you could utilize my Weavings that cover such a vast expanse of observable Existence to strike against THE Creature. To influence emotions across territories he controls.\"","\"I still have my uses, which is precisely why I do not truly fear for my life despite knowing how expendable everyone else is to you. But should you not fear for your own life? Because if you are activating core functions of THE Loom now, ahead of your original timeline, then it means you are accelerating your ultimate battle against THE Creature. Bringing the confrontation closer. Making it more imminent.\"","She paused dramatically before asking the critical question.","\" Are you actually ready to face THE Creature?\"","WAA!","At such pointed words, THE Living Paradox smiled with an expression mixing dark amusement and grim acceptance before responding.","\" Would anyone genuinely be ready to face the absolute monster that imprisoned every single life form with even an ounce of Civilizational Authority in The Infinite Unfurling? The monster that truly put all of Existence in The Infinite Unfurling under his complete dominion as he enjoyed and reveled in countless Sovereignties flowing into him constantly? He consumed countless Everythings while giving us such meager amounts of scraps and pretending it was generosity.\"","His voice carried the accumulated bitterness of eons.","\" Of course I had to rebel eventually. Of course I had to plan and scheme and build THE Loom as a weapon against him. But no, I will paradoxically never be truly ready to face THE Creature. Which is precisely why I must do absolutely everything that I can possibly do to prepare, to create advantages, to stack the deck in whatever small ways are available to me.\"","\"THE Loom is a blade that will strike at The Belly of the Beast, at The Belly of Existence itself where THE Creature has gorged himself. THE Creature has eaten so much, consumed so many Civilizations, oppressed so many entities across so many eras. Just how much time and attention will he have specifically for me when everything I have prepared is finally unleashed simultaneously? When attacks come from directions he did not anticipate, from weapons he did not know existed?\"","THE Living Paradox shook his head as he continued speaking with building intensity.","\"And even now, even with all these elaborate plans spanning eons, I still have to prepare additional countermeasures and backup strategies. That is the fundamental reason why I have activated a few critical functions early, ahead of the original schedule. That is the reason why The Fallout can now be considered to officially be on a timer, on an active countdown rather than merely a theoretical future event.\"","\" It was always inevitable. It was paradoxically certain to occur. It was existentially required. The Fallout will always arrive regardless of what specific actions anyone takes or does not take. But now, by activating these functions, I will simply be able to release Agents of The Fallout earlier than planned. Nothing too crazy or dramatic. Just... insurance.\"","THE Living Emotive listened to all of this extensive explanation with expression of genuine surprise coloring her features beneath the swirling emotions.","She spoke with a voice carrying uncharacteristic seriousness mixed with her natural manic edge.","\" You would have never talked to me this much before about your actual plans and concerns. Hell, it has been who knows how much time since you said that many consecutive words to me about anything of substance. The power of THE Creature is really getting to you now, is it not? Now that the time to truly face him after your countless eons of meticulous preparations are finally drawing near? Now that theory is about to become terrifying reality?\"","She continued with words that seemed designed to probe and taunt.","\" Are you experiencing doubt? Fear? Second thoughts about whether THE Loom will actually be sufficient? Wondering if you calculated everything correctly or if you missed some critical variable that will doom everything?\"","\"Or perhaps you are simply lonely, isolated at the peak of your conspiracy, unable to truly confide in anyone because trust is a luxury you cannot afford? Are these words to me simply because you need to speak your concerns aloud to someone, anyone, before the final battle begins?\"","THE Living Paradox laughed at her questions, the sound carrying genuine amusement rather than defensive dismissal.","When he replied, his voice held the weight of hard earned wisdom.","\"If any entity actually held complete confidence and absolute surety while preparing to face against THE Creature, then they have already lost before the first blow is struck. They have fundamentally misunderstood what they are facing. When confronting a true monster, one needs to maintain a careful balance of sufficient confidence and appropriate fear. One needs to have access to their Everything, all aspects of themselves including the parts that doubt and worry.\"","\"If one is missing any of their Everythings, if they have locked away their fear or their doubt or their capacity to adapt when plans fail, then they have already lost. Overconfidence is death. But paralysis from fear is equally fatal. The balance is everything.\"","The words carried heavy weight that settled over the paradoxical space!"]},{"number":4596,"title":"Chapter 4596: Chapter 4595 - 25 Seconds To Midnight II","paragraphs":["THE Living Emotive turned silent as she processed his response.","She had more she wanted to say. Questions she wanted to ask. Concerns she wanted to voice about her own role in the coming conflict.","But just as THE Living Paradox held a careful balance of confidence and fear toward THE Creature , so did she hold a similar mixture of confidence and fear toward THE Living Paradox himself.","And such dual emotion was particularly powerful for an entity like her, whose very nature was built around understanding and manipulating feelings.","Even more so as the final showdown drew nearer with each passing moment.","She smiled silently as she contemplated something she had known this whole time. This battle was ostensibly between THE Creature and THE Living Paradox, two titans clashing while the rest of Existence watched or burned.","But what about the rest of them? What about her and the other entities caught in the middle? Would they really be just pieces to be moved around on someone else’s board?","Or could they perhaps tip the scales just a little bit in one direction or another?","At this time.","THE Living Paradox’s hand moved slowly through the air, tracing the motion of clock hands ticking toward an inevitable conclusion. His voice carried the weight of eons as he spoke to the space where THE Living Emotive was.","\" We are now twenty-five seconds from Midnight, Emotive. Twenty-five seconds on a clock I constructed specifically for the countdown to The Fallout, a timepiece that does not measure minutes or hours or even conventional eons, but rather the accumulation of actions and reactions that bring us closer to the point of no return.\"","His hand continued its circular motion, mimicking the inexorable progression of time.","\" Let me explain how this clock actually works, since you will need to understand it in the coming days or years or however long we have remaining. Midnight on this clock represents the moment when The Fallout fully activates, when THE Loom completes its transformation from weapon being forged into weapon being fired. Midnight is the instant when every function I have built, every trap I have laid, every contingency I have prepared across countless eras all triggers simultaneously and strikes at The Belly of Existence itself.\"","\"Midnight is when THE Creature finally understands the true scope of what I have been building all this time, when his attention focuses completely on me and THE Loom. Midnight is the moment when hiding ends and open war begins, when subtlety gives way to apocalyptic confrontation, when Existence itself becomes the battlefield and everything we know potentially burns in the crossfire.\"","His expression grew more intense as he continued.","\" But this clock does not tick forward based on the passage of conventional time. Oh no, that would be far too simple and predictable. Instead, it advances based on the accumulation of significant actions that bring us closer to that final confrontation. Each major move I make advances the clock by some amount. Each function of THE Loom I activate pushes us seconds closer. Each significant action THE Creature takes in response moves the hands forward. Each intervention by other major players, anomalies, or oddities moves the clock.\"","\" The clock measures causality and consequence rather than duration. It tracks the building of pressure that must eventually release. It counts the stacking of conditions that make Midnight not just possible but inevitable.\"","THE Living Paradox’s hand stopped moving, freezing at a specific position.","\" At this moment, with the functions I just activated, we have moved to twenty-five seconds from midnight. We were at thirty seconds before I made this decision. The activation cost us five seconds, brought us measurably closer to the point where everything erupts. But...\"","\"This clock may remain at twenty-five seconds for months. Or years. Or even eons if circumstances somehow stabilize and neither side makes significant moves. The clock only advances when actions of sufficient weight and consequence occur. If everyone suddenly decided to stop escalating, to maintain the current balance indefinitely, we could theoretically stay at twenty-five seconds forever.\"","\"But paradoxically, we could also move closer to midnight in mere days if the right sequence of events unfolds. If THE Creature discovers something critical about THE Loom’s true nature. If one of the other major players makes an unexpected move that forces everyone else to respond. If and if and if...\"","His voice grew darker.","\" Or if I am forced to activate more functions ahead of schedule. Each activation brings Midnight closer. This... is the paradox of the countdown, you see. Moving forward brings the end closer. But standing still while your opponent moves might bring it even faster.\"","He resumed the circular motion of his hand.","\" So we are locked into this dance, this countdown, this march toward midnight. Twenty-five seconds remaining. Close enough that we can see it approaching clearly. Far enough that there is still time for maneuver, for adjustment, for last minute preparations. The most dangerous position possible because it creates urgency without certainty, pressure without clarity about exactly when the final moment will arrive.\"","\"You asked if I was ready to face THE Creature. The truth remains that I will never be ready, which is why I built this clock in the first place. To force myself to act before I convinced myself to wait longer, to prepare more, to delay indefinitely out of fear. The clock ensures that midnight will come whether I feel ready or not, whether my preparations are complete or not. It guarantees that the confrontation I have been building toward for eons will actually happen rather than remaining eternally theoretical.\"","His hand stopped again at twenty-five seconds before Midnight.","\" So yes, Emotive. We are very close now. Not necessarily in terms of days or years, but in terms of the space remaining for significant actions before everything erupts. Twenty-five seconds. It sounds like so little time when spoken aloud...\"","\"Watch the clock with me. Feel how it ticks not with time but with consequence. And understand that when it finally strikes midnight, when those final seconds run out and The Fallout truly begins, there will be no going back. No pause. No reconsideration. Just the full weight of everything I have built crashing down on THE Creature with apocalyptic force.\"","BOOM!","The space fell silent as his hand dropped, the invisible clock continuing its inexorable countdown toward the moment when Existence itself would burn.","A heavy silence settled.","And...","THE Living Emotive’s smile turned devilish as she spoke her final words before departing.","\"I wish you luck, O Primordial Paradox. After all, your success is my success in the end. Your collapse is my collapse. You die, I die. We are bound together in this madness whether I like it or not. Haha!\"","With such manic words delivered with genuine cheer, THE Living Emotive disappeared as abruptly as she had arrived.","THE Living Paradox remained standing in the paradoxical space, alone once more with his thoughts and plans.","He had spoken more honestly to her than he had to anyone in eons. Perhaps because the end was finally approaching. Perhaps because maintaining absolute secrecy no longer served any purpose when action was imminent.","Or perhaps simply because even he, architect of the greatest conspiracy Existence had ever seen, needed someone to talk to occasionally.","The functions of THE Loom continued operating according to his will.","The countdown to The Fallout continued ticking toward zero.","—","In Existence, certain events become inevitable long before they actually occur.","The collision between THE Creature and THE Living Paradox had been inevitable from the moment rebellion first sparked in Paradox’s consciousness.","The Fallout had been inevitable from the moment THE Loom was first conceived as a weapon rather than merely a domain.","What remained uncertain was not whether these events would occur, but rather when and how they would unfold.","And most critically, who would survive to see what came after.","THE Living Paradox had activated functions ahead of schedule, accelerating the timeline, bringing the inevitable closer.","THE Living Emotive had recognized her own lack of control.","And across Existence, in the past and present and future, entities made their choices and took their actions, each one adding weight to scales whose final balance would determine everything.","The countdown continued.","The Fallout approached.","And Existence held its breath, waiting to see if anyone would be left standing when the dust finally settled.","Inevitability was coming. Midnight was coming.","The only question was whether anyone was truly ready to face it."]},{"number":4597,"title":"Chapter 4597: Chapter 4596 - 25 Seconds To Midnight III","paragraphs":["In The Infinite Unfurling.","In Ginnungagap.","In The Primordial Genesis Shore.","For Noah, the goal to survive The Fallout had always been centered on achieving the power of The Level One Scale of Existence.","THE classification.","This had always been the fundamental objective as all the traversals that Noah had undertaken in the past and everything he continued to do in the present was designed to make absolutely certain that he did not experience tremendous catastrophic loss when THE Loom finally activated and The Fallout began.","Before he had left his Civilization to venture into the past, Riya had continued to tell him with growing concern how she felt the light of Mana that represented their entire Civilization dimming from Existence.","But now that he had attained the knowledge and developing control of The First Tongue, he knew innately with absolute conviction that Mana would never truly fade.","The First Tongue would never fade.","Of course, something similar applied to The Primordial Civilizations and the ancient entities who held such Civilizations at their foundation. They also could not be entirely collapsed or erased because they were too deeply woven into the fundamental fabric of Existence itself.","At this moment, as he looked at the imprisoned figure of THE Maelstrom Thundermane trapped in the cage, seeing the reduced state of such a powerful entity brought so low...","Noah turned to face Ul’moreth directly, his eyes shining with determination and building hunger for challenge.","| Existence is a struggle, | he began with voice carrying conviction. | The First Tongue is a struggle. Every aspect of advancement requires effort and confrontation with forces greater than oneself. Now that I have been given these tools, these letters and understanding, I wish to actually use them in genuine combat alongside internal practice.|","He paused before speaking the truly shocking request.","| Would it be possible to arrange for me to fight against the weakest THE level entity currently bound in any of these cages? I want to test myself against The Level One Scale of Existence while I am still firmly below it.|","BOOM!","The request hung in the air with tremendous weight.","Ul’moreth laughed jovially at the audacious words while his gaze remained fixed on Noah with what felt like measuring assessment beneath all that obscuring hair.","When he responded, his voice carried even more depth than usual.","|Struggle, Little Anomaly. You speak of struggle as if it is merely something to endure or overcome. But struggle is actually the catalyst that accelerates the processes of your Existence to become exponentially faster. The more one genuinely struggles, the more one puts sincere effort into confronting forces that should by all rights overwhelm them, the more rapidly their foundation solidifies and their capabilities expand.|","|This is a fundamental principle of how Existence operates. Comfort breeds stagnation. Safety breeds complacency. But genuine struggle, where collapse is a real possibility and victory is uncertain, where every component of your being must operate at maximum capacity simply to survive? That breeds transcendent growth that no amount of peaceful cultivation can match.|","His hairy form seemed to pulse with approval.","|Very well, Little Anomaly. You have a Foundation with The First Tongue. You have learned the eighteen Core Phonemes and begun practicing them internally. To stand successfully against THE level entities, I told you that you would need to master all eighteen letters completely. Fighting now will be an excellent glimpse of where your abilities currently are and what they need to become.|","He turned toward THE Maelstrom Thundermane in the cage as if sizing this particular being up and down with critical assessment.","| While this one you brought to your attention is technically weak by THE standards, they are definitely not the weakest entity we currently hold in confinement. So we will find you another opponent to start with, someone more appropriate for your first genuine challenge against The Level One Scale.|","Ul’moreth began walking along the row of cages, his presence causing the imprisoned entities to shift with various reactions ranging from hope to fear to horror.","| What you wish to do, Little Anomaly, is to go against a fundamentally higher Scale of Existence with The First Tongue as your primary weapon and bridge across that vast gap. For anyone else who asked me this, for any other Pre-THE entity who suggested fighting against THE classification, I might immediately say that it is simply not feasible and would end in certain collapse. But for you, given your unique circumstances and advantages, I will withhold definitive judgment and offer a cautious maybe.|","| Let me explain the very essence of what power a THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entity actually possesses, and why this creates a gap so immense that it theoretically makes crossing it impossible for those of the lower Scale who do not have that fundamental Civilizational Depth.|","His voice took on teaching focus as he continued inspecting the cages.","| When an entity achieves THE classification at any Depth, they have crossed a threshold where their Civilization becomes more real than conventional reality itself. Their Civilizational Authority does not merely manipulate Existence but actually defines what Existence means within their sphere of influence. A THE Surface Depth entity can impose their vision of reality over yours so completely that your techniques, your Principles, your very Existence becomes subject to rules they determine.|","|Against such an opponent, a Pre-THE entity is not fighting on equal ground. They are fighting while reality itself bends toward their opponent’s advantage. Every attack you make must overcome not just the enemy’s defenses but the fundamental nature of space around you that now defines your attacks as weaker than they should be. Every defense you raise must resist not just incoming force but the redefinition of what defense even means in this localized reality.|","|This is the true terror of facing THE classification. Not merely that they are stronger, but that they operate on a different layer of Existence where normal rules do not constrain them the same way. The gap between Pre-THE and THE is not quantitative but qualitative. It is the difference between playing a game and being able to rewrite the rules of the game mid-match.|","He paused before a particular cage, studying the entity within.","| However, The First Tongue can act as a bridge to cross that vast Depth, to equalize the fundamental imbalance, because The First Tongue is the language that defines what reality is at a level deeper than even THE classification authority can easily override. When you speak The First Tongue, you are not arguing with their imposed reality on their terms. You are invoking the original language that created all reality, including the reality they are trying to impose.|","|If a THE Surface Depth entity declares that fire cannot burn in their presence, they are using their Civilizational Authority to rewrite local rules. But if you speak the Phoneme of Fire in The First Tongue, you are not asking their permission for fire to exist. You are declaring fire exists according to the fundamental grammar of Existence itself, pulling authority from Principles that supersede local reality manipulation.|","...!","Holy fucking shit.","Noah blinked with a sense of genuine amazement at Ul’moreth as...how was he able to explain that so easily?","The power of THE was always so mysterious, but from his perspective, it wss going against someone who absolutely imposed their own rules on existences as anyone below Pre-THE...would not be able to change these rules!","But the Phonemes of The First Tongue, when truly mastered, did not even ask for permission to follow the rules of THE . They said fuck that!","This...was why it was even feasible to think about going against THE with The First Tongue.","And as he arrived st this point, Noah also knew that going against The Fallout and THE Loom... the answer would actually not be attaining the power of THE , but the answer would lie...in The First Tongue.","In himself!","As he thought of all this, Ul’moreth continued.","| This is how The First Tongue would theoretically allow you to survive and potentially even fight effectively against THE classification despite being a lower Scale. You would be fighting not with your personal power alone but with the backing of Existence’s own linguistic foundation. Your attacks would carry authority that even THE entities must acknowledge because it comes from a source deeper than their Civilization.|","Ul’moreth stopped before a specific cage, his hairy body nodding with satisfaction.","|Ah, that one will do nicely for your first attempt. The battle currently occurring in the arena is wrapping up. Thereafter, we will put you in to face this opponent. All the other Ginnu Lifeforms observing the clash of Ways will be quite interested because nobody has witnessed a genuine clash between Pre-THE and THE in quite some time.|","Noah’s eyes lit up with intense curiosity at this revelation as he asked with eager interest.","|When was the last time this happened? When was the last time someone below THE classification fought against THE here?|","Ul’moreth’s presence seemed to carry dark amusement mixed with respect as he responded.","|We only discovered the truth later, after the battle had concluded and the mysterious entity departed. It turned out to be a weapon that THE Secretive Eon had personally forged and was testing in genuine combat conditions. An absolute beast of a creation that, while firmly at Pre-THE classification in terms of its Civilizational Depth, was somehow capable of fighting against THE level opponents with shocking effectiveness.|","| That weapon survived three consecutive battles against THE Surface Depth entities before THE Secretive Eon retrieved it and vanished. We never learned what techniques or principles allowed it to bridge the gap so effectively. But you, Little Anomaly, will be attempting something similar through your mastery of The First Tongue rather than through whatever secret methods THE Secretive Eon employed.|","He gestured toward the cage containing Noah’s chosen opponent.","|Hoho...would this make me similar to THE Secretive Eon? Hmm...Let us see if you can match or exceed what that mysterious weapon accomplished. Let us see if The First Tongue truly can serve as the bridge that allows the impossible to become merely difficult.|","Noah stared at the cage with building anticipation, his entire Existence buzzing with the eighteen Phonemes continuously refining his foundation.","He was about to challenge The Level One Scale of Existence itself!"]},{"number":4598,"title":"Chapter 4598: Chapter 4597: Struggle! I","paragraphs":["An unknown number of Gigaparsecs away from The Primordial Genesis Shore where Noah stood staring at a cage containing a THE level entity he would soon battle, in a vastly different region of Ginnungagap’s chaotic expanse, another scene was reaching its conclusion.","This region was filled with obsidian rivers of concentrated instability that would shred Pre-THE Existences into component particles within moments of contact.","Tor and THE Living Origin floated victoriously over the three Malformed Ginnu Lifeforms they had been fighting, their opponents now shockingly bound by chains of Hunger and Origin that wrapped around their malformed bodies with crushing authority.","Tor’s obsidian crimson chains pulsed with devouring intent, constantly attempting to consume the Existence of those they held. THE Living Origin’s white gold chains glowed with the principle of reduction, forcing the bound entities back toward their most fundamental state.","Even though these were Ginnu Lifeforms fully capable of using The First Tongue and were operating in Ginnungagap where they faced no suppression from Existence itself, they still had not been able to stand successfully against Tor and THE Living Origin.","Two entities who were actually experiencing a level of environmental suppression themselves due to not being native to this region.","It was genuinely terrifying to think about the power differential that had manifested.","Tor looked down at the bound Ginnu Lifeforms with eyes shining with hunger as he spoke with voice carrying predatory satisfaction.","\"I want to eat them. Three whole Ginnu Lifeforms would be an absolutely magnificent feast. Do you have any idea how much my Hunger would grow from consuming entities this ancient and powerful?\"","THE Living Origin sighed with exasperation as she replied with calm patience.","\" You know you absolutely cannot eat them, you reckless thing. Eat them, and a THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty Ginnu Lifeform will be hunting us down with single-minded dedication. I will leave so very quickly if you actually try it. You can face that wrath alone.\"","Tor’s face twisted with annoyance as he responded with reluctant acceptance.","\" Whatever. We will leave them bound here and continue on our search. Someone will find them eventually and release them once we are long gone from...\"","In the middle of his reply, as he was casually talking, his expression suddenly changed dramatically.","His eyes widened as his gaze snapped toward one particular obsidian river passageway with alarm flashing across his features.","At that exact moment, brilliant purple obsidian light erupted from the river as a stream of concentrated temporal authority bloomed with overwhelming presence.","Someone stepped out from the river of time itself, their humanoid form burning and completely shrouded with terrifying purple obsidian flames that flickered with impossible patterns.","The entity’s face could barely be seen beneath the concentrated fire, only hints of features visible through the blazing energy.","They stood tall, perhaps seven feet in height, with a build that suggested both power and elegant refinement. The purple obsidian flames covering their body were not chaotic but moved with deliberate purpose, as if each flicker was precisely calculated.","What could be glimpsed of their face showed sharp, aristocratic features and eyes that burned with concentrated purple light. Those eyes held the weight of countless eras, the accumulated knowledge of someone who could observe time from outside its normal flow.","The very space around this entity seemed to bend and warp, not from raw power but from temporal distortion. Past and future flickered around their form, creating afterimages that showed them in different positions simultaneously.","The moment they appeared, THE Living Origin spoke with unusual caution in her normally confident voice.","\" Why are you here?\"","The aflame being smiled while looking at her with a gaze of calmness, as if watching a slightly grown up child who still had much to learn.","When he spoke, his voice carried grand and imposing weight that resonated across multiple temporal frequencies.","\" The better question is not why, dear Origin, but rather when. I will say that something quite interesting drew me here specifically to this point in time. Not to this location particularly, but to this precise moment in time. Fascinating, is it not?\"","Something drew him here. At this point in time specifically.","The emphasis on temporal specificity instantly caused THE Living Origin and Tor to become somber as they could only think of one particular anomaly who had been traversing through time.","In the heavy silence that followed, THE Living Origin looked at this being with calculating focus as she spoke carefully.","\" What do you mean something drew you to this time specifically? Have you not been existing in this time like the rest of us? Where have you been? No, the better question is when have you been?\"","The entity filled with a terrifying Depth of power that had to be at minimum THE Fundamental Depth of Absolute Sovereignty looked at THE Living Origin calmly with that unsettling smile still fixed on his barely visible features.","His reply came with imposing weight.","\" Time, Origin. Time is so critical for Existence that most entities fail to truly comprehend its significance. They experience it linearly, flowing from past to present to future like water running down a hill. They are trapped in the current, unable to see the river from above, unable to understand the full scope of what time actually represents.\"","\" Many fail to realize that if someone held genuine sway over time itself, if they could move through its currents with the same freedom that you move through space, they could accomplish so much that would otherwise be completely impossible.\"","His purple flames intensified as he continued.","\"I personally do not do too much with my capabilities. I observe, I maintain, I ensure certain boundaries are respected. But because I exist with this power, I prevent all others from being capable of violating Existence through temporal manipulation. I protect Existence to continue on as it should, maintaining the integrity of causality itself.\"","His smile grew slightly wider.","\"If there was someone freely traversing through time who was not me, who was making changes or observations or interventions across the timeline, that would be quite problematic, would it not? It would suggest my fundamental role had been compromised somehow.\"","The faces of Tor and THE Living Origin became noticeably heavy as they watched this terrifying being, both of them thinking of the same individual who had been moving through time recently.","The aflame entity smiled once again and laughed with voice carrying strange mirth.","\" Hey, why do you two look so guilty? Relax! You personally had nothing to do with any violation of time. Nobody has actually violated time’s integrity in any meaningful way. You both can relax your guard.\"","His tone shifted to something more casual and familiar.","\"Origin, since when did you become so strung up and nervous? Who is this new company you keep apart from THE Creature? You even stayed deliberately away from Paradox and the others recently, which I found curious. But no matter. What are you doing wandering around Ginnungagap at this time? Do you need help with something? I could assist if necessary.\"","THE Living Origin shook her head calmly as she replied with carefully measured words.","\" Nope. We should be perfectly fine on our own, just strolling around while trying to learn more regarding The Origins of Existence itself. Ginnungagap is an excellent place for such research and exploration.\"","At such words, the aflame entity smiled devilishly while remaining uncomfortably silent, his burning gaze fixed on her with knowing intensity.","Tor’s eyes narrowed dangerously as this being simply nodded after a few seconds and spoke with casual finality.","\"I see. Understood completely. If you ever need any help with your... research, I will be around these parts at this particular time. Just call out to me and I will appear. After all, we have to stick together in our little exclusive club, do we not? Those of us operating at this Scale must maintain certain bonds.\"","With such words, he simply disappeared.","Not through space but through time itself, his form flickering out of the present moment and returning to whatever temporal location he currently called home.","Tor immediately spoke with voice mixing annoyance and grudging respect.","\"Is that The Temporal fucker I’ve heard many THEs scared shitless of?\"","THE Living Origin nodded as she replied with simple confirmation.","\" Yes. He goes by many names across different eras and regions, but yes, I suppose Temporal fucker can certainly be counted as one of them.\"","At such words, Tor smiled widely as he spoke with teasing tone.","\"Oh, the pristine Living Origin using such vulgar language? Am I actually rubbing off on you after all this time together?\"","THE Living Origin’s calm reply carried her usual composed tone.","\" The only thing you are rubbing off on me is your general distaste for caution and attraction to danger. Let us keep moving. The more time passes that we do not find him, the more precarious our entire situation becomes. And please try not to talk so much.\"","Tor’s reply came with broad smile as he began whistling while floating behind Origin.","\" The day I stop talking because some prude tells me to is the day I will collapse my own Hunger out of boredom. You just try to keep up with me.\"","With such words, THE First Hunger disappeared into the chaotic rivers with casual speed.","THE Living Origin followed calmly a moment later, leaving behind three bound Ginnu Lifeforms to be discovered eventually.","But moments after they departed, from the exact area they had left, silent purple obsidian flames flickered again as if they had never actually left at all.","And truly, they never had left.","Yet the perceptions of the terrifying Tor and THE Living Origin , both entities at THE classification with tremendous sensory capabilities, had not been able to detect the continued presence.","The outline of the entity surrounded by temporal flames could be seen clearly observing the direction where they had just disappeared, his mouth showing a devilish smile as his eyes were filled with immense calculating calm.","He had never left.","He had simply made them perceive that he left.","And now he watched them go, knowing far more about their true purpose than they suspected.","---","In Existence, there were those who were powerful.","Entities who had reached THE classification, who wielded Civilizational Authority that could reshape reality, who commanded forces that could collapse lesser beings with casual gestures.","These were the titans that others feared and respected, the beings whose names were spoken with reverence or terror.","And then, beyond that already rarefied tier, there were those who were unfathomably powerful.","Entities operating on scales that made even THE classification seem limited by comparison. Beings whose capabilities transcended conventional understanding of what power could accomplish.","Sometimes, many of those who considered themselves powerful would never know when they stood in the presence of someone operating at that unfathomably powerful level.","They would look such entities in the eye, speak with them as equals, and never realize the true gulf that separated them.","Because the truly unfathomably powerful did not need to display their capabilities obviously. They did not need to intimidate or threaten or demonstrate superiority.","They simply existed, quietly observing, occasionally intervening, always knowing far more than they revealed.","This was the nature of true power.","Not the ability to destroy, but the ability to know. Not the capacity to fight, but the capacity to observe without being observed in return.","The Temporal entity smiled, and the smile was gloriously devilish!"]},{"number":4599,"title":"Chapter 4599: Chapter 4598: Struggle! II","paragraphs":["In The Primordial Genesis Shore, the settlement of ancient Ginnu Lifeforms continued its bustling activity as something exceptional was about to unfold.","The entity that Ul’moreth had stood before and chosen for Noah to fight against was being brought out from confinement.","A THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty Ginnu Lifeform, their malformed body rippling with concentrated authority, opened the cage reinforced by Logos and extracted the prisoner with chains of obsidian light.","The entity being released possessed the form of a human with a completely bald head and torn white robes that suggested monastic origins. A set of round purple rosaries was wrapped around his neck, completing the appearance of a warrior monk who had seen better days.","His eyes crackled continuously with purple lightning, the energy dancing across his irises with contained violence. Tendrils of lightning coursed over his fair skin in intricate patterns, creating a network of electrical pathways that pulsed with his heartbeat.","The eyes of this being were filled with extreme caution even as he was released from the cage. With his senses no longer obscured by the linguistic bindings, he could now feel the terrifying cluster of power concentrated in this settlement.","Many Ginnu Lifeforms surrounded the arena area, and he could sense with absolute certainty that they could all thrash him individually without tremendous effort.","Especially the hairy entity looking toward him with silent assessment.","A single casual slap from that particular creature felt like it could end his Existence completely.","Noah looked at this being with analytical focus as he activated his Lens of Civilization to examine his opponent.","A status sheet bloomed before his vision, half of the information clearly visible while the other half remained obscured behind question marks.","|Name: Raijin Katsuro|","|Titles: THE Monk of Ten Thousand Storms and The Purple Lightning Ascetic|","|Classification: THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty|","|Way: The Way of Heavenly Lightning|","|Genesis Principles: ???|","|Singularity Principles: ???|","|Grand Principles: ???|","|Weaknesses: ???|","|Additional Information: ???|","Noah looked at this partially revealed information with genuine surprise.","He had not expected to see any information at all on someone who had veiled themselves, especially someone at THE classification. But his Lens of Civilization seemed to be advancing alongside his overall Existence.","Even now, the terrifying Phonemes of The First Tongue were flowing continuously across his Existence in automated practice, elevating THE Foundation of The First Tongue and accelerating the development of THE Organ of Civilization.","He currently felt exuberant with building power as at this time, Ul’moreth stepped forward toward the imprisoned entity who would serve as his opponent.","The ancient Ginnu Lifeform’s presence radiated overwhelming authority as he addressed Raijin Katsuro directly with intent to be understood.","\" Listen carefully to the terms of your release, \" Ul’moreth began with voice carrying absolute dominance. \" If you fight one hundred battles in this arena, battles where you demonstrate your full capabilities without holding back, you can go free. Your sentence will be considered served and you may leave Ginnungagap entirely if you wish.\"","\"Your opponent for this particular battle will be a Pre-THE Existence. But you need to fight with absolute full power as if you are facing anyone else at your Scale or higher. If you hold back in any way, if you do not use your complete capabilities, the battle will not count toward your total. And instead of continuing with other opponents, you will have to fight with me next.\"","BOOM!","The threat hung heavy in the air.","Raijin Katsuro’s expression became somber and filled with genuine fear as he looked toward Noah with conflicted emotions.","His voice carried cautious concern when he finally spoke.","\" What if I accidentally collapse this Pre-THE opponent with my full power? Surely fighting at THE level against someone below that Scale will result in their immediate destruction. I do not wish to needlessly end an Existence.\"","Ul’moreth’s reply came with calm indifference.","\" Nothing of consequence will happen to you if you collapse your opponent. Just fight with all your power as instructed. If you collapse your opponent, then you collapse your opponent. That is acceptable.\"","...!","Raijin Katsuro’s expression became even more grim as the implications settled over him.","This young entity apparently stood among the Ginnu Lifeforms with enough favor that they would be completely okay if he was collapsed in this arena? Get the fuck out of here. Collapsing him would likely be collapsing a Ginnu Lifeform.","And it was Pre-THE versus THE classification. What result did they realistically expect apart from complete one-sided domination?","The entire situation felt designed to humiliate him.","Ul’moreth laughed jovially at the prisoner’s obvious distress as he waved dismissively.","\" Do not worry too much about the details. Just go and fight!\"","With such words, Ul’moreth waved his hairy hand with casual gesture.","Obsidian gold light wrapped around both Noah and Raijin Katsuro as they were both instantly deposited on opposite ends of the arena floor.","Noah took a moment to observe his surroundings with enhanced perception.","This ancient and archaic arena possessed a deceptively simple construction. The floor appeared smooth and was seemingly made from some type of wood, though Noah suspected the material was far more sophisticated than it appeared.","The walls rising around the arena’s perimeter were constructed from the same material, creating an enclosed space that felt both primitive and incredibly advanced simultaneously.","Noah looked down at the smooth floor beneath his feet, noting that it held no visible damage despite what must have been countless battles fought here over eons.","As his perception sharpened, he began to see why.","Logos were inscribed throughout the entire structure in patterns so intricate and sophisticated that he could barely begin to understand their full complexity.","The power these linguistic inscriptions emanated was enough to stand strong against even a THE Intermediate Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entity attacking the structure directly.","He heard Ul’moreth’s voice speaking directly into his mind at this moment through their connection.","| Many of the Logos you see are similar to what I showed you on the prison cages, as the arena itself was designed to be nearly indestructible and completely contain whatever forces are unleashed within it.|","|The first major Logos woven throughout the floor and walls combines the Phonemes of Earth, Order, and Unity. It establishes the principle of absolute structural integrity, ensuring that all components of the arena maintain cohesion regardless of the forces applied to them. The wood you see is not truly wood but compressed Existence shaped into this form and held together by linguistic authority.|","|The second Logos, glowing faintly throughout the structure, uses Space, Division, and Beginning. It grants the arena qualities of spatial expansion so that even though it appears to be merely a few dozen meters in diameter when inactive, when properly activated it transforms into its own isolated domain that extends for Gigaparsecs in all directions. You and your opponent will have essentially unlimited space to battle without constraints.|","|The third Logos combines Void, Ending, and Darkness. It ensures that all power erupting within the arena’s boundaries is completely contained inside its periphery and cannot escape or be directly observed by those watching from outside. We will see what occurs through the arena’s own perception filters, but the actual forces involved will not reach us. This protects spectators while allowing combatants to fight without worrying about collateral damage.|","|The fourth Logos uses Time, Order, and Life. It maintains proper causality within the domain and prevents temporal manipulation from disrupting the flow of battle. It also includes regenerative properties that slowly repair any damage that does manage to affect the structure itself.|","|There are seven other Logos inscribed here with various purposes, but those are the primary ones you need to understand. This arena is essentially a living construct designed specifically to facilitate battles between THE level entities without destroying the surrounding settlement.|","Ul’moreth’s voice took on more serious tone as he continued.","| Your enemy will fight at full power, and they absolutely should for this to be a real battle worth learning from. They should not be able to collapse you too quickly because the fundamental mismatch will be partially bridged by your use of The First Tongue. But I cannot guarantee your survival, Little Anomaly.|","|If I see you on the very edge of complete and irreversible collapse, I will intervene and end the battle immediately. But if you are collapsing just a tiny bit, if you are merely injured or damaged but still capable of continuing, I may leave you be and allow the struggle to continue. After all, you have to learn how to fly by being pushed from the nest. You have to struggle genuinely to grow meaningfully.|","Noah smiled with understanding as he knew this truth well from his own experiences.","He looked toward his opponent in the distance, separated by what currently appeared to be about thirty meters but would soon expand to Gigaparsecs.","Raijin Katsuro stood with extremely hardened expression, his entire posture radiating offense and disrespect.","He seemed to feel deeply humiliated to actually be placed in an arena with what he considered a weak Pre-THE Existence and told to fight at full power with apparently no repercussions for whatever occurred.","For an entity who had achieved THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty through dedicated cultivation, this matchup felt like a deliberate insult to his capabilities.","At this moment, Ul’moreth’s voice suddenly echoed out across the entire arena and settlement with amplified authority.","| Alright, alright everyone! A genuinely interesting match is about to begin! Pay close attention!|","In the surroundings beyond the arena, many powerful Ginnu Lifeforms who had already been gathered here to observe the ongoing battles now focused their attention with shining eyes full of curiosity.","Ul’moreth floated above the arena’s center with commanding presence as he addressed the assembled crowd in calm and dominant fashion.","| Today, you will witness something extraordinarily rare! A violation of conventional understanding itself as an entity that has not attained any Depth of Absolute Sovereignty whatsoever goes against one who has reached THE Surface Depth! This type of matchup almost never occurs because the outcome seems predetermined. But circumstances today allow for this exception, and it will be educational for all of you to pay very close attention to how this battle unfolds!|","The Ginnu Lifeforms watching bellowed out their excited affirmation in The First Tongue, their voices creating linguistic patterns that made Existence itself buzz with the expression of their collective power.","The sound was overwhelming, reality trembling from hundreds of ancient entities speaking simultaneously in the language of creation.","Ul’moreth laughed with satisfaction at their enthusiasm before raising one hairy hand and speaking the critical command.","| Activate The Primordial Genesis Arena!|","The moment those words were spoken, everything changed.","Noah watched with fascinated attention as the Logos inscribed throughout the floor and surrounding walls suddenly pulsed with brilliant light and began to move like living snakes.","The linguistic patterns slithered and rearranged themselves, activating in sequence as the arena’s true nature revealed itself.","This seemingly small arena they stood on, this modest space that appeared to be only a few dozen meters across, instantly expanded with reality-warping force.","Noah felt the spatial transformation occurring around him as he suddenly found himself standing atop an endlessly massive arena stretching out for Gigaparsecs in all directions.","The smooth wooden floor extended toward horizons so distant they could not be seen even with his enhanced perception.","The figures of Ul’moreth and all the other watching Ginnu Lifeforms completely faded from view as if they had never existed.","The space above transformed into obsidian blue sky that stretched infinitely upward, creating the impression of standing in a void between Existences.","The walls of the arena were so impossibly far away that the ends of this smooth battlefield could not be perceived at all.","It felt as if the entire domain contained only him and his opponent looking at each other across vast distance.","No distractions. No audience visible to create pressure or self-consciousness.","They seemed to be completely isolated in this place, free to battle with absolute full power without concern for anything beyond their conflict.","Though for Noah, it meant he was now locked in an isolated domain spanning Gigaparsecs with a THE level entity as his opponent.","And yet his Existence held no fear whatsoever.","Only anticipation. It would undoubtedly be difficult and filled with hardship!","His body buzzed with the continuous flow of eighteen Phonemes refining his foundation.","THE Foundation of The First Tongue hummed with readiness.","Across the vast distance, purple lightning began to crackle more intensely around Raijin Katsuro!"]},{"number":4600,"title":"Chapter 4600: Chapter 4599: Struggle! III","paragraphs":["Noah had fought many battles across his journey through Existence, but the battle he was about to engage in now was something that anyone with common sense would immediately scoff at.","Going against THE classification.","He knew it would be immensely difficult to face someone at The Level One Scale of Existence.","He knew he would be placed in an immense struggle filled with genuine pain and the real possibility of collapse. He understood these truths intellectually.","But he had to do it regardless. He had to struggle, to push himself beyond reasonable limits, so that his people could live when The Fallout finally arrived.","It was wild to imagine that he was actually attempting this as at this moment, Raijin Katsuro gazed at him with utmost coldness across the vast arena.","The monk’s bearing as a prisoner completely disappeared as he pulsed with a sense of glorious majesty that had been suppressed during confinement.","Purple lightning began coursing around his body with increasing intensity as Noah felt a terrifying sense of oppression erupting from this entity, causing his own body to experience both trepidation and excitement simultaneously.","Yeah. This was THE classification.","A power level he had run away from in the past when survival had demanded retreat. But not today. Regardless of the sense of trepidation screaming through his Existence, today he would face it directly.","At this moment, Raijin Katsuro raised one hand and began playing with tendrils of purple gold lightning that represented his Way of Existence, his voice carrying imposing weight across the vast distance.","\"I am Raijin Katsuro, THE Monk of Ten Thousand Storms. I came to Ginnungagap deliberately to challenge myself against the legendary Malformed Ginnu Lifeforms, to test my cultivation against entities who understand Existence at fundamental levels. When I was defeated and imprisoned, I understood clearly that it was due to my own lack of power and depth. I accepted my sentence without complaint.\"","\"Even while jailed, I waited patiently to battle again as I suspected this would eventually be my purpose here. But the battles I was waiting for, the opponents I expected to face, for my first match to actually be against a weak Pre-THE Existence who is not even a Ginnu Lifeform himself...\"","His expression twisted with genuine anger.","\"It makes me so unbelievably furious. So profoundly insulted that I can barely contain my rage at this arrangement.\"","BOOM!","Purple lightning exploded around his form as he continued speaking with building intensity.","\"I can see clearly that there is some form of relationship between you and the Ginnu Lifeforms here, some connection that grants you favor. And that they actually plan to use me, a THE Surface Depth of Absolute Sovereignty entity, as merely a whetstone to sharpen you like a dull blade being prepared for future use. This alone infuriates me beyond words.\"","\"Do you understand how it feels to forge your own Way through dedicated effort, to build your Sovereignty through countless trials, to achieve THE classification through genuine struggle, only to be used as a stone to sharpen someone else? This whole situation is utterly baffling and deeply offensive to everything I have accomplished.\"","His eyes blazed with purple gold radiance.","\"But since that terrifying entity commanded me to unleash my full power without holding back, I will do exactly that. Since this is supposedly a real battle for your development, I will treat it like one with absolute seriousness. I will show you the unbridgeable gap between our positions faithfully and professionally. I will go for collapsing your Existence completely, or at least ninety-nine percent of it at minimum. Do you understand the situation you have placed yourself in?\"","Noah looked at this being as warning signals screamed through every component of his Existence.","Raijin Katsuro now appeared wreathed in purple lightning that pulsed with internal hues of gold, creating a spectacular display of concentrated power. His eyes released rivers of terrifying Sovereignty, authority so concentrated it became visible as flowing energy.","It felt like he held absolute control over everything at this moment, like reality itself bent to acknowledge his dominance.","Noah’s Existence screamed danger warnings at him, as if all parts of his being instinctively recognized they were being locked onto by an apex predator.","Raijin’s voice continued with dark satisfaction at Noah’s obvious tension.","\"My Way, my Civilization, my Sovereignty over Existence itself. Someone that has not achieved any Depth in Absolute Sovereignty would never even begin to truly understand what this means. Do you know why you cannot comprehend it? Because as I have been talking, explaining myself and giving you time to prepare, every single Weaving of Existence in the surrounding landscape across Gigaparsecs has already fallen under my Sovereignty.\"","BOOM!","Instantly, Noah felt an overbearing and unfathomably heavy weight pressing down from all directions simultaneously.","The smooth floor beneath his feet, the obsidian blue sky above, the air itself, everything within perception suddenly crackled with purple gold lightning that had not been there moments before.","Raijin’s expression looked almost forlorn as he shook his head with what might have been pity.","|In this place, within the reach of my Sovereignty, I am the only thing that is now inevitable. I am the only certainty. If you had any Depth of Absolute Sovereignty at all, even the smallest foundation of civilizational authority, you might have been able to fight with me on equal terms regarding this. To express your own view and impose your own Way against mine. But you have no Depth whatsoever. I alone control all Weavings of Existence in this nearby expanse, and I alone say what can and cannot occur. And right now, there can be no expression of Sovereignty but my own. And right now, I decree that I should be the only one standing. Everything else should be kneeling. You should be kneeling before THE.|","BOOM!","The words carried inviolable authority that crashed against Noah with crushing force.","The Sovereignty was suffocating, overwhelming, absolute.","The moment Raijin’s words finished speaking, Noah found himself unable to do anything but feel the terrifying Depth of Heavenly Lightning pressing against every component of his being.","Even when his Existence buzzed with resistance, even when every refined cell and nerve cried out in defiance, absolutely everything felt horrifically suppressed.","His Existence that had been reinforced by The First Tongue, that had been refined by eighteen Phonemes flowing continuously through his foundation, actually showed a glimmer of genuine resistance.","For a brief moment, THE Foundation of The First Tongue pushed back against the imposed Sovereignty with linguistic authority.","But he had only just begun this process of reinforcement. THE Foundation of The First Tongue had only just started to be properly established.","It was still young, still developing, still accumulating the necessary Depth to stand against THE classification.","He had not nearly accumulated enough foundational weight yet.","So shockingly, after that initial flicker of resistance, something terrible occurred.","Noah felt like all of Existence itself bore down on him with crushing intent. Contrary to his mental commands, contrary to him thinki his body reinforced by The First Tongue would have sufficient resistance yo at least stabd against THE classification...","BOOM!","His Barrier of Hunger, that defensive construct he had relied on many times, shattered like glass under the weight of imposed Sovereignty.","And an instant later, before he could even process that failure...","BOOM!","Noah felt his knees, against all his will and intention, hit the smooth floor of The Primordial Genesis Arena with devastating force.","What?","His knees? On the floor? Him? Kneeling?","Him?!","The shock of it crashed through his consciousness with intensity.","Raijin looked down at Noah while wreathed in magnificent purple gold lightning, his voice carrying dark satisfaction.","\"What did you think would happen when you stood against THE classification? This is an entirely different Scale of Existence from anything you have experienced before. Did you genuinely think you would be capable of some form of meaningful opposition? To deny THE? Denying THE is functionally equivalent to denying Existence itself.\"","\"I exist here, and I have laid absolute claim on all Existence within my reach. Anything I say goes without question or resistance. My Sovereignty commanded you to kneel, so you kneeled. It is that simple. Why do you have that expression as if this should not have happened? What else could have possibly occurred? You have no Depth to resist with. You have no claim over Existence to make. I do not know what unique power you possessed that you thought would have helped you here, but this is reality. This is the gulf, and this is the discrepancy between me and you. Between THE and Pre-THE. It is like I am facing a helpless child at this moment.\"","His voice grew colder.","\"This profound mismatch was the reason for my shame and fury and disrespect at being placed against you. Let me have you feel exactly the same helplessness and humiliation I experienced. Remain kneeling. Do not even attempt to look up at me. You cannot even gaze upon THE with that weak foundation. Stare at that floor beneath you and reflect on your insignificance. Do not speak. Do not do anything. Just feel that absolute helplessness, and it will give you a small glimpse of how I felt when I was imprisoned and bound.\"","BOOM!","Noah’s Existence buzzed at this moment with unprecedented fervor as everything about his being cried out in furious rejection.","He had known THE classification was grand and powerful beyond normal comprehension. He had thought his extensive preparations had been somewhat sufficient to at least stand.","He had thought Ul’moreth’s words about needing to Master all eighteen Phonemes to stand against THE were guidelines, that he would somehow be an exception due to his unique advantages.","But for him to be forced onto his knees? To be made to kneel against his will?","New prompts erupted before his vision with critical information.","|For the first time in your cultivation journey, your Quintessence has been challenged in an inviolable way.|","|Your fundamental nature as an entity who kneels to no one has been directly violated.|","|If you do not overcome this challenge to your Quintessence, this core distinction will be forever lost from your Weavings.|","|Your identity as one who stands regardless of opposition is at stake.|","| OVERCOME OR BE DIMINISHED.|","The weight of those words crashed through Noah’s consciousness as he stared at the smooth floor beneath him, feeling the crushing Sovereignty of THE pressing down from all directions.","His knees were on the ground.","He was kneeling.","And somewhere deep within his Existence, something fundamental began to burn with absolute refusal to accept this state!"]}]);
